1 OCCU warden of St. Clements, Ipswich
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Church was warden of St. Clements, Ipswich, in 1597
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of JOHN CHURCH and CATHERINE SWAN.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Thomazine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomazine and Thomas Church are:
2 CONT # Thomas Church.
2 CONT # John Church.
2 CONT # Charles Church. He married Constant Sapcott 8 JUN 1580 in England.
2 CONT # Robert Church. He married Elisabeth Barnards 25 MAR 1609 in England.
2 CONT # Richard Church died 24 AUG 1603 in England. He married Agnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From Simeon Church of Chester, Connecticut, 1708-1792, and His Descendants, by Charles Washburn Church. Press, Waterbury, CT 1914 [https://archive.org/stream/simeonchurchofch1914chur#page/6/mode/2upÂ Page 6 - 7]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Church, son of Robert Church of Castell Camps, of Sanford, Co. Essex, as appears from a Harleian manuscript, married Catherine Swan, probably in 1547, and was made freeman in that year. He had an armory. Their children were J
2 CONC ohn and Thomas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas''' married Thomazine. He was warden of St. Clements, Ipswich, in 1597. They had a son Thomas who settled in London and had children baptized in St. James ; also son John, who settled at Wymingwell, Kent ; Charles, who ma
2 CONC rried June 8, 1580, Constant Sapcott ; Robert, who married March 25, 1509, Elisabeth Barnards; and Richard, who married Agnes and died Aug. 24, 1603. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=pete%5Fwitze&id=I22397
2 CONT * https://archive.org/stream/simeonchurchofch1914chur#page/6/mode/2up
