2 CONT Acquisition Information  - Gift, 29 June 1950, of Frank Taylor of Fredericksburg, Virginia, through George H. S. King of Fredericksburg. Descriptive Summary  - Repository: The Library of Virginia Accession Number: 23554.  Title: B
2 CONC all Family Papers, 1680-1785 - Physical Description: 12 leaves and 47 pages. Language: English Creator: Ball Family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Scope and Content:  Papers, 1680-1785, of the Ball family of Lancaster County, Virginia, consisting of wills, 1680-1785, of William Ball (1615-1680), Richard Ball (ca. 1675-1726), Margaret Ball (ca. 1702-1783), and William Ball (d
2 CONC . 1785), all of Lancaster County; inventories, 1727-1773, of the estates of Richard Ball, William Ball, Jr. (1700-1741), John Ball (d. 1772), and an unidentified estate; deeds, 1733-1758, for property in Lancaster County and slave
2 CONC s; letters, 1764 and 1780, discussing the property of Margaret Ball; depositions, 1775-1782, concerning the purchase of slaves from the estate of William Ball, and concerning crops made on the estate of John Ball; legal opinions, 
2 CONC 1779 and no date, concerning the estate of Mary Ball, and concerning a deed between Margaret Ball and William Ball; a list, no date, of slaves from an unidentified estate; and Ball family genealogical notes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographical Information  - *'''Born about 1615, [https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000014280951747?through=6000000000591496498 William Ball] emigrated to Virginia and became a prosperous landowner in 
2 CONC Lancaster County, Virginia. He served as a justice, a colonel of the militia, and as a delegate to the House of Burgesses. He fathered four children, including''' 
2 CONT **[https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000000591496498 William Ball] (1641-1694).. [who] had nine children, including 
2 CONT ***[https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000002713586427?through=6000000000591496498 William Ball] (ca. 1674-1744). He married [https://www.geni.com/people/Hannah-Beale-Ball/6000000002713586455?through=60
2 CONC 00000002713586427 Hannah Heale] (d. ca. 1744) and they had 6 children, including 
2 CONT ****https://www.geni.com/people/William-Ball-IV/6000000004555806518?through=6000000002713586455  William Ball] (ca. 1700-1741). He married his cousin [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Ball/6000000008066903605?through=6000000004555
2 CONC 806518 Margaret Ball]  (ca. 1702-1783), the daughter of his uncle [https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Ball-of-Lancaster-VA/6000000000591521279?through=6000000008066903605 Richard Ball] (ca. 1675-1726) 17 February 1723/4. They had
2 CONC  6 children, including 
2 CONT ****William Ball (d. 1760), who had 2 children, including 
2 CONT ******Dr. William Ball (d. 1785).
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents List:  
2 CONT *Will, dated 5 October 1680 and recorded 10 November 1680, of William Ball (1615-1680) of Lancaster County.  
2 CONT *Will, recorded 8 February 1726/7, of Richard Ball (ca. 1675-1726) of Lancaster County.  
2 CONT *Inventory, recorded 9 August 1727, of the estate of Richard Ball.  
2 CONT *Deed, dated 12 May 1733, for 1/2 acre in Lancaster County from Hopkins Wilder to Lawrence Blade, both of Lancaster County, subsequent assignments dated 29 June 1742 and 22 October 1745.  
2 CONT *Inventory, dated 4 October 1742, of the estate of William Ball Jr. (ca. 1700-1741).  
2 CONT *Deed, dated 8 May 1747, for land and slaves from Margaret Ball (ca. 1702-1783) to William Ball (d. 1785), both of Lancaster County.  
2 CONT *Ball family genealogical chart, 24 August 1748.  
2 CONT *Deed, recorded in general court 27 October 1758, for 50 acres in Lancaster County from Margaret Ball to William Ball.  
2 CONT *Letter, 30 October 1764, from David Boyd to Margaret Ball concerning property inherited from her husband.  
2 CONT *Deposition, 1 August 1775, of James Newby (1723-1791) concerning the purchase of slaves by John Lee of Essex County, Virginia, from the estate of William Ball.  
2 CONT *Deposition, 1 August 1775, of Richard Ball (b. 1732) concerning the purchase of slaves by John Lee of Essex County, Virginia, from the estate of William Ball.  
2 CONT *Inventory, recorded 19 July 1773 in Lancaster County and 27 July 1773 in Fauquier County, Virginia, of the estate of John Ball (d. 1772).  
2 CONT *Legal opinion, 15 April 1779, of David Boyd concerning the estate of Mary Ball.  
2 CONT *Legal opinion, 22 December 1779, of Edmund Randolph concerning the estate of Mary Ball.  
2 CONT *Legal opinion, 22 December 1779, of Edmund Randolph concerning the estate of Mary Ball.  
2 CONT *Letter, 21 April 1780, from Margaret Ball to William Ball concerning her property.  
2 CONT *Deposition, 22 September 1782, by Norman Utterback, overseer, concerning crops made on the estate of John Ball.  
2 CONT *Will, dated 21 June 1777 and recorded 16 October 1783, of Margaret Ball.  
2 CONT *Will, dated 17 June 1785 and recorded 22 July 1785, of William Ball.  
2 CONT *Inventory, no date, of an unidentified estate.  
2 CONT *List, no date, of slaves of an unidentified estate.  
2 CONT *Legal opinion, no date, concerning a deed between Margaret Ball and William Ball.  
2 CONT *Genealogical notes, no date, on the Ball family.  
2 CONT *Will, no date, of Margaret Ball. 
2 CONT *Captain William Ball's Will (2nd Generation) (1641-1694)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Inventories and Wills 8 Page 90, Lancaster Court Records (Probated November 2, 1694) - '''In the name of God Amen I Capt William Ball''' of the parish of St. Marys White Chapel in the County of Lancaster in Virginia being sick & 
2 CONC weak in body butf sound & Perfect memory Praised be ye Almighty God for the same & considering the frailty of this life being but a blast I doe make this my Last Will and Testament in manner and form Following hereby revoking and 
2 CONC making Void all other Will or Wills formerly by me made sealed or published. 
2 CONT
2 CONT First I give my soule to God that gave it me & commit my body to the Earth to be burried in decent order at the Discretion on my Executors hereafter named in hope and true confidence that I shall have a joyful resurrection at the 
2 CONC Last day thru the merits of my most dear & precious redeemer the Lord Jesus Christ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my dear wife all and every part of this 270 acres of Land whereupon I now Live with all the housing & appearances thereunto belonging and also my mill hereon standing during her Natural life and also full Power to plan
2 CONC t, make and manure for her own use a Plantation if she please on every other Parcel of Land hereafter by me hereby given & my will is that she bring up my dear Children until they be 16 yrs. Of age in Writing, Reading & that they 
2 CONC may be under the tuition of my sons William and Richard, and that whenever the said mill be out of repair my will is that my said sons William Ball & Richard Ball give their assistance to mend repaire or new build her and that the
2 CONC y be paid for their paines as the mill earns it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my said sons William Ball & Richard Ball all my Tract lyeing in this Neck next to Richard Cundiffs being about 950 acres to be equally divided between them provided they acquit all their right which they or either of t
2 CONC hem may possibly have of any and to that Divident of Land in Richmond County nest above Perpetua Creek being about 1,000 acres on which my Quarter Plantation now is unto their two brothers Joseph Ball & George Ball then I do give 
2 CONC unto my said sons William Ball and Richard Ball to them and their heirs forever all and every part of the above said 950 acres of Land Lying in this Neck next Richard Cundiffs as aforesaid but if my said two sons William Ball & Ri
2 CONC chard Ball molest their two brothers Joseph Ball & George Ball in their Quiet Possession at any time or times hereafter either them or their heirs in the said 1,000 acres of Land at Perpetua Creek where my Quarter now is that I th
2 CONC en do hereby give my said two sons Joseph Ball & George Ball and their heirs all and every part & Parcel of that 950 acres before hereby given unto my two sons William Ball & Richard Ball as aforesaid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my two sons Joseph Ball & George Ball to them and their heirs all and every part & parcel of that Divident of Land in Richmond County whereon my quarter now is near the head of Perpetua Creek to be Equally divided betw
2 CONC een them. I give unto my four sons (viz) James Ball, David Ball, Stretchley Ball & Samuel Ball to them and their heirs forever all and every part of my upper divident of land being 1600 acres more or less Lying in Richmond County 
2 CONC above Mr. James Harrison's to be equally divided between them. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my dear Daughter Margaret Ball and to her and her heirs forever all that and every part & Parcel of the Divident whereon my mother Lives at the mouth of Corratomon being about 350 acres more to bee laid out of my ajoyn
2 CONC ing Divident next to the Plantation that James Wood lives on only reserving to my dear (wife or mother?) one third part of all the sider made thereon clear of all charge making & cask. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my said son William Ball a man serv't named Luke Dickson and a Negro man named Robin.... ?  James Canady & Sarah and a Silver salt siller, Tankard & drinking Cup of Silver and which of my Cups she shall make Choice of. I
2 CONC  give unto my son William all the residue of my cups after my dear wife hath her choice of one. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my son James Ball two slaves called Dominy & Kate and a boy and a girle. I give to my son David Ball a girle slave called Poll. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my daughter Margaret Ball two slave girls called Hannah & Betty that's at mother's. I give unto my son Stretchley Ball a girl Slave called Saran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my son Samuel Ball a girl slave called Doll. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The rest of my white servants and slaves not before hereby given. being Cox. Scotch, Tom, Betty & her mulatto child, 3 negroe women called Doll & Betty & Bess at mother's. I give unto my three eldest sons, viz., William Ball, Rich
2 CONC ard Ball, and James Ball in consideration that they be at the charge of bringing up and maintaining their three youngest brothers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give and Bequeath unto my said sons William & Richard Ball 2/6s part of all the rest of my estate not hereby before given Desiring them to take all the care they can of their dear mother. And the residue of all my estate whereon
2 CONC  had, found or being not before hereby given. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to be equally divided between my dear children here named, James, Joseph, David, George, Margaret, Stretchley & Samuel after their mother's decease but my will is that my dear wife have the use of it During her Natural Life
2 CONC . I doe make & Ordaine my son William Ball and my son Richard Ball the executors of this my last Will and testament and my loving Brother Captain David Fox and my loving friends Mr. George Heale & Mr. Edwin Conway the overseers of
2 CONC  this my last will and testament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness Whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seale this 28th day of Sept A* 1694. William Ball (Seal) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed, sealed & Published in Presence of Abraham Taylor, George Hinch, Edwin Conway
2 CONT
