2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/89/98/d4/f6/5344484157878496/ball_of_virginia_coat_of_arms_from_colonial_families_original.jpg?hash=159c331538de621b80af3180ca25c976d5c3583e7b5383554c4194111720ee33.1794297599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Ball of Virginia Coat of Arms from "Colonial Families"
2 NOTE Coats-of-Arms in Virgnia, "William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Papers," Vol. 1, No. 3. (Jan., 1893), pp. 167-171.
3 CONT
3 CONT COATS-OF-ARMS IN VIRGINIA.
3 CONT (Additions to the List given in last Quarterly.)
3 CONT HANNAH BALL: will, Lancaster, June 25th, 1695, and Richard and David Ball, bond, Lancaster, 1712, apparently the same arms. the seals of the two last are perfectly pre- served, and bear a bend between two lions rampant holding a g
3 CONC lobe in the dexter paw. That on Mrs. Ball's will is somewhat defaced, but shows the bend between what appears to be lions. Her crest, perfectly preserved, is a lion rampant with dexter paw extended (probably holding a globe). This
3 CONC  coat differs somewhat from the well known emblazoning of the Ball arms, described by Hayden (Va. Genealogies) and others.
