2 CONT He married Mary (Bennett) Johnson about 1707-8 (post 6 Feb 1707).
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died between 25 June & 11 July 1711 at "Epping Forest", Lancaster Co.,VA.
1 NOTE from Colonial Families of the Southern Sgtates of America
2 CONT  COL. JOSEPH BALL (8-3) of "Eping Forest," Lancaster Co. Va, b. May 24, 1649 in England; d. June 1711, In Virginia; he was the third son of Col. William and Hannah (Atherold) Ball of "Millenbeck," Lancaster Co. Va; will dated June
2 CONC  25, 1711; probated July 11, 1711; served as Lieut. col. of Lancaster Co.; was a staunch and liberal supporter of the Established Church, and a Vestryman; m. (first) 1675, in England Elizabeth Romney, d. prior to 1703; dau. of Wil
2 CONC liam Romney of London, England; (second) 1707 Mary (Montague) Johnson of lancster Co. Va. a native of England
1 NOTE William Ball b 1615 d 1680.. Virginia genealogies
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=b5f9febe-f7ad-44c1-a80b-7aaec99ad33e&tid=7209793&pid=-1125211293
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Joseph Ball
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=3eff1164-6f6e-4dbe-bdfc-e4af71a2507a&tid=7209793&pid=-1125211293
1 NOTE Colonel William Ball was the great-grandfather of George Washington; hewas also the grandfather of George Ball (born: abt 1683), who marriedGrace Haynie, daughter of Anthony Haynie and Sarah Harris and granddaughter of CPT John Ha
2 CONC ynie and JaneMorris.
