1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 MAR 1650
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Hannah Ball (1650 - 1694)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah (Atherold) Ball and William Ball had at least four children. He was estranged from his daughter, '''Hannah''', who had married David Fox. In his will he left her "5 shillings steerling, which...is an overplus of her portion
2 CONC  or desserts." He took precautions to keep her mother from leaving her any part of estate but did not altogether succeed. When Hannah (Atherold) Ball died in 1694, she bequeathed to her :heir loving daughter Hannah Fox, wife of Da
2 CONC vid fox, a suite of red curtains, valens and counterpane and bolster, a pewter cistern to set bottles in, a pewter custard pan, a cabinet that stands next the kitchen, a silver sugar dish, mustard pot, three spoons, a silver trenc
2 CONC her." She also tried to leave the :negro and the mulatto girl given me by my husband to dispose of as I please." Whether this attempt to leave the two slaves to Hannah succeeded isn't known, or whether the will was admitted to pro
2 CONC bate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents:   Col. William Ball & Hannah Atherold
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # on 22 July 1670 in Lancaster VA to David Fox (1646-1699).  He was the son of "the emigrant" David Fox & Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Hannah Fox (1671 -).  Married 1) Rodham Kenner.  2) Clement Spellman.
2 CONT # David Fox, Jr. (1672 - 1679/80).  Died young.
2 CONT # William (1672/73 - 1718).  Married Anne Chin.
2 CONT # Capt. Samuel (1673/74 - 1712).  Married Anne Daingerfield
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT None of the three children of William Ball and Hannah Atherold Ball are buried at St. Mary's Chapel at White Hall -- the three children being Hannah (married David Fox), Joseph Ball [grandfather of President George Washington), or
2 CONC  William
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * Hill, p. 49; Cukro, p. 13-14 (#5); Hayden, p. 60-61 (#5).
2 CONT * See: "Fox Family", William and Mary Quarterly, First Series, Vol. 17, No. 1, July 1908, p. 59-64.
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=mrmarsha&id=I24558  
2 CONT *(1) "Virginia Genealogies - A Genealogy of the Glassell Family," by Rev. Horace Edwin Hayden (Genealogical Pub. Co., Baltimore, 1966) p.53, 82.
2 CONT *  (2) "1658-1758 Charles County MD Familes 'The first 100 years': Wills, Court, Church, Land, Inventories & Accounts," by Michael Marshall  (http://wc.rootsweb.com, mrmarsha database, 7 Nov 2007).
2 CONT *!  Birth: (1,2) d/o William BALL/Hannah ATHEROLD. 12 Mar 1650. (1) England. (2) London, England.
2 CONT *  Marriage to David FOX: (1,2) 22 Jul 1670. (2) Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT *  Death: (2) Dec 1748. Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=adgedge&id=I37706 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 1 2016, 7:50:52 UTC''
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ball-216
2 CONT *D. J. French, "The Ancestry of the Balls of Berkshire, Northamptonshire and Virginia," 2013, v1.2 (PDF) (accessed 18 July 2014); p. 40.
2 CONT * Horace Edwin Hayden, Virginia genealogies: a genealogy of the Glassell family of Scoland and Virdinia: also fo the families of Ball..., Wilkes-Barre, PA: E.B. Yordy, printer, 1891, c1885, starting on page 60, citing a Fox family
2 CONC  bible. ↑ Hayden, p 60-61
2 CONT *Thomas L. Broun, The Ball, Conway, Gaskins, McAdam and other kindred of William and Janetta Broun of Northern Neck, Virginia, Charleston, W.Va. : T.L. Broun, [1911?]
