1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Margaret Williamson===
2 CONT * Birth: BET 1644 AND 1652 in Isle of Wright Co., VA.
2 CONT * Will: 08 FEB 1696/97 Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Death: BEF 09 FEB 1707/08 in Lancaster Co., VA. 5
2 CONT * Burial: BEF 09 FEB 1706/07 Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Probate: 09 FEB 1708/09 Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: James Williamson b: ABT 1621 in Isle of Wight Co., VA. 
2 CONT * Mother: Anne Underwood b: ABT 1629 in England
2 CONT * Husband:  William Ball b: 02 JAN 1640/41 in Lancaster Co., VA. Married: 11 NOV 1672 in Lancaster Co., VA. at 'Marattico' 6 7 8 Note: One ref. suggests that the marriage of Margaret & William occured 21 March 1672. (Ref: Rappahan
2 CONC nock Co., Virgnia Records Book 1671 - 1676,p. 93.  William Ball was the son of William Ball (b abt 1615 - d. 1680) & Hannah Atherold his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * William Ball b: BET 1673 AND 12 SEP 1676 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * James Ball b: BET 1673 AND 1678 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Richard Ball b: 12 AUG 1675 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Joseph Ball b: 16 OCT 1680 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * George Ball b: BET 1683 AND 1687 in Northumberland or Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * David Ball b: 26 SEP 1686 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Samuel Henry Ball b: 26 SEP 1686 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Stretchley Ball b: BET 1687 AND 1688 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT * Margaret Ball b: BET 1691 AND 20 SEP 1694 in Lancaster Co., VA. - at Millenbeck
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Margaret_Williamson_%2814%29
2 CONT
2 CONT >Note of Caution: Many researchers have claimed that William Ball had 2-3 wives. The 1697 Will of Margaret (Williamson) Ball names her as a widow and names the same children as those found in William Ball's 1694 Will, thereby prov
2 CONC ing that if she was not the only wife of William Ball, she was certainly the last one.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Williamson b. 1644 m. William Ball II
2 CONT
2 CONT Tyler's Quarterly Magazine
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogists seem in the past to have all conceding that he [William Ball] was married several times but until recently it was uncertain by which wife he had the various children. It has now been proved by records that his third a
2 CONC nd last wife was Margaret Williamson who died and left a will dated 1697 mentioning all the children of Captain William Ball and herself ( the said Margaret Williamson) and designating herself the sister of Mary Rozier, both daugh
2 CONC ters of James Williamson and Ann Underwood. Colonial record has been established for Margaret Williamson for an original land grant in Rappahannock County, Virginia, Book 4, page 57, March 11, 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT James Hughes 2005-07-06 19:39:53
2 CONT The Descendants of Captain Thomas Carter , Page 102
2 CONT
2 CONT Mar. 7, 1671, William Moseley delivered to Mr. Wm. Ball, Jr., Mr. James Williamson's patent for 1,800 acres of land dated 22 May, 1651, and the Underwood patent to Margaret and Mary Williamson for 882 acres, dated March 11, 1662. 
2 CONC March 20, 1673, Capt. Wm. Ball, Gent., and Margaret his wife, a daughter and co-heir of Mr. James Williamson, and Anthony Bridges of Westmoreland, attorney for John Rosier, Gent., of Westmoreland, and Mary his wife, daughter and c
2 CONC o-heir of James Williamson, sold to Charles Dacres, Clerke (Minister) of Westmoreland, 450 acres, part of a patent for 1,800 acres granted to Mr. James Williamson, dec'd, etc. They guaranteed title against themselves and the heirs
2 CONC  of William Williamson, also dec'd.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret Williamson
2 CONT * Lancaster County
2 CONT * Virginia Court Records
2 CONT * Will Book No. 10 - Pt. 1, p. 53
2 CONT * In the name of God, Amen - I Margaret Ball of the County of Lancaster in Virginia Widow being Sick and weak in body but of Sound and Perfect Memory, Praised be ye Almighty God for ye same and considering the frailty of this Life
2 CONC  being but a blast I do make This my last will and Testament in manner and form following hereby revoking all former wills formerly by me made.
2 CONT * Imp' I bequeath my Soul to God that gave it to me, Commending my body To ye Earth to be buried in decent ord' at ye descretion of my Exect' hereafter named in hopes and true Confidence that I shall have a Joyful Resurrection at 
2 CONC ye Last Day Through the mercies of my most dear and precious Redeemeer ye Lord Jesus Christ.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my Loving Son William Ball and his heirs forever one Negro woman named Mary and her future increase forever.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my Loving Son Richard Ball and his heirs forever one Negro man named Sambo.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my Loving Son James Ball and his heirs forever one Negro man named Tom.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my Loving daughter Margaret Ball Soe much money as will buy her a Negro woman to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my two sons Joseph and George Ball and their heirs for Ever all my Right Title of that Divident of Land Situate in Richmond County at the head of Perpetua Creek as is expressed in my deceased husband's will to m
2 CONC y two sons Jos. and Geo. Ball.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my loving sister Mary Rosier one Stuff gowne and Peticoat one Shift one pr worsted Stockens and one p' of Shoes.
2 CONT * It is my will therefore that my Loving daughter Margaret Ball have all my wearing (clothes viz) Silk Stuf Linen and Lace Except what I have already bequeathed and given by word of mouth. I give to my Daughter Margaret one Silver
2 CONC  Tankard w'ch was Given me by my husband.
2 CONT * Item - It is my will Therefore that my Sons, Wm. Richard and James Ball purchase out of ye produce of ye Cropps of Tobb of ye above Negroes Given my sons one Negro apiece for my Sons Jos., George, David and Samuel Ball to them a
2 CONC nd their heirs forever.
2 CONT * Item - I give to my Son James Ball my Silver cup which was given me by husband. I doe make and ordaine my two Sons Will' Ball and Richard Ball the Executors of This my Last Will and Testam' in Witness whereof I have here unto Se
2 CONC t my hand and Seal this 8th day of February, 1697.
2 CONT * Signed Cleared and Delivered in Presence of ye mark of Margaret Ball, Ye Seale
2 CONT * Edward Cox, Mary x Gracie At a Court held for Lancaster County ye 9th of Febr. 1709 at ye request of Mr. George Ball this will was admitted to Record and is Recorded.
2 CONT * This was certified to by C. T. Peirce, Jr. Drp. Clerk, Mar. 1, 1939.)
2 CONT
