1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Major James Ball "of Bewdley," Lancaster county, Virginia, was born in 1678 and died 13 Oct 1754, age 76.  He was the son of Son of William Ball II (1641 - 1694) and Margaret Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ball-166
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT #15 June 1699 Eliza Howson who d 22 Jan 1704/5, probably daughter of Leonard Howson
2 CONT #10 Apr 1707 Mary (Conway) Dangerfield, dau of Col. Edwin and Sarah (Fleete) Conway and widow of John Dangerfield 
2 CONT #25 Apr 1742 Mary Ann (Bertrand) Ballendine, b 1670, d 12 Feb 1749/50, dau of Rev. John Bertrand of Rapp'k Co., and wid. of Cap. Wm. Ballendine
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT James' will was dated 15 July 1754 and probated in Lancaster County, 15 Nov 1754. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *"In the name of God Amen I James Ball....
2 CONT *"Item I give to my Grand Son Burgess Ball all my lands in King George, Spootsilvania and Stafford Counties during his Natural life & at his decease I give it to his child or children as he shall think fit and to their heirs.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my Said grand son Twenty one Slaves viz. Dick, Brister, Adam Rawleigh, & Alice, I bought of my son James, Lucy & her four children and her three grand children, Letty and her Seven children and all their future in
2 CONC crease when he [grandson Burgess] shall arrive to the aforeaid age or have lawful issue, that he be possessed and entitled to ye the said slaves and their increase as also what shall arrive from the profits of the said slaves, but
2 CONC  in case my said Grand Son die before he come tothe age of twenty one and without lawful issue then I give the Said Slaves and profits to be eqully divided among my Son and five Daughters and their heirs.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my Said Grandson my clock and my two mares Blase and Francy & what stock I shall have on the land before given him and all their incrase when he shall come to the age aforesaid or have lawful issue.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my Daughter Sinah and my four grand Sons viz Jesse Ball, son of my Daughter Frances, James Ewell and James Ewell [sic] son of eve Ewell and John Selden and their heirs five thousand acres of land inPrince Wm Count
2 CONC y be laid off at the upper end ofmy mountain ract to them and their heirs equally amongst them.
2 CONT *"I give to my Daughter Eve one Slave named Sarah and all her Encrease which she has now only the use of.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my daughter Selden and her heirs ye land I bought of Benjamin Taylor. I give to my grandson Jon Taylor Fifty pounds Sterling to be paid him when he shall come to the age of twenty one but if he should die before t
2 CONC hat age then I give it to his Mother it being part of her portion.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my five Daughters all my household goods except my plate. The best bed and furniture which I give to my Son James.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my Grand Son Tobey Downman Thirty pounds to be laid out in land or a Slave and no otherways.
2 CONT *"I give to my grandson James Downman my watch and Silver Buckles.
2 CONT *"Item I give to my son James the use of all the remainder of my estate including my Slaves in his possession which he has now the use of all during his natural life and at his death to dispose of as he shall think fit.
2 CONT *"Item I do appoint my Son Exr of this my last will and testament and guardian to my grandson Burgess Ball and my will is that my estate be not appraised. In witness my hand and seal this 15th day of July 1754. JAMES BALL [Seal]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At a Court held for Lancaster County on the 15 Day of November 1754 This will was presented in Court by James Ball Gent Excr therein named who made Oath thereto and the same was ordered to be recorded. teste, Thos. Edwards, Jr. C.
2 CONC L.C. A copy Attest Benj'n M. Walker C. C. 1830 Dec 3d
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ball-166
2 CONT
