1 NAME Samuel /Ball/
2 GIVN Samuel
2 SURN Ball
2 _MARNM Ball
2 NICK Samuel Henry Ball
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 SEP 1686
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 NOV 1751
2 PLAC St. Mark's Parish of Culpeper County in colonial Virginia
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   He was Vertryman of St. Marks Parish, Culpepper County,Virginia. Brother of Joseph Ball, grandfather of George Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Ball b. 1686 m. Catherine Ann Tayloe 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel died when his children were underage ... and under guardian bond -   there were only five children...
2 CONT
2 CONT # Judith Ball b: 1718 m: John Hackley
2 CONT # Margaret Ball b: 1724 m: John Barrow
2 CONT # Mary Ball b: 1732 m: Robert Green
2 CONT # William Ball b: 1734 m: Frances Slaughter
2 CONT # Susanna Ball b: Nov 1737 m: John Lillard
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: James, David, Stretchley and Samuel Ball received various lands in Richmond County to be equally divided. It is refrenced that Samuel had several daughters in addition to his son William. Samuel is believed to have been a wi
2 CONC tness to the will of his brother Joseph in 1721
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Samuel Ball Will==
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL: William & Mary College Quarterly. pg 201
2 CONT Samuel Ball's will made 16th Aug. 1751, probated 22d Nov 1751, Culpeper Co. Va. Will Book 1, p. 60. His daughter Margaret was not then married, and William was not twenty-one years of age. He mentions his wife as "Ann Catharine."
2 CONT
2 CONT Will:  In the name of GOD AMEN. I, Samuel Ball, being weak in Body  but of sense and memory, thanks be to GOD, calling to mind  the mortality of my body and knowing it is appointed for  all men to die I do make and ordain this my 
2 CONC last will and  testament in manner and from as follows.  ITEM: I give to my loving wife ANNA CATHARINE BALL the use  of my Negro Man, Adam, during the time she lives my widow;  and afterwards to my son William Ball and his heirs  
2 CONC forever.  ITEM: I give to my son William Ball all my land and six  Negroes by name Daniel, Kitt, Cloandy, Rose, Rachel, Ester,  to him and his heirs lawfully begotten of his body forever,  and for want of such heirs then as follow
2 CONC eth:  ITEM: I give to my daughter Margaret Ball five Negroes by  name Sam, Murriah, Milla; Kittener, Will, and a feather bed  and furniture and a mare Tillie and her colt and my horse  Batcheller and if in case my son William shou
2 CONC ld die without  heir lawfully begotten of his body then I give four hundred  acres of land which is already bounded by my said daughter  Margaret Ball and her choice of two Negroes belonging to  her brother, part other and her hei
2 CONC rs forever, and the rest  to be divided amongst the three sisters.  ITEM: I give to my daughter Judith Hackley two Negroes byname Cate, Jack, to her and her heirs forever and four  hundred and sixty acres of land to her and her he
2 CONC irs  forever in case her brother should die as aforesaid.  ITEM: I give to my son William Ball all my estate that is  not mentioned already to his and his heirs forever.  ITEM: I give to my daughter Mary Green twenty shillings.  T
2 CONC he reason I give her no more is because, she has had her  part already.  ITEM: I give to my Son, William Ball, all my Estate that is  not mentioned already to him & his Heirs forever.  ITEM: I give to James Pollard five acres of l
2 CONC and bounded  thus Beginning at a Spanish Oak the South Side Brooks run,  along close by the Run Westward to a Red Oak, thence along  the old Line Northward up the Branch to a White Oak, thence  Southward to the Beginning, more or 
2 CONC less, to him and his  heirs forever.  ITEM: I do appoint my son William Ball and my two  sons-in-law, John Hackley and Robert Green to be sole  executors of this my last will and Testament in Witness  whereof I have set my hand an
2 CONC d seal This Sixteenth day of  August in the year Seventeen Hundred and Fifty one.  Samuel Ball (I.S.) Paul Howell - his mark X William Rains - mark X It is my desire that my Estate be not apprase. (Will proved at court held Friday
2 CONC , Nov. 22, 1751)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links 
2 CONT * http://files.usgwarchives.net/va/schools/wmmary/j5250000.txt
