2 CONC  age. He mentions his wife as "Ann Catharine."
2 CONT
2 CONT  Will:  In the name of GOD AMEN. I, Samuel Ball, being weak in Body  but of sense and memory, thanks be to GOD, calling to mind  the mortality of my body and knowing it is appointed for  all men to die I do make and ordain this my
2 CONC  last will and  testament in manner and from as follows.  ITEM: I give to my loving wife ANNA CATHARINE BALL the use  of my Negro Man, Adam, during the time she lives my widow;  and afterwards to my son William Ball and his heirs 
2 CONC  forever.  ITEM: I give to my son William Ball all my land and six  Negroes by name Daniel, Kitt, Cloandy, Rose, Rachel, Ester,  to him and his heirs lawfully begotten of his body forever,  and for want of such heirs then as follo
2 CONC weth:  ITEM: I give to my daughter Margaret Ball five Negroes by  name Sam, Murriah, Milla; Kittener, Will, and a feather bed  and furniture and a mare Tillie and her colt and my horse  Batcheller and if in case my son William sho
2 CONC uld die without  heir lawfully begotten of his body then I give four hundred  acres of land which is already bounded by my said daughter  Margaret Ball and her choice of two Negroes belonging to  her brother, part other and her he
2 CONC irs forever, and the rest  to be divided amongst the three sisters.  ITEM: I give to my daughter Judith Hackley two Negroes byname Cate, Jack, to her and her heirs forever and four  hundred and sixty acres of land to her and her h
2 CONC eirs  forever in case her brother should die as aforesaid.  ITEM: I give to my son William Ball all my estate that is  not mentioned already to his and his heirs forever.  ITEM: I give to my daughter Mary Green twenty shillings.  
2 CONC The reason I give her no more is because, she has had her  part already.  ITEM: I give to my Son, William Ball, all my Estate that is  not mentioned already to him & his Heirs forever.  ITEM: I give to James Pollard five acres of 
2 CONC land bounded  thus Beginning at a Spanish Oak the South Side Brooks run,  along close by the Run Westward to a Red Oak, thence along  the old Line Northward up the Branch to a White Oak, thence  Southward to the Beginning, more or
2 CONC  less, to him and his  heirs forever.  ITEM: I do appoint my son William Ball and my two  sons-in-law, John Hackley and Robert Green to be sole  executors of this my last will and Testament in Witness  whereof I have set my hand a
2 CONC nd seal This Sixteenth day of  August in the year Seventeen Hundred and Fifty one.  Samuel Ball (I.S.) Paul Howell - his mark X William Rains - mark X It is my desire that my Estate be not apprase. (Will proved at court held Frida
2 CONC y, Nov. 22, 1751)
2 CONT   Father: William BALL  b: 2 Jan 1640/41 in England  Mother: Margaret WILLIAMSONb: Abt 1644 in Isle Of Wight County, Virginia Mentioned in his father's will   Samuel Ball was one of the first vestry of St. Mark's Parish, Culpepper
2 CONC r Co, Jan. 1, 1731. (A Geanealogy of the Glassell Family, page 55)
