1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://www.mountvernon.org/educational-resources/encyclopedia/ball-family Ball Family - George Washngton's Mt. Vernon]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Ball (1649-1711) was born in England and came to Virginia sometime before his father's death, making his home at a plantation called Epping Forest. He served as a justice of the county court, a vestryman for his church pari
2 CONC sh, as a Burgess (in 1698, 1700, and 1702), and as a lieutenant colonel in the county militia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ball was married twice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From his first marriage to '''Elizabeth''' Rogers (or '''Romney'''), who died by the early 1700's, he had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anne Ball (later the wife of Colonel Edwin Conway),	
2 CONT # Elizabeth Ball (later the wife of the Reverend Joseph Carnegie)
2 CONT # Esther or Easter Ball (later the wife of Rawleigh Chinn), 
2 CONT # Hannah Ball (later the wife of Rawleigh Travers, II, and afterwards the wife of Simon Pearson), and 
2 CONT # Joseph Ball (died 1760).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=105696424
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *The Branch, Harris, Jarvis, and Chinn book: a family outline. Composed by members of these families, and brought together in this form by Benjamin H. Branch Jr. by Branch, Benjamin Harrison, 1919-  page 258. <[https://archive.org
2 CONC /details/branchharrisjarv00bran/page/514/mode/1up?view=theater&q=Rawleigh Archive.Org]>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ! Col. Wm. Ball of Virginia, pp 39, It looks like Elizabeth and William resided in England until his first wife&apos;s death. Her death seems to be prior to 1703. It looks like Elizabeth and William resided in England until his fi
2 CONC rst wife&apos;s death. Her death seems to be prior to 1703. It looks like Elizabeth and William resided in England until his first wife&apos;s death. Her death seems to be prior to 1703.
