1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Ball
2 CONT * b.1683 Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT * d.12 Nov 1748 Stafford County, Virginia
2 CONT * Parents: Joseph Ball (1649-1711), Elizabeth Romney
2 CONT * Married: Raleigh Travers, Simon Pearson
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Ball was born anytime between about 1674-1685.  The exact year of her first marriage is not yet known (only that she was married, by the 1711 will of her father); this range is an estimate. She was also probably born in Lan
2 CONC caster county, Virginia, though exactly where is also not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah was married first to Raleigh Travers and second to Simon Pearson.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died 12 NOV 1748 in Stafford, Virginia, age: 64-65 [citation needed].
2 CONT
2 CONT Her will was proven December 13, 1748, naming grandson Travers Cooke, granddaughter Hannah Cooke, granddaughter Hannah Daniel, granddaughter Elizabeth Travers Daniel, daughters Elizabeth Cooke & Sarah Daniel.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From "A History of Chapman and Alexander Families", from Genealogy.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT The second wife of Simon Pearson, Hannah Pearson, survived him. She was the half-sister of Mary Ball Washington, mother of Gen. Washington. She was the daughter of Joseph Ball, who married, in 1696, Raleigh Travers. Her will, prov
2 CONC ed in Stafford County 1748, names her three children, Raleigh Travers, Eliza Cooke, and Sarah Daniel, son-in-law Peter Daniel, and grandchildren, Travers Cooke, Hannah Cooke, Hannah Daniel, Elizabeth Travers Daniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hill, p. 46; Cukro, p. 39-40 (#17)
2 CONT
2 CONT ▼References
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Will Abstract of Joseph Ball, in Lee, Ida J. Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills, 1653-1800. (Richmond: Dietz Press, 1959).
2 CONT
2 CONT p 6 -  BALL, Joseph,. Psh. St. Mary's White Chapel. Will. 25 June 1711. Rec. 11 July 1711. Wife Mary; son Joseph; daus. Hannah Travers; Anne Conway; Esther Chinn; Elizabeth Cornegie; Mary Ball; Eliza Johnson (dau. of his wife), da
2 CONC u. Mary, 400 acres of land in Richmond county; grandson James Cornegie (not 21) acknowledges gift to son Joseph Ball, and daus. Hannah Travers, Anne Conway and Esther Chinn made 11 Feb. 1707; Overseer John Hagan; negroes formerly 
2 CONC belonging to Jon. Carnegie, decd. Extr. Joseph Ball. Wits. Geo. Finch, Elizabeth Finch, Margaret Miller, Joseph Taylor. W.B. 10, p. 88.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT [Identifies father of Hannah (Ball) Travers.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Letter from Peter Vivian Daniel  Obituary of Peter Vivian Daniel states Sara Travers parents, and that Hannah Ball is Mary Ball&apos;s half sister who is George Washington&apos;s mother.  Hanna Ball divorced Simon Pearson then mar
2 CONC ried Rawleigh Travers. ! Col. Wm. Ball of Virginia, pp 39. Letter from Peter Vivian Daniel  Obituary of Peter Vivian Daniel states Sara Travers parents, and that Hannah Ball is Mary Ball&apos;s half sister who is George Washington
2 CONC &apos;s mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Hannah_Ball_%284%29_
2 CONT * http://www.geneagraphie.com/getperson.php?personID=I186184&tree=1
2 CONT * http://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I024234&tree=Tree1
