1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Esther Ball
2 CONT * b.1685 Millenbeck, Lancaster, Virginia, United States
2 CONT * d.1751 Lancaster, Lancaster, Virginia, United States
2 CONT * Parents: Col. Joseph Ball of Epping Forest, Elizabeth Romney
2 CONT * Married: Rawleigh Chinn; 6 children 
2 CONT * AKA: Ester, Easter
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Joseph Chinn 1703 - 1784
2 CONT # Rawleigh Chinn, Jr. Abt 1708 - Bef 1756
2 CONT # Chichester Chinn 1709 - Bef 1749
2 CONT # Thomas Chinn, of St. Mary's White Chapel Parish 1710 - Bef 1768
2 CONT # Ann Chinn Abt 1712 - 1793
2 CONT # Sarah Chinn Abt 1715 - Bef 1741
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 Will Abstract of Joseph Ball, in Lee, Ida J. Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills, 1653-1800. (Richmond: Dietz Press, 1959).
2 CONT
2 CONT p 6 - 
2 CONT BALL, Joseph,. Psh. St. Mary's White Chapel. Will. 25 June 1711. Rec. 11 July 1711. Wife Mary; son Joseph; daus. Hannah Travers; Anne Conway; Esther Chinn; Elizabeth Cornegie; Mary Ball; Eliza Johnson (dau. of his wife), dau. Mary
2 CONC , 400 acres of land in Richmond county; grandson James Cornegie (not 21) acknowledges gift to son Joseph Ball, and daus. Hannah Travers, Anne Conway and Esther Chinn made 11 Feb. 1707; Overseer John Hagan; negroes formerly belongi
2 CONC ng to Jon. Carnegie, decd. Extr. Joseph Ball. Wits. Geo. Finch, Elizabeth Finch, Margaret Miller, Joseph Taylor. W.B. 10, p. 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Will and Inventory Abstracts of Easter Chinn, in Lee, Ida J. Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills, 1653-1800. (Richmond: Dietz Press, 1959).
2 CONT
2 CONT p 50 -  CHINN, Easter. Will 2 August 1749. Rec. 10 May 1751. Sons: Joseph, Rawleigh and Thomas Chinn; Daughter Ann Shearman; Heirs of Chichester Chinn; Gr.son Rawleigh Shearman, son of Martin Shearman and Ann his wife; Gr.daughter
2 CONC  Mary Shearman, dau. of Martin Shearman and Ann his wife. Gr.dau. Easter Shearman. Wits. Henry Tapscott*, Margaret Tapscott. W.B. 15, p. 32.
2 CONT
2 CONT [*cos1776 Note:Identity of Henry Tapscott not yet confirmed.]
2 CONT
2 CONT CHINN, Easter. Inventory 10 May 1751. Rec. 14 June 1751. Returned by Easter Chinn, Extrx. W.B. 15, p. 41.
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 Will Abstract of Joseph Ball, in Lee, Ida J. Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills, 1653-1800. (Richmond: Dietz Press, 1959).
2 CONT
2 CONT p 6 -  BALL, Joseph,. Psh. St. Mary's White Chapel. Will. 25 June 1711. Rec. 11 July 1711. Wife Mary; son Joseph; daus. Hannah Travers; Anne Conway; Esther Chinn; Elizabeth Cornegie; Mary Ball; Eliza Johnson (dau. of his wife), da
2 CONC u. Mary, 400 acres of land in Richmond county; grandson James Cornegie (not 21) acknowledges gift to son Joseph Ball, and daus. Hannah Travers, Anne Conway and Esther Chinn made 11 Feb. 1707; Overseer John Hagan; negroes formerly 
2 CONC belonging to Jon. Carnegie, decd. Extr. Joseph Ball. Wits. Geo. Finch, Elizabeth Finch, Margaret Miller, Joseph Taylor. W.B. 10, p. 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Identifies Esther (Ball) Chinn as the daughter of Joseph Ball.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Ester Chinn and Rawleigh Chinn, in Lancaster, Virginia, United States. Lancaster County Court Orders. Book 7, p 51 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT At a Court held for Lancaster County, Wednesday, the 11th July, 1722; On the prayer of Ester Chinn setting forth that her husband Rawleigh Chinn doth daily abuse her and refuse her any competency whereby she may subsist and that b
2 CONC y sd means thereof she hath lately been obliged away from her home to be delivered of a child which she prays may be by her sd husband maintained. It is ordered that the Sheriff of this county acquaint the sd Rawleigh that it is t
2 CONC he courts direction that he take care of and maintain the sd child and that he have ten days notice from the time of his being served with this order to provide for the same, and it is further ordered that in case the sd Rawleigh 
2 CONC do not then take care of the sd child as before directed, the sheriff take him into custody till he give security for so doing.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
