1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frances Ball was the first of three wives of John Carter (b. 1674), according to [http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofcap00mill#page/n741/mode/2up page 271 of The Descendants of Capt Thomas Carter].
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances died less than a year after her marriage to John, 3 hours after delivering her only son Joseph, who himself died ten months later.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT * NOT listed as a daughter of Joseph Ball (1649-1711) of Epping Forest on [http://www.mountvernon.org/educational-resources/encyclopedia/ball-family George Washington's MT Vernon]
2 CONT * NOT listed in his will (nor would she be if pre- deceasing him)
2 CONT * IS listed as a daughter of "Joseph Ball" in her husband's note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis the loving dear Wife of John Carter and Dau. of Mr. Joseph Ball and Elizabeth his Wife Departed this Life at 5 mins to 8 a clockin the Morning of ye 3d day of Sept 1699 three hours after she was delivd of a Son in the 18th
2 CONC  year of her life. And was buried on the 5h day at St Marys White Chapell attended by an affectionate and sorrowing Husband and a large concorse of Relatives and friends. Joseph Ball Carter followed his mother to the Grave on the 
2 CONC 1st Day of July 1700 of a flux and was burd at So. Marys on ye 2d. [Prayer Book of Captain Thomas Carter of Barford, Lancaster County, VA, US GenwebArchives, Virginia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hill, p. 46; Cukro, p. 38-39 (#16)
2 CONT
