1 NOTE !MAR #1 - ANCESTORS OF AMERICAN PRESIDENTS by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 1
2 CONT Very likely she was the Mary Bennett of West Chester, England who married William Johnson of Norwich, Middlesex Co.,VA 10 Feb 1688/9 and was probably a near kinswoman of a Thomas Bennett of Westmoreland Co., living 1738/9.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 15
2 CONT Mary Ball, who became Augustine Washington's 2nd wife in 1731, was the daughter of her father's 2nd wife, Mary Montague, the widow Johnson, whom Joseph Ball married early in 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT She married Joseph Ball about 1707-8 (post 6 Feb. 1707)
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #3 - Ibid
2 CONT She married 3rd Richard Hewes.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 19
2 CONT Col. Joseph Ball died in 1711.  Her mother then married her 3rd husband, Capt. Richard Hewes, who lived at Cherry Point, near Lewisetta, on the Potomac, in Northumberland Co., about 15 miles north of Epping Forest.  Cherry Point, 
2 CONC now Cowart's Point, was accordingly the home of Mary Ball from the time she was 3 or 4 years old until whe was thirteen, her mother dying in 1721.  Capt. Hewes had died several years earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT She died about 1721.
