1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1.	David Fox was born 12 Mar 1646/1647 in , Lancaster Co., Virginia, and died 10 Oct 1702 in , Lancaster Co., Virginia. He was the son of 2. David "Davie" Fox and 3. Mary. He married Hannah Ball 22 Jul 1670 in , La
2 CONC ncaster Co., Virginia, daughter of William Ball and Hannah Atherold (Atherall). She was born 12 Mar 1650 in London, Middlesex, England, and died Dec 1748 in , Lancaster Co., Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children
2 CONT * Hannah Fox b: 25 Jul 1671.  Married 1) Clement Spelman 2) Rodham Kenner
2 CONT * William Fox b: 20 Jan 1672/1673 in Virginia. Married Ann Chinn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT !  (1) "Virginia Genealogies - A Genealogy of the Glassell Family," by Rev. Horace Edwin Hayden (Genealogical Pub. Co., Baltimore, 1966) p.53, 82.
2 CONT   (2) "The Chinn and Myers Families," by Randie Myers (http://wc.rootsweb.com, rjm66 database, 29 Apr 2007). Cites: (a) Hayden's "VA Genealogies," p.75, 299.
2 CONT   (3) "1658-1758 Charles County MD Familes 'The first 100 years': Wills, Court, Church, Land, Inventories & Accounts," by Michael Marshall  (http://wc.rootsweb.com, mrmarsha database, 7 Nov 2007). Cites: (a) "Virginia Colonial Abs
2 CONC tracts, Series 2, Vol 1, Northumberland County, Virginia 1678-1713," p.75.
2 CONT
2 CONT !  Birth: (3) s/o David FOX/Mary. 12 Mar 1646/7. Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT   Marriage to Hannah BALL: (1,3) 22 Jul 1670. (3) Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT   Death: (3) 10 Oct 1702. Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT   (2a) 1662, 3 Jul: Thomas WILLIAMS of Morattico sold to John CHYNN of Morattico, Lancaster Co., planter, and Henry DAVYS, of do., shipwright, a tract of 372 a. of land given to David FOX by Gov. BERKLEY, and on which WILLIAMS the
2 CONC n lived.
2 CONT   (2a) 1667/8, 17 Mar: John CHINN received 370 a. some locality, formerly granted to David FOX, gent.
2 CONT   (3a) 1680, 19 May: Mr. William FFOX sonne to Capt. David FFOX, dec'd, chose his brother Capt. David FFOX to be his guardian and Col. St. Leger CODD to have possession of Estate of sd. William FFOX, to desist from sowing seed on 
2 CONC the said land and Col. St. Leger CODD to have timely notice.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
