3 CITY Maldon
3 STAE England
1 OCCU Alderman and bailiff of Maiden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Church (REYNOLD CHURCH4, JOHN CHURCH3, JOHN CHYRCH2, JOHN at CHURCH1) died 19 NOV 1559 in England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan Henkyn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Tyrrell, daughter of Edmund Tyrrell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Church and Mary Tyrrell are:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Church died 14 JAN 1565 in England.  Married Margaret Greene (daughter of Rooke Greene)
2 CONT # Edmund Church. He married Dorothy Green 8 JUN 1574 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From Simeon Church of Chester, Connecticut By Charles Washburn Church [https://archive.org/stream/simeonchurchofch1914chur#page/4/mode/2up page 4-5]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Church, son of Reynold and Margaret, was alderman and baileff of Maiden. He married ist Joan Henkyn; and 2d Mary, daughter of Edmund Tyrrell, a descendant of Walter who slew Wm. Rufus. He died Nov. 19, 1559. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were John and Edmund. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Margaret, daughter of Rooke Greene of Little Sampford, Co. Essex. He died Jan. 14, 1565. His son Rocke, bap. Apr. 9, 1564, was surveyor to King James. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund married June 8, 1574, Dorothy Green. Prof. A. H. Church says Percy, one of his grandsons, was groom of the Privy Chamber in 1634. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The armory of the Maiden branch is almost identical with that of Nantwich. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT *https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=pete_witze&id=I22268
