1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Porter'''  was born 1560 in Little Baddow, Essex, England and died on 26 November 1625 in Comessary Cart, London, Essex, England.  His will was written Will 26 Nov 1625, Felsted, Essex, England. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Thomas Porter (b. abt. 1528-1614) and Ann (b. abt 1532-1616)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # on 12 September 1587  in Little Baddow, Essex, England to Sybil Vessey (1561-1625).  She was the daughter of Tomas Vessey.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 children include:
2 CONT # Francis Porter,   b. 12 Sep 1585, Felsted, Essex, England, United Kingdom ,   d. 26 May 1635
2 CONT # Thomas Porter,   b. 1590, Felsted, Essex, England, United Kingdom ,   d. 20 Dec 1638
2 CONT # Margaret Porter,   b. Abt May 1593, Felsted, Essex, England, United Kingdom ,   d. 21 Apr 1648
2 CONT # '''John Porter,   b. Abt 1594, of Felsted, Essex, England ,   d. 21 Apr 1648, Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, United States''' He married Anna White (b. abt 1660-1647).  She was the daughter of Robert White and Bridget Allgar.
2 CONT # William Porter,   b. 25 Nov 1596, Felsted, Essex, England, United Kingdom ,   d. Abt 1635
2 CONT # Rose Porter,   b. 1598, Felsted, Essex, England, United Kingdom ,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT John Porter, may have been a native of the parish of Little Baddow Co. Essex, England, but who may also have come from some neighboring parish, was probably born shortly before 1560. He was married at Little Baddow 12 Sept 1587 to
2 CONC  Sible pr Sybil Vessey, daughter of Thomas Vessey of Little Baddow. She was Baptised at Little Baddow 30 Nov 1561. None of the children of John and Sible Vessey Porter appear to have been baptised at Little Baddow, so the Porters 
2 CONC must have left that parish soon after their marriage. Where they lived between 1587-1593 is still unknown, though presumably they did not leave Essex. During that period, apparently, two sons were born to them, Francis and Thomas,
2 CONC  of whom the latter was undoubtedly named for his grandfather, Thomas Vessey. By 1593, John and Sible were settled at Felsted, co. Essex. Their daughter Margaret was baptised there 17 May 1593, and their son John on 21 Jun 1594. T
2 CONC he Porters probably continued to live at Felsted for the next thirty years. John Porter of Felsted, co. Essex, Yeoman Died between 30 May 1623 , the date of his will and 26 nov 1625 the date of probate. His wife Sybil was executri
2 CONC x of the will so she survived him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ref: The American Genealogist I Porter. pg 58. 1587 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Porter and Sible Vessey the daughter of thomas Vessey of Little Baddow were maried ye xii daye of September. Ref: Extracts from the Parish registers of the Church of St. Mary the Virgin, Little Baddow, co. Essex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ref: The American Genealogist vol. 16: 49-53 15: 122 18: 58 N.E. Hist. Reg. vol. 55: 28-30, Book of Ghosts p 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
