2 CONT #http://richardpyoung.org/getperson.php?personID=I3858&tree=Hogan01
2 CONT #[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=kendallhope&id=I0863 Scottish/English roots last updated Dec 2  2003] 
2 CONT # (1) Info from Barbara P Tolbert (bt-gaga@juno.com.  
2 CONT #(2) Info from Barbara P Tolbert (bt-gaga@juno.com; Helga Andrews gives 1590.  
2 CONT #(3) Info from Barbara P Tolbert (bt-gaga@juno.com; Helga Andrews gives 21 April 1648.  
2 CONT #(4) Information from Helga Andrews; Info from Barbara P Tolbert  bt-gaga@juno.com. Contact: donglenn@cox.net
2 CONT #(5) FamilySearch (TM) International Genealogical Index v5.0, Intellectual Reserve, Inc., (The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints http://www.familysearch.org), Film 184752 
2 CONT #'Parishes: Claines', A History of the County of Worcester: volume 3 (1913), pp. 300-308. URL: http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=43126&strquery=Porter Date accessed: 02 March 2014. 
2 CONT # Burial: St Andrew Churchyard Holborn London Borough of Camden Greater London, England  Created by: Karla Record added: Sep 20, 2014 Find A Grave Memorial# 136183582 -tcd
2 CONT # John Porter (1560–1625) born in Tapenhall, Worcestershire, England, and died at Comessary Cart, London, Essex. He was married to Sybil Vessey the daughter of Tomas Vessey and Elizabeth Church. They had six children.
2 CONT # http://www.kukkus.com/FelsingFamilies/getperson.php?personID=I4285&tree=tree1 cites
