2 CONT John Porter II (1594–1648) born in Felsted, Essex, England, and died in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. He was baptized on 21 June 1594 in Holy Cross Church, Felsted, Essex, England. He married Anna Roseanna White, daughter of Rob
2 CONC ert White and Bridget Allgar, on 18 October 1620 in All Saints Church, Messing, Essex, England. Both were of prosperous families. They had thirteen children, nine born in England and four in Connecticut.
2 CONT  “In 1638, when John was 44, the family emigrated to New England, probably with the Huit party on the "Susan and Ellen", in company with Anna's brother-in-law, Joseph Loomis.” “He was active in the community serving in both town a
2 CONC nd colony offices, serving as Deputy from Windsor to the Connecticut Legislature … He was involved in the merchant trade, probably in cloth, and probably traded with his son James, who was a merchant in London.”   
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (f/g) John Porter Birth: 	Jun. 21, 1594 Felsted Uttlesford District Essex, England Death: 	Apr. 22, 1648 Windsor Hartford County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT husband of Anna White, married Oct, 18, 1620 in Messing Essex , England ,they had 13 children together 
2 CONT
