2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT 1.  Beverly Fleet.  1988.  "York County, 1648-1657."  Pp. 99-142 in Virginia Colonial Abstracts.  Vol. III.  Genealogical Publ. Co., Baltimore, MD (Broderbund CD-187):
2 CONT
2 CONT No. 1. p.309.  It appearing that High Kinsey is heir to his brother Robt Kinsey deceased in this Co "whoe dyed without any written Will". Order that said Hugh have his brother's land and that Nathaniell Bacon Esqr Lt Coll Wm Barbe
2 CONC r, Collo George Read and Lt Coll Thomas Ludlow, or any 3 of them, divide the land in 3 parts, of which Mr Gooch who married the relict of Robt Kinsey to have his choice of 1/3 part. Red 15 8ber 1656 [15 Oct. 1656]. Ver Copia, Test
2 CONC e, Tho: Ballard, Cl Cur.
2 CONT
2 CONT No.1. p.310. By order of Quarter Court dated James Citty 10 Oct, Bacon, Read, Barber, and Ludlow, Gentlemen [as above] to divide land late of Robt Kinsey dec'd betw Capt Henry Gooch in right of his wife Millicent the relict of sai
2 CONC d Robt, and Mr Hugh Kinsey heir of the said dec'd Robert who was his brother.  Meeting at the dwelling house of Gooch find that Gooch's 1/3 part valued at 7250 lb tobo, etc. This is a long-winded, involved entry.  It goes on, and 
2 CONC on and on.  Dated 14 Oct 1656. Signed Nathaniell Bacon, George Read, Wm Barber, Tho: Ludlow. Rec 15 Oct 1656 by Tho Ballard, Cl Cur.
2 CONT
2 CONT No. 1. p. 312.  14 Oct 1656.  Hugh Kinsey assignes interest in land inherited from his late brother Robt Kinsey to Capt Henry Gooch. Signed the mark of Hugh KH Kinsey. Wit: Nathaniell Bacon, George Read, Tho: Ludlow. Rec 15 Oct 16
2 CONC 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT No. 1. p.313.  Another entry same date, same witnesses, signed by Hugh x Kinsey, discharging Gooch from all bills, bonds, etc.  This followed by an entry in like manner signed by Henry Gooch.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  Jane Baldwin, ed.  1988.  The Maryland Calendar of Wills. Vol. I.  Family Line Publ., Westminster, MD (Broderbund CD-206).  "A.A." = Anne Arundel.  On p. 40:
2 CONT
2 CONT Kinsey, Hugh, A.A. co., 6th May 1667;
2 CONT * To grandson Paul Kinsey, "Walnutt Neck."
2 CONT * To Sara Clarke, grandchildren Hancock [sic: Hannah] Ball and Margaret Kinsey, and Charles Gorsuch, personalty.
2 CONT * To wife Margaret, residue of estate, real and personal.
2 CONT * To young. dau. Eliza: Kinsey and hrs., said estate at death of wife afsd.
2 CONT * In event of death of said Eliza: without hrs., estate to pass to Mary Humphreys, at whose death, sd. estate to be divided among rest of testator's children, equally.
2 CONT * Test: Wm. Hare, John Malom. .
