1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ann Underwood (born abt 1629 - died BEF 8 Dec 1656, Lancaster Co, Virginia) was the daughter of William Underwood and Margaret 'Mary' [Masan]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT *James WILLIAMSON MARRIAGE: 15 Dec 1652, Isle of Wight, Virginia.  Son of Richard Williamson & Margaret Sherwood 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne Underwood and James Williamson are:
2 CONT *+	2	  i.	Margaret Williamson was born BET 1644 AND 1652 in Isle of Wright Co., VA., and died BEF 09 FEB 1707/08 in Lancaster Co., VA..  Married William Ball Jr.
2 CONT *+	3	  ii.	William Williamson was born AFT 1652, and died BEF 1689 in VA. (Died young)
2 CONT * 	4	  iii.	Elizabeth Williamson was born AFT 1652. She married John Moseley.
2 CONT *	5	  iv.	Mary Williamson was born ABT 1654 in Isle of Wright Co., VA., and died ABT 1715 in King George Co., VA. Married John Rosier. 
2 CONT *+	6	  v.	Henry Williamson was born AFT 1652, and died 11 SEP 1699 in Essex Co., VA..
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT "I am guessing that Anne is an unmarried sister of Thomas and George Underwood as she came over on the same ship as they. Capt. Moore Fauntleroy, the captain of the ship on which they travelled, received 450 acres of land on the R
2 CONC appahannock River on the N. side of Swan Bay on May 22, 1650, for transporting 9 individuals including George Underwood, his wife Mary and Anne Underwood. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I have placed her as the daughter of Margaret and William Underwood, because Margaret's 2nd husband, Gentleman John Upton, bequeathed lands or monies to what appear to be all children of his 2nd wife: William, Elizabeth, Sarah and
2 CONC  Margaret Underwood and Ann Wiliamson, wife of James Williamson who still lived in the area. (C-2403)" 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT * Underwood Family of Virginia (Continued) Augusta B. Fothergill The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography Vol. 39, No. 3 (Jul., 1931), pp. 272-276 Published by: Virginia Historical Society https://www.jstor.org/stable/424442
2 CONC 1 Page Count: 5
2 CONT *  Genealogies of Virginia Families, Vol. V, William & Mary Quaterly Text: pp. 247-248
2 CONT * Genealogies of Virginia Families, Vol V, R-Z, from Virgnia Mag. of Hist. Genealogical Publishing Co., Baltimore, 1981 Text: p. 629, 634
2 CONT *Ancestral File at www.familysearch.com ID#: C-2247, C-2395.
2 CONT *Chapman, Blanche Adams, Marriages of Isle of Wight County, Virginia, 1628-1800 ID#: C-2402.
2 CONT *Boddie, John Bennett, Isle of Wight Co., VA, (Chicago: Chicago Law Printing Co.) ID#: C-2403."
2 CONT
