1 NOTE  Ann UNDERWOOD Sex: F Birth: in Virgina Birth: 1629 in Isle Of Wight, Virginia, USA 1 Death: 1662 in Rappahannock, Virginia, USA 1 Note: Some say she died before her husband, James.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT NOTE: Ann came from England to Virginia with her family some time before land patent to Capt. Moore Fautleroy. -- Ann was single when arrived to Virginia -- married to Dr. James Williamson prior to the 9 June 1649 deed he witnesse
2 CONC d for his father-in-law John Upton  "Underwood, Ann, 1650, by Capt. Moore Fautleroy, ___ Co." (Early Virginia Immigrants, 1623-1666, p 336, On-Line Genealogy Library database)  "Capt. Moore Fauntleroy, the captain of the ship on w
2 CONC hich they traveled, received 450 acres of land on the Rappahannock River on the N. side of Swan Bay on May 22, 1650, for transporting 9 individuals including, George Underwood, his wife Mary and Anne Underwood." (My Southern Famil
2 CONC y, Becky Bass Bonner & Josephine Lindsay Bass, Internet)  "James Williamson married Ann Underwood and removed from Isle of Wight, with the Underwoods, to Rappahannock." (William and Mary College Quarterly, Vol 7, #7, Isle of Wight
2 CONC  County Records, p 221, On-Line Genealogy Library database)  "Dr. James was a justice of Isle of Wight County in 1646. On June 9, 1649, James and Thomas Wombwell witnessed a deed of John Upton." (Benjamin Williamson, Williamson Ge
2 CONC nforum database, #5116, 20 Jan 2005)  "Dr. James Williamson, Justice of Isle of Wight in 1646, was apparently a brother of Richard Williamson. On June 9, 1649, he and Thomas Wombwell witnessed a deed of Captain John Upton of Isle 
2 CONC of Wight County to William Dawson." (The Williamson Family of Isle of Wight County, VA, Hugh Buckner Johnston, Historical Southern Families, Vol III, p 158, On-Line Genealogy Library database)  Inventory of estate of husband and a
2 CONC dministration of his orphans: 8 Dec 1656, Lancaster Co., VA.  Ann died after John Upton's 16 Dec 1652 Will and before 8 Dec 1656 inventory of husband's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Father: Col. William UNDERWOOD  b: 1606 in Kent, England  Mother: Margaret MASON  b: 1605 in England  Marriage 1 Dr. James WILLIAMSON  b: in Rappahannock Co., Va 
2 CONT Married: BEF. 1652
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: One World Tree (sm) Author: Ancestry.com Publication: Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network, Inc., n.d.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann [UNDERWOOD] was mentioned in the will of Col. John Upton as being married to James Williamson in 1651. The said James Williamson was living in Isle of Wight County 20 Sept. 1649 when a power of attorney was made by William Lea
2 CONC  of Middlesex (England) to William Sheard of London to collect a debt of 3200 pounds of tobacco from James Williamson Gent. of Red Poynt, Isle of Wight County Virginia for the use of Elizabeth Fadloe widow. It was entered of recor
2 CONC d at August Court 1652. (Records 1652-57, page 5, Lancaster Co.)  22 May 1650, Sir William Berkeley, Governor, granted to James Williamson 1800 acres of land lying in Rappahannock River near the mouth of Millock Creek at the line 
2 CONC of William Underwood, on the mayne river side above the land of Anthony Jackman, For the transportation of thirty six persons into the colony. (Land Patents II, page 212).  The lands of Mr. Williamson adjoined that which was allot
2 CONC ted to the Rappahannock Indians and on the north side of Totuskey Creek. This was cited in a patent to John Sherlock 15 Nov. 1653. (Records 1656-64, page 140, Rappahannock County).  He did not leave a will but the inventory of his
2 CONC  estate was returned 16 December 1656. William Underwood was his executor. (Records 1656-64, page 79, Rappahannock).  He seems to have been a friend of John Hammond of Isle of Wight who removed to Maryland where he was a very prom
2 CONC inent figure and was the author of the tract "Leah and Rachel" which he dedicated to James Williamson.  He and his wife Ann (Underwood) had issue[:] two daughters Margaret and Mary who, on 11 March 1662, had a grant of land?882 ac
2 CONC res?lying in Rappahannock County between the head branches of Pepetick Creek and Mr. Popes Creek nigh the Rappahannock path to the land of Sylvester Thacher and Thomas Whitlock, formerly granted to William Underwood Gent. 10 Sept.
2 CONC  1658 and by him given by his last will unto the said Margaret and Mary Williamson. (Land Patents No. IV, page 597).
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT (1) Source: Roberts, Gary Boyd, Ancestors of American Presidents, Santa Clarita, CA: Carl Boyer, 3rd, 1995, p. 309.  [Note by compiler: Anne UNDERWOOD was an 8th great-grandmother of Theodore ROOSEVELT, Jr., 26th President of the 
2 CONC United States.]  (2) Source: Williams, Sherrill Underwood, "Margaret UNKNOWN of Isle of Wight and Old Rappa. Cos., VA" <http://www.combs-families.org/combs/assoc/u-1.htm>.  (3) Fothergill, Augusta B., "Underwood Family of Virginia
2 CONC ," in Family History: Virginia Genealogies #1, pre-1600 to 1900s, Genealogies of Virginia Families V, R-Z, Underwood Family of Virginia, p. 629, © MyFamily.com, Inc., September 1, 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann UNDERWOOD born before 1638; d bef 8 Dec 1656, Lancaster Co VA; m bef 1652, James WILLIAMSON, born before 1634, died 8 Dec 1656 in Lancaster Co, Virginia. Known Issue: Margaret WILLIAMSON (w/o William BALL, Jr.); Mary WILLIAMSO
2 CONC N (w/o John ROSIER); William WILLIAMSON, born before 1656, died young.  From Janet Ariciu family BUSH *(monkey @getgoin.net) "I am guessing that Anne is an unmarried sister of Thomas and George Underwood as she came over on the sa
2 CONC me ship as them. Capt. Moore Fauntleroy, the captain of the ship on which they travelled, received 450 cares of land on the Rappahannock River on the N. side of Swan Bay on May 22, 1650, for transporting 9 individuals including, G
2 CONC eorge Underwood, his wife Mary and Anne Underwood. I have placed her as the daughter of Margaret and William Underwood, because Margaret's 2nd husband, Gentleman John Upton, bequeathed lands or monies to what appear to be all chil
2 CONC dren of his 2nd wife: William, Elizabeth, Sarah and Margaret Underwood and Ann Wiliamson, wife of James Williamson who still lived in the area. (C-2403)"
2 CONT Ann UNDERWOOD <u-1.htm>, d/o Unknown & Margaret UNKNOWN Underwood (Upton) (Lucas), was born before 1638; married (1) bef 1652, James WILLIAMSON, born before 1634, died 8 Dec 1656 in Lancaster Co, Virginia . Known Issue: Margaret W
2 CONC ILLIAMSON; Mary WILLIAMSON; & William WILLIAMSON, born before 1656, died young. (See Also additional Williamson records under both Col. Wm. UNDERWOOD and Archdale Combs I ). Following a deed whereby Elizabeth, widow of Wm. UNDERWO
2 CONC OD, now wife of Archdale Combs, relinquished her dower, on 26 Feb 1672/3, William BALL the Younger of the County of Rappa (marked out) Lancaster in the Collony of Virginia and Margaret his Wife and John ROSIER of the County of Wes
2 CONC tmoreland in the Collony aforesaid and Mary his Wife wch Margarett and Mary were the daughters of James WILLIAMSON deceased …deeded 350 acres of land to Thomas KIRTON, said land having been granted to "Margaret and Mary WILLIAMSON
2 CONC  Coheirs to James WILLIAMSON… being on Rappa River and lying thirty nine miles up the North side of the said River as by Pattent under the seale of this Collony bearing date the first day of May One thousand Six hundred Sixty and 
2 CONC five… (Old Rappa VA Records, Book 5:199-203)
