1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I022533&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT ===James Williamson
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1621 - Perhaps at London 
2 CONT * Death:	Dec 8, 1656 intestate; inventory of estate on January 23, 1657, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia Colony 
2 CONT * Parents: Richard Williamson and Margaret Sherwood
2 CONT * Wife:	Anne Underwood
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd Great-Grandfather of James Madison, 8th Great-Grandfather of Theodore Roosevelt (needs double check)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Ann UNDERWOOD MARRIAGE: 15 Dec 1652, Isle of Wight, Virginia, daughter of William Underwood & Margaret 
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Issue: 
2 CONT *Margaret WILLIAMSON (w/o William BALL, Jr.); 
2 CONT *Mary WILLIAMSON (w/o John ROSIER); 
2 CONT *William WILLIAMSON, born before 1656, died young." 
2 CONT * Henry 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Williamson-3773
2 CONT
2 CONT James Williamson was born abt. 1621 of Richard Williamson and Margaret Sherwood in Isle of Wight, Virginia. [Location might be wrong] He married Ann Underwood on 16 December 1652, He died in 1656 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: He served as Justice of the Isle of Wight court this year. 1646 Isle of Wight, Virginia. He served as a Justice of the court, and served as such until his death in 1656. JAN 1652. Lancaster, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Events
2 CONT *Land grant. 22 MAY 1650. Lancaster (later Rappahannock), Virginia. Note: He was granted 1,150 acres. 
2 CONT *Land grant. 9 MAY 1651. Lancaster (later Rappahannock), Virginia. Note: He was granted 720 acres of land. 
2 CONT *Land grant. 22 MAY 1651. Lancaster (later Rappahannock), Virginia. Note: He was granted 1800 acres of land, and settled on this land. 
2 CONT *Event-Misc 18 AUG 1654. Rappahannock, Virginia. Note: He appears on a list of names of those to depart the colony this year. 
2 CONT *Land sale. 3 SEP 1656. Rappahannock, Virginia. Note: He sells 1000 acres of land to Ambrose Meather. 
2 CONT
