1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Rawleigh Chinn''' was a tobacco planter and an early settler of Virginia's Northern Neck with extensive land holdings. He was a highly regarded member of Virginia society, and a Deacon in St. Mary's White Chapel
2 CONC  Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Esther Ball, a half sister to Mary Ball, the mother of George Washington. Rawleigh and Esther had several children, but eventually divorced. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Rawleigh's marriage with Esther continued to deteriorate, he began having an affair with Esther's cousin Margaret Ball Downman. The pair had 3 children together, and most likely lived together from 1723 when their first son 
2 CONC Charles was born, until 1741 when Rawleigh died.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Joseph Chinn 1703 - 1784
2 CONT # Rawleigh Chinn, Jr. Abt 1708 - Bef 1756
2 CONT # Chichester Chinn 1709 - Bef 1749
2 CONT # Thomas Chinn, of St. Mary's White Chapel Parish 1710 - Bef 1768
2 CONT # Ann Chinn Abt 1712 - 1793
2 CONT # Sarah Chinn Abt 1715 - Bef 1741
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
