1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hannah Beale''' married Captain William Ball of Millenbeck  (the eldest son of Capt William Ball Jr and whose mother was Margaret Williamson) bef. Oct 15 1710. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Beale was the daughter of George Beale and Ellen Beale  (Rogers).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Information  
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born about 1615, [https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000014280951747?through=6000000000591496498 William Ball] emigrated to Virginia and became a prosperous landowner in Lancaster County, Virginia. He
2 CONC  served as a justice, a colonel of the militia, and as a delegate to the House of Burgesses. He fathered four children, including 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000000591496498 William Ball] (1641-1694).. [who] had nine children, including 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Ball-of-Millenbeck/6000000002713586427?through=6000000000591496498 William Ball] (ca. 1674-1744). '''He married [https://www.geni.com/people/Hannah-Beale-Ball/6000000002713586455?through=
2 CONC 6000000002713586427 Hannah Heale] (d. ca. 1744) and they had 6 children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I029360&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hannah BEALE and William BALL are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. William BALL was born ABT 1698 in Millenbeck, Lancaster County, Virginia, and died BEF 9 APR 1741 in Millenbeck, Lancaster County, Virginia. He married Margaret BALL 17 FEB 1723 in Lancaster County, Virginia, daughter of Richar
2 CONC d BALL and Sarah YOUNG. She was born ABT 1704, and died BEF 16 OCT 1783 in Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Sarah BALL was born 1700 in VA. She married Dennis MCCARTY 22 SEP 1724 in Yeocomico Church, Westmoreland County, Virginia, son of Daniel MCCARTY and Elizabeth POPE. He was born 7 NOV 1703 in Richmond County, Virginia, and died
2 CONC  1743 in Prince William, Virginia. She married Abram BARNES AFT 14 AUG 1744. He was born ABT 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. George BALL was born ABT 1702 in VA. He married Judith PAYNE 10 DEC 1735 in Lancaster County, Virginia, daughter of William PAYNE and Judith MERRIMAN. She was born ABT 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Judith BALL was born ABT 1704, and died ABT 19 SEP 1766 in Richmond County, Virginia. She married George GLASSCOCK 13 APR 1720 in Lancaster County, Virginia, son of George GLASSCOCK and Million DOWNMAN. He was born ABT 1700, a
2 CONC nd died BEF 6 SEP 1796 in VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Ellen BALL was born ABT 1706. She married Richard CHICHESTER 3 JUL 1734 in Lancaster County, Virginia, son of John CHICHESTER and Elizabeth SYMES. He was born ABT 1706, and died 30 DEC 1742 in Exeter, England. She married Willi
2 CONC am DOWNMAN 12 JUN 1747 in Lancaster County, Virginia, son of Raleigh DOWNMAN and Margaret BALL. He was born ABT 1717 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died 1765 in Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Hannah BALL was born ABT 1708, and died 10 JUL 1769. She married Robert MITCHELL 7 SEP 1746 in Lancaster County, Virginia, son of Robert MITCHELL and Susannah PAYNE. He was born 15 NOV 1724, and died 3 JAN 1758 in Richmond Cou
2 CONC nty, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hale-2734
2 CONT
2 CONT >George Hale, father of Nicholas, Sr., of Baltimore County, was a Justice in Lancaster County, Virginia, in 1684, a Burgess 1695-1697, and his will, leaving a large estate in lands, was probated January 12, 1698. He named "my lovi
2 CONC ng friend, Mr. Robert Carter, and my son-in-law Mr. William Ball ye overseers of this my last will and testament." George Hale and his wife, Ellen, who died in 1710, left in addition to their son Nicholas, Sr., who settled in Mary
2 CONC land, the following children: '''''Hannah''', ''who married Col. William Ball, the third generation of a distinguished name in Virginia.''''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT PLEASE NOTE ON THE MEDIA   HALFWAY DOWN . HER NAME AND WHOSE CHILD SHE IS AND THE INCORRECT BEALE SPELLING.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT
2 CONT A Guide to the Ball Family Papers, 1680-1785 
2 CONT Accession Number 23554 
2 CONT A Collection in  the Library of Virginia 
