2 CONT * from [http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/VA-NORTHERN-NECK/2012-10/1349456148  "Mrs." Elizabeth Ball wife of Joseph -3 Chinn]
2 CONT
2 CONT "I will keep repeating this until it sinks in. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "(1) In May 1727, Elizabeth Ball consents to her marriage to Mr. Joseph Chinn in a contract of marriage. Both are of White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County (2) 2 May 1727, marriage bond of Joseph Ball to MRS. Elizabeth Ball, George
2 CONC  Payne security, penal sum a very hefty £50
2 CONT
2 CONT "She is obviously, to me at least, a WIDOW Ball. Widow of whom I cannot fathom, but she is not a DAUGHTER of James, David or any of the Joseph Balls.
2 CONT
2 CONT "I have uploaded both of these documents to the record of Joseph-3 Chinn on I have uploaded both of these documents to the record of Joseph-3 Chinn on the ancestry tree. Everyone can go look at them. These are the ORIGINAL documen
2 CONC ts, not abstracts or transcripts. They came from microfilm reel 58 at the Mary Ball Washington Museum & Library, and are also on film at the LVA.
