1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jesse Ball,''' son of Col. James Ball and Mary Conway, was born 27 June 1716 and died 11 August 1747 in Lancaster County, Virginia, where he is buried in the White Chapel Church Yard.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first on 10 December 1737 in Lancaster County to Frances Fox, daughter of Samuel Fox and Anne Daingerfield and the widow of Charles Burgess, who had three daughters: Frances, Margaret and Elizabeth Burgess.  
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 February 1741 at Northumberland County, Jesse Ball married, as her first husband, to Mary Smith, daughter of Philip Smith, of Fleets Bay and his wife Mary Matthews. The widow Mary (Smith) Ball married John Lee, son of Henry 
2 CONC Lee and Mary Bland in December, 1749, which confirms Jesse's death before that date.  She married third to John Smith of Shooter's Hill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jesse Ball had no known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # MARRIAGE BONDS IN LANCASTER COUNTY "Saturday, Dec. 10, 1737, Sir. I desire you'l send a License to conjoin my son Jesse & Mrs. Frances Burges in the Bond of Hymen, & you'l oblige, Sir, you humble servt James Ball."
2 CONT # “Early Tombs in Westmoreland, Richmond, and Northumberland Counties.” The William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine 11, no. 3 (1903): 191–95. https://doi.org/10.2307/1920029.  "Jesse Ball, an older brother to Jeduth
2 CONC an, married Mary, daughter of J. Philip Smith, who names her in his will of July 11, 1743. She was sister to Baldwin M. Smith, and was married a second time (1749) to Col. John Lee, of Westmoreland. She again married John Smith. J
2 CONC esse Ball's marriage is usually incorrectly given in the published genealogies of the Balls."
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I32810&tree=Tree1
