1 NOTE {geni:about_me} For more pictures/documents go to the Media/Documents sections.
2 CONT
2 CONT COL. JAMES BALL, (10—9), of "Bewdley," Lancaster Co., Va., b. Dec. 31, 1718; d. Nov. 24, 1789; served as a Vestryman of St. Stephen's Parish, Northumberland Co., 1744-89, and Warden in 1745; and Treasurer in 1785; was a Burgess fr
2 CONC om Lancaster, 1755; High Sheriff and of the Convention of 1788; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (first) unknown (Margaret Burgess) ; (second) Mildred  (Mildred Smith), b. 1725; d. Dec. 1, 1751; (third) 1753, Letitia Lee b. 1731 died 1811.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Lee of Virginia 1642-1892 edited by Edmund Jennings Lee. Heritage Press 2008, pages 234 - 236, especially page 235.  
2 CONT
2 CONT See his wife, Letitia Lee's profile for a link to her gravestone which gives her husband as Col. James Ball and her father as Richard of Ditchley.
