1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was married 3 times. Her first husband was Charles Ewell whome she married in 1705. Husband number 2 was William Ballentine whom she married in 1724. Husband 3 was Maj James Ball whom she married in 1742.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was not married to Capt. Leroy Griffin who had a wife by the same name but from different parents.  Do not connect her to his family or merge the two different Mary Ann Bertrands.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sherrysharp.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I47525&tree=Roots
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bertrand-207
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Rev. John Bertrand and Charlotte de Jolie of France
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/EwellTheEwellsInAmericaAndSomeAlliedFamilies16351990/Ewell+-+The+Ewells+in+America+and+Some+Allied+Families%2C+1635-1990_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT To make the tie-in between the families even closer, CharleB and  Solomon's mother, Mary Ann Bertrand Ewell, married for her third marriage, the  father of her daughters-in-law, Major James Ball. This made her the  step-mother to 
2 CONC her own sons. Major Ball became stepfather to his own daughters  and the stepfather to his sons-in law. Both the Ball and Ewell families were  big supporters of St. Mary’s White Chapel. Major Ball and Mary Ann were buried  at Whit
2 CONC e Chapel, Lancaster Co. , Virginia. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21301535/mary-ann-ball
