2 CONT George Ball mentioned his mother in law in his 1746 Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1713-1749 Northumberland County, Virginia Wills-Admin; [Lewis & Booker]; Page 144a
2 CONT * Ball, George
2 CONT * W. W. 14 April 1746---W. P. 9 June 1746
2 CONT * My mother-in-law Sarah '''Waddy'''-the land that she now lives on and one half of my tract of land I now live on, during her natural life.
2 CONT * Wife '''Grace Ball'''-one half of the tract of land I now live on
2 CONT * during her natural life, and if my wife should outlive her mother, she to have the other half during her natural life in lieu of her dower of my lands elsewhere.
2 CONT * Son John Ball-use of all the other tracts of land except one hundred acres adjoining along "Waddy's Creek", which I give to my son David Ball after the death of his grandmother and mother, during my son David's natural life. …
2 CONT
