1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT On 11 Jun 1729, Mary Tayloe was given permission by her mother, Anne Burn, to marry John Loyal [Lyill, Lyall, Lile]. Another daughter of William Tayloe and Anne, his 2nd wife,  is Anna Catherine who married Samuel Ball.  She and S
2 CONC amuel Ball were administrators of James Burn/Bourne's estate in 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chidren
2 CONT
2 CONT # Judith Ball b: 1718 m: John Hackley
2 CONT # Margaret Ball b: 1724 m: John Barrow
2 CONT # Mary Ball b: 1732 m: Robert Green
2 CONT # William Ball b: 1734 m: Frances Slaughter
2 CONT # Susanna Ball b: Nov 1737 m: John Lillard
2 CONT
2 CONT 4941 The Kentucky Explorer, Volume 15, No. 4, September 2000, "Genealogy from the Long Ago", by permission. Montgomery Co. Mrs. Walker Bournee (nee Willey Belfield Jameson) was descended from the Ball family; Joseph Ball, the fath
2 CONC er of Mary, the mother of Washington, had an older brother, William Ball, who married Margaret Downman. The latter couple had, among other children, Capt. Samuel Ball, one of the first vestry of St. Mark's Church, elected January 
2 CONC 1, 1730-1; who remained an officer of that parish until his death in 1751; Samuel Ball married Ann Catherine Taylor, in Lancaster County, Virginia, November 25, 1717. They had four children, one of whom, Judith Ball, married John 
2 CONC Hackley, also a vestry man. The issue by this marriage was many children, among them John Hackley, who married Thomas Jameson, the oldest brother of Lieut. John Jameson, to whom Maj. Andre was delivered. Thomas Jameson and wife mo
2 CONC ved to Fayette County, now Montgomery County, Kentucky, in the year 1782 and settled upon 2,500 acres of land he had entered May 9, 1780; and upon which land the famous Estill's defeat took place. Tombtones mark the graves of Thom
2 CONC as Jameson and Judith Ball Hackley Jameson, in the garden near a brick house he built in 1802. The home is still owned by one of the descendants the farm having been in the family for more than 115 years. Thomas Jameson and wife h
2 CONC ad a large family, and one of the sons, Thomas Jameson, was the father of Willey Belfield Jameson.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT married Nov. 25, 1711
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
