2 CONT STAFFORD COUNTY VA WILL BOOK O; 1748-1767; THE ANTIENT PRESS p. 76 
2 CONT * In Name of God Amen the 10th October 1749 I RAWLEIGH TRAVERS being sick but of sound mind do make this my last will & Testament Imprimis I give to Mr. PETER DANIEL four Negroes & to the children of his present Wife SARAH,
2 CONT * Item I give my Negroe fellow Joe to my Sister ELIZABETH COOKE her life after to her son TRAVERSE COOKE
2 CONT * I give to my Sister SARAH DANIEL a negro girl called Sarah and her Increase to her three children Vizt. HANNAH, TRAVERS & ELIZABETH DANIEL.
2 CONT * Item I bequeath to HANNAH COOK negro to TRAVERS COOKE all my negroes not yet mentioned. All my personal estate in corn, tobacco money & cattle to be divided in three parts one of which I will leave to my Sister Elizabeth Cooke t
2 CONC he other two parts to my Nephew & heir Traverse Cooke all my debts being duly paid. Item I give to my neice Hannah Cook one of the best beds & furniture in my house together with four cows & calves.
2 CONT * I ordain my trusty loving friends Elizabeth Cooke & Travers Cooke my whole & sole Executors. 
2 CONT * Presence David Waugh, John Sutherland, Thomas Hay, Raw: Traver Michael Ryan
2 CONT * At Court held for Stafford County 12th Decr 1749 Last Will & Testament of Rawleigh Travers deced presented to Court by Travers Cooke Executor named .. being proved admitted to record. Certificate granted him for obtaining Probat
2 CONC e ..
2 CONT
