1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary (unknown) Johnson Ball was remarried the following year (1712) to a man named Richard Hewes, who left her a widow for the third time in 1713. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >After the death of Mr. Ball, Mary Johnson Ball became the wife of Captain Richard Hewes, a vestry man  of St Stephen's parish, Northumberland, and removed to this parish with her three children, John and Elizabeth Johnson, and Ma
2 CONC ry Ball, who had not reached her fifth birthday. Captain Hewes died in 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT Refs
2 CONT # Pierce, Elizabeth Combs. "Mary Johnson, second wife of Col. Joseph Ball," William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine 15, no. 2: 176-7.
