1 NOTE THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 19
2 CONT Mary Ball's father, Col. Joseph Ball, died in 1711.  Her mother then married her 3rd husband, Capt. Richard Hewes, who lived at Cherry Point, near Lewisetta, on the Potomac, in Northumerland Co., about 14 miles north of Epping For
2 CONC est.  Cherry Point, now Cowart's Point, was accordingly the home of Mary Ball from the time she was 3 or 4 years old until she was 13, her mother dying in 1721.  Captain Hewes had died several years earlier.
