1 NOTE !BIRTH - ANCESTORS OF AMERICAN PRESIDENTS by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 1
2 CONT Capt. Augustine Washington born 1694 at Wakefield, Westmoreland Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson
2 CONT Married Jane Butler born 24 Dec. 1699, died 24 Nov 1728, daughter Caleb Butler.
2 CONT Note:  Every other reference gives 1729 and her tombstone says that. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 26
2 CONT Augustine Washington and Mary Ball were married at Sandy Point, Westmoreland Co.,VA on March 17, 1731 (N.S.), The Rev. Walter Jones of Cople Parish officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - ANCESTORS OF AMERICAN PRESIDENTS by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 1
2 CONT He died at Ferry Farm, King George Co., VA. 12 April 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 14
2 CONT Tombstone reads:
2 CONT CAPTAIN
2 CONT AUGUSTINNE
2 CONT WASHINGTON
2 CONT 1694 - 1743
2 CONT
2 CONT LANDMARKS OF OLD PRINCE WILLIAM, VOL I & II by Fairfax Harrison, p. 107
2 CONT It was not until 1734 that Capt. Augustine Washington, seeking a healthier residence for the young children of his second wife, moved from his grandfather's house, Wakefield, on Pope's Creek in Westmoreland, to the high land of th
2 CONC e plantation on Little Hunting Creek, which likewise he had inherited from his grandfather, but he too was only a temporary resident of old Prince William; for, in 1739, when his modest home was destroyed by fire, he moved again t
2 CONC o the house where he died, on the north bank of the Rappahannock, opposite Fredericksburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT LAND RECORDS OF KING GEORGE CO., VA 1721-1743 by Sue Ann Damron, p. 188
2 CONT 2;22 - deed of release - 3 November 1738 - John Grant of the County of Stafford, Gent., and Margaret his wife Executors of the Last Wiull and Testament of William Strother late of the county of King George, Gent., deceased to Augu
2 CONC stin Washington of the county of Prince William, Gent. 317 pounds for 280A described in lease.  Whereas the said William Strother in his last will and testament dated 20 Nov. 1732 did declare that his lands in Prince William and K
2 CONC ing George Cos. be sold to the highest bidder by his executor his loving wife Margaret, if she should think convenient, John Grant and Margaret his wife Excutrix have exposed to sale the premises and the said Augustin Washington w
2 CONC as the highest bidder.  Signed John Grant, Margt. Grant Delivered in presence of William Thornton, junr., Antho. Hayne - Recorded 3 November 1738 T. Turner
2 CONT
2 CONT DEED OF RELEASE - Deed was released to Augustin Washington of the Co. of King George, Gent, 317 pounds for 280A described in lease. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT SURVEYS made by John Savage in King George Co - on April 1726 for Capt. Augustn. Washington 4,560A on the branches of Deep Run. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT SOME WILLS FROM THE BURNED COUNTIES OF VIRGINIA AND NOTHER WILLS NOT LISTED IN VIRGINIA WILLS AND ADMINISTRATIONS 1632-1800 by William Lindsay Hopkins, p. 71
2 CONT AUGUSTINE WASHINGTON     King Geo. Co        11 Apr 1743/6 May 1743
2 CONT Son Lawrence Washington.  Son Augustine Washington.  Son George Washington land bought from the executors of Mr. William Strother, decd.  Son Samuel Washington.  Son John Washington.  Son Charles Washington land whereon Thomas Lew
2 CONC is not lives and the land purchased of Gabriel Adams in Prince William Co.  Land purchased of Mr. James Hooe.  Daughter Betty Washington (under 18).  Present wife (not named).  Exors:  Son Lawrence Washington, Daniel McCarty and N
2 CONC athaniel Chapman.  Wit:  Robert Jackson, Anthony Strother, James Thompson.  Also land in Westmoreland Co. where Benjamin Wicks and Thomas Finch now live, lots in fredericksburg purchased of the Executors of Col. Henry Willis and a
2 CONC  piece of land where Matthew Tiffy late lived.
2 CONT Tyler V.9, pp. 35-38 New England Hist. & Gen. Register V. 45 (1891)  pp. 209-213 and King George Co. W III Book A-1, 1721-1752
1 NOTE Dec 22, 2009
2 CONT It was only about nine months ago that I came to the conclusion that Joseph Harwood, 1630s-1681, is not the son of William and Elinor Harwood, (Who aren't Harwood's at all but Hayward's according to the original land patents.), bu
2 CONC t rather the brother of Samuel Hayward of Stafford Co, VA. This position breaks ranks with other Harwood researchers, but when I looked at the original documents it appears to be true.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hayward married Martha Washington who is the great-aunt of George Washington. Samuel Hayward and Martha Washington are second cousins, through her mother Amphillis Hayward or Harwood. The Haywards, were neighbors of John Wa
2 CONC shington, George Washington's immigrant ancestor and great-grandfather. Nicholas Hayward, Sr., and Jr and Samuel Hayward had business dealings with John Washington.
2 CONT Source: Randy Harwood
1 NOTE Captain
1 NOTE Dec 22, 2009
2 CONT It was only about nine months ago that I came to the conclusion that Joseph Harwood, 1630s-1681, is not the son of William and Elinor Harwood, (Who aren't Harwood's at all but Hayward's according to the original land patents.), bu
2 CONC t rather the brother of Samuel Hayward of Stafford Co, VA. This position breaks ranks with other Harwood researchers, but when I looked at the original documents it appears to be true.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hayward married Martha Washington who is the great-aunt of George Washington. Samuel Hayward and Martha Washington are second cousins, through her mother Amphillis Hayward or Harwood. The Haywards, were neighbors of John Wa
2 CONC shington, George Washington's immigrant ancestor and great-grandfather. Nicholas Hayward, Sr., and Jr and Samuel Hayward had business dealings with John Washington.
2 CONT Source: Randy Harwood
