1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rodham and his father, Richard, were both Burgesses of Northumberland County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Kenner Family" - The William and Mary Quarterly, Vol. 14, No. 3 (Jan., 1906), pp. 173-181 (see attached
2 CONT
2 CONT RODHAM2 KENNER (Richard') married Hannah Fox, born July 25, 167I, daughter of Capt. David Fox and Hannah Ball (Quarterly, VIII., 109; Hayden, Va. Genealogies, 60); captain, justice, member of the House of Burgesses in 1696 and in 
2 CONC other years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue: 
2 CONT * 8 Richard; 
2 CONT * 9 Elizabeth, married  (I)  Richard Bushrod, son of Thomas Bushrod; (II) Robert Vaulx of Westmoreland (Note 2); (III)  Rev. Lawrence de Butts; 
2 CONT * 10 Hannah, born August 31, 1695, married (I) Richard Hull, (II) John Harris, (III)  Thomas Cralle, (IV.) John Cralle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Rodham Kenner died  in 1706 in Northumberland County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodham Kenner's widow, Hannah, married 2dly. Clement Spelman (Note 3), and had issue: Frances Spelman, who married Parish Garner (See wills of Col. Rodham Kenner proved Aug. 21, 1706, and of Richard Kenner proved January 18,  I727
2 CONC , in Northumberland Co., and William Fox, proved Nov.  2, 1718, in Lancaster Co.)
