1 NAME Frances /Fox/
2 GIVN Frances
2 SURN Fox
2 _MARNM Ball
2 NICK widow Burgess
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1690 AND 1706
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1737 AND 1741
2 PLAC 	St Mary's White Chapel Parish
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frances Fox,''' daughter of Samuel Fox and Anne Dangerfield, was born about 1704 in Lancaster County, and died between 1737 and 1741 in St. Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT #  Charles Burgess (b. 1682-d 14 March 1732) - married 5 Oct 1721,  St Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT # Jesse Ball (b. 27 Jun 1716-d. 14 Aug 1747) - married 10 Dec 1737 Lancaster County, Virginia.  Jesse Ball was a son of James Ball and Mary Conway.  He married 14 February 1741 to Mary Smith, so Frances had died before that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Charles Burgess and Frances Fox:
2 CONT * 1. Frances Burgess,   b. Abt 1718, St Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia d. 1750, Lancaster County, Virginia.  Married Baldwin Matthews Smith.
2 CONT *  	2. Margaret Burgess,   b. Abt 1721, St Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia.  Married James Ball (1718 - 1789), son of James Ball and Mary Conway.
2 CONT *  	3. Elizabeth Burgess,   b. 1732, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia d. Between 1754 and 1758, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia. Married 1) Jeduthan Ball (1725-1749), son of  James Ball & Mar
2 CONC y Conway 2) Robert Armistead.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT * 2.Capt. Samuel Fox, b. 28 Feb 1672/3. Married Ann Daingerfield. Died 1712, Lancaster County, intestate. His two children are named in the will of his brother William Fox as "niece Frances Fox" and "nephew David Fox." This will a
2 CONC lso names his "sister" [i.e. "sister-in-law"" Ann Fox. Some have confused the language of William's will go mean it was his blood sister and thus a daughter of David-2 Fox and Hannah Ball. This is not the case.http://archiver.root
2 CONC sweb.ancestry.com/th/read/VA-NORTHERN-NECK/2011-09/1315956181
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # MARRIAGE BONDS IN LANCASTER COUNTY. 5 Oct., 1721, Chas Burges & Frances Fox, daughter of Anne Fox. Sec.+ David Ball. 4 Oct., 1721, Anne Fox consents to marriage of daughter, Frances Fox, to Charles Burges. Witnesses, David Ball,
2 CONC  Richard Cooper.
2 CONT # MARRIAGE BONDS IN LANCASTER COUNTY "Saturday, Dec. 10, 1737, Sir. I desire you'l send a License to conjoin my son Jesse & Mrs. Frances Burges in the Bond of Hymen, & you'l oblige, Sir, you humble servt James Ball."
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I40309&tree=Tree1
2 CONT # http://lvaimage.lib.va.us/cgi-bin/drawerIII/disk8/CC/BA/015/F0185?128
2 CONT # Seldens of Virginia and Allied Families, Vol. 1, 1911
2 CONT # URL: http://vagenweb.rootsweb.com/hening/vol04-23.htm#page_452  Hening's Statutes at Large Note: An Act for the better enabling the Executors of the last Will and Testament of Charles Burges, gent. deceased, to pay his Debts, an
2 CONC d Legacies.
2 CONT #In Christ Church Vestry Book I find that "May 5, 1741, Mr. Jesse Ball and Mrs. Margaret Ball, wife of Mr. James Ball, Jun'r, Mrs. Frances Burgess and Mrs. Elizabeth Burgess, daughters of Charles Burgess, Gent., dec'd, by his wife
2 CONC  Frances, daughter of Samuel Fox, Gent, dec'd, have liberty to build Galleries on the East side of the South wing of the new Church."
