1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Given name has also been reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Rose
2 CONT * '''Roseanna
2 CONT * '''Rosanna
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:   Robert White (1561-1617) and Bridget Allgar (1562-1605)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna White''' was baptized in Shalford, Essex, England, on Sunday, July 13, 1600, and died in Windsor, Connecticut in 1647.  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to one unsourced assertion, arrived in North America with the 1638 sailing of the ''Susan and Ellen''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #  on Wednesday, October 18, 1620 in Messing, Essex, England, to John Porter (1594-1648), of Windsor, Connecticut.  He was the son of John Porter (1560-1625) and Sibyl Vessey (1561-1625).
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Anna's known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Porter (1620 England - 1697 Hartford, Connecticut) married Sarah Hart
2 CONT # Anna Porter was baptized in Felsted, county Essex, England, on September 22, 1621. She married William Gaylord on February 24, 1644/5.   
2 CONT # '''John Porter''' was baptized in Felsted on February 9, 1622/3.   
2 CONT # Sarah Porter (Gerald Ford's line): She was baptized in Felsted, Essex, England, on March 15, 1624/5, and died in Stratford, Connecticut, on March 16, 1696/7.   
2 CONT # James Porter was baptized in Felsted on February 20, 1627/8.   
2 CONT # Rebecca Porter was baptized in Felsted on September 16, 1630.   
2 CONT # Samuel Porter was baptized in Felsted on May 26, 1632, and died in July, 1632. He died in infancy and was buried on July 15, 1632.   
2 CONT # Rose Porter was baptized in Felsted on June 24, 1633, and died in 1648. Her burial is recorded in Matthew Grant's Old Church Record as being on May 12, 1648.   
2 CONT # Samuel (Grover Cleveland's line) Porter was baptized in Felsted on June 2, 1635.   
2 CONT # Mary Porter (Ulysses S. Grant's line) was baptized in Felsted on October 1, 1637.   
2 CONT # Nathaniel Porter was born in Windsor on July 19, 1640, and died in Stratford in January, 1679/80.   
2 CONT # Hanna Porter was born in Windsor in 1642.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of burial has been (erroneously?) reported to be July 1647.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Porter-of-Farmington/6000000012742844314 is not a known son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Porter-II-of-Windsor/6000000000436494125?through=6000000012742844314 & his wife https://www.geni.co
2 CONC m/people/Anna-Porter/6000000000436734994?through=6000000012742844314.  Detached 7 September 2025.  - EH
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (f/g) Rosanna "Anna" White Porter Birth: 	Jul. 13, 1600 Harwich Tendring District Essex, England Death: 	May 11, 1648 Windsor Hartford County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Robert & Bridget (Allgar) White. Sister of three other New England emigrants: John White, Elizabeth (White) Goodwin. & Mary (White) Loomis. She and John Porter had eleven known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Parish records of Shalford & Messing, Essex, England list Anne Whighte baptised July 13, 1600 in Shalford, daughter of Robert Whighte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers have confused her name as Rose, but that was actually the name of her daughter, Rose Porter baptised June 24, 1633 in Felstead, Essex, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *  Robert White (1560 - 1617)
2 CONT *  Bridget Allgar White (1561 - 1605) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *  John Porter (1594 - 1648) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #   Anna Porter Gaylord (1621 - 1653)* 
2 CONT #   John Porter (1622 - 1688)* 
2 CONT #   Sarah Porter Judson (1624 - 1696)* 
2 CONT #   Rebecca Porter (1630 - ____)* 
2 CONT #   Rose Porter (1633 - 1648)* 
2 CONT #   Samuel Porter (1635 - 1689)* 
2 CONT #   Mary Porter Grant (1637 - 1681)* 
2 CONT #   Anna Porter (1638 - 1638)* 
2 CONT #   Nathaniel Porter (1640 - 1680)* 
2 CONT #   Nathaniel Porter (1640 - 1680)*  
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT *   Sarah White Boutell (1586 - ____)*
2 CONT *   Mary White Loomis (1590 - 1652)*
2 CONT *   Elizabeth White Goodwin (1591 - ____)*
2 CONT *   John White (1600 - 1684)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: children: Mary Porter 1637 - 1681
2 CONT
