1 NOTE {geni:about_me} New England families, genealogical and memorial: a record of the ..., Volume 2 edited by William Richard Cutter [http://books.google.com/books?id=1M8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1069&lpg=PA1069&dq=Joshua+Judson+1656&source=bl&ot
2 CONC s=QwECaTHJzr&sig=jvTr9pvVDkL1NwEIe0LXYHYYAbc&hl=en&ei=FBnwTJrVMpD2swPoy6i5Cw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CC8Q6AEwBw#v=onepage&q=Joshua%20Judson%201656&f=false Pg.1069]
2 CONT
2 CONT Willam Judson, the immigrant ancestor, was born in England, in Yorkshire, according to tradition, and came to America in 1634, to Concord, Massachusetts, where he lived for four years. Then he located at Hartford, Connecticut, ...
2 CONC ...He died July 29, 1662. His wife Grace died at New Haven, September 29, 1659 and he married (second) Elizabeth, widow of Benjamin Wilmot. The will of Elizabeth was dated January or February, 1685, and the inventory was taken Nov
2 CONC ember 10, 1685. Children, born in England: 1. JOSEPH, 1619, lived in Roxbury, Massachusetts, four years, then moved to Wethersfield, Connecticut, where he was made a freeman in May 1638; elected representative to general assembly,
2 CONC  1639; lieutenant of train band of Stratford, June, 1672, and served in King Philip's war in 1676; was very prominent in town affairs, and owned a large amount of land in Stratford, of which he was a founder; was deputy from that 
2 CONC place to general assembly several times; commissioner of the town, also; married SARAH, daughter of John PORTER, and had ten children. 2. Jeremiah. 3. Joshua, mentioned below.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT A history of the old town of Stratford and the city Bridgeport ..., Volume 2 By Samuel Orcutt, Fairfield County Historical Society, Bridgeport
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=uvMLAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1111&lpg=PA1111&dq=Joseph+Judson,+Lt&source=bl&ots=knLntFHjuv&sig=JfWrdmRjNmwRvaMb46T03dM0AIk&hl=en&ei=DyfwTOL_LIqusAPa6cHACw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CCYQ6AEwA
2 CONC w#v=onepage&q=Joseph%20Judson&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg. 1228
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieut. JOSEPH, son of William and Grace JUDSON, came with his father to Stratford when nineteen years of age, in 1639. He m. SARAH, dau. of John PORTER (?), of Windsor, Oct. 24, 1644. She died mar. 16, 1696-7, aged 70. He died Oct
2 CONC . 8, 1690, aged 71. It is also stated that John Porter, of Windsor, had no daughter SARAH. (See sketches on pages 110 and 250.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, b. Mar. 2, 1645; m. Edmund Howell, of Southampton, L. I., in 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, b. Dec. 10, 1647.
2 CONT
2 CONT James, b. Apr. 24, 1650.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace, b. Feb. 19, 1651; m. Samuel Prudden, 1669.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b. mar. 10, 1654; d. Feb. 1, 1678, unm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah, b. Dec. 13, 1657; m. Samuel Wadsworth, of Farmington, in 1689, and had Hannah, Sarah and Samuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Esther, b. Aug. 20, 1660; m. Benjamin Curtis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joshua, twins, b. Oct. 27, 1664; d. y.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth, twins, b. Oct. 27, 1664, m. Samuel Wells, of hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe, b. Oct. 29, 1666; d. Nov. 1, 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail, b. Sep. 15, 1669; m. Josiah Curtis.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT History of ancient Woodbury, Connecticut: from the first ..., Volume 2, Part 1 By William Cothren
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=SHEFAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA162&lpg=PA162&dq=Joseph+Judson,+Lt&source=bl&ots=DIcEeeJqED&sig=r31sTwDhFRTBdH7kpojCXXOPu70&hl=en&ei=JCrwTP3AD4aqsAP21KjICw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CDcQ6AEwCA#
2 CONC v=onepage&q=judson&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg.588
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. JOSEPH, (2) eldest son of William, was fifteen years of age when his father came to New England. He lived with him at Concord, Mass., four years, removed thence to Stratford, Conn., married in 1644, in his 25th year, SARAH, da
2 CONC u. of John PORTER of Windsor, she being 18 years of age. He was a leading man in the early days of the colony, being frequently called to sustain the duties of public office. He d. Oct. 9, 1690, and was buried in Stratford. His wi
2 CONC dow d. March 16, 1696. Children,
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Sarah, b. March 2, 1645; m. Edward Howel of South Hampton, L. I., in 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. John, b. Dec. 2, 1647; d. Jan. 12, 1709, aged 62.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. James, b. April 24, 1650; m. Rebecca Wells of Stratford.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Grace, b. Feb. 19, 1651; m. Samuel Prudden of Milford.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Joseph, b. march 10, 1654; d. Feb., 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Hannah, b. Dec. 13, 1657; m. Samuel Wadsworth of Farmington.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Joshua, b. Dec. 3, 1658. (THIS IS STATED AS INCORRECT, THIS JOSHUA BEING THE SON OF JOSHUA AND ANN PORTER in History of ancient Woodbury, Connecticut: from the first Indian ..., Volume 2 By William Cothren, http://books.googl
2 CONC e.com/books?id=uQwCAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1510&lpg=PA1510&dq=Joshua+Judson+1656&source=bl&ots=AEt9NeQHBA&sig=G_xe0LECO2MBEENs-4iTZ9GhqD4&hl=en&ei=mh3wTNv4DIGasAPPrMnZCw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=0CDQQ6AEwCQ#v=onepage&q=Jo
2 CONC shua%20Judson%201656&f=false , Pg.1510 Corrections & Additions)
2 CONT
2 CONT VIII. Esther, b. Aug. 20, 1660; m. Benjamin Curtiss of Stratford.
2 CONT
2 CONT IX. Joshua, b. Oct. 27, 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT X. Ruth, b. Oct. 27, 1664; m. Samuel Wells of Hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT XI. Phebe, b. Oct. 29, 1666; d. Nov. 1, 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT XII. Abigail, b. Sept. 15, 1669; m. Josiah Curtiss of Stratford, and d. Nov. 21, 1697.
2 CONT
