1 OCCU Merchant in Hadley, Mass., One of the original 59 citizens that signed the agreement Apr 18, 1659 at Goodman Ward's home in Hartford to settle at Hadley
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was a merchant in Hadley, MA, where he went in 1659. During King Philip's War, Hadley was an important place. Samuel Porter took care of most of the wounded soldiers who were brought there, and did much for their provision 
2 CONC and comfort.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  1635 Felsted Essex, England  Death:  Sep. 6, 1689 Hadley Hampshire County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized 3 June 1635 at Holy Cross Church, Felsted,Essex, England. He was one of the Founders in 1659 of Hadley. He was the father of 10 children. The inventory of his estate can be found in Hampshire Probate Records, Box 117, No.
2 CONC  25,3-9.
2 CONT
