2 CONT SAMUEL PORTER (1635–1689) born in Felsted, Essex, England, and died in Hadley, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. He married Hannah Stanley in Massachusetts. “Baptized 3 June 1635 at Holy Cross Church, Felsted, Essex, England. He wa
2 CONC s one of the Founders in 1659 of Hadley. He was the father of 10 children.” “Samuel was a merchant in Hadley, MA, where he went in 1659. During King Philip's War, Hadley was an important place. Samuel Porter took care of most of t
2 CONC he wounded soldiers who were brought there and did much for their provision and comfort.” 
2 CONT --------------------
