2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Porter-163
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Coleman formerly Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Born before 4 Sep 1642 in Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John Porter and Anne (White) Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Abigail (Porter) Olcott, Thomas Porter, Anna (Porter) Gaylord, James Porter, John Porter Jr, Robert Porter, Sarah (Porter) Judson, James Porter, Rebecca (Porter) Spencer, Rose Porter, Joseph Porter, Samuel Porter, Mary (
2 CONC Porter) Grant and	Nathaniel Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Coleman — married 29 May 1663 in Felstead, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Thomas Coleman, Hannah (Coleman) Nash, John Coleman, Noah Coleman, Sarah (Coleman) Field and Berthia Coleman
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 17 Sep 1677 in Deerfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 22 Mar 2018 | Created 13 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Hannah Porter Christening: 4 September 1642 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Colony Marriage: 29 May 1663, to Deacon John Coleman [1] Death: September 19, 1677, Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony [2] Hannah (PORTER)
2 CONC  COLEMAN and her baby daughter, BERTHIA COLEMAN were both KILLED by Indians who attacked them in their home while John COLEMAN was out in the fields working. Another child was wounded and two children were taken hostage. Eight mon
2 CONC ths later they were found in Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Hill Cemetery, Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Early Families of New England. (Original Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2013. (By Alicia Crane Williams, Lead Genealogist.) entry for Humphrey Johnson, page 5 ↑ 2.0 2.1 Find A 
2 CONC Grave: Memorial #35617791 Welles, Edwin. Births, Marriages, and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., 1898) Page 37
