1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Coale / Cole was given a legacy mentioned in the will of Richard Johns written at Calvert Cliffs, 15 AUG 1717 as follows: I give to my daughter-in-law Elizabeth Cole the sum of £5, a token of love.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage of Elizabeth Sparrow to William Cole Jr., planter of Anne Arundel Co. on the 30th day of the month commonly called July took place at the home of Richard Johns at the Cliffs.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT > William Cole Jr. of A.A. Co. Md. (planter), was m. on 5th mo. 30 day of 1689to Elizabeth Sparrow of Clifts in Calvert Co. at Richard Johns house. See page 39.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Coale is mentioned in the will of his father, and his birth is recorded in the West River Monthly Meeting register. His marriage to Elizabeth Sparrow of the Clifts in Calvert County on 30 JUL 1689 is recorded in the same p
2 CONC lace.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Coale III signed his will on 05 July 1713, Anne Arundel Co., Maryland, and it was probated on 24 June 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Coale and Elizabeth Sparrow were the parents of ten children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth Jr. b. 1692
2 CONT # Mary b. 1694
2 CONT # William b. 1697
2 CONT # Hannah b. 1699
2 CONT # Samuel b. 1701
2 CONT # Priscilla b. 1703
2 CONT # Thomas b. 1705
2 CONT # Sarah b. 1706
2 CONT # Ann b. 1709
2 CONT # Margaret[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in Her father’s will
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sparrow, Thomas, A. A. Co.,1st Jan., 1674; 5th June, 1675.
2 CONT * To wife Eliza: ½ home plantation, during life.
2 CONT * To son Thomas and hrs., whole of sd. plantation and plantation at Patapsco at 21 yrs. of age.
2 CONT * To sister Eliza: Champe, certain land, (unnamed).
2 CONT * To dau. Eliza: and brother Solomon, personalty.
2 CONT * Exs.: Wife Eliza: and brother Solomon.
2 CONT * Test: Nath. Heathcote, Richard Tydeings. 2. 76
2 CONT
