2 CONT # Fact 1: 8 MAY 1674 Purchased "Rattle Snake Hill", 200 acres from Thomas Truman who bought it in 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fact 2: 1671 "Convinced by George Fox to become a Quaker"
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fact 3: 1675 Settled in Cliffs, Calvert Co., Md Bought Rattle Snake Hill, 200 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fact 4: 1697 Visited England to lobby agains the establishment of the Anglican Church in MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fact 8: 1694 Member of the Lower House inCalvert Co., MD
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fact 9. 1698 Returned from England yet again incidentally accompanied by the young Quaker enthusiast https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Chalkley/6000000004969779943 (see page 29 of Chalkley's journal)
