2 CONT To grandson Richard and hrs. (eldest son of deceased son Abraham), two tracts made over to testator by Wm. Billingley, being 136 A., “Billingsley's Swamp,” and 150 A., “Friendship Rectifyed”; also 160 A., “Fellowship,” bou. of Wm.
2 CONC  Dorrumple, and all three tracts lying bet. the “Clifts” and the branches of Battle Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT To grandson Abraham and hrs. (youngest son of deceased son Abraham), two tracts bou. of Wm. Williams, Sr. and Jr., “Chance,” cont. 108 A., the other adj. “Dodson's Desire,” cont. 100 A., also “The Purchase,” bou. of Thomas Johns, 
2 CONC these three tracts being in Calvert Co. and cont. 308 A.
2 CONT
2 CONT Testator states that having made over by deed of gift to the hrs. of his deceased son, Aquilla, part of a tract called “Letchworth's Chance,” cont. 400 A., it passed to Richard, eldest son of sd. Aquila.
2 CONT
2 CONT To grandson Aquila and hrs. (youngest son of deceased son Aquila), a tract bou. of John Edmonson, 600 A., “Cold Spring,” in freshes of Gr. Choptank R.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Richard and hrs. (having already made over to him by deed of gift the plan. where he dwells, being 300 A. of “Letchworth's Chance” afsd.), 300 A., “Fuller.”
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Kensey and hrs. (having already made over to him part of tract called “Meares,” cont. 200 A., and also 100 A. adj., being part of a tract testator now lives on called “Angellica”), 100 A. of “Angellica” adj. part already gi
2 CONC ven him, also 157½ A., “White's Rest,” bou. of James Bechamp, and 50 A., “Chance,” bou. of Wm. Griffen and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Isaac and hrs. (having already given him two tracts, 100 A., “Batchelors Fortune,” and 112 A., “Johns Addition”), remaining part of dwel. plan., “Angellica.”
2 CONT
2 CONT To granddau. Rebecca Johns, personalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son-in-law Robt. Roberts and hrs., 200 A. the s. side of “Grey's Chance” on the Clifts, being the plan. where he now dwells, and acquit him of all indebtedness to estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT To dau.-in-law Eliza: Cole, Quakers on Western Shore, Sarah Day, Job Hunt and his brother Thos., personalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Residue of personal est. to be divided into 10 equal parts and allotted as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 pts. to child. of deceased son Abraham, as eldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 pt. to be equally divided among child. of deceased son Aquila.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 pt. each to sons Richard, Kensey and Isaac.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 pt. each to daus. Priscilla Roberts and Margaret Hopkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT The remaining 2 pts. to dau. Eliza: Troth, she not having had a full portion with her other sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Exs.: Sons Richard, Kensey and Isaac, jointly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Test: Geo. Harris, Jno. Wilkinson, Elizabeth Giles, Eliz. Wilkinson, Anne Harris. 14. 532.
