1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''Do not confuse this Richard with https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Johns/6000000015086369234.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This Richard has been confused with https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Johns-of-King-William-Co/6000000008451449241  (For example, both have been linked as husband to Elizabeth Kinsey.)  Further research is warranted to dissoc
2 CONC iate them.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT justice of King William County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT An extensive discussion was posted on the topic of Richard's parentage by Joe Payne, among people who had researched the Johns tree in order to determine who were his parents. Best I could tell, there hasn't been anyone who has be
2 CONC en able to determine the correct parents, though Joe Payne himself suggests Roger Johns (an early settler of Calvert County who transported five servants) and Elizabeth (one of his servants, whom he freed from indentured servitude
2 CONC  on marriage in 1651). The conversation participants seemed to accept that Roger was somehow related to Richard, but was not Richard's actual parent:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.joepayne.org/richard.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT (As an aside, King William County in Virginia formed in 1702 from the southern half of King and Queen County. Accessed Nov. 13, 2017: http://publications.newberry.org/ahcbp/map/map.html#VA )
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From Joe Payne's Descendants of Richard Johns (Accessed Nov. 13, 2017)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.joepayne.org/johns.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST GENERATION 
2 CONT *(1) Roger1 JOHNS married (2) Elizabeth. 
2 CONT **Notes for Roger JOHNS: 
2 CONT ***Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/willrj.htm Will of Roger Johns]
2 CONT ***Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/willtjjj.htm Wills of Thomas Johns and John Johns], by Sam Randle
2 CONT ***Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/quaker.htm Thoughts on Quakerism and the Johns family]
2 CONT ***Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/grants.htm Johns Land Grants in Virginia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT *3 + Richard2 JOHNS 
2 CONT **Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/willrij.htm Will of Richard Johns]
2 CONT **Link to [http://www.joepayne.org/wrjohns.htm The Search for the Parentage of William  R.Johns] by Michael Pollock, containing more on the Will of Richard Johns and the early Johns family.
2 CONT
2 CONT SECOND GENERATION 
2 CONT *(3) Richard2 JOHNS, (Roger1 JOHNS) married spouse unknown.
2 CONT **[http://www.joepayne.org/calvert.htm Richard Johns of Calvert County Maryland]
2 CONT **[http://www.joepayne.org/richard.htm Notes for Richard JOHNS:]
2 CONT ***Children: 
2 CONT ****4 + William3 JOHNS b.c 1690 d.c 1775 
2 CONT ****       Thomas JOHNS 
2 CONT ****       John JOHNS 
2 CONT ****       Robert JOHNS 
2 CONT ****       Richard JOHNS 
2 CONT ****       Arthur JOHNS
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION 
2 CONT *(4) William3 JOHNS, (Richard2 JOHNS, Roger1) was born about 1690 at King William Co., Va, and married (5) Ann. William died about 1775 at Amherst Co., Va. 
2 CONT **[http://www.joepayne.org/william.htm More on William Johns of Cumberland, Buckingham and Amherst Co.'s Va.] 
2 CONT ***Children: 
2 CONT ****6 + Robert4 JOHNS, Sr b.c 1723 d.b 1778 
2 CONT ****7 + Thomas JOHNS b.c 1725 d. 1787 
2 CONT ****8 + William JOHNS 
2 CONT ****Bob Newsome's [http://www.joepayne.org/jessecam.htm Jesse son of William of Buckingham Co., Va]
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Roger Johns b: in England or Wales 
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth ?
