1 NOTE Name: Col. William UNDERWOOD Sex: M Birth: 1606 in Kent, England Death: ABT. 1642 in Rappahannock Co., Va
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 19 Apr 1612 in St Stephen, Walbrook, London, Middlesex, England Death: ABT 1638
2 CONT Immigration: BET 1636 AND 1642 England to Virginia Colony 5 6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT Justinian Cooper patented 1050 acres on 13 September 1636 in Warrisquick Co. for the transportation of twenty persons that included William Underwood. (Ref: Virginia Land Patent Book 1, Part 1, p. 380). The same Justinian Cooper p
2 CONC atented 1050 acres of land in Isle of Wright County on 16 August 1637, lying upon the head of Lawnes Creek; 50 acres for his own personal adventure, 1000 acres for twenty others among whom was the instant William Underwood. (Ref: 
2 CONC Virginia Land Patent Book 1, Part 1, p. 454 - August 16, 1637) On 16 March 1642, (one reference suggests this transaction took place in 1647 ?) the same Justinian Cooper patented a tract of 2400 acres listing himself as coming ove
2 CONC r four times, Ann his wife and William Underwood. (Ref: Land Patent Book 1, Part II, p. 874) As a result, it is established that the instant William Underwood was in the Virginia colony by 1636, but the exact year of his arrival i
2 CONC s still in doubt.  In 1643, William is referenced in the adjoining county of Surry when on 20 August the following is dated: "This bill bindeth us William Underwood and William Burwell our executors, administrators or assigns to p
2 CONC ay or cause to be paid unto John Flower of the rest of the owners of the ship Virg(a) Merch(t) teh jsut sum of eleven pounds of Current and Lawful Money of England which is for the passage of Wililam Underwood home for England".  
2 CONC One source references the instant William, as of the 'The Mount' in Rappahannock Co., Virginia. Another source (Douglas and Purcell's of Tidewater, VA.) suggest that William's parents were George Underwood and Alice Papworth, but 
2 CONC offers no citations.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Fact 1: Ancester of Pres. Madison & T. Roosevelt Note: Immigrated 1634 on board ship Bonaventure? Descendants: potus: James Madison & Theodore Roosevelt. 
2 CONT  Father: George UNDERWOOD b: 1585 in Weston, Hertford, England  Mother: Alice PAPWORTH  b: 27 APR 1589 in Hitchin, Hertford, England  Marriage 1 Margaret MASON  b: 1605 in England 
2 CONT Married: 1623 in York Parish, VA
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT Ann UNDERWOOD  b: in Virgina 
2 CONT William UNDERWOOD 
2 CONT Elizabeth UNDERWOOD  b: 1622 
2 CONT Margaret UNDERWOOD
2 CONT Mary UNDERWOOD 
2 CONT Sarah UNDERWOOD  b: 1635
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: William Underwood Sex: M Birth: ABT 1610 Death: AFT 1642 in Rappahonnock Co., VA Note: 
2 CONT Burgess for Lancaster Co., VA - 1652 Justice for Rappahonnock Co., VA - 1656
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: augustine slaughter bn 1724 son of rbt i wksmith.FTW Repository:  Media: Other Text: Date of Import: Apr 4, 2004 
2 CONT Title: Family Tree Maker: World Family Tree Repository:  Media: Book Page: 3:5794 
2 CONT Title: Elizabeth Catlett roesler2.FTW Repository:  Media: Other Text: Date of Import: Dec 31, 2005 
2 CONT Title: worldconnect@rootsweb.com (unverified) Repository:  Media: Book Page: The Crivellari and Related Families, Irisgay Crivellari, <imccriv@hal-pc.org> 
2 CONT Title: Family Tree Maker: World Family Tree Repository:  Media: Book Page: 3:5794 Note: Family Tree Maker: World Family Tree, 3:5794. Doesn't jibe well with dates for daughters. [MR, 1935-] 
2 CONT Papers of Gabriel Brooke Church Roesler Randolph 
2 CONT Title: Family Tree Maker: World Family Tree Repository:  Media: Book Page: 3:5794 Note: Family Tree Maker: World Family Tree, 3:5794. Col. in papers of Gabriel Brooke Church Roesler Randolph.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT (1) Source: Roberts, Gary Boyd, Ancestors of American Presidents, Santa Clarita, CA: Carl Boyer, 3rd, 1995, p. 11.  [Note by compiler: William? UNDERWOOD was a 3rd great-grandfather of James MADISON, Jr., 4th President of the Unit
2 CONC ed States. William? UNDERWOOD was also a 9th great-grandfather of Theodore ROOSEVELT, Jr., 26th President of the United States. See Roberts, Gary Boyd, Ancestors of American Presidents, Santa Clarita, CA: Carl Boyer, 3rd, 1995, p.
2 CONC  309.]  (2) Source: Williams, Sherrill Underwood, "Margaret UNKNOWN of Isle of Wight and Old Rappa. Cos., VA" <http://www.combs-families.org/combs/assoc/u-1.htm>.  (3) Fothergill, Augusta B., "Underwood Family of Virginia," in Fam
2 CONC ily History: Virginia Genealogies #1, pre-1600 to 1900s, Genealogies of Virginia Families V, R-Z, Underwood Family of Virginia, pp. 601-635, © MyFamily.com, Inc., September 1, 2006.
