1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Margaret 
2 CONT * Birth: ABT 1611 in England
2 CONT * Death: BEF 1669 in Old Rappahannock County, Virginia
2 CONT * Parents unknown
2 CONT * Married 1) William Underwood 2) John Upton 3) Thomas Lucas
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT * 1. William Underwood - England - 1627
2 CONT * 2.Anne Underwood - England - 1629
2 CONT * 3.Mary Underwood - Virginia - Old Rappahannock County 1626
2 CONT * 4.Elizabeth Underwood - England - 1632
2 CONT * 5. Sarah Underwood - England - 1634
2 CONT * 6. Margaret Underwood: - England - 1634 - 1638
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===disputed origins===
2 CONT Seen as Mason or Masan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Mason-Peck/6000000036970664856 & without attribution.
2 CONT
2 CONT we do not have documentation of Margaret's maiden name and do not know her origin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:638441&id=I2313
2 CONT
2 CONT The Will, of Margaret Underwood's second husband Captain John Upton was probated Dec. 16, 1652, sheds a lot more light on who were her children. John Upton was very generous to all the children involved: his one child John Upton a
2 CONC nd Margaret's children.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Virginia Genealogies #1, Genealogies of Virginia Families V, R-Z and The Descendants of Captain Thomas Carter page 101
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Capt. John Upton in his will, prob. Isle of Wight County, Dec. 16, 1652, left his land on the north side of Rappahannock River to his stepdaughters Elizabeth, Sarah, and Margaret Underwood, and Anne Underwood, now the wife of Mr
2 CONC . James Williamson. Also gave them 1,500 acres in Isle of Wight County, and likewise 850 acres if his son John Upton died before he reached the age of twenty-one years."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://dgmweb.net/FGS/S/SlaughterFrancis-ElizabethUnderwood.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >Margaret MASON (1610-1665), d/o John MASON (1586-1635) & Ann PECK (1575- )  m2. Capt. John UPTON (c1596-1652); m3. 10 Apr 1657, Thomas LUCAS (1600-167
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (Biography in progress)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret DEW (or DEWE) was the daughter of Thomas DEWE, London Stationer (1584-1625), and his 1st wife Annie (HELMES) DEWE (1581-c.1620).  Margaret married William UNDERWOOD in about 1623, when they were both probably about 17 yea
2 CONC rs old.
2 CONT
2 CONT (All these dates are still being researched, but the relationships and names seem to be accurate.  As more parish records are transcribed, photographed, indexed, and made available to more researchers, there is growing confidence 
2 CONC that these necessary details will become filled in with proven data.)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/175712487/margaret-underwood Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 15 2020, 16:24:02 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Ths FindaGrave site entry has already been disproved. There is no supercomputer reference to source citation of a document.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Major John Mason couldn't be her father if she was born in Virginia. He never came to Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
