1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.combs-families.org/combs/assoc/u-pierce.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Sarah UNDERWOOD, born before 1645, died after 1702 in (of) Westmoreland Co, Virginia; married between 1650 and 1668, Col. William PIERCE (son of Capt. William PIERCE), died in 1702 in Westmoreland Co, Virginia. Known Issue: A
2 CONC nn PIERCE; Elizabeth PIERCE; Mary PIERCE; Margaret PIERCE; John PIERCE; Sarah PIERCE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Although Sarah, wife of Col. Wm. PIERCE is believed to have been the Sarah UNDERWOOD named in the will of Col. John UPTON, and the "sister PIERCE" named in the will of Elizabeth UNDERWOOD Taylor Slaughter Catlett Butler, the
2 CONC  latter is thus far the only documentation located re her relationship. If so, it is quite insubstantial. A growing collection of records that may be of assistance in strengthening (or destroying) the case for Sarah follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 June 1663,(VA LPBV:29) William PIERCE 4054 acres of land lying on the north side of Rappahannock River and on the east side of the main Rappahannock Creek (UNDERWOOD, Fothergill)
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Jul 1668 (Old Rappa. Records, 1677-1682, Part 1:178) William PEIRCE of Westmoreland to George BRUCE 150 A of land scituated in ye Forest between ye Rivers of Potomack & Rappae: being pt. of a Pattent of 4,310 A granted unto me y
2 CONC e sd PEIRCE 4 Oct 1666 ye 150 A â¦ line of marked trees of Mr. Jno. LORD, Wm. HORTONâ¦ S/Wm. PEIRCE. Wits: Wm. HORTON, Jno. RIDDELL. 28 Oct 166 ack. by Major Wm. PEIRCE & then rec. in Westmoreland p me Robt. NURCE Clâ¦ Memd: th
2 CONC at I Sarah PEIRCEâ¦ all my interestâ¦ 26th Aug 16668. S/Sarah PEIRCE; Wits: Wm. LLOYD, Wm. [W] ROBINSON. Ack. in Court by John QUCLY Atty of Mrs. Sarah PEIRCE & rec. in Westmoreland. (Sparacio)
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Feb 1701 - 7 April 1702. (Westmoreland Wills, p. 31) Will of William PIERCE. Bequests to Pierce and Stanley GOWER [sons of Francis GOWER and his wife who was a daughter of Col. William PIERCE], to grandson Samuel BAILEY, grands
2 CONC on William PIERCE, daughters Elizabeth BRIDGES, Margaret GRAHAM, Mary ROWSEY, mentioned son John deceased and to wife Sarah one negro and her thirds of the estate. (Underwood, Fothergill).
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 Jun 1707 (Westmoreland Co VA Court Orders) Upon the Petition of Sara PIERCE, Relict of William PIERCE, of this County, Gent. deced, on behalf of William PEIRCE their grandson now under the tutorage and care of Nathaniel POPE, m
2 CONC erchant, now in England, who married one of the daughters of William and Sara PEIRCE (Sparacioâ¦)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Daughter Elizabeth PIERCE Bridges m Nathaniel POPE, guardian of the grandson, William PIERCE who was named in the will of Col. Wm. PIERCE. This or another of the 50,000 Nathaniel POPES was alias Nathaniel BRIDGES. The latte
2 CONC r's mother, Mary SISSON, m (1) Nathaniel POPE; (2) Anthony BRIDGES; (3) another David WICKLIFFE, the brother of the above Robert WICKLIFFE; and (4) Lewis NICHOLAS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 Jan 1697/8 - 30 Mar 1698 (Westmoreland Wills) Robert WICKLEFF names wife Margaret; son David, brother David, father in law Col. Wm. PIERCE (Fothergill)
2 CONT
