1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT Richard Williamson is said to be the ancestor of all the Virginia Williamsons. He first came to Virginia in 1638 but returned to England shortly thereafter. In 1641, Richard returned to Virginia for good. His passage was paid for 
2 CONC by Ambrose Bennet.  Settling in Isle of Wight County, Richard soon began acquiring property. He named the family home "Cobham Hall." That land was thought to have been purchased in 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages & Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources disagree regarding the wife or wives of Richard Williamson. Some sources. e.g., Ray, state she was Margaret Brown. Others, such as Boddie, give her name as Margaret Sherwood. It does not appear Richard was married twice. I
2 CONC t is known her first name was Margaret, the last name is in question. More research is needed. (Strutton-11 18:46, 5 June 2021 (UTC))
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard married Margaret Unknown about 1620 in England. known children include:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Richard Williamson
2 CONT # James Williamson, 1621-1656
2 CONT # John Williamson
2 CONT # Dr. Robert Williamson, 1625-1670
2 CONT # Henry Williamson
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret is named as widow and administrator of the estate Richard Williamson, deceased, in a land transaction dated 21 September 1655.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Note: children are seen as born in IOW, but no one before 1638 could have been 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
