1 NOTE {geni:about_me} URL: http://mkhgenealogy.com/ URL title: Research Notes for the Family of Henry Williamson and Unknown Loes and Catherine Weekes Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF HENRY WILLIAMSON
2 CONT
2 CONT ELIZABETH WILLIAMSON
2 CONT
2 CONT "William and Mary Quarterly" Armistead Family John Armistead married first, Elizabeth (?Gill), mentioned as sister Elizabeth Armisread in the will of James Burwell and second, Susanna, daughter of Thomas Meriwether of Essex who ma
2 CONC de his will in 1708 when Susanna was not then baptized.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Thomas Meriwether, son of Nicholas Meriwether, of Surry, the immigrant, names brother Francis of Essex: Nicholas of New Kent; sister Jane Brown, wife of William Brown of Surry; wife Susannah; nephew William Meriwether,
2 CONC  son of brother Nicholas, to have his land in Surry; nephews William, David and Francis, sons of brother Nicholas; Rallph Shelton; land to child unbaptized; Nicholas and Francis Meriwether executors. Dated Jan. 7, 1708 , proved Fe
2 CONC b. 10, 1708-09.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Meriwether was one of the feoffees of Tappahannock. He married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Williamson, Gent bequeathed lands in 1699 given to him by Captain Richarrd Loes and Mr. Abraham Weeks and Millicent his wife of Rappahannock to his 3 daughters, Elizabeth, Katherine and Frances. Aterwards in 1707 William You
2 CONC ng of Essex and Katharine his wife, one of the daughters, confirmed to Thomas Meriwether half of the lands devised by William(??) unto his daughter Elizabeth Meriwether, deceased and in case of his death to said Katherine Young an
2 CONC d Frances Bird, his other daughters. (Essex Records).
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Henry Williamson made his 3 daughters executors of his Will. On Sept. 11, 1699 when the will of Henry Williamson was proved, Thomas Meriwether and wife Elizabeth signed.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I032545&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
