1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT === Catherine Weeks
2 CONT *Female 1661 - Bef 1699
2 CONT *Daughter of Abraham Weeks, Gent. and Millicent (unknown) Weekes 
2 CONT * Wife of Henry Williamson 
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * She is not named in her father's 1691 will, but her husband Henry _____son was named as an executor. She is said to have later married her nephew, Thomas Montague, son of her sister "Letty." Her christening record has her as Kat
2 CONC herine, daughter of Abraham & Millicent Weekes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I32554&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT 1679-1688 Middlesex Co Va Deed Book 2; Antient Press: (Page 324)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > 1679-1688 Middlesex Co Va Deed Book 2; Antient Press: (Page 324)
2 CONT KNOW ALL MEN by these presents that I ABRAHAM WEEKES of the County of Middx in ye Collony of Virga Gent & MILLICENT my Wife for ye naturall affection wee bare to our Daughter CATHERINE the Wife of Mr. HENRY WILLIAMSON of ye County
2 CONC  of RAPPAHANOCK & for divers other considerations, have granted unto ye said Mr Henry Williamson & Catherine his Wife & ye heires of their Body all our right of part of a Patten & track of land conteining Nine hundred and fifty ac
2 CONC res in the County of Middlesex upon ye North East side of ye great Swamp on ye head of Pean - katanck River as by ye said Patten dated the 20th of September 1683 the other part of the said Patten being sould unto my Sonn Mr FRANCI
2 CONC S WEEKES as by Deed of Sale it being ye land ye said Francis Weekes doth now live on. IN WITNESS we have sett our hands and fixed our seales the 30th day of June 1688
2 CONT In presence of RICHARD ROBINSON. Abraham Weekes
2 CONT EDWARD THOMAS RICHARD WILLIS Millicent Weekes
2 CONT Acknowledged the 2d July
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
