1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Catherine Williamson
2 CONT *Female Abt 1683 - Abt 1751
2 CONT * Daughter of Henry Williamson and Katherine (Weekes) 
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Young
2 CONT # 25 MAR 1720 in Middlesex Co., VA to Thomas Montague b: BEF 1691
2 CONT # 1724 in Essex Co., VA to Richard Tyler
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Adventurers of Purse and Person", P 252
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Montague married Katherine, daughter of Henry Williamson and widow of William Young. The will of Thomas Montague Feb. 7, 1720 to May 16, 1721 Essex County, named wife, "son-in-law" (step-son) William Young and "daughter-in-
2 CONC law" (step-daughter) Elizabeth Young, bequeaths "all that parcel of land called 'Montague's Island' to "cozen (nephew) William Montague, son of my brother William Montague" and leaves to "Thomas Paine of Middlesex County, 150 acre
2 CONC s out of upper side of my land lying in Essex County."
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 3rd to Richard Tyler.
2 CONT
