2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Added on 7/1/2023:  From the records of the Texas Colonial Grand Dames the listing of John Chilton
2 CONT and wife, Jane and children.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chilton is listed as being born in 1640, Kent County, England.  His will was proved on
2 CONT April 29, 1708.  He died before February 25, 1707 when his will was probated.  In his will John's 5 children are named and wife, Jane.  It was stated that John died in Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his 2 brothers arrived in Virginia by 1660. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chilton was appointed in 1687 for horse service in the county militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1668, the son of John Chilton was listed on the Lancaster County, VA tithable list.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1690's the son of John Chilton, also named John Chilton moved to Westmoreland County.  He first
2 CONT appears in court records on 24 November 1697, as a planter in Cople Parish.  By 1699 the son, John
2 CONT Chilton had acquired extensive property, which included the junction of Currioman Creek with the Potomac,  
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1700 John Chilton had 3 tithes, for Lancaster County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1703 John Chilton sold his home plantation to Robert Carter, moved to Westmoreland County where
2 CONT he died 4 years later.  
