1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Tyler/6000000140523807836?through=6000000008229349153 (son of Francis & Rebecca).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Downman''', seen as daughter William Downman (d. 1712) and his wife Million Travers, was born about 1678 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died after 1766 in King George County, Virginia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A John Tyler lived at Falmouth in Stafford County, but he appears to have been too old a man to have been John Tyler, third son of I Francis Tyler.  His will was made November 4, 1755, and proved in King George County, June 2, 175
2 CONC 7. By his wife Mary Downman, he had one child, Margaret, who married first, William Waugh, September 10, 1738, and had issue: ... She married 2ndly, Daniel Royalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Will of John Tyler (1753)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tyler: his will which was made Nov. 4 1753 and proved June 2 1757, John mentioned the children of William and Mary Waugh:Tyler, Priscilla, William, Thomas, and Million.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was made and proved in King George Co. but he had lived at Falmouth, Stafford Co.for some time prior to that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Will of JOHN TYLER. I JOHN TYLER of King George County .. revoking all wills made before this 4th day of November 1755 .. 
2 CONT *as co my body  my will is that it be Decently buried in Falmouth Church Yard without much noise or funeral .. *I bequeath to my beloved wife MARY the use of all my estate .. at her second marriage or death I give to my Grandson
2 CONT * TYLER WAUGH my plantation whereon 1 now live laying in King George & Stafford Counties containing 200 acres .• in lieu of a piece of land in Fairfax County containing about 250 acres which WILLIAM WAUGH notwithstanding the said 
2 CONC land was Iotailed left in his will to his son THOMAS ., 
2 CONT *to my Grandson WILLIAM WAUGH; 
2 CONT *to my Grandson THOS WAUGH;
2 CONT * to my Granddaughter PRICELLA WAUGH " and a pott commonly called my Grand Mothers Pott; 
2 CONT *to my granddaughter MILLION WAUGH . I leave two negroes in the hands of my Executors for the use of my Daughter MARGARET for her support .. 
2 CONT *'''without any benefit to DANIEL ROYALHY her wicked & ill disposed Husband who I disclaim for his ill treatment of her as unworthy to be called my son in law'''
2 CONT * I appoint my worthy friend and benefactor CHARLES CARTER Esqr. of Stanstid also HARRY TYLER and JOHN FITZHUGH of Stafford to be Executors .
2 CONT * Presence of John Rose, John x Tyler
2 CONT * John Fitzhugh, Saml. Mitchel
2 CONT * Richard Randall, John Bell
2 CONT * At a court held .. 2nd June 1757 .. will presented into court by MARY TYLER widow of JOHN .. ordered to be recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Not named as daughter of William Downman here:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1709-1717 Richmond County, Virginia Wills Book 3 and Inventories [Robert K. Headley, jr.];
2 CONT William DOWNMAN, NFP, will; 23 May 1711, 4 Jun 1712 son Rawleigh tract of land bought of Edward KING called "Mt. Sion" and 250 ac. bought of Charles CALE;
2 CONT son Robert 300 ac. near the branches of Totuskey;
2 CONT son Travers all the land I bought of Arthur [ATTEY] in the forest of Moraticon;
2 CONT son William what moneys son GLASCOCK owes me for the millstones and what belongs to them;
2 CONT daus. Million, Elizabeth, Priscilla;
2 CONT ex: wife
2 CONT wits: Abraham GOAD, William ACKERS, William GOAD.
2 CONT
2 CONT [The births of the fol. chil. of William and Million DOWNMAN are rec. in the NFPR: Rawleigh (1680), Wilmoth (1681), Million (1683), William (1685), Robert (1686), Elizabeth (1688), Travers (1696), and a second son Travers (1700). 
2 CONC Page 51.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Or here:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond Co., VA, Will Book 5, Page 75-76, photocopy in possession of K. Much:
2 CONT
2 CONT "March 31: 1727. In the name of God amen. I Millan [sic] Downman of the County of Richmond and in the parrish of North Farnham ... and all the rest of my Estate I give to be equally Divided Between my two sons and my three Daughte
2 CONC rs William Downman and Travers Downman Millian Glasscock Elisabeth Downman and Priscilla Heale ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
