1 NAME Catherine /Chinn/
2 GIVN Catherine
2 SURN Chinn
2 _MARNM Heale
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 JUN 1686
2 PLAC Morattico Creek
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 BURI
2 DATE 1736
2 PLAC Heale Family Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 SEP 1736
2 PLAC Peach Hill
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Catherine Chinn, daughter of John Chinn & Alice his wife, as born 7 Jun 1686 in Morattico Creek, Lancaster Co., Virginia and died on 25 Sep 1736 in Lancaster Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 1702 in , Lancaster Co., Virginia to George Heale, son of George Heale and Ellen Rogers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT # Eleanor "Ellen" Heale b: 19 Nov 1705 in North Farnham Parish, Richmond Co., Virginia.  Married David Ball.
2 CONT # George Heale b: 4 Jan 1706/1707 in North Farnham Parish, Richmond Co., Virginia.  Married Susannah Edrington.
2 CONT # Joseph Heale b: ABT 1708
2 CONT # Elizabeth Heale b: 8 Mar 1709/1710 in North Farnham Parish, Richmond Co., Virginia.  Married William Davenport.
2 CONT # John Heale b: ABT 1711.
2 CONT # William Heale b: ABT 1712 in ,, Virginia.  Married Judith Swann.
2 CONT # Sarah Heale (Hoale) b: ABT 1714 in ,, Virginia.  Married Lindsay Opie.
2 CONT # Katherine (Catherine) Heale b: ABT 1716 in ,, Virginia.  Married John Cannaday.
2 CONT # Ann Heale b: ABT 1718 in ,, Virginia.  Married Moore Fauntleroy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT !15 Dec 1691:  Mentioned in her father's will. !6 Dec 1694:  It was stated that Katherine daughter of Rawleigh Chinn would be nine years old on 7 June next.  William and Mary Quarterly, 17, 1908, p. 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT !6 Dec 1698:  She is mentioned in the will of her step-father.  i give and devise my land and plantation in Richmond Co which I bought of Mr Wm Tomlyn to my loving wife Alice Stretchley during her natural life and after her deceas
2 CONC e to my daughter in law Kathrine Chinn and her heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Married Mr. Mc Carty.  William and Mary Quarterly, vol 1, series 2, 1921, p. 294.
2 CONT
2 CONT !29 August 1701:  Mentioned in mothers will as daughter Catherine Heal.
2 CONT
2 CONT !1736:  Katherine is buried on the Heale Family graveyard.  Her tombstone reads:  "Here lyes intered the body of Catherine ...George Heale ...his wife departed ye 25th day of September in ye 60th year.....they had three sons .....
2 CONC daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *  (1) "Mostly Southern," by Mark Freeman (http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com, markfreeman database, 6 Jul 2007).
2 CONT
2 CONT *  (2) "The Chinn and Myers Families," by Randie Myers (http://wc.rootsweb.com, rjm66 database, 29 Apr 2007). Cites: (a) Tishomingo County Records. (b) Will of John Chinn Sr. Copied from a photostat obtained from The Virginia Stat
2 CONC e Library by Nanon L. Carr, Kansas City, MO. (c) "Wm. & Mary Quarterly," Vol 17 (July 1908) p.63. Lancaster Recorder.  (d) Lancaster Co., Wills, etc. No 8 (1690-1709) p.210-211. Copied from a handwritten copy in the Chinn Family f
2 CONC ile #73 developed by Miss Nanon L. Carr and located in the Mid-Continent Genelogy Library, Independence, MO.
2 CONT *  (3) "Heale Family," "William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine," Vol. 17, p.297 (rpt. http://books.google.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT *!  Birth: (1,2a) d/o John CHYNN/Alice SMOOT. (2c,3) d/o John CHINN. (1,2a) 7 Jun 1688. (2c,3) On 6 Dec 1694, to be age 9 on next 7 Jun [b. 7 Jun 1686]. (1,2a) Morattico Creek, Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT *  Marriage to George HEALE: (2) George Nicholas HEALE. (3) George HEALE. (2) 1702. Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT *  Death: (1,2a) 25 Sep 1736. Lancaster Co., VA.    (2b) 1691, 15 Dec: John CHINN Senr of the Co. of Lancaster made his will. "I give unto my daughter Katherine CHINN All the Right and title which I have to a tract of Land laying 
2 CONC at the heade of Morattico which I purchased of Thomas MADDISON to her and her heirs forever, tenn head of cattle four sheep a mare A Rugg, bolster, and one pillow one iron pott a frieng pan when she shall come to the age of sixtee
2 CONC n years and not before."
2 CONT *  (2c) 1694, 6 Dec: Ann daughter of John CHINN would be 13 years old on May 5 next, Rawleigh son of same, 11 years old on May 23 next, and Catherine, dau of same would be 9 on June 7 next.
2 CONT *  (2d) 1701, 29 Aug: Alice STRETCHLEY of the parish of St Mayries, White Chapell in the Co. of Lancr made her will. "I give unto my Daughter Cathrine HEAL all my Stock of Cattle hoggs and sheep that is upon my plantation that my 
2 CONC husbabd Mr. Jno STRETCHLEY bought of Mr William TOMLYN Except four Cowes and Six Sheep which I give to my Sister Dorothy DURHAM. I give unto my Daughter Cathrine HEAL one of the smallest silver Tankards & one of the smallest Silvr
2 CONC  Tumblors and three Silvr Spoons and one hundred fourty and five pounds Sterling being due to me and in the hands of Mr Tho ELLIS Merchant of London and one negro woman named Sue of Short Stature and one negro man named Jack and o
2 CONC ne black mare Runeny at Morratico Point branded on the rear Buttook and shoulder with JC. I give to the sd Cathrine HEAL two featherbeds with ruggs & blanketts and four pare of sheets three pillows and six pillow cears six pewter 
2 CONC dishes tow pewter Basons one Doz of plases one doz. wooden ditto and one pewter Chamber pott six Leather Chairs out of the new house Chamber and one suit of my best wearing cloaths Excepting them before given to my Daughter Anne F
2 CONC OX this being in Lieu and full satisfaction of her portion left her by her father Mr Jno CHIN and of the legacy left her by her father in Law Mr Jno STRETCHLEY she the sd Cathrine having noe other Right or Claims from my estate."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
