1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Spouse:
2 CONT 	Sarah Ball,   b. Abt 1709, Lancaster County, Virginia d. Bef 6 Aug 1742, Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT -Marriage	14 Oct 1725 	Lancaster County, Virginia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT  	1. Richard Selden,   b. Bef 1722, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia d. 17 Jan 1771, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia - Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John Selden,   b. 4 Oct 1738, Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sarah Selden,   b. Bef 1742   d. Aft 1760, Bedford County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT SELDEN, John, of Elizabeth City Co., Gent. Rec. 21 Aug. 1752.
2 CONT Apprenticed son John Selden "age 13 years the 4th day of October last" to Thos. Edwards, Jr., Clerk of Lancaster Co. Court, to learn the science or trade which he now useth. Wits: Richard Selden, Wm. Mountague. W.B. 15, Page 107
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT BALL, Sarah. Will. 6 Aug. 1742. Rec. 10 Sept. 1742.
2 CONT Legatees: Daus. Easter Glascock, Margaret Ball, John Selden, Gr. son Wm. Montague, Gr. dau. Frances Lawry. Extr. Wm. Glasscock. Mention is made of a marriage betw. her gr. son Richard Selden and the dau. of James Ball. Wits. Marga
2 CONC ret Williamson, Eliz. McTire and Wm. Ball. W.B. 13, Page 301.
2 CONT
2 CONT lawyer; Sheriff of Lancaster Co; JP & King's attourney for Elizabeth City Co.  Married three times, no information on first wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT *     a= dau ??
2 CONT *     b=(13 Oct 1725, Lancaster Co) Sarah Ball; dau of Richard Ball & Sarah Young
2 CONT *     c=(ca. 1740) Grace Boswell; dau of William Boswell & Eleanor Corprew.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.1.1 a Richard Selden; b. 1721; d. 1789. Married Mary Ball; b. 6 Apr 1721, Lancaster Co; dau of Maj. James Ball of "Bewdley" & Mary Conway (QV).
2 CONT * 1.1.2 a Elizabeth Selden
2 CONT * 1.1.3 a Eleanor Selden
2 CONT * 1.1.4 b Richard Selden
2 CONT * 1.1.5 c Rev. William Selden; b. 1741; d. 25 June 1783, Hampton. See below.
2 CONT * 1.1.6 c Joseph Selden; d. 1775, Eizabeth City Co. See below.
2 CONT * 1.1.7 c John Selden; d. 1775. See below.
2 CONT * 1.1.8 c Elizabeth Selden
2 CONT * 1.1.9 c Eleanor Selden
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Selden_%285%29 WeRelate Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 31 2016, 4:15:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-541155528/john-seldon-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 31 2016, 4:47:06 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == John Sheldon==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Samuell Sheldon and Rebecca Yeo 
2 CONT * The possessions in land of John Selden, son of the first settler, were at the head of Hampton Creek, extending across to Back River and also into Nansemond County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Sheldon, married, first ——-, (2) '''Sarah Ball''' on October 13, 1725, daughter of Captain Richard Ball and & Sarah Young (3) '''Grace Boswell''' about 1740, daughter of  Captain William Boswell & Eleanor Corprew, appears t
2 CONC o have also married a Selden (See note Of Lyon G.Tylor, Doctor William Boswell Selden, in 1831), states that his greatgrandmother, Eleanor Corprew, wa s first married to Robert Brough, whose son, William Brough, had daughters Eliz
2 CONC abeth, who married McCaw, Mary, who married Scott and a third daughter who married Harris.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Richard Sheldon,''' married Mary Ball.
2 CONT * '''Joseph Sheldon,''' married Mary (Armistead) Curle.
2 CONT * '''John Sheldon,''' married Elizabeth Wallace.
2 CONT * '''William Sheldon,''' married Mary Ann Hancock.
2 CONT * '''Elizabeth Sheldon,''' died unmarried.
2 CONT * '''Eleanor Sheldon,''' died unmarried.
