1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == John Sheldon==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of John Sheldon and Grace Boswell 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:, about 1760, '''Elizabeth Wallace''',  daughter of James Wallace, II and Martha Westwood  erected in the churchyard of St and bears the following epitaph : ( See Wallace Family (No 1).“Here lyes the body Of the Reverend
2 CONC  Mr. James Wallace, late Minister Of this Parish. in Perthshire, in North Britain. He was serviceable to, James Wallace, whose tomb, was John’ s Church at Hampton, Virginia, by the Hampton in Perthshire, in North Britain. He was b
2 CONC orn in Errol Perthshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT * In 1758 John Selden Sold to his cousin, Cary Selden, his estate “Strawberry Banks ”in Elizabeth City County, devised to him by the Will of his father, John Selden. John Selden died intestate in 1775. His wife inherited from him 
2 CONC his family plate. The following named children are recorded in the account given by Doctor William Selden. According to another account, they had  three daughters, and one son. Douglas of Scotland, and, after his death, Col.Chatha
2 CONC m, near Fredericksburg . Another daughter married Mr. Thornton Of Fall Hill, near Fredericksburg.  One daughter married Mr. Jones Of Fitzgerald, and left an only son (See William and Mary Quarterly) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Martha Sheldon,''' born about 1762 ; married Mr. Jones; widow, aged 69, in 1831, without children. a ii 
2 CONT * '''Ann Sheldon,''' married Mr. Fitzgerald ; her son , James Fitzgerald, was living in 1831.
2 CONT * '''Elizabeth Sheldon,''' married Mr. McMurder ; one daughter, who married Mr. Gibson, and was living in Richmond in 1831.
2 CONT * '''John Sheldon,''' living in 1831 ; had a large family.
2 CONT * '''James Sheldon,'''
2 CONT * '''Rebecca Sheldon,'''
2 CONT
