2 TITL Ancestry Family Trees
1 NOTE !BIRTH - BALTIMORE COUNTY FAMILIES, 1659 - 1759 by Robert W. Barnes p. 289
2 CONT George Haile, son of Nicholas (1) was born about 1647, died in Lancaster Co., VA in 1698.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT Married Ellen (---) - Ellen Rogers - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - See Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT ABSTRACTS LANCASTER CO., VA WILLS - 1653-1800, by Ida J. Lee, p. 110
2 CONT HEALE, Geo. 30 Dec 1697  Rec. 2 Feb 1698
2 CONT Sons:  George all lands and plantation, Joseph, John, Nicholas
2 CONT Daus:  Sarah, Elizabeth, Ellen.
2 CONT Exor:  Geo. Heale
2 CONT Overseers: Robt. Carter and my son-in-law William Ball
2 CONT Wits:  Joseph Ball, Jas. Innis, Wm. Ball
2 CONT Will Book 8, p. 74
2 CONT Note:  George Heale mentions his son-in-law, William Ball who was evidently married to George's daughter, Hannah Heale which is more proof that Col. William Ball married Hannah Heale and not Hannah Beale. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT VIRGINIA GLEANINGS IN ENGLAND by Lothrop Withington, p. 264
2 CONT GEORGE HEALE of City of Lancaster in Rappahanock, Will 30 December 1697; proved 10 March 1708-9.  Land and Plantation wherein I now live bounding upon South east side of the main road which leads from Mr. Ball's Mill to a Mill whi
2 CONC ch was formerly Josias Draper's, between the said Roads and Thomas Davises, containing about 1300 acres to my son George Heale.  Remainder of dividend Land upon North West of said Main Road, then up along the white Marsh to Timoth
2 CONC y Stamp's, then to aforesaid Main Road, 500 acres to my son John Heale.  Main Road to be dividing line between George and John, and if either are without heirs, to longest liver whole 1800 acres.  My land in the Forrest at the hea
2 CONC d of Corotom' on west side of the Main Swamp, bounding on land formerly Nathaniel Browne's then along the Head line that divides this land from the land of Giles Robinson and Randolph Miller, so far along said head line that a dir
2 CONC ect course to Main Swamp shall include 400 Acres, to my son Joseph Heale, if he die, then to John.  My land in Cherry Point, bounding on land of Mr. Keen and Mr. Crawley, 100 acres, to my daughter Ellen Heale, if she die to daught
2 CONC er Elizabeth Heale, then to daughter Sarah Heale.  My land down at Corotoman, 350 acres adjoining lands of William Clarke, Mathew White, Mr. Arms, Mr. Harrison and the main road to my two daughters Elizabeth and Sarah Hele.  My qu
2 CONC arter Plantation in the Forrest at the head of Corotoman to son George Heale for use of son Nicholas Heale, but if he die, to child, be male or female, my wife is now with, and if he to die Son George Heale is to have the quarter.
2 CONC   Executor:  Son George Heale.  Overseers:  Mr. Robert Carter and my son-in-law Mr. William Ball.  Witness:  Jas. (sic. Query "Jos." in original) Ball, James Innis, Wm. Ball.  Administration to Arthur Bailey, Esquire, attorney for
2 CONC  son George Heale, now in Virginia, executor, as to effects in Great Britain and Ireland.  Lane, 58
2 CONT (This name is more generally spelt Heale.  This will was also proved in Lancaster County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT HEALE, Geo. Inv. & Division 11 Mar. 1702
2 CONT Inventory returned by Madam Heale.
2 CONT Division:  Mrs. Heale, Mr. George Heale, Mr. John Heale, Mr. Joseph Heale.
2 CONT Will Book 10, p.228
2 CONT
2 CONT HEALE, George Inv. Rec. 14 Feb 1710
2 CONT Estate delivered to Mrs. Ellen Opie, Elizabeth Heale, Sarah Heale, John and Joseph Heale for the use of Wm. Heale as their part of the estate W.B. 10, p. 71
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate of Mrs. Ellen Heale, dec., divided in 4 parts and delivered to Mrs. Ellen Opie, Mrs. Eliz. Heale, Mrs. Sarah Heale, Mr. John Heale and Jos. Heale for the use of Mr. Will Heale. 5 Jan 1710 W.B. 10, p. 78
