1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Nicholas HALE was born in Jan 1663 in Lancaster, Lancaster, Virginia. He died on 13 May 1737 in Lancaster, Lancaster, Virginia. George married Catherine CHINN on 29 Aug 1701 in Lancaster, Lancaster, Virginia
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine CHINN was born on 7 Jun 1686 in Morattico Creek, Lancaster, Virginia. She died  25 Sep 1720, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine married George Heale, Jr. on 29 Aug 1701 in Lancaster, Lancaster, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I29530&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * HEALE, George. 3 Sept. 1736. Rec. 13 May 1737.
2 CONT * Name of wife not given.
2 CONT * Sons: None mentioned.
2 CONT * Daus: Elizabeth Davenport, Sarah Heale land in Northumberland in Cherry Point; Catherine Heale, plantation on which I now live.
2 CONT * Son-in- law: Lindsey Opie.
2 CONT * Brothers: Joseph, and John Heal.
2 CONT * Other legatee, Christopher Dominick Jackson, Surgeon in Westmoreland Co. to be paid for his attendance on me.
2 CONT * Benjamin Neale.
2 CONT * Exors: Brothers, John and James.
2 CONT * Wits: Chris. D. Jackson, Wm. Mitchell and Benjamin Neal. W.B. 13, p. 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1695-1699 Lancaster County Order Book 4; [Antient Press]; pg 33
2 CONT Lancaster County Court 12th of January 1697/98
2 CONT - A Probate of the Last Will and Testament of Mr. GEORGE HEALE deced is granted to Mr. GEORGE HEALE, JUNR. his Executor and an Inventory thereof is to he returned to ye next Court
2 CONT ===
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * HEALE, Geo. & Judith. Bond between Geo. Heale & Judith Heale, widow. Rec. 12 Nov. 1736.
2 CONT * William Heale, Jr., decd., only son of George Heale did sometime before his death intermarry with Judith Heale, daughter & co- heir of John Swan, of Parish of Christ Church, dec. W.B. 13, p. 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Heale Family. (1909). The William and Mary Quarterly, 17(4), 296-299. doi:1. Retrieved from http://www.jstor.org/stable/1915539 doi:1 !2 Feb 1698:  Mentioned in father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT !14 Nov 1716:  Att a Court held for Lancaster County, the 14th day of November Anno Dom: 1716.  PRESENT Capt. Henry ffleett, Mr. Thomas Carter, Mr. John Turberville, Richard Chichester Esqr Justices, Major William Ball, Capt. Geor
2 CONC ge Heale, Mr. Thomas Lee.  The County of Lancaster being indebted the sum of six thousand pounds of tobaco do order that a levy of five pounds and three quarters of a pound of tobacco by the poll be collected by Capt Richard Ball 
2 CONC Sheriff of this County off and from every tithable person in this County and that he pay the same to the severall Creditors hereafter named, viz To the Honrble Robert Carter Esq. for keeping the ferry 1400; To Mrs. Barbara Tayloe 
2 CONC 1000; To Wm Dare Attrny for the King 1000; To Mrs Martha Howard for water, candles and cleaning the Court House 800; To the Sheriff for extraordinary service 500; To Mr John Turberville for Coroners Enquiry 133.  Tithables in Lanc
2 CONC aster Co., 1716, William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine, Vo. 21, No. 2. (Oct., 1912), pp. 106-112. !24 May 1727:  David Ball & Ellen Heale, daughter of George Heale, who consents to dau's marriage.  Marriage Bonds 
2 CONC in Lancaster County.   William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine, Vol. 12, No. 2  (Oct., 1903), pp. 98.
2 CONT
2 CONT !9 Feb 1725:  Mentioned in Ann Chinn  Chichester's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT !13 May 1737:  George Heale in Lancaster Co, VA:  Deeds, Etc., No. 13, 1736-1743 (Reel 4)     p. 45-48. Will pro. 13 May 1737.     p. 58-62. Inv. rec. 9 Sept. 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT !13 May 1737:  Heale, George.  3 Sept 1736.  Rec 13 May 1737.  Name of wife not given.  Sons:  None mentioned.  Daus:  Elizabeth Davenport, Sarah Heale land in Northumberland in Cherry Point; Catherine Heale, plantation on which I
2 CONC  now live.  Son-in-Law:  Lindsey Opie.  Brothers:  Joseph and John Heal.  Other legatee, Christopher Dominick Jackson, Surgeon in Westmoreland Co., to be paid for his attendance on me.  Benjamin Neale.  Exors:  Brothers, John and 
2 CONC James.  Wits: ; Chris. D. Jackson, Wm. MItchell and Benjamin Neal.  W. B. 13, p. 45.  Ida J. Lee, Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800, The Dietz Press, Inc., Richmond, VA, 1959.
2 CONT
2 CONT !13 Jan 1738:  Heale, John.  27 Nov. 1737.  Rec. 13 Jan. 1738.  Legatees:  Sister, Mrs. Hanah Ball and her children.  Brother Capt. George Heale's children; brother William Heale's daughter, Betty.  Cousins:  Roadham Kenner and hi
2 CONC s sister.  Nephew:  George Heale son of my brother, William Heale, dec'd.  Brother:  Joseph Heale.  Others:  Henry Jenkins, Joseph Carter, John Rogers, William Stamps.  Exoprs:  George Heale, and Joh rogers.  Wits:  William Ball, 
2 CONC Jr., James Bailey, Joseph Carter, Gavin Lawry.  W. B. 13, p. 74.  Ida J. Lee, Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800, The Dietz Press, Inc., Richmond, VA, 1959.
2 CONT
2 CONT !15 Jul 1763:  Opie, Lindsey.  14 June 1763.  Rec. 15 July 1763.  Deed between Lindsey Opie of Northumberland Co., and Elizabeth his wife and Andrew Robertson of Lancaster Co., physician, for 105 lbs. current money land in Lancast
2 CONC er containing 103 1/2 acres being part of a tract devised by last will and testament of George Heale, gent., of Lancaster Co. bearing date 13 Dec 1697, to son Joseph, remainder to his son John, both of whom died without issue.  Th
2 CONC e 1st tract descended to Elizabeth, Sarah, Anne, & Catherine, dauthers and coheirs of George, eldest son of sd. Geo. Heale, in Fee simple but being equally divided the above mentioned part descended to Lindsey Opie heir at law of 
2 CONC sd. Sarah except 1/3 part which Mrs. Hannah Crump holds as her dower during her natural life.  W. B. 17, p. 11.  Ida J. Lee, Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800, The Dietz Press, Inc., Richmond, VA, 1959.* Refere
