2 CONT John Haile, son of George and Ellen Haile, was born about 1678 and died 1737 unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - ABSTRACTS LANCASTER CO., VA WILLS - 1653-1800 by Ida J. Lee, p. 111
2 CONT Will of John Heale - made 27 Nov 1737 - Recorded 13 Jan. 1738
2 CONT Legatees:  Sister, Mrs. Hanah Ball and her children; brother Capt. George Heale's children; brother, William Heale's daughter, Betty.  Cousins:  Roadham Kenner and his sister; Nephew, George Heale, son of my brother, William Heale
2 CONC , dec'd.  Brother, Joseph Heale; Others - Henry Jenkins, Joseph Carter, John Rogers, William Stamps.
2 CONT Exors: George Heale and John Rogers.
2 CONT Wits:  William Ball, Jr., James Bailey, Joseph Carter and Gavin Lawry.
2 CONT W.B. 13, p. 74
2 CONT
2 CONT Ibid, p. 169
2 CONT Opie, Lindsey states that last will and testament of George Heale, gent., of Lancaster Co. bearing date 13 Dec. 1697, to son Joseph, remainder to his son, John, both of whom died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - WILLIAM & MARY QUARTERLY - HEALE FAMILY, p. 297
2 CONT John Heale made his will in Jan. 13, 1737-38 and it was proved in Lancaster Co. Jan. 13, 1737-38.  He had no issue and distributed his large estate of negroes, land and cattle among his relatives, giving by far the most to his nep
2 CONC hew, George Heale, son of William Heale, Sr.
