1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Col. Abraham Barnes
2 CONT * Gender:	Male
2 CONT * Birth:	before 1694 - Northumberland, Province of Virginia, Colonial America
2 CONT * Death:	January 13, 1778 - Leonardtown, St. Mary's County, Maryland, United States 
2 CONT * Parents: Thomas Barnes of Kent Island and Jane Wilkins
2 CONT * Spouse: Mary King - married Abt 1730, St. Mary's County, Maryland 
2 CONT * Spouse: Elizabeth Rousby - married between 1740 and 1742, St. Mary's County, Maryland 
2 CONT * Spouse: Sarah Ball - married Aft 14 Aug 1744, Richmond County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SONS: 
2 CONT # John Barnes (ca.1743-1800); 
2 CONT # Richard Barnes (?-1804).
2 CONT
2 CONT DAUGHTER:
2 CONT #Mary King, who married Thomson Mason (1733-1785), of Virginia, a lawyer and the brother of George Mason (1725-1792), of "Gunston Hall,"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Abraham Barnes was born in either Richmond County, or Westmoreland Co.,, VA.. According to a deed filed in Westmoreland County, VA in 1744, he was the son and heir of Thomas Barnes, deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in the will of his brother, Richard Barnes: Richmond County, Virginia Will Book 6, 1753-1767p.212 - Richard BARNES, Lun.Par., will; 15 Jul 1754, 2 Mar 1761 
2 CONT
2 CONT >dear bro. and friends Maj. Abraham BARNES and his two sons, John and Richard ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=BZFEAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA287&lpg=PA287&dq=Richard+Barnes,+of+York+County&source=bl&ots=EZhLevq4fT&sig=YTHRb4ofXfKF3gK-8S-hUiS14o0&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjqucWImeLdAhVnCDQIHV8IDD0Q6AEwEXoECAMQAQ#v=onepage
2 CONC &q&f=true Page 287] of Dixie: A Monthly Magazine, Volumes 2-3. “Maryland Delegates to the Albany Congress”
2 CONT
2 CONT >He is the Abraham Barnes, as seems most likely, who, sometime after 1743, married Sarah Ball, widow of Dennis McCarty, also a vestryman of Truro Parish. There was a [https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Barnes-of-York-County/60000
2 CONC 00082764074486 Richard Barnes] of York County, Virginia, in the seventeenth century (his widow married in 1675) who may have been of the same family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in the will of his brother, Thomas Barnes: WILLS OF Westmoreland County, Virginia 1654--1800 BY AUGUSTA B. FOTHERGILL APPEALS PRESS 1925 BARNES, THOMAS, 28 Nov. 1728; 29 Jan. 1728/9.
2 CONT
2 CONT >I give to my Loving Brother, ABRAM BARNES, ten thousand pounds of tobacco together with my two Servant men as namely THOMAS CHITLEE & JOHN WALTER & my Horse called Maryland;
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ADDITIONAL COMMENTS: In 1764 Abraham gave his son John Barnes (ca. 1743-1800) enough goods to go into trade. By 1773 John was deeply in debt, caused, according to Abraham, by his being obstinate and rejecting all his father's advi
2 CONC ce. Consequently, Barnes left all of his estate to his other son Richard Barnes (?-l 804).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links 
2 CONT # Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Barnes-3874 WikiTree Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 20 2020, 0:13:06 UTC''
2 CONT # Reference: [https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I118064&tree=tree1 TNG Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 1 2021, 16:43:59 UTC''
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I118064&tree=Tree1
2 CONT #  "Biography of Abraham Barnes": p 114 in Papenfuse, Edward C. et. al. ''A Biographical Dictionary of the Maryland Legislature, 1635-1789.'' (Johns Hopkins University Press: Baltimore, 1979) [http://aomol.msa.maryland.gov/000001/
2 CONC 000426/html/am426--114.html Maryland Archives Online]
