2 CONT LEONARD HOWSON 1704 WILL (INTERPRETATION) 1704 , St Stephens Parish, Northumberland, Virginia Colony 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen December  y 13 Day 1704 I Leonard Howson of St Stephens Parish in the County of Northumberland, Colony of Virginia being sick and weak of body but of perfect memory, remembrance,  grateful to Almighty God f
2 CONC or his . . . . . . . . y Last Will and Testament in form and in manner . . . . my soul unto God that labors as redeemer . . . . for my sins and offenses.  My body I commit to the Earth from whence it was taken . . .   at the direc
2 CONC tion of my Exor hereafter nominated Worldly Estates that God has pleased to endow us to hold I give as follows . . . First, I desire that my daughter in law Mary Nutt may be paid her portion left to her by her father and mother ou
2 CONC t of my estate proportionally as by judicable will approval.  The remaining part of my household Goods except what my executor . . . may think  . . . to  . . . my child I desire may be sold at an auction for ready funds to pay my 
2 CONC debts and my whole crop of tobacco . . . to be freighted . . . for London or Bristol and be . . . that my Aunt Webb may keep my child for so long as they shall think fit this said Aunt Webb should have a board maintenance out of m
2 CONC y estate for as long as they shall live but if this said Aunt Webb should C. . . to die in the minority of my child I . . .  live with my Brother John Howson or whosoever they may think fit to . . . her to for her Education.  I . 
2 CONC . . give unto  Mary Nutt one small . . . Ring of Gold . . . I give unto Elizabeth Brereton two Gold Rings th (faded) . . . a small seals ring (faded containing her) Grandfather Breretons Coat of Arms  . . . an (portions not readab
2 CONC le )Emerald ring and silver bookend. . . I give unto David Williams my . . . for my broad cloth coat  . . . I give unto my brother John Howson a mourning ring of gold of twenty shillings price . . . I give and bequeath unto Richar
2 CONC d Wright a mourning ring of twenty shillings price . . . all of my (partials) of land which I later purchased from . . . I give and bequeath unto my daughter Hannah Howson forever  lawfully begotten out of her body but if my daugh
2 CONC ter Hannah Howson should . . . lawfully begotten out of her body then all . . . portions of land which I . . . to her bequeathed, I give unto my Cousin Leonard Howson . . . to my brother John Howson to be the . . . all the rest of
2 CONC  my Estate already not bequeathed both real and personal now belonging to me by eany manor of . . . whatsoever I do give and bequeath unto my Daughter Hannan Howson and to her . . . for ever also I desire that others may be a Good
2 CONC  Hor. . . Kept and maintained on the Plantation I have bequeathed to my Daughter Hannah Howson . . . possibly a Good Orchard of Apples . . . plants of Thorson etc. to be kept under good and sufficient . . . and lastly I Authorize 
2 CONC and appoint my Brother John Howson and Richard Wright Execo  in . . . my Last Will and Testament but if any of my Executors should . . . /s/ Signed and Sealed in   }Leonard Howson Seal. . . of Richard Corbrill, Edward CorbrillThe 
2 CONC mark of David William(three witnesses)   February 25   1705  This Will proved in Northumberland County Court . . . 
2 CONT
