1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah, daughter of Lieut-Col. John Walker, Esq., of Gloucester County, and Sarah, his wife, widow of Lieut. Colonel Henry Fleete, Lancaster county, Va., married Edwin CONWAY Jr.,  son of Edwin CONWAY Sr. and Martha
2 CONC  ELTONHEAD in Old Rappahannock, Virginia. (Edwin CONWAY Jr. was born about 1644 in Virginia, British Colonies and died in Aug 1698 in Richmond Co., Virginia.)  His first wife; he married Elizabeth Thompson in 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT While in England, Fleete married Sarah Burden, a widow and brought her to Virginia. They had one son, Henry Fleete." (p.66) He left his widow so well provided for that she could twice remarry respectably, first Col. John Walker, a
2 CONC  member of the King's Council and later, Dr. John Stone. She could also send for her daughter in England, and bequeath young Henry (not yet of age) a deed of gift to all his father's lands. Even after remarriage she always signed 
2 CONC her name on legal documents as "Widow Fleete". (pp.72-3)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Adventurers of Purse and Person" Vol. 1, (p.972) has more: "Rather late in life Henry Fleete married a widow, Sarah ( ) Burden, who had a young daughter Mary Burden. Sarah married third, bef 28 Oct 1661, Col. John Walker of Glouc
2 CONC ester County (died 1668/9) and had two daughters by him, Sarah Walker and Hester Walker, and married fourth, by 2 Nov 1672, Col John Stone, by whom she has no children. As Sarah Walker she left a will, 28 Jan 1668/9 - 29 Dec 1679.
2 CONC " A footnote says: She named her son Henry, daughters Mary Burden,Sarah Walker and Hester Walker and Colonel Walker's six daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From  [http://books.google.com/books?id=SJcsAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA225&ots=z5H5Ubo51G&dq=Edwin%20conway%201642&pg=PA231#v=onepage&q=Edwin%20conway%201642&f=false Virginia Genealogies:] A Genealogy of the Glassell Family of Scotland and Vi
2 CONC rginia : Also of the Families of Ball, Brown, Bryan, Conway, Daniel, Ewell, Holladay, Lewis, Littlepage, Moncure, Peyton, Robinson, Scott, Taylor, Wallace, and Others, of Virginia and Maryland (Google eBook) Horace Edwin Hayden E.
2 CONC B. Yordy, printer, 1891 - Virginia - 759 pages.  Page 231:
2 CONT
2 CONT EDWIN2 CONWAY (Edwin1), "of the County of Lancaster, Gent," b. pro. Eng. cir. 1640-4; d. Aug., 1698; will dat. Mar. 19, 1698; pro. Richmond county, Sep. 7, 1698.* 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 
2 CONT # (I.) cir. 1675-80, Sarah Fleete, dau. of Lieut. Colonel Henry Fleete, Lancaster county, VA
2 CONT # (II.) cir. 1695, Elizabeth Thompson,! pro. of Lanc'r county. These marriages do not appear among the Lancaster marriage bonds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, first marriage: 
2 CONT # + 4. i- Edwin,' b. —, I681-2; d. Oct. 3, 1763; m. (I.) —, 1704, Anne Ball; (II.) —, Ann Hack.
2 CONT # 5. ii. Mary, b. Feb. 16, 16S6; d. Sep. 15, 1730, le 44; m. (L) Nov. II, 1703, John Dangerfield; (II.) Apr. 16, 1707, Major James Ball (ball 8, p. 63.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, second marriage: 
2 CONT # -(- 6. iii. Francis, b. —, 1697; d. —; m. —, 1720, Rebecca Catlett. 
2 CONT # 7. iv. Posthumous child, b. 1698-9.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1695, before his 2d mar., Mr. Conway, like,Col. Joseph Ball (p. 57), conveyed his estate in part to his children by his first wife, and moved to Richmond Co. His eldest child, Edwin, was then only 14 years old. It is pro. that 
2 CONC the land conveyed came to him by his first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the second wife nothing is known beyond'her name. Mr. Warner, Clerk of Rich'd Co., writes me (1890): '* I find nothing touching this 2d mar. No Thompson seems to have lived in this Co. at that time. The Edwin Conway that owned 
2 CONC large tracts of land in Rich'd Co. was living in Christ Ch. Parish 1681 and 1694." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Conway was Surveyor of Lanc'r Co., 1679-80. Like Mary Johnson Ball, we must measure Elizabeth Thompson Conway by her posterity. The one gave to the world a Washington, the other a Madison.
2 CONT
