2 CONT EDWIN2 CONWAY (Edwin1), "of the County of Lancaster, Gent," b. pro. Eng. cir. 1640-4; d. Aug., 1698; will dat. Mar. 19, 1698; pro. Richmond county, Sep. 7, 1698.* 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 
2 CONT # (I.) cir. 1675-80, Sarah Fleete, dau. of Lieut. Colonel Henry Fleete, Lancaster county, Va.; [SIC: Sarah Walker, his step daughter]
2 CONT # (II.) cir. 1695, Elizabeth Thompson,! pro. of Lanc'r county. These marriages do not appear among the Lancaster marriage bonds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, first marriage: 
2 CONT # + 4. i- Edwin,' b. —, I681-2; d. Oct. 3, 1763; m. (I.) —, 1704, Anne Ball; (II.) —, Ann Hack.
2 CONT # 5. ii. Mary, b. Feb. 16, 16S6; d. Sep. 15, 1730, le 44; m. (L) Nov. II, 1703, John Dangerfield; (II.) Apr. 16, 1707, Major James Ball (ball 8, p. 63.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, second marriage: 
2 CONT # -(- 6. iii. Francis, b. —, 1697; d. —; m. —, 1720, Rebecca Catlett. 
2 CONT # 7. iv. Posthumous child, b. 1698-9.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1695, before his 2d mar., Mr. Conway, like,Col. Joseph Ball (p. 57), conveyed his estate in part to his children by his first wife, and moved to Richmond Co. His eldest child, Edwin, was then only 14 years old. It is pro. that 
2 CONC the land conveyed came to him by his first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the second wife nothing is known beyond'her name. Mr. Warner, Clerk of Rich'd Co., writes me (1890): '* I find nothing touching this 2d mar. No Thompson seems to have lived in this Co. at that time. The Edwin Conway that owned 
2 CONC large tracts of land in Rich'd Co. was living in Christ Ch. Parish 1681 and 1694." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Conway was Surveyor of Lanc'r Co., 1679-80.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like Mary Johnson Ball, we must measure Elizabeth Thompson Conway by her posterity. The one gave to the world a Washington, the other a Madison.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Edwin Conway 
2 CONT *Birth: 	1653 Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Death: 	1698 King George County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Edwin was related to a number of distinguished colonial families and progenitor of some famous Americans including President James Madison. He was married first to Sarah Walker and then to Elizabeth Thornton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conway's will was recorded in Richmond County (now King George Co.) Virginia in March 1698; it was probated in September 1698. He was returned to Lancaster County for burial beside his first wife Sarah. (By Mark Hale - unfortunate
2 CONC ly this bio has been edited by myself because of instances of copying without my being credited.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses:
2 CONT * Elizabeth Thornton Gibson (1675 - 1733) [NO - Elizabeth Thompson, 2nd wife 
2 CONT *  Sarah Walker Conway (____ - 1690)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Edwin Conway (1681 - 1763)*
2 CONT *  Mary Conway Ball (1686 - 1730)*
2 CONT *  Francis Conway (1696 - 1733)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial :
2 CONT Non-Cemetery Burial Specifically: Buried on private property in Lancaster Co., Virginia
