1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daniel McCarty, only son of Daniel McCarty & Sinah Ball, was born at Fairfax Co., Va., on 5 January 1758. He married Sarah Eilbeck Mason at Fairfax Co., Va., in 1778. Daniel died on 1 March 1801 at Fairfax Co., Va.
2 CONC , at age 43 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.gunstonhall.org/georgemason/mason_family/sarah_eilbeck_mason.html Children of George Mason of Gunston Hall]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sarah was the first of the Mason children to marry. At age 18 she wed Daniel McCarty, Jr., the son of a neighbor who lived at Cedar Grove (on Mason's Neck on a point on Pohick Bay). McCarty had served in the Revolutionary War and
2 CONC  taken part in the battles of Brandywine Creek and Germantown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # Sarah Eilbeck Mason b. 11 Dec 1760, d. 11 Sep 1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT # Edgar McCarty d. Apr 1819
2 CONT # Sarah McCarty
2 CONT # Thomson McCarty
2 CONT # Ann Eilbeck McCarty+1
2 CONT # Daniel McCarty III+ b. 5 Jan 1780, d. Jun 1811
2 CONT # George Mason McCarty b. 1786, d. 7 Aug 1808
2 CONT # William Mason McCarty+ b. 1790, d. 20 Dec 1863
2 CONT # John Mason McCarty+ b. 14 Mar 1795, d. 13 Sep 1852
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=kjESAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA130&ots=LKu3BXErhR&dq=sarah%20masoh%20daniel%20mccarty&pg=PA129#v=onepage&q&f=false page 129] of William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine
2 CONT
2 CONT >Col. Daniel McCarty, son of Daniel and Sinah Ball McCarty, married about 1778 to Ann Mason, daughter of George Mason, author of the famous "Bill of Rights". They had Hon. William Mason McCarty, who represented his district in Con
2 CONC gress for several times, and John McCarty, who killed his cousin Gen. Stephens Mason in a duel in 1818. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From [https://fxgs.org/cemeteryRecords.php?cid=179 McCARTY FAMILY CEMETERY at CEDAR GROVE]
2 CONT
2 CONT The three gravestones recorded by Doctor MillerÃÂ now stand in the upper churchyard at Pohick ChurchÃÂ (q.v.), in front of the vestry house.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sacred
2 CONT * to the memory of
2 CONT * Daniel McCarty
2 CONT * who departed this life
2 CONT * March 1st 1801
2 CONT * in the 43d year of his age.
2 CONT * He was at 16 years of age a Lieut.
2 CONT * in the Revolutionary war and was
2 CONT * in the battles of Brandywine,
2 CONT * and Germantown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
