1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =William Lowry Gent. of Essex County=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Big Ydna Results, I-BY19889, - Scotch Irish'''
2 CONT * Son of William Lowry and Frances Purifoy
2 CONT
2 CONT * William Lowry Jr. inherited land in Essex and King and Queen Counties, a lot in Hampton Town, twenty head of cattle, money, and tobacco.
2 CONT *1704: MR. WILLIAM LOWRY  - 1044 acres Essex County, Virginia.  "Cavaliers and Pioneers-Abstracts of Virginia   Patents and Grants, Nugent Vol 3, 1695-1732.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001097467257&photo_id=6000000101161818854&position=0 '''Source''' Hoskins of Virginia and related families of Hundley, Ware, Roy, Garnett, Waring, Bird, Buckner,
2 CONC  Dunbar, Trible, Booker, Aylett - West Virginia Ancestry Records - WVancestry.com]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001097467257?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000101161818854&position=0 '''(1) Mary MOTTRAM Ball'''] on 15 June, 1725 in Virginia USA - Second Marriage of Mary MOTTRAM Ball 
2 CONC to William LOWRY on a deed from William Lowry and Mary, his wife, deed to Richard BALL of Lancaster for 400 acres, part of a patent for 122 acres granted to Colonel John MOTTRAM 19 October 1653 and known by the name of "Black Poin
2 CONC t", situated in Northumberland county and to be laid off next and adjoining the land belonging to Colonel Peter HACK for the use and behalf of Joseph BALL and  William BALL, sons of the said Mary Lowry, late widow and relict of Jo
2 CONC seph BALL, deceased. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Rachell Moore''' daughter of John Moore, of Elizabeth City and Elizabeth Merritt. There has been some confusion on who married William Lowry from Essex County, Virginia, (There is also some confusion here) Listed in 
2 CONC The Tabb Family, The William and Mary Quarterly, Vol. 7, July 1, 1898. William Lowry married probably twice, as John Moore in his will (dated 1715) Names Uncle William Lowry & Aunt Rachel Lowry and Cozen John Lowry. I think we fou
2 CONC nd the answer and why their is confusion, in this section they had the two William father & son mixed up and thought the Father William also married Rachel Moore but the birth and death dates put her to be the wife of the son Will
2 CONC iam Lowry III, unless we find other documents that show otherwise. I have put her as being the wife of William Lowry Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (3) '''Rebecca Unknown ''' married in Virginia, United States.  The third marriage of William Lowry was documented in Henings Statues for time; and by his 1750 Essex County Will: Rebecca Lowry, wife of William LOWRY. It
2 CONC  doesn’t look like they had any children together due to Mary Mottrom and this Act states she married the afore mentioned Captain Joseph Ball and William Lowry, Gent. of Essex County and had five children by each spouse all of who
2 CONC m were living in 1732. (see Hening's Statutes, vol. 4, p. 379 and Hoskins of Virginia and related families of Hundley, Ware, Roy, Garnett, Waring, Bird, Buckner, Dunbar, Trible, Booker, Aylett - West Virginia Ancestry Records - WV
2 CONC ancestry.com)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with MARY MOTTRAM BALL=
2 CONT
2 CONT William Lowry Jr. first shows up in Essex County records in 1706 when he had land cleared. An Act of the House of Burgesses in May 1732 regarding land in Essex County (British Colonial Office 5/1389 , ff. 70-71) proves that Captai
2 CONC n Joseph Ball married Mary Mottrom, the only child of Spencer Mottrom, Gent. (1670-1700 ) of Northumberland County, and he was the only son and heir of John Mottrom and his wife nee Hannah Fox whose father David Fox of Lancaster C
2 CONC ounty made her a deed poll on 11 November 1662 for 800 acres on Piscataway Creek which fell into Essex County. This land descended to the afore mentioned Mary Mottrom and this Act states she married the afore mentioned Captain Jos
2 CONC eph Ball and William Lowry, Gent. of Essex County and had five children by each spouse all of whom were living in 1732. The Registers of North Farnham Parish 1663-1814 and Lunenburg Parish 1783-1800, Richmond County, VA, compiled 
2 CONC and published by George Harrison Sanford King (Fredericksburg, VA , 1966), p. 87:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Robert Lowry of Edgecombe County, ''' born, 1705 in Essex County, Province of Virginia, Colonial America, Married Ann Lewis in 1727 in Essex, Virginia, Colonial America.  He is listed in his father’s Will.
2 CONT * '''William Lowry,''' born In 1708 in Virginia, Colonial America.
2 CONT * '''John Lowry,''' 1718-1758, married, Sarah Rust before February 19, 1754 in Northern Neck of Virginia Colonial America. He is listed in his father’s Will.  He is listed in his father’s Will.
2 CONT *  '''Francis Lowry,''' born around 1726 in Essex County Virginia. Frances LOWRY, daughter of Mary MOTTRAM, who married William LOWRY was identified in the 1742 Will of her grandmother, Sarah YOUNG (1) MOTTRAM (2) HOWSON and (3) B
2 CONC ALL. She is listed in her father’s Will as a minor.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children probably with Rebecca Unknown=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Richard Lowry;''' married Ann Unknown.  Listed in his father’s Will. 
2 CONT * '''Thomas Lowry,''' He is listed in his father’s Will.
2 CONT * '''Martha Purefoy Lowry;''' married William Richards.  She is listed in her father’s Will.
2 CONT * '''Sally Lowry''' Birth: July 21, 1745 in Essex, Virginia, USA.  She is listed in her father’s Will.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000185620299831 William Lowry's Complete Will from Southfarnham Parish, Essex County, Province of Virginia, Colonial America, Will Date: 31 May 1750, Probate Date: 8 May 1750.]
2 CONT
2 CONT =NOTE:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * In the 1724 Will of William LOWRY, Sr, his son William LOWRY is named. Two daughters-in-law are named as Mrs. Jane Lowry and Mrs. Mary Lowry in this will. As several other sources document that Mrs. Jane Lowry was the former Jan
2 CONC e NUTTING who married John LOWRY, Sr, it therefore follows that Mrs. Mary Lowry was the wife of William LOWRY. Further, the 1724 Will bequeathed land in Essex and in King and Queen Counties to William LOWRY whereas John LOWRY stay
2 CONC ed in Elizabeth City County where he served, both as a justice and as a surveyor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001097467257?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000082715112050&position=0 Legislative Journals of the Council of Colonial Virginia..., Volume 2, Regarding 2nd Wife Mary Mottram]
2 CONT
2 CONT *1732  House of Burgesses ACT which clearly identified Mary MOTTRAM as the 1st wife of Colonel Joseph BALL - An Act of the House of Burgesses in May 1732 regarding land in Essex County (British Colonial Office 5/1389 , ff. 70-71) 
2 CONC proves that Captain Joseph Ball married Mary Mottrom, the only child of Spencer Mottrom, Gent. (1670-1700 ) of Northumberland County, and he was the only son and heir of John Mottrom and his wife nee Hannah Fox whose father David 
2 CONC Fox of Lancaster County made her a deed poll on 11 November 1662 for 800 acres on Piscataway Creek which fell into Essex County. This land descended to the afore mentioned Mary Mottrom and this Act states she married the afore men
2 CONC tioned Captain Joseph Ball and William Lowry, Gent. of Essex County and had five children by each spouse all of whom were living in 1732. The Registers of North Farnham Parish 1663-1814 and Lunenburg Parish 1783-1800, Richmond Cou
2 CONC nty, VA, compiled and published by George Harrison Sanford King (Fredericksburg, VA , 1966), p. 87:
2 CONT
2 CONT * William LOWRY - (2)  Marriage of Mary MOTTRAM Ball before 15 June , 1725 15 June 1725 Deed from William Lowry and Mary, his wife, deed to Richard BALL of Lancaster for 400 acres, part of a patent for 122 acres granted to Colonel
2 CONC  John MOTTRAM 19 October 1653 and known by the name of "Black Point", situated in Northumberland county and to be laid off next and adjoining the land belonging to Colonel Peter HACK for the use and behalf of Joseph BALL and  Will
2 CONC iam BALL, sons of the said Mary Lowry, late widow and relict of Joseph BALL, deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rebecca Lowry, wife of William LOWRY had 3 minor children in 1750.  '''She is known to have married Wm sometime after 1732 when Wm's 2nd wife, Mary still living, as proved in a land record of that date (see Hening's Statutes, vo
2 CONC l. 4, p. 3
2 CONT
