1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From George Ball, Sr. b. 1683 m. Grace Haynie "Genealogies of Virginia Families" p. 474
2 CONT
2 CONT >The land inherited by Mrs. Sarah Haynie Waddy from her father, Major John Harris, is the famous "Bayview" plantation, given to her daughter Grace Haynie Ball, which has remained in the possession of some of the descendants of Cap
2 CONC t. George and Grace Haynie Ball to this present time. This land was adjacent to the Dameron plantation and, in 178_, George Dameron brought suit against Major Harris over their boundary lines, and a final settlement was made by th
2 CONC e official survey of Capt. John Haynie.
2 CONT
2 CONT >1715, Feb. 17, Mrs. Sarah Haynie acknowledges a deed of indenture for land unto Geo. Ball gent. Order Book, 1713 to 1715, p. 98. Shortly thereafter Sarah Haynie married Francis Waddy for on March 16, 1715, Mr. Francis Waddy and S
2 CONC arah, his wife acknowledge a deed of Indenture of lease for land unto George Ball, gent.
2 CONT
