2 CONT Biography Note:
2 CONT William came to Virginia in the latter part of the 17th century (about 1650) and settled in the part of Rappahannock County that became Richmond County. Later, he inherited his Uncle William's estate.  William was the Sheriff of R
2 CONC appahannock County in 1687. He became one of the first justices of Richmond County. William served as a member of the House of Burgesses from Richmond in 1700-02 and in 1706. In 1704, as the colonel and commander of the Richmond m
2 CONC ilitia, William subdued an uprising of the local Indians.
2 CONT
