2 CONC Fanquier County, Virginia. He also owned land in King George and Culpeper counties. John was one of the early vestrymen in St. Mark's Parish in Culpeper County.  Event: Military Unknown Revolutionary War - Lieutenant in Virginia C
2 CONC ontinental Line
2 CONT  Father: James HACKLEY  b: Abt 1690 in Rappahannock County, Virginia  Mother: Elizabeth SHIPPEY  b: Abt 1703 in King George County, Virginia John, was one of the early vestrymen in St. Mark's Parish in Culpeper County. John owned 
2 CONC land in both King George and Culpeper counties, and eventually married Judith Ball.  There are several references to Hackleys serving in the Revolutionary War. The most documented case is that of John Hackley, son of John and gran
2 CONC dson of James and Elizabeth Hackley of Summerduck Run. He served as Lieutenant in the Virginia Continental Line, and was an original member of the Society of the Cincinnati in the State of Virginia.(17) In addition, a list of the 
2 CONC men selected by Culpeper County to aid Lafayette and the Continental Army during the war includes the names of Francis, James and Richard Hackley.
