2 CONT
2 CONT * STAFFORD COUNTY VA WILL BOOK O; 1748-1767; THE ANTIENT PRESS p. 371 In Name of God Amen I RAWLEIGH CHINN of Overwharton Parish in County of Stafford being sick but of perfect mind .. do make this my last will & Testament ..
2 CONT * Item I leave to my Daughter BETTY one shilling Sterling. Item I leave to my Son JOHN CHINN one shilling Sterling. Item I leave to my Daughter HANNAH CHINN one shilling Sterling.
2 CONT * Item I leave to my Son RAWLEIGH CHINN one pair of Bellows for his own particular use, and that he shall neither make vast or sale of them & if he should they shall return to John Chinn.
2 CONT * Item I leave to my Son JAMES CHINN all my smiths Tools.
2 CONT * Item I leave to my Daughter ANN CHINN one shilling Sterling.
2 CONT * Item I leave to my Daughter LETTICE CHINN one shilling Sterling. Item I appoint this my well beloved Wife ELIZA. all my whole Executor ..
2 CONT * Presence Seml. Garner, Rawleigh Chinn Jos. White
2 CONT * At Court held for Stafford County 10th March 1760 Will presented proven .. admitted to record .. Certificate granted for obtaining Probate .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
