2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Short Bio ===
2 CONT Birth: 	Oct. 16, 1630 London Greater London, England Death: 	Oct. 22, 1700 Lancaster County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Thomas Carter, son of William Ancell Carter and Jane Myles Carter, was born in London, Middlesex, England, October 16, 1630. He embarked from London for the British colonies in America and settled on land in Lancaster County
2 CONC  in the Colony of Virginia. He spent the rest of his life there on his Barford Plantation where he died October 22, 1700 and was buried. He had two spouses, the first, Mary Anscell Parkhurst and the second, Katherine Dale, daughte
2 CONC r of a British military commander assigned to duty in the colonies. Thomas and his second wife, Katherine, were members of the Church of England and their twelve children are listed in the Capt. Thomas Carter Prayer Book in the po
2 CONC ssession of the Historical Society of Richmond, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Came to Namesond City, Virginia in 1650/ ===
2 CONT Came to Namesond City, Virginia in 1650/52 from London in the "safety". This was about the time that Charles I was beheaded. Thomas appears at 22 years of age as paying tithes on himself and 4 servants. He bought 800 acres in Lanc
2 CONC aster City, on the eastern branch of the Corotoman River from Col. John Carter. He later moved to Lancaster County, Virginia and purchased a large plantation on the Rappahannock River. Thomas Carter Senior served as commissioner o
2 CONC f the City in 1663, Deputy Clerk of City in 1663-65, and as Burgess in 1667. Captain of the Lancaster Militia. A vestryman in Christ Church and Saint Marys White Chapel. A planter and trader. Thomas Carter named his estate in Lanc
2 CONC aster County, Virginia, probably after Great Barford, Bedfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Will Abstract ===
2 CONT CARTER, Thomas. Will. 24 Apl. 1728. Rec. 10 Oct. 1733. Wife Arabella;  sons: Thomas, land where I now live;. Peter, land in King George Co.,  James, Dale, Charles, Edward, Joseph and Daniel.  Gr.sons Jesse Carter and Thos. Carter.
2 CONC   Extrs. Wife and son Peter.  Wits. John Harry and Job Carter.  W.B. 12, p. 279. Source: Ida J. Lee, Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia Wills, 1653-1800 (Richmond, Virginia: The Dietz Press, Inc., 1959), pg. 40
2 CONT
