1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT James Carter was mard ye 3d Octbr 1715 to Hannah Neale daur. to DanI Neale    
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Hannah Carter departed the Life on 9th Octo. 1722 and left a sorriful husband and 4 tender children Tho. DanI Presly & Hannah (this was the first wife of James Carter.( He married Mary Brent, 10 August 1724)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~grayson/family/html/genealogy.html
2 CONT
2 CONT TRANSCRIPTION OF WILL OF JAMES CARTER. STAFFORD COUNTY 1743: Stafford County Will Book M. pp 391-392
2 CONT
2 CONT * "In Name of God Amen I James Carter of Overwharton Parish in County of Stafford being sick but of sound mind .. make this my last will.. I give soul to my mercifull creator.. my body to be buried.
2 CONT * Imps. (after my just debts are honestly paid) I give to my sons JOHN & GEQRGE all that tract of land on the north side of Acquia Creek where I now live to be equally divided between them only that my eldest son JOHN shou'd have 
2 CONC the half on which my dwelling house now stands to them and their heirs but if either or both shu'd die without heirs then I give the reversion of all or either of their shares to my son Hugh and heirs of his body and incase of def
2 CONC ault of such heirs to be equally divided among all my surviving sons.
2 CONT * Item I give to my sons JAMES & WILLIAM my lands in Fairfax County after William Brewster has gott his complement which I sold him out of it to be equally divided between my said sons to them and heirs but if either of them shuld
2 CONC  die without issue I bequeath their reversion of their part thereof to my son GEORGE and his heirs in case of default of such heirs to be equally divided among my surviving sons.
2 CONT * Item I give my son HUGH two negroes Mingo & Sharlott.
2 CONT * Item I give my son CHARLES and his heirs two negroes Sue and Winny and their increase.
2 CONT * Item I give to my daughter ANN and her heirs two negroes great Dick and Hannah with Robin and Dinah with her increase.
2 CONT * Item what negroes I die possessed of not yet willed or bequeathed I leave to my dear and loving WIFE MARY during her widowhood only and after her marrying again or decease to be equally divided among my surviving children.
2 CONT * Item my personal estate I leave to be equally divided among my wife and children or the survivors of them.
2 CONT * Lastly I nominate and appoint my dear and loving wife MARY and Charles Brent Executors of this my last will and testament my son JOHN to be joined with them as soon as he comes of age and I appoint the reverd Mr. John Moncure a 
2 CONC guardian to my children and as a trustee to see this will execute.
2 CONT * Hereby revoking all former wills .. In witness .. set my hands this 23rd day of October 1743,
2 CONT * Presence THOMAS EVES. JAMES CARTER, WM. KNIGHT, JEAN TURNER his mark
2 CONT * At court held for Stafford County March 13.1743. Will presented by Mary Carter and Chas. Brent.. made oath .. proved .. admitted to record .. Certificate granted for obtaining Probate.."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mr. Jno Edwards, Mr. Tho Wilkes and Mrs Edwards standing as God Parents., Ibid, p.9    Owned about 2900 acres of land in Stafford, King George, and Prince William Counties
2 CONT
