1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Bonum, Jr. was sister to Rebecca Bonum Eskridge. Rebecca was married to Col. George Eskridge. Samuel was married to Elizabeth Johnson. Her mother married an unknown Johnson then Joseph Ball, a widower with c
2 CONC hildren of his own, then Capt Hewes. Between them, Mary and Joseph, had one child, Mary Ball Washington, President George Washington's mother. When Mary Hewes passed away, her daughter Mary Ball was left as a ward of Col. Eskridge
2 CONC  until she married Augustine Washington. I've seen references that say Mary Ball met Augustine while visiting her half brother John Johnson. Mary split her time, before her marriage, between Sandy Point (home of her guardian, Col.
2 CONC  Eskridge) and Cherry Point  (home of her half-sister, Elizabeth Johnson Bonum, wife of Samuel Bonum, Jr.)
