1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland
2 CONT Augustine Washington II, son of Augustine Washington, I and his wife Jane Butler was born about 1718, prob. in Westmoreland Co.,VA.  He was often called Austin.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 1st Ann Aylett who had children, William Augustine and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 2nd Jane, granddaughter of Col. Ashton.  
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He lived at Wakefield and died in 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 42
2 CONT To his son Augustine (II), he gave all his lands in Westmoreland, except as otherwise disposed of, together with 25 head of neat cattle, 40 hogs, 20 sheep, "and a negro man named Frank besides those negroes formerly given him by h
2 CONC is mother"; also the 3 young working slaves to be purchased for him out of the first profits of the iron works.  Lawrence and Augustine were to pay half the debts of the testator and to have half of the debts owing to him.
