1 NOTE Dec 22, 2009
2 CONT It was only about nine months ago that I came to the conclusion that Joseph Harwood, 1630s-1681, is not the son of William and Elinor Harwood, (Who aren't Harwood's at all but Hayward's according to the original land patents.), bu
2 CONC t rather the brother of Samuel Hayward of Stafford Co, VA. This position breaks ranks with other Harwood researchers, but when I looked at the original documents it appears to be true.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hayward married Martha Washington who is the great-aunt of George Washington. Samuel Hayward and Martha Washington are second cousins, through her mother Amphillis Hayward or Harwood. The Haywards, were neighbors of John Wa
2 CONC shington, George Washington's immigrant ancestor and great-grandfather. Nicholas Hayward, Sr., and Jr and Samuel Hayward had business dealings with John Washington.
2 CONT Source: Randy Harwood
1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson p. 270
2 CONT Maj. Lawrence Washington born Sept. 1659 at Mattox, Westmoreland Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married on 20 Sept. 1690 Mildred Warner of Warner Hall, Gloucester Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Died 30 March 1697 on Pianketank River Estate, will dated 11 Mar 1698.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawrence Washington was a member of the House of Burgesses in 1685 and High
2 CONT Sheriff in 1692. - Ibid
1 NOTE Captain
1 NOTE Dec 22, 2009
2 CONT It was only about nine months ago that I came to the conclusion that Joseph Harwood, 1630s-1681, is not the son of William and Elinor Harwood, (Who aren't Harwood's at all but Hayward's according to the original land patents.), bu
2 CONC t rather the brother of Samuel Hayward of Stafford Co, VA. This position breaks ranks with other Harwood researchers, but when I looked at the original documents it appears to be true.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hayward married Martha Washington who is the great-aunt of George Washington. Samuel Hayward and Martha Washington are second cousins, through her mother Amphillis Hayward or Harwood. The Haywards, were neighbors of John Wa
2 CONC shington, George Washington's immigrant ancestor and great-grandfather. Nicholas Hayward, Sr., and Jr and Samuel Hayward had business dealings with John Washington.
2 CONT Source: Randy Harwood
