1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 337
2 CONT Mildred, daughter of Maj. Lawrence Washington and wife, Mildred Warner; aunt and godmother to George Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMOIRS by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 270
2 CONT Mildred Washington born 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 337
2 CONT She married 1st Roger Gregory by whom she had 3 daughters, who married 3 Thornton brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT She married 2nd as the 3d and last wife of Col. Henry Willis, founder of Frederickcsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the will of her father she received a 4th of his estate and (or including) 2500 acres of land on Hunting Creek, Stafford Co.,VA now in Fairfax. (now known as Mount Vernon - JMC)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1726 Augustine Washington purchased from his sister Mildred and her husband, Roger Gregory, a large tract up in Stafford (now Fairfax) County, on Hunting Creek, part of which is familiar to us as Mount Vernon.  To this tract in
2 CONC  1735, soon after the death of his young daughter Jane, he moved going up the Potomac by boat.  At Hunting Creek he remained until the latter part of 1738, then moved to the Ferry Farm opposite Fredericksburg. - Ibid p. 8
2 CONT
2 CONT VIRGINIA CO. RECORDS, VOL I, SPOTSYLVANIA CO. 1721-1800 Edited by William Armstrong Crozier, P. 150
2 CONT Deed Book C - 1734-1742
2 CONT Mildred Willis, late Mildred Gregory, now the wife of Henry Willis of Spts. Co., Gent.  By Indenture Jany. 5, 1733.  Between sd. Henry Willis of first part, sd. Mildred of second part, and John Washington of Gloucester Co. of thir
2 CONC d part, reciting a marriage was to be speedily solemnized between sd. Henry and sd. Mildred, etc.; sd. Mildred in persuance of authority reserved by sd. Indenture, etc.; my son, Lewis Willis, etc.; sd. Henry Willis, my husband, et
2 CONC c.; my three daughters, Frances, wife of Francis Thornton, Jr.; Mildred and Elizabeth.  Witnesses:  Augustine Washington, Jno Taliaferro.  Dat. Dec. 15, 1739.  Recd. May 6, 1740.
