2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Fielding Lewis''' (July 7, 1725 – December 7, 1781) was a Colonel during the American Revolutionary War and the brother-in-law of George Washington..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Lewis was born at Warner Hall in Gloucester County, Virginia, the son of John Lewis (1694-1754) and Frances Fielding (c1702-1731). He was the third of seven children..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Lewis married Catharine Washington on October 18, 1746. She was his second cousin, daughter of John Washington and Catharine Whiting...'
2 CONT
2 CONT "...The marriage produced three children. Catharine died on February 19, 1750..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "His second marriage was to another second cousin, Betty Washington, the sister of George Washington, on May 7, 1750. The marriage produced 11 children..."
2 CONT
