1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 55
2 CONT Elizabeth Lewis was born 23 Feb. 1765 in Fredericksburg, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Tombstone gives date of death as 9 April 1830 in Clarke Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE LIBRARY OF VIRGINIA - HENLEY MARRIAGE & OBITUARY DATABASE - Lynchburg Virginian, Lynchburg, VA (1829) 
2 CONT Died - At "Audley" in Frederick Co. on April 9, Mrs. Betty Carter, relict of the late Charles Carter and niece of the late Gen. George Washington in her 65th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 55
2 CONT Betty Lewis Carter, is buried at "North Hill" in Clarke Co.,VA. near "Springbury" where her brother, Major George Lewis had lived for some years.  North Hill is just southwest of the highway near the NW end of the bridge over the 
2 CONC Shenandoah River at Castleman's Ferry.  The old graveyard is half-way up the hill in a small grove of ash and walnut trees.  Mrs. Carter's is the only one with an inscribed marker, a large slab of marble broken through the middle.
2 CONC   Some years ago it was fixed on a brick base by the Fort Loudoun Chapter, D.A.R.  On the slab her virtues are commemorated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone:
2 CONT IN MEMORY OF
2 CONT Mrs. Betty Carter
2 CONT relict of the late Charles Carter, Esqr.
2 CONT She was born in the town of Fredericksburg
2 CONT on the 22nd day of February, 1765
2 CONT and departed this life on Good Friday
2 CONT the 9th of April, 1830
2 CONT Aged 65 years
2 CONT She was the daughter of Mrs. Betty Lewis,
2 CONT only sister of Genl. George Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Also in memory of
2 CONT Mrs. Sarah C. Peyton
2 CONT Elizabeth W. and Edward Carter,
2 CONT Children of Charles & Betty Carter,
2 CONT interred in this place.
