2 _MARNM Washington
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1724
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1755
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT >Col. Champe of Lamb's Creek had six daughters, all noted beauties. Elizabeth married Judge Plemlng; Jane married Col. Samuel Washington; Mary married Col. Lewis Willis; Lucy married Austin Brockenbrough; Ann married Col. John Tal
2 CONC laferro; and Sarah married Col. Edward Carter of "Bleinheim," Albemarle County. See FTM, CD186, p. 742.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=psCawzVzhAkC&lpg=PA143&ots=ddajyBxwLZ&dq=Jane%20champe%20Washington&pg=PA143#v=onepage&q&f=false page 143] of "The Washingtons and Their Homes By John W. Wayland"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Jane Champe, 1st wife of Samuel Washington, daughter of Col. John Champe of King George County, Virginia.  If they had any children they died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Mount Vernon Ladies' Association, non-profit organization founded in 1853 by Ann Pamela Cunningham.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Stella Pickett Hardy, "Colonial Families of the Southern States of America: A History and Genealogy of Colonial Families Who Settled in the Colonies prior to the Revolution," Baltimore, MD: Southern Book Co., 1958.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=5MFJAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA553&ots=6D0mn2Z6BO&dq=Jane%20champe%20Washington&pg=PA550#v=onepage&q=Jane%20champe%20Washington&f=false page 553] of The Writings of George Washington: Life of Washington By
2 CONC  George Washington, Jared Sparks
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=pE4SAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA28&ots=feVDc-8DbP&dq=Jane%20champe%20Washington&pg=PA28#v=onepage&q=Jane%20champe%20Washington&f=false page 28] of Touring Historyland: The Authentic Guide Book of Historic .
2 CONC .., Volume 186
2 CONT >"WOODSTOCK occupies a sort of promontory, the Potomac on one side, the lowlands of Upper Machodoc Creek on the other. It is one of the fine modern estates of King George, a home of the Grymes family, having been the home of Custi
2 CONC s Grymes, son of Benjamin Fitzhugh Grymes, second son of Benjamin and Elizabeth (Fitzhugh) Grymes of Eagle's Nest (27). Benjamin F. Grymes married a sister of Lucy Brockenbrough Pratt, wife of Daingerfield Lewis of Marmion (25), d
2 CONC aughters of Jane (Brockenbrough) Pratt, daughter of Austin Brockenbrough, who married Lucy Champe, daughter of Colonel John Champe of Lamb's Creek and sister of Jane Champe, first wife of General Washington's brother, Samuel Washi
2 CONC ngton (9). Woodstock descended to Custis Grymes' son, Benjamin Custis Grymes (1861-1930) ...."
