1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 334
2 CONT Lawrence Augustine, born 1768?, son of Col. Samuel Washington and his 4th wife Anne Steptoe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Education directed by General Washington, his uncle. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Mary Dorcas Wood in Frederick Co.,VA Nov. 6, 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived for some time at Hawthorn, part of the Glen Burnie estate at Winchester; removed in 1811 to the Ohio Valley. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died near Wheeling, Feb. 15, 1824, in the 56th year of his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage & Death Notices from the GENIUS OF LIBERTY 1817-1843, p. 9
2 CONT Died on the 15th ult., Laurance Augustine Washington at his residence in Wheeling, age 50 years.
