2 CONT # [http://www.politicalfamilytree.com/samples%20content/members/PDF%20Content/Washington-VA-2.pdf Partial Genealogy of the Washingtons Part ll (of Virginia and Maryland)] PDF file
2 CONT #Corbin Washington (1765–c.1799) lived with his wife Hannah Lee Washington (1765–c.1801) at Selby in Fairfax County. His mother, '''Hannah Bushrod Washington,''' who in 1756 married GW’s brother John Augustine Washington (1736–178
2 CONC 7), was the grandmother of 17–year-old Augustine Washington, son of William Augustine Washington (1757–1810) and Hannah’s daughter Jane (Jenny) Washington. William Augustine Washington, son of GW’s half brother Augustine, lived at
2 CONC  Haywood in Westmoreland County. William Augustine Washington’s two sons, Augustine and Bushrod Washington, Jr. (1785–1830), by his first wife Jane, had been attending school in Andover, Massachusetts. Young Augustine died before 
2 CONC the end of the year.
2 CONT #https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Washington/06-01-02-0365 Note: The annotations to this document, and any other modern 
2 CONT #http://www.westfordlegacy.com/article/15
2 CONT # “[Diary entry: 22 May 1769],” Founders Online, National Archives, https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Washington/01-02-02-0004-0013-0022. [Original source: The Diaries of George Washington, vol. 2, 14 January 1766 – 31 Decem
2 CONC ber 1770, ed. Donald Jackson. Charlottesville: University Press of Virginia, 1976, pp. 153–154.].  Mildred Washington Bushrod (c.1720–1785), of Gloucester County, a cousin of GW, was the sister of Warner Washington, Sr., and the w
2 CONC idow of John Bushrod (d. 1760) of Westmoreland County. She had been his second wife, and he her second husband, but she had no children by either of her two marriages, John Bushrod’s daughters Hannah and Elizabeth having been born
2 CONC  to his first wife, '''Jenny Corbin Bushrod''' (kenner, 177–78; GW to Ruthey Jones, 25 Sept. 1783, DLC:GW
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I50436&tree=tree1
