1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 109
2 CONT Hannah was the daughter of John Bushrod of Bushfield and his wife, Mildred Corbin.  John Bushrod made his will Feb. 14, 1760 and it was proved before the court of Westmoreland Co. on Dec. 30 of the same year.  He left land, furnit
2 CONC ure and 35 slaves to his daughter Hannah Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid, p. 125
2 CONT Hannah Bushrod Washington...had a horror of being buried alive and in a long will which she wrote with her own hand gave specific directions intended to protect herself against such a fate.  Her grave is at Bushfield (unmarked).
