1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jane Washington''' was born on 20 Jun 1759 in Bushfield Plantation, Westmoreland Co., VA and died 16 Aug 1791 in Sweet Springs, VA.  She was also known as Jenny.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://gwpapers.virginia.edu/documents/will/text.html The Will of George Washington, Mount Vernon, 9 July 1799 - Transcription]
2 CONT
2 CONT 37. Corbin Washington had recently moved from his farm on the family place in Westmoreland County. He was living at Selby, Fairfax County, where Washington visited him in November 1799 (Diaries, 6:374). '''Jane (Jenny) Washington'
2 CONC '' was married to William Augustine Washington, the son of her father's half brother Augustine Washington. She was living with him at Haywood in Westmoreland County in 1791 when she died. Her surviving children in 1799 were George
2 CONC  Corbin Washington, Ann Aylett Washington, and Bushrod Washington, Jr. As the major beneficiary of Washington's will, Bushrod, John Augustine Washington's oldest son, received only one third of a share (see note 33).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: daughter of John Augustine Washington and Hannah Bushrod 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # on 25 Sep 1777 to Brigadier General William Augustine Washington ( Augustine, Augustine, Lawrence, John, Lawrence ) as his 1st wife; he married 2nd to Mary Lee & 3rd to Sarah March.  William Augustine Washington was born on 25 N
2 CONC ov 1757 in Wakefield, Westmoreland Co. VA. He died on 2 Oct 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # Hannah Bushrod (1778-1797)
2 CONT # Augustine (1780-1798)
2 CONT # Anne Aylett (1783- )
2 CONT # Bushrod (1785- )
2 CONT # George Corbin (?)
2 CONT #  Notes
2 CONT * [http://rotunda.upress.virginia.edu/founders/default.xqy?keys=GEWN-index-1-25-534-1#GEWN-01-02-02-pb-0215 Washington Papers Consolidated Index | W |  Washington, Jane Washington (1759-1791)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://www.familysearch.org/Eng/Search/af/family_group_record.asp?familyid=1899750&frompage=0 Jane (Jenny) WASHINGTON (AFN:1860-RN9)] FamilySearch™ Ancestral File v4.19
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT # [http://www.politicalfamilytree.com/samples%20content/members/PDF%20Content/Washington-VA-2.pdf Partial Genealogy of the Washingtons, Part ll (of Virginia and Maryland] PDF file
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=HTsq0_bZpEQC&pg=PA413&lpg=PA413&dq=Jane+Washington+1759&source=bl&ots=iMJ_xjryoC&sig=Hkwh9LfIjG4afR85NIaQCVz8jec&hl=en&sa=X&ei=AQLcT9CuCsqe2gW648mrDQ&ved=0CGgQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Jane%20Washingto
2 CONC n%201759&f=false George Washington's Legacy of Leadership. By A. Ward Burian.  Page 413.]
2 CONT # [http://marciesalaskaweb.com/fourth_generation.htm Descendants of Lawrence Washington - Sixth Generation]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/101105579/jane_washington
2 CONT Daughter of John Augustine Washington and
2 CONT Hannah Bushrod
2 CONT
2 CONT Cousin of William
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st wife of Capt William Augustine Washington
2 CONT Married September 25, 1777
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of:
2 CONT 1. Hannah Bushrod Washington
2 CONT 2. Augustine Washington
2 CONT 3. Ann Aylett Washington
2 CONT 4. Bushrod Washington
2 CONT 5. Corbin Aylett Washington
2 CONT 6. George Corbin Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT I originally posted as buried at Bridges Creek Washington Family Cemetery or aka George Washing Nat'l Monument based on several book references.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, several other relatives have gotten extremely rude with emails to me that I dare even put her here stating she is not buried here, yet they are unable to provide proof that she is buried elsewhere and do not provide me wi
2 CONC th their credentials.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am also a distant relative,, but I will remove the cemetery reference but will keep the memorial up.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note
2 CONT Jenny died at Sweet Springs, Monroe Co., VA (now WV) and from all accounts was buried there, but I have not been able to verify! I am a Washington cousin, and Washington researcher. She is not listed on any of the known list of bu
2 CONC rials at "Bridges Creek" also known as the vault at George Washington's Birthplace National Monument.
2 CONT Contributor: Dal Mallory (46586597) • dal.mallory@yahoo.com
