1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mildred Gregory Washington (1772-1804) married in 1797, Capt. Thomas Hammond (1770/1-1820). They resided at "Happy Retreat" in Jefferson County, [W]Va. which Mildred inherited upon her father's death in 1803. She d
2 CONC ied in childbirth or from complications shortly afterward. Their children were Charles Henry (1798), George Washington (1802-03), and Thomas Washington Hammond (1804-05).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mildred Gregory Washington's father was Colonel Charles Washington (1738-99), fourth son of Capt. Augustine (c1694-1743) and Mary Ball Washington (1708/9-89), who was born in Stafford Co., Va. He was a magistrate for Spotsylvania 
2 CONC County, Va. He built a house in Fredericksburg which later became the historic Rising Sun Tavern which is on Caroline St. In 1780 he moved to Charles Town, [W.]Va. which he laid out on his land and for him the town is named. He in
2 CONC herited the land from his brother Lawrence Washington. There he built around 1780 the brick mansion "Happy Retreat." It's listed on the National Register of Historic Places. He married in 1757, his first cousin once removed, Mildr
2 CONC ed Thornton (c1739-post1804), daughter of Col. Francis (1711/2-49) and Frances Gregory Thornton (post1719-ante1794), of "The Falls," Spotsylvania County, Va. Their four children were Lt. George Augustine (c1758-93), Frances (1763-
2 CONC 1815), Samuel (1770/1-1831), and Mildred Gregory Washington (1772-1804).
2 CONT
2 CONT See Albert Welles, The Pedigree and History of the Washington Family (New York, 1879), 167-168, 186-188; John W. Wayland, The Washingtons and Their Homes (Genealogical Pub., 1944), 317; Stella Pickett Hardy, Colonial Families of t
2 CONC he Southern States of America (Genealogical Publishing Co., 1958), 520, 522; John B. Burke, Burke's Presidential Families of the United States (London, 1975), 63; John Augustine Washington (1920-2020), Descendants of Rev. Lawrence
2 CONC  (c1602-52/3) and Amphyllis Twigden Washington (-1655) Five Generation Chart (Chevy Chase, Md. 1982); Washington Heritage Trail Guide (picture of Happy Retreat), 25; Dr. Justin M. Glenn, The Washingtons, A Family History, Volume O
2 CONC ne, Seven Generations of the Presidential Branch (Savas Beatie, El Dorado Hills, Ca. 2014), I: 83; James Houston Barr III, Lt. Colonel Nathaniel Pope, c1610-1660, of Virginia, Ancestor of Washington, Governors and Legislators, His
2 CONC tory of His Descendants (Louisville, Ky. 2018), 27.
