1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 338
2 CONT Mildred G. Washington, dau. of Col. Charles Washington of Charles Town and wife Mildred Thornton; born about 1777; was unmarried Jan. 24, 1793, when her brother George Augustine made his will - he names her as "my sister Mildred W
2 CONC ashington."
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT She was the first wife of Thomas Hammond who married (2) Nancy Collins.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Her will was made in Jefferson Co.,VA., in 1804; proved 1805.  Gen. George Washington in his will (1799) calls her Mildred Hammond.
2 CONT
2 CONT INDEX TO LOUDOUN CO, VA. WILLS, 1757-1850 by Louisa Skinner Hutchison, p. 52
2 CONT BALL, BURGESS, F:226, 1800 
2 CONT Names Mildred Gregory Hammond in his will as sister-in-law.
2 CONT Note:  She was the sister of his wife, Frances Washington. - JMC
