1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Morrow of northern Mecklenburg Co., North Carolina is first mentioned in county land records in 1777. A Richard Morrow, likely his son, is alluded to being in Mecklenburg County by 1773 when he bought land fro
2 CONC m Ezekiel Sharpe. They lived in the northern part of Mecklenburg County, close to the Catawba River and Davidsons Creek. In his Will of 1795, John refers to himself as "Planter".
2 CONT Worth Ray in "Tennessee Cousins" and the FamilySearch Databases are incorrect in surmising John Morrow to be the son of David and Hannah Hopkins Morrow from Norfolk, VA. DNA testing of descendants shows no connection. Nor is there
2 CONC  any proof of this John Morrow in Virginia prior to coming to Mecklenburg Co., North Carolina. His origins, at this point, are unknown.
