1 NOTE {geni:about_me} First marriage to Col. Porter, who was an intimate friend of and in charge of the Parliamentary regiment Capt. Robert Bruce Polk was in. After Col. Porter's death, Magdalen married Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT The are said to have been of French descent and were related to the Countess of Normington and her sister Prudence; aunts to the Duke of Wellington. Captain Robert Bruce Polk and his family were Presbyterians. They came to Marylan
2 CONC d, presumably about 1672; landed at "Damn Quarter" (now called "Dane's Quarter") and planted there new home in that locality, between Nonokin and Nanticoke Rivers, near the junction of those streams with Chesapeake Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/n/o/l/Melanie-C-Nolan-2/GENE1-0001.html
