2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:17th Century American Immigration]] [[Category: Mary and John sailed March 20 1630]]
2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration}}
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT === Immigrated on the ''Mary and John'' in 1630 ===: William Gaylord, Jr. was about twelve years old when he sailed from England on the "Mary and John" with his parents and siblings in 1630.<ref>[[#ENEF|''Early New England Familie
2 CONC s, 1641-1700'']], page 1</ref> The ship ''Mary and John'' was the first ship with settlers coming into Massachusetts Bay. Later ships of the Winthrop Fleet dropped settlers all around the bay, including the location that became Bo
2 CONC ston, Massachusetts. William and his family were among the 130 people who were planted at what became Dorchester, Massachusetts. The sufferings they experienced that first year, of which exposure to the elements, hunger, disease a
2 CONC nd malnutrition were but a part, are unfamiliar to us today.
2 CONT : Dorchester prospered so rapidly, that by 1636 there was a dearth of available pasture for their cattle and horses. A group from the town ventured across the wilderness to a location scouted for them earlier, and established Wind
2 CONC sor, Connecticut, on the great Connecticut River. The Gaylord family was in that group of intrepid farmers. : William Gaylord (Jr.) had an original grant of a home-lot 18 rods wide in Windsor and his name is found, along with his 
2 CONC father's name, on the Founders Monument in Windsor. In 1654 it is noted that William Gaylord, the younger, was a joint purchaser with his father and brother, John, in a parcel that was John Warham's, on the East side of the Great 
2 CONC River. : William married at Windsor, Connecticut, Ann Porter 24 Feb 1641/2,<ref name=GMB/> who died in 1653 leaving William with 5 small children. A short time later, 9 Feb 1653/4, William married Elizabeth Drake at Windsor, <ref 
2 CONC name=GMB/> with whom he had two more children. William died in 1656 at the young age of 38 leaving his relatively new bride with seven children ranging in age from 11 years to the youngest, Nathaniel, who was only fifteen weeks ol
2 CONC d at the death of their father. Four years later, his widow married John Elderkin. William's estate was inventoried at £423-00-09 and £383-06-06 after all debts were paid. Because of the young age of his children, his estate wasn'
2 CONC t distributed to the widow and children until 1673, 17 years after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Name ===: William Gaylord <ref name=GMB>''The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III, profile for William Gaylord'', page742</ref> <ref>[[#PMT|Public Member Trees]]</ref> This is ''son'' of 
2 CONC the elder William Gaylord. Both of them arrived 1630 on the Mary & John.
2 CONT === Baptized ===
2 CONT :: 28 Dec 1617, Crewkerne, Somersetshire, England <ref name=GMB/>
2 CONT === Marriages ===
2 CONT :: 24 FEB 1641[2?] Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut <ref name=GMB/>
2 CONT : Husband: [[Gaylord-2|William Gaylord]]: Wife: [[Porter-1|Ann Porter]] <ref name=GMB/><ref Name="HoH">Sylvester Judd and Lucius Manlius Boltwood "History of Hadley, Including the Early History of Hatfield, South Hadley, Amherst a
2 CONC nd Granby, Massachusetts" p 497</ref> : Child: [[Gaylord-32|William Gaylord]]<ref name=HoH/> :: Marriage (2nd): 9 Feb 1653, Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut <ref name=GMB/> : Husband: [[Gaylord-2|William Gaylord]] : Wife: [[D
2 CONC rake-476|Elizabeth Drake]] <ref name=GMB/>
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT :: 14 Dec 1656 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut <ref name=GMB/>
2 CONT === Burial ===
2 CONT :: 1656 Palisado Cemetery, Hartford County, Windsor, Connecticut 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references/>* <span id='Welles'></span>Welles, Edwin. ''[[Space:Births, Marriages,and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield, and Entered in the Early Land Records of the Colony of Connecticut|Births, Marriages, an
2 CONC d Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield]]'' (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., Hartford, Conn., 1898) ::* [https://books.google.com/books?id=0woWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA41 Page 41]: "William Gaylor and Elisabeth Drake both of W
2 CONC yndfor weare married ffebr 9th 1653"::* [https://archive.org/stream/birthsmarriagesd00well_1#page/43/mode/1up Page 43]: "William Gaylor the younger of Windzor died, decem 14th 1656"
2 CONT * <span id=ENEF></span>''Early New England Families, 1641-1700''. (Original Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2013. (By Alicia Crane Williams, Lead Genealogist.)[https://www.america
2 CONC nancestors.org/DB501/i/13909/1/33460694 William Gaylord (1621 - 1653)] (Three Page Bio)
