1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Gaylord===
2 CONT * Birth:	 	Jan 30 1646, Windsor, Hartford Co, CT
2 CONT * Death:	 	Aug 3 1678, Westerly, Washington Co, RI
2 CONT * Burial: possibly in the Crandall Family Burial Ground, Westerly, Washington Co, RI.  (Cenotaph)
2 CONT * Parents: William Gaylord & Anna Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # 2nd Wife of Elder John Crandall (1617 - 1676)
2 CONT # after 1676  to John Cottrell. (disputed)
2 CONT Children by 1st husband 
2 CONT # Jeremiah Crandall (1673-1718)
2 CONT # Eber Crandall (1676-1727)
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps Hannah Cottrell was her daughter.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Hannah Gaylord Crandall Cottrell is buried in the Old Crandall Cemetery, Westerly, Washington County, Rhode Island.
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/27183581/hannah-crandall
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gaylord-1
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah (Gaylord) Cottrell has English ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Gaylord, daughter of William Gaylord and Anna Porter, was born 30 January 1646/7 in Windsor, Connecticut.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married after 2 August 1670 (date of death of his first wife) to John Crandall.[2] They had two children, as follows:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah, b. aft. 1670, died between 1 and 28 Aug 1718 at Westerly, m. Priscilla Warner, daughter of John and Ann (Gorton) Warner; she m2. Abraham Lockwood of Providence;
2 CONT Eber, b. 1675, d. betw. 22 Aug and 15 Sep 1727 at Westerly, m1. Unknown, m2. Patience, daughter of George Lanphear, m3. Mary Cottrell, possible dau. of John.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Crandall died in 1676 and Hannah married, as her second husband, John Cottrell of Westerly.[1] John came to own land in 1680 that belonged to Rev. John Crandall, and it is thought that it might be because his wife was a Crand
2 CONC all.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah died 3 August 1678,[2] probably at Westerly, Rhode Island, where she is likely buried. Her husband remarried and had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT (f/g) Hannah Gaylord Crandall Birth: 	Jan. 30, 1646 Windsor Hartford County Connecticut, USA Death: 	Aug. 8, 1678 Westerly Washington County Rhode Island, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ~2nd Wife of: Elder John Crandall 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *William Gaylord (1617 - 1656)
2 CONT *Anna Porter Gaylord (1621 - 1653) 
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *John Crandall (1617 - 1676) 
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *Jeremiah Crandall (1673 - 1718)*
2 CONT *Eber Crandall (1676 - 1727)* 
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT *   Anna Gaylord Phelps (1645 - 1689)* 
2 CONT *   Hannah Gaylord Crandall (1646 - 1678) 
2 CONT *   John Gaylord (1648 - 1689)* 
2 CONT *   William Gaylord (1651 - 1680)* 
2 CONT *   Nathaniel Gaylord (1656 - 1720)**  
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT **Half-sibling
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Crandall Cemetery Westerly Washington County Rhode Island, USA  Created by: Superkentman Record added: May 29, 2008 Find A Grave Memorial# 27183581 -tcd
2 CONT
