1 NOTE From "A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England, ... , Vol. III, by James Savage, p. 461:  JAMES, Windsor, sec. s. of the sec. John of the same, m. 15 Jan. 1680, Sarah, eldest d. of Owen Tudor, had James, b. 1
2 CONC 3 Oct. 1680, d. soon; Mary, 4 June 1682, d. at 2 yrs. Isaac, 13 July 1683, d. 1 May foll.; Mary, 23 Sept. 1684.; and Sarah, 31 May 1686; went to Eng. was in 1690 a merch. of distinct. in London, wh. declin. the office of agent for
2 CONC  the Col.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-7369
1 NOTE Bkulliard and allied families, #929, 2B, 867B.  Page 138, 141, 246.
1 NOTE Probably died as a child as another child born later was named James.
