1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=14220463
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Samuel was a representative to General Court, sheriff and j udge of the county of Hampshire, MA. an extensive merchan t and trader; he imported direct from England. He left hi s family an immense estate of over 10,000 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Bernard Burke, Burke's American Families with British Ancestry, page , 2869.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Adams Virkus F.I.A.G., Compendium of American Genealogy, ......, Volume 5, page , 662.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, Burke's Presidential Families of the United States of America, page , 332.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/14220463/samuel-porter
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife was Johannah Cook Porter.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Hannah Hawley Nichols Wolcott, widow of Josiah Nichols and John Wolcott. Her fourth husband was Henry Wolcott. She was the daughter of Joseph Hawley and Catherine Birdseye Hawley of Stratford,CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Samuel Porter and Hannah Stanley Porter of Windsor and Hadley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by first marriage): Samuel Porter III, Joanna Porter Marsh(wife of John Marsh), Aaron Porter, Moses Porter, Sarah Porter Goodrich, Mehitable Porter Marsh, Miriam Porter, Eleazer Porter, Hannah Porter, Nathaniel Porter, Ru
2 CONC th Porter Steele, Mary Porter, an infant daughter(dy), and an infant son(dy).
