1 NOTE Samuel Grant is 100% English
1 NOTE Resided at Windsor; removed to East Windsor Hill as early as 1672, where he built a house on the bank of the river in the rear of the Theological Institute; he afterwards removed to the site of the present residence of Hon. Roswel
2 CONC l Grant. When 18 years old he was employed to attend the Connecticut River ferry; in 1661 was employed to shingle the inside roof of the meeting house; part owner of saw-mill; sealer of measures, lister, constable, surveyor, bound
2 CONC goer many years; on committee to run bounds between Windsor and Simsbury; they joined the church at Windsor in 1685, and were members of the church at East Windsor in 1700.
