2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Grant, born at Windsor, Connecticut, was a son of Samuel Grant and Mary Porter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed to East Windsor, then in 1695 to Stonington, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Grant married 8 Jul 1696 at Stonington, Connecticut, Rebecca Miner [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT This couple joined the First Congregational Church of Stonington Aug. 27, 1699. They had 5 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah & Rebecca Grant were dismissed from the Stonington church in 1727 to form the church at North Stonington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Grant was a (tax) collector, lister, constable, and tythingman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Grant died 28 Mar 1732 at Stonington. His grave is in Old Taugwonk Cemetery, Stonington, New London County, Connecticut, USA [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth year expression 1668/69 is probably correct for this person, accounting for the Julian/Gregorian calendar shift which pertained to all persons born during the first 3 months of every year from 1582 until 1752 when the Britis
2 CONC h adopted the Gregorian calendar. His grave marker is inscribed that he was "Aged 63 yrs" on 28 March 1732, hence he would have been born in March 1668 of the old (Julian) calendar, 1669 of the new (Gregorian) calendar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850", , FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QPSF-22KM : Sun Mar 10 00:38:39 UTC 2024), Entry for Rebeckah Minor and James Fitch, 8 July 1696.
2 CONT ↑ Find A Grave: Memorial #26507039
