1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Treat, daughter of Thomas Coleman and his first wife (name Unknown) was born before 1638 at Evesham, Worcesteshire, England. Sarah's father Thomas Coleman married his second wife, Francis (Albright) Wells, before 6 March 163
2 CONC 8, at Evesham, Worcestershire, England, where they both lived at the time. They had one child, a daughter, Deborah. Francis brought her three children from her first marriage to Thomas Wells: Mary Wells,, Thomas Wells, and John We
2 CONC lls. Thomas Coleman had four children from his first marriage, one of them being Sarah Coleman, who married Richard Treat.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Coleman-374
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon John Coleman
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1639 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Coleman and his 1st wife 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Wells [half], Thomas Wells [half], Mary (Wells) Gilbert [half], Esther (Coleman) Davis, Sarah (Coleman) Treat, Noah Coleman and	Deborah (Coleman) Gunn
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Porter) Coleman — married 29 May 1663 in Felstead, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mehitable (Johnson) Coleman — married 11 Mar 1679 in Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Day) Coleman — married 11 Dec 1696 in Springfield, Hampshire County, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Thomas Coleman, Hannah (Coleman) Nash, John Coleman, Noah Coleman, Sarah (Coleman) Field, Berthia Coleman, Ebenezer Coleman and Nathaniel Coleman
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 21 Jan 1711 in Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 4 Dec 2018 | Created 7 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Coleman is the son of Thomas Coleman and his 1st wife  [1] [2] He was born 1639 in England and was christened on 7 April 1739 at Saint Margaret, Westminster, London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married, first, Hannah Porter. [3] She died on September 17, 1677 in Deerfield, Massachusetts Bay Colon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 11 March 1679, Mehitable Johnson, daughter of Humphrey Johnson, as his second wife. [4] She was the widow of Samuel Hinsdale and then the widow of John Root, both killed by Indians during King Philip's War.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Coleman married, 11 December 1696, for his third wife, Mary Day, daughter of Deacon Robert Day and Editha Stebbins. She was the widow of Samuel Ely, and of Thomas Stebbins, Jr. [5] [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT John died on 21 January 1711 at Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts. He was 76 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Hill Cemetery Hatfield Hampshire County Massachusetts, USA GPS (lat/lon): 42.367, 72.60651
2 CONT
