1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cole Jr. of A.A. Co. Md. (planter), was m. on 5th mo. 30 day of 1689 to Elizabeth Sparrow of Clifts in Calvert Co. at Richard Johns house.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * COALE, WILLIAM, Anne Arundel Co. 15 Sep, 1761; 11 Dec, 1761
2 CONT * To wife Sarah Coale, dwelling house and land Bever Dams; at her decease, to son John Coale.
2 CONT * To son Wm. Coale, land in Baltimore Co. called Young Marrs Adventure.
2 CONT * To son Samuel Coale, 3 tracts in Baltimore Co., Martinton, Martinton's Addition and Coal's Good Luck.
2 CONT * To grand-sons, William and John Coale, sans of dec'd. son Thomas Coale, land in Baltimore Co., known by names of Owens Adventure, Owens Addition, excepting 150 A., to be laid out on the west end of sd. land. All remainder to gra
2 CONC ndsons, to be equally divided between them.
2 CONT * To dau. Ann Stockett, 150 A. in Baltimore Co., Owens' Adventure, Owens Addition.
2 CONT * To son John Coale, 2 tracts in Anne Arundel Co., Hills Chance and Talbott's Angles. At death of wife, son John to have dwelling house, Beaver Dams, etc.
2 CONT * Exec: Wife Sarah Coale, and son John.
2 CONT * Wit: B. Ward, Wm. Briant, John Barker, Jr., wm. Journey, Geo. Neale, Jr. 31. 524
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I042929&tree=tree1
