2 CONT Robert Roberts, b. 7. 11 mo. 1673 (January 7th, 1674). By his father's will, he and his brother Owen received jointly his Merion land. On 26. Imo. 1706, this land was patented to them, in two tracts, of 222 acres, and 31 acres eac
2 CONC h, and by deed of 16 October, 1707, "Robert Roberts, of Maryland," conveyed his 222 (220) acres, which lay along the Lancaster road (Montgomery avenue) from the Meeting House to the Gulf road, and 10 acres, called "Clean John Mead
2 CONC ow," on the "Upper Mill Creek," to Edward Rees, Robert Roberts was twice married, and is supposed to. have removed to Maryland, and died there. He m. first, Catharine Jones, and m. secondly, Priscilla Jones.
