1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 18 JUN 1756 Davis Creek, Granville Co., NC - Son-in-law William Wharton helped survey land for Richard Roberts.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 AUG 1771 Granville Co., NC - Court Minutes - Richard Roberts to Son-in-law William Whoton - Deed Book I page 242
2 CONT
2 CONT 1772 - Richard Roberts died. In his will dated April 17, 1772 (prob, May Court, 1772), Richard left most of his land along Cub Creek in Orange County and possessions to his sons and daughters. He left to his daughter, Jane Whorton
2 CONC , one bed and furniture. The will was witnessed by William Chandler and Britain Johnston. It's not clear what happed to other items: "One still, a parsil of books and 2 Negroes. However Richard did leave his son Joseph "one iron p
2 CONC ot with a nick broke in the top of the brim". The rest of the estate was divided equally.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/o/n/Kristy-Gonzalez-tx/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-1136.html
2 CONT
