2 CONT ==LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT of Richard Roberts==
2 CONT :Richard Roberts, of Gr. Co.  (Granville County), Will, dat. (dated) April 17, 1772, prob. (probated) May Ct. 1772.:To son Willis, 250 A. (acres) from the north end of my tract of land in Orange Co. on Cub Creek;:(2) to son David,
2 CONC  250 A. from the South end of my tract of land in Orange Co. on Cub creek, including his plantation and my chest;:(3) to gr. (grand) son Richard Bridges, 200 A. of land in Orange Co., on Cub creek, being the remainder of my land t
2 CONC here, and lying bet. (between) the lands of Willis and David Roberts;
2 CONT :(4) to son Shadrach, 1 negro woman and half of his wearing clothes;:(5) to daut. (daughter) Celia, 1 negro woman, 1 bed and furniture, being same on which testator lies, and the use of testator’s room while she lives single;:(6) 
2 CONC to son Jesse the plantation test, now lives on, containg 200 A. more or less, 1 negro man, 1 bed and furniture and half of his wearing clothes;
2 CONT :(7) to daut. [[Roberts-6784|Jane Whorton]], 1 bed and furniture;
2 CONT :(8) to daut. Lyddia Bridges, his flock of sheep;:(9) to son Joseph, “one Iron pot, with a nick Broke in the top of the Brim”; and:(10) rest of est. (estate) to be equally div. bet. (divided between) all his chidren.:Exs (Executor
2 CONC s) : son Joseph, James Walker and Luke Landers. Wit (Witnesses): Wm. (William) Chandler, Britain Johnston.
