2 CONT ???????:Richard Roberts, a Revolutionary soldier; born in Albermarle County, N. C. (?) 1735; son of Richard Roberts and Elizabeth (Allen) Roberts of Maryland; served seven years in Revolution; lived in Granville County, N. C. Sour
2 CONC ce: Google Books,  The Georgia Historical Quarterly, Page 998, Society, 1952.
2 CONT :Richard Roberts and first wife, Elizabeth, lived in Albermarle County, Va., 1733-1740, when they moved to ... Richard moved to Granville County, N. C., where he and his wife died.Source: Google Books, “The Alabama Historical Quar
2 CONC terly” – Volumes 6-9, Page 146.
2 CONT ???????
2 CONT :Richard Roberts received a land grant in l760 in Granville County, N. C. He died l772. His will mentioned the following children: Willis, David, Shadrack, Celia, Jesse, Jane, Lydia and Joseph, a Revolutionary veteran, who moved t
2 CONC o Hancock County, Ga. around 1785 where he lived until 1832; he then moved to Warren County where he died 1836. Several of his brothers also moved to Hancock County, Ga.Source: Google Books, “Gone to Georgia: Jackson and Gwinnett 
2 CONC Counties and their neighbors in the western migration”, by National Genealogical Society, 1965 – Georgia – 325 pages.
2 CONT
