1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Lucas
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1610 - England 
2 CONT * Death:	Before Mar 24 1673/74 - Sittenbourne Parish, Rappahannock, VA.
2 CONT * Wife:	1) (Margaret  Sweeney?) 2) Margaret 'Mary' Mason, widow of John Upton
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, all by 1st wife
2 CONT
2 CONT # Constance MNU Johnson
2 CONT #  Thomas Lucas b: ABT 1636 in Sittenbourne Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia - Probate
2 CONT #  Mary Lucas b: ABT 1638 in Sittingbourne Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia
2 CONT #  Henry Lucas b: BEF 1646 in Holland
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT URL title: Family Tree Maker Online: GenealogyLibrary.com: Lucas Genealogy, Page 36
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt Thomas Lucas arrived in Va about 1641 from Surrey, Eng. He was one of the early settlers to Va. Records show he patented lands in Gloucester Co, Virginia, as early as 1645 in which he is styled as Thomas Lucas, Gentleman. He 
2 CONC was Burgess of Rappahannock Co, Virginia where he settled in 1657 or 1658; was a Justice and occupied many offices of trust and distinction. He is believed to have been of the same family as Sir Thomas Lucas, Justice of Surrey and
2 CONC  Middlesex, and a descendant of Baron Lucas of Crudwell, Eng, of the 24th Century. He is said to have been a man of wealth, for in his will he leaves family jewels of diamond rings and pearl necklaces. (See Amer of Gentle Birth by
2 CONC  Pittman & Walker vol 1, p 68.) This Capt Thomas Lucas was closely associated with Colonel John Catlett and Ralph Rowzee in bringing persons to Va "to inhabit," in this new colony and for this they were awarded a great deal of lan
2 CONC d. Captain Lucas mar first in Eng and records show he brought his wife, his son T! homas Lucas, Jr., and a dau Mary to Va. He later mar Mrs. Margaret Upton, widow of Capt John Upton of Rappahannock Co, Virginia. (See Amer of Gentl
2 CONC e Birth vol 1, p 68.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogies of Virginia Families, Vol V, R-Z, from Virginia Mag. of Hist. Genealogical Publishing County, Baltimore, 1981 Text: p. 607
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Rappahannock or Lancaster County, Virginia. On 10 April 1657, a marriage agreement was discovered between Captain Thomas Lucas, the Elder of Rappahannock in Virginia, Gentleman, Col. More Fantleroy and Captain William Underwoo
2 CONC d of the county aforesaid on - - in consideration of a marriage (God Willing) shortly to be solemnized between the said Thomas Lucas and Margaret Upton. The bond for the marriage was for the sum of 12,000 pounds of tobacco to be e
2 CONC xecuted by Col. More Fantleroy and William Underwood.
2 CONT
