2 CONT Richmond County, Virginia Wills and Inventories 1707-1719; {Robert K. Headley, Jr}:
2 CONT
2 CONT p.344 - William UNDERWOOD, Sitt. Par.: Will, 19 Jul 1717; Probate, 7 Aug 1717:
2 CONT
2 CONT son John the reversion and reversions of one water mill now in the hands of Richard TUTT and 300 ac. of land; son William all land and plant. within the isthmus or neck of land where I now live; dau. Mary TUTT 200 ac. beginning at
2 CONC  the Rich Fork Point; dau. Sarah GILBERT; 200 ac. beginning at the Beaver Dam; grsons. John and William THATCHER 200 ac. of land; dau. Elizabeth THATCHER;
2 CONT
2 CONT ex: sons John and William; wits: William PULLEN, Catherine PULLEN, Margaret BURKE.
2 CONT
2 CONT p.346 - William UNDERWOOD, inv; 4 Sep 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Richmond Co., VA, Deed Book 1, 1692-1693:
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Dec 1691. Deed. Whereas there is a tr of land formerly belonging to WARWICK CAMMOCK whereof 600 a. of the tr having formerly been conveyd over unto AMMAREE {Amory} BUTLER and from him conveyd unto WILLIAM UNDERWOOD Senr as marr
2 CONC ying the sister of the said AMMAREE BUTLER, and from the said WILLIAM UNDERWOOD conveyd in the exchange of the thirds of lands belonging unto ELIZABETH COUMBS, with her consent, unto WILLIAM UNDERWOOD Junr, JOHN COUMBS & WILLIAM C
2 CONC OUMBS, now the said WILLIAM UNDERWOOD Junr for a valuable consideration sold unto WILLIAM TOMAS of the parish of Washington, Westmoreland Co, 200 a. being his right in the 600 a. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wit: THOMAS TYNWHITT, WILLIAM UNDERWOOD, JOHN PITTMAN. Ackn 4 May 1692.  Attest: JO A EMOND dep clerk. (Bk 1:pg 4)* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/175712074/william-underwood Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 15 2020, 16:13:39 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/175712074/william-underwood Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 15 2020, 16:16:40 UTC''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood Sr. was a Virginia colonist.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Space:US_Southern_Colonies_Colony_of_Virginia_Team
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood was born about 1648/49 in Isle of Wight County, Virginia Colony. He was included as a headright of his father, William Underwood, in a patent recorded 22 May 1650:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1650 - Same, [William Underwood], 600 acs. in Rappa. Riv. on N. side, beg. at a poynt nigh the mouth of Indian Cr., running N. E. by N. & above land of Mr. James Williamson. Trans. of 12 pers: Wm. Moseley, Wm. Underwood 4 tymes, M
2 CONC ary his wife, Wm. Underwood his son, Henry Succor & ux, George Bryer, Joseph Robins, Elizabeth Penn (or Prenn) 22 May 1650, p. 213.[1]
2 CONT On 22 July 1663 a document was recorded:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood son and heir of William Underwood Senr. late of Rappahannock County in Virginia in this part of America appoint my uncle William Moseley as guardian and attorney for me to care for the estate bequeathed by my fat
2 CONC her's will. He to send to my uncle Edward Burton Gent. of Kedeminster in county of Worcestor to whom I have entrusted my education the income out of my estates in Virginia. I the said William Underwood am of the age of fourteen an
2 CONC d one half years." 20 July 1663, signed by William Underwood; witnessed by Edward Giggs, Will Jenkins.[2]
2 CONT 1662 -William Underwood, sonn & heire of Coll. Wm. Underwood, 2561 1/2 acs. Rappa. Co., 11 Mar. 1662, p. 103 (598). ... 2784 granted Coll. Underood 10 Sept. 1658, whereof 238 sold to Samuell Nicholls & 15 1/2 acs. now adjoined. Du
2 CONC e said William as sonn & heire of the abovesaid.[1]
2 CONT Marriage & Children
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood married Mary (Butler) Underwood before December 1672 in (Old) Rappahannock County, Virginia Colony. On 24 December 1672 William, "with Mary his wife, of Rappahannock county stated that whereas Mr. John Catlett su
2 CONC rveyed for Samuel Nicholls a tract of 688 acres of land ...." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children (named in his will) include:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Underwood
2 CONT William Underwood
2 CONT Mary Underwood, md Richard Tutt
2 CONT Elizabeth Underwood, md Mr. Thatcher
2 CONT Sarah Underwood, md Mr. Gilbert
2 CONT Death & Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood, Sr., of Sittenbourne Parish, Richmond County, wrote his will on 19 July 1717. Inventory of the estate was entered on the same day the will was probated, 7 August 1717.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Underwood-851
2 CONT
2 CONT William Underwood Sr. (1649 - aft. 1717) I
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===William Underwood Sr.===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1649 in Isle of Wight, Colony of Virginiam [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William Underwood and Mary (Moseley) Underwood
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Butler) Underwood — married before 1672 in Rappahannock County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of William Thomas Underwood, John Underwood Jr., Thomas Underwood, Mary (Underwood) Tutt, Elizabeth Underwood and Sarah Underwood
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 19 Jul 1717 after age 68 in Richmond County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Underwood-851 created 13 Feb 2012 | Last modified 23 Nov 2021
2 CONT
