1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. Southern Colonies Project logo
2 CONT Nicholas Catlett was a Virginia colonist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Catlett was born in 1645 in Sittingbourne, Kent, England[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Catlett and his father John Catlett arrived in Virginia in 1650.[3][4] Another passenger record for John Catlett is for the year 1653.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas' father John Catlett remarried in Virginia to Elizabeth Underwood Slaughter.[5][6][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Catlett was killed by Native Americans while he defended Port Royal in 1670.[8][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT A Nicholas Catlett married Elizabeth Mathews before 1672.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Catlett died in 1695 in Essex County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributed by Kay Schmidt
2 CONT
2 CONT a post by Lee Hoffman ("Wife of Nicholas Catlett," 27 Nov 1999, CATLETT-L Archives) questions whether Susannah's surname was MERIWETHER because David MERIWETHER apparently had no daughter named Susannah. In addition, Margaret Amun
2 CONC dson notes that Nicholas had a wife Elizabeth on several deeds. Seems further research is needed on the wife of Nicholas CATLETT.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Meriwether-276
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I28572&tree=Tree1
