1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jamestowne Society
2 CONT Catlett, John - A1414; born ca. 1658, died 1724, Essex Co.: 1693, 1695-97 (Burgess).
2 CONT * https://www.jamestowne.org/castle---challis.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Col. John Catlett, Jr. was known as the 2nd John.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was probated in Essex County on 18-Nov-1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married first, a Miss Smith. Some researchers believe that she was a daughter of Maj. Lawrence Smith since deeds recorded in Spotsylvania Co., VA, to Jon Catlett, Jr. and Richard Buckner, in 1722, from Augustine Smith, the so
2 CONC n of Major Lawrence Smith. The Catlett's owned a large estate at the mouth of Golden Vale Creek in present Caroline County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his first wife were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lawrence Catlett
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Elizabeth Catlett, who married Rowland Thornton
2 CONT
2 CONT John Catlett married second time, to Elizabeth[sic - Mary] Gaines. [Charles Hughes Hamlin, Professional Genealogist, who worked in conjunction with David A. Avant, Jr., could not find evidence to prove that Col. John Catlett, Jr. 
2 CONC married Elizabeth Gaines--nor any information about her parentage. Their marriage is, however, widely accepted by several writers and genealogists of the family. In 1706, Mary Catlett released her dower when her husband, John, sol
2 CONC d lands ....SO her name could have been MARY--not ELIZABETH. No original documents are available to prove the name "Elizabeth."]
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. John Catlett,Jr. and his second wife were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John Catlett, III. who married Elizabeth Taliaferro (daughter of John "The Ranger" Taliaferro, and Sarah Smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Maj.Thomas Catlett, who married Martha Thornton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mary Catlett who married Lt. Col. John Taliaferro, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Rebecca Catlett who married first Francis Conway and second John Moore, Gent.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Margaret Catlett who married Jonathan Gibson, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. John Catlett, Jr. was a Burgess (1693-1702); Justice of the peace (1692); coroner (1700); President of the Court, Sheriff (1705); Essex Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patented lands extensively in Spotsylvania Co. & elsewhere; in 1701 gave power of attorney to John Mumford of London to sell all lands at Sittingbourne, Kent County, Eng., and at Radwischeim, which he inherited from his father. Hi
2 CONC s last will was recorded in Essex County, VA, Wills, Bonds, Inv. #4 (1722-1730) Part 1, p. 84. His will was very long because he was a very wealthy man with much land, slaves, silver,etc.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/#view=ancestor&person=LYCW-D99 FamilySearch Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 11 2018, 20:50:57 UTC''
2 CONT *https://famouskin.com/family-group.php?name=9339+james+madison&ahnum=14
