1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/254326872/sarah_taliaferro
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (CATLETT) TALIAFERRO SALLIS; she died by 1719.  Daughter of John Catlett & Elizabeth Underwood.
2 CONT
2 CONT !1670: COLONEL CATLETT was killed by Indians while defending a fort at Port Royal in 1670 and by his Will he left his daughters, ELIZABETH and SARAH CATLETT, who married brothers, FRANCIS and ROBERT TALIAFERRO, 600 acres of land i
2 CONC n Rappahannock County
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born say 1668. Sarah had three marriages, with Samuel SHORT being the third.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her three marriages and children by each were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert TALIFERRO d. 1688 Old Rappahannock [now Essex] Co., VA.  !Robert married at 35 and died the following year with no will. His wife Sarah Catlett petitioned the court for administration of his estate. In the rent rolls of 170
2 CONC 4, Sarah Catlett(Taliaferro) Sallis is recorded in the quit rolls as owning 1,150 acres,all in Essex County,the exact amount remaining of her deceased husband Robert Taliaferro's inheritance from his fathers estate in Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Taliaferro and Sarah Catlett's child was  
2 CONT #  Robert TALIAFERRO lll born ca. 1688; m.1. Margaret FRENCH; m.2. Ann PITTMAN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters Martha, Mary and Elizabeth are seen, but they were the daughters of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Taliaferro/6000000008630867639?through=6000000025084583244
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel SALLIS married in 1688; d. 1704 Essex Co.
2 CONT #   1. Sarah SALLIS m.1 Alexander DONIPHAN; m. 2. William HANSFORD  William HANSFORD died d. 1754 Culpeper Co., VA         1a. William HANSFORD  d. 1779 1a1. Mary HANSFORD m. John SHORT [S-19, S-22, S-51 and S-58]                 
2 CONC   [her first cousin once removed]
2 CONT # 2. Anne SALLIS m. 1. Thomas MEADES who d. 1717; m. 2 Thomas AYRES who d. 1722;         m. 3. Jeremy BIZWELL who d. 1732
2 CONT #  3. John SALLIS
2 CONT #  4. Samuel SALLIS d. 1730; named "half brother" Samuel SHORT in his will
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Samuel SHORT "Sr."
2 CONT # Samuel SHORT Jr. b. ca. 1705; m. Ann PRICE; d. 1764 Frederick Co., VA 1a. John SHORT [S-19, S-22, S-51 and S-58] b. 1756; m. Mary HANSFORD; d. 1836 Lawrence Co., Ind
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel SHORT, Sr., also had at least three marriages, with Sarah CATLETT, the widow TALIFERRO and SALLIS being his first. This marriage may had been at least partially for financial gain and he may have been several years younger 
2 CONC than her.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT from "Historic Georgia Families" by L W Rigsby: 
2 CONT
2 CONT A deed in Essex Co VA, dated 1687, shows that Robert Taliaferro and Francis Taliaferro and their wives, Sarah and Elizabeth, sold 300 acres, part of the land bequeathed to said Sarah and Elizabeth by John Catlett, their father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Catlett was born in Old Rappahannock County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage of Sarah Catlett and Robert Taliaferro, II is proved by Deed, 1687, and Court Record, 25 March, 1692, Essex Co., VA. Wm. & Mary Quarterly, Vol. 20, p. 266 et seq..."Robert Taliaferro Junior and Francis Taliaferro, with th
2 CONC eir wives, Sarah and Elizabeth, sold 300 acres of land in Essex County in 1687 which was part of the land bequeathed to the said Sarah and Elizabeth by their father, John Catlett..." In 1688 both Francis and John Taliaferro gave b
2 CONC ond for Mrs. Sarah Taliaferro, widow of their brother Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (Catlett) Taliaferro and Robert Taliaferro, II were married in 1682, and had one son, Robert Taliaferro, III, who married first Margaret French, before 7-Aug-1711, and second Ann Pittman about 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ESSEX COUNTY 
2 CONT * 6 June 1688 Sarah TALIAFERRO admx. of the estate of her husband Robert TALIAFERRO
2 CONT * 6 Dec. 1688 Samuel SALLIS and wife Sarah, admx. of the estate of her deceased husband Robert TALIAFERRO
2 CONT * 10 June 1704 Administration f the Estate of Samll. SALLIS Deced. was this Day Granted to Sarah SALLIS his Widow Giving Bond & Security according to law with Bond being acknowledged is ordered to be Recorded.
2 CONT * 10 June 1704 James HARRISON, Charles TALIAFERRO, Lees EVANS & William WILLIAMS or any three are appointed & ordered Sometime between this and the next Court being first Sworn before one of her Majts. Justices of the poare for th
2 CONC is County to Inventory and Appraise the Estate of Samll. SALLIS Deced and Return their proceeding to the Next Court. And Ordered that Sarah SALLIS admrx. of the sd. Deceds Estate then appear & Make Oath to the Inventory.
2 CONT * 11 Oct. 1704 The order for the appraisement of the Estate of Samll. SALLIS Deced. is Continued till the next Court and ordered that Sarah SALLIS admrx. of the Deced then appear & make oath to the Inventory.
2 CONT * 10 Sep. 1705 Samuel SHORT & Sarah his wife admrx. of Samll SALLIS Deced Confessed Judgmt. to Cornelius SARJANT & Compn. Merchts. in Bristol for one Thousand Eighty & Six pounds of Sweet Sented Tobacco & Caske which to the Plt. i
2 CONC s due by one Bill under the aforesd. Deceds hand & Seal Dated the 12th Day of May 1702. It is therefore Considered by the Court that the aforesd. Quantity of Tobo. & Caske be paid with Costs.
2 CONT * 11 Dec. 1705 The action of Case brought by Stephen SHARP agt. Samll. SHORT & Sarah his wife is Dismd. for want of prosecution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://dgmgenealogy.info/Andersen/ps25/ps25_392.htm
2 CONT * http://sharpwriters.com/genealogy/taliaferro.html#robert
2 CONT * http://home.netcom.com/~fzsaund/shortva.html
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=thamm&id=I16544
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  Sarah Taliaferro (Catlett) Birth: 	1666 Death: 	1726 (60) Immediate Family: 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Col. John Catlett and Elizabeth Underwood Wife of Samuel Sallis; Samuel Short and Robert Taliaferro II Mother of Sarah Sallis; Samuel Short; John Short; Thomas A. Short and Robert Taliaferro III Added by: 	JC Flynt on 
2 CONC February 18, 2013 Managed by: 	JC Flynt
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-68641274/sarah-catlett-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 20 2016, 23:27:24 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Caroline, Virginia, United States
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LD8H-5VR FamilySearch Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 30 2020, 20:59:46 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Catlett was born in Old Rappahannock County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage of Sarah Catlett and Robert Taliaferro, II is proved by Deed, 1687, and Court Record, 25 March, 1692, Essex Co., VA.  Wm. & Mary Quarterly, Vol. 20, p. 266 et seq..."Robert Taliaferro Junior and Francis Taliaferro, with t
2 CONC heir wives, Sarah and Elizabeth, sold 300 acres of land in Essex County in 1687 which was part of the land bequeathed to the said Sarah and Elizabeth by their father, John Catlett..."  In 1688 both Francis and John Taliaferro gave
2 CONC  bond for Mrs. Sarah Taliaferro, widow of their brother Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (Catlett) Taliaferro and Robert Taliaferro, II were married in 1682, and had one son, Robert Taliaferro, III, who married first  Margaret French, before 7-Aug-1711, and second Ann Pittman about 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Robert Taliaferro, Sarah married Samuel Sallis.  Later she married Samuel Short.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional note submitted by:  Fredric Z. Saunders, FG Contributor
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah didn't die in 1726. She was deceased by 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth & Sam Sparacio, "Order Book Abstracts of Essex County, Virginia, 1716-1723 (Part II), (McLean, Virginia: R. & S. Sparacio, 1990), page 94, citing p.359 of 1716-1723 order book.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 August 1719 In the action of Debt brought by Patrick Gilbreath of Glasgow, Mercht. vs. Saml. Short and Sarah his wife, late Sarah Armstrong, Admx. &c. of John Armstrong, late of Richmond County, deced., the Deft. prays an impar
2 CONC lance to next Court & it is granted him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comment: Samuel Short was the third husband of Sarah Catlett. She died before 1719 by which time Samuel had married Sarah, the widow of John Armstrong who wrote his will in 1718 in Richmond County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers had confused Samuel Short's first wife Sarah Catlett Taliaferro-Sallis with his second wife Sarah, the widow of John Armstrong. Samuel Short's second wife Sarah was deceased by 1724 when his wife was Frances.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The notes below are incorrect'''. Robert Taliaferro of Church Neck who married Sarah Catlett lived 1652 - 1688 and had one child only, Robert lll.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://sharpwriters.com/genealogy/taliaferro.html#francis2
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert TALIAFERRO, (II) born in 1667, died in 1728. He married first Sarah CATLETT, a sister of the Elizabeth CATLETT who married Francis TALIAFERRO (our ancestor) and a sister of Mary CATLETT who married John TALIAFERRO, son of C
2 CONC ol. John TALIAFERRO. Robert and Sarah's children included: Mary TALIAFERRO; Martha TALIAFERRO; Elizabeth TALIAFERRO; and Robert TALIAFERRO III. He married second Margaret BUCKNER and died June 6, 1726, at St. Paul's Parish, King G
2 CONC eorge, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
