1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT Notes for Francis Williamson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills and Administration of Isle of Wight Co., V A, v. 2, page 1 16 (Reese Library) original page  47. "Williamson. Francis, Leg. Wife Ann, sons Arthur, Joseph. Benjamin, granddaughter Mourning  Williamson, daughter MARTHA ATKINSO
2 CONC N, grandson. Francis Williamson. Arthur Williamson  and Burwell, Joseph. Hardy, Absolom, Benjamin and James Williamson. Executors Arthur and  Benjamin Williamson. Died May 14, 1743, Recorded August 22, 1743." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Francis Williamson and Ann Exum are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Martha 5 Williamson, bom Abt. 1690; died Abt. 1740 in Isle of Wight Co, VA. 
2 CONT * Francis Williamson, Jr. died 1737
2 CONT * Arthur Williamson, died 1772. 
2 CONT * Joseph Williamson, died 1753. 
2 CONT * Benjamin Williamson, died 1772
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheetyson&id=I00556
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in his father’s 1669 will.
2 CONT
2 CONT A copy of Robert's will still exists. It is dated 16 February 1669. In the will Robert leaves his possessions to his wife and children. Among these possessions are a considerable number of AFrican slaves. The will was probated on 
2 CONC 2 May 1670. This means Robert died sometime between February 1669 and May 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT >”"In the Name of God Amen, the Sixteenth Day of February A Dom 1669 - I, Robert Williamson of the Isle of Wight County in Virginia, Doctr in Phisicke: ...
2 CONT
2 CONT >”Item: I give all my land att Blackwater, beinge three thousand seven hundred acres, more or less, wyh all the appaurtenances thereto belonginge, into my deere and welbeloved sonns, Robert, George, Arthur, & '''Francis''', & to t
2 CONC he heirs of theire bodies, lawfully begotten for ever, to be equally divided between my said sonns, share and share alike, & in case my said sonns or any of them shall dye wyhout such heirs then my will and intent & meaninge is th
2 CONC at the pte & share of said land of him or them soe dyeing shall come to & be divided amoungest the sivivors, of them & their heirs. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT >”... And my other negro called great Moll, I give into my said Sonne Francis & his heirs for ever, from and after the death of my said wife. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * ''Historical Southern Families. Volume III'' [database on-line].    “Williamson Family of Isle of Wight County, VA.”  Page 160.  < [https://www.ancestry.com/sharing/6316717?mark=7b22746f6b656e223a2233722b74724f3342366769344b6939
2 CONC 576f3358786e4441335139444573354d715230707477794f326e33453d222c22746f6b656e5f76657273696f6e223a225632227d AncestrySharing] >
