1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A010356 DAR Ancestor # A010356] 1) PRINCE EDWARD COUNTY MILITIA
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAMSON & PHILEMON WHO MARRIED MARY LEE ARE BROTHERS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Williamson Bird m. 1750 Phbe Price (b. 1732); 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Williamson Bird, Sr.
2 CONT *   Born 1728 Prince Edward, Virginia 1
2 CONT *      Died  Buried March 1802 Wilkes County, Georgia, USA
2 CONT *     Father Robert BIRD (P353) 2, 3, 4
2 CONT *Mother Adicia Dicia "Dicey" WILLIAMSON (P344)   Married 1739 Virginia, United States 1, 5
2 CONT * Wife  Phoebe PRICE (P316) 5    Born 1721 Virginia, United States 5   Christened   Died Wilkes, Georgia, United States   Buried    Father () Mother ()
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - dates need work !!! Yes, dates are way off! Here are updated dates which may or may not be correct:
2 CONT
2 CONT However, they are closer and backed up by other data. Marriage date seems right @ 1750
2 CONT
2 CONT Dyce, 1750 John 1754 Philemon 1761 Price 1762 Fanny 1767  Williamson 1772-1842 Caty 1776 Tabitha 1778-1858 Betsy 1785
2 CONT
2 CONT *   F Catherine "Caty" BIRD (P297)   Born   Christened   Died   Buried   Spouse Leonard SWITZER (P295) 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11
2 CONT * F Betsy BIRD (P350) 13 1785 - Georgia USA 12  F   Born   Christened   Died   Buried   Spouse Michael WOODALL (P376)
2 CONT *  M Price BIRD (P352)   Born 1738 Virginia, United States   Christened   Died 1820 Putnam, Georgia, United States   Buried
2 CONT *  M Philemon BIRD (P351)    Born 1740 Virginia, United States   Christened   Died 1810 Wilkes, Georgia, United States   Buried
2 CONT *  F Fanny BIRD (P349)   Born 1744 Virginia, United States
2 CONT *  F Dyce BIRD (P348)   Born  Christened 1746 Virginia, United States    Died Georgia, United States   Buried
2 CONT *  F Tabitha BIRD (P347)   Born 1748 Virginia, United States   Christened   Died  Buried
2 CONT *M John BIRD (P346) Georgia, United States    M    Born 1754 Virginia, United States    Christened    Died   Buried Georgia, United States   
2 CONT *M Williamson BIRD (P345) 14    Born   Christened 30 Nov 1772 Prince Edward, Virginia, United States     Died 1842 Crawfordsville, Wilkes, Georgia, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: BIRD, WILLIAMSON. 
2 CONT *To son Price 100 acres where he now lives. 
2 CONT *To son Philemon 100 acres where he now lives. 
2 CONT *To daus, Betsy Woodall and Fanny Price, certain slaves. 
2 CONT *To dau. Tabitha slave and bed. 
2 CONT *To dau. Caty Switcher a slave. 
2 CONT *To dau. Dyce a slave and bed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Oct 25 1809   Wilkes Co., GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Williamson Bird, Philemon's older brother, purchased property in Wilkes County, Georgia in 1785, and presumably moved to Georgia shortly thereafter. The deed is recorded as Joseph Williams and wife, Frankey, of Wilkes Co., having 
2 CONC sold to Williamson Bird of Prince Edward County, Virginia, 400 acres of land on Upton's Creek, adjoining the property of Gideon Anderson and William Thorton. The transaction was recorded January 26, 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philemon migrated southward to Wilkes County, Georgia, around the late 1780's, joining his brother, Williamson. The earliest record of Philemon's arrival in Wilkes County is recorded in Deed Book CC, and is dated January 1787. The
2 CONC  land transaction was recorded as William Bentley selling 300 acres of land to Philemon Bird. The land is described as 300 acres on the Little River, adjoining John Bell. Testators were listed as Daniel Price, Balaam Bentley, and 
2 CONC Job Bird.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 16, 1802, the Creek Indians ceded their lands in Georgia in a treaty, which was signed at Fort Wilkinson. This land included "the Territory south of the Oconee and Altamaha rivers", and was divided into three separate coun
2 CONC ties - Wayne, Wilkinson, and Baldwin. The land was divided into various sized lots, depending on in which county they were located, and given away in lotteries to settlers who met specific qualifications. The Lottery of 1803, list
2 CONC s Philemon Bird, Sr. as qualifying for two draws of this lottery. To qualify for these two draws, Philemon was a free white male, twenty-one years or older, and resident of the state for at least one-year prior the passage of the 
2 CONC lottery act, who had paid tax; having a wife and one or more legitimate children. Philemon's brother, Williamson, is also listed as receiving two draws. Another Philemon Bird is listed as receiving two draws, and is probably Phile
2 CONC mon's son, Philemon Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT A similar lottery in 1806 gave settlers of the same qualifications lots of 202.5 acres each. In this lottery, Philemon, Sr. received two draws for himself, and one draw for his deceased son, Philemon, Jr. Philemon, Sr. is listed a
2 CONC s being grandfather of the orphans of the deceased Philemon, Jr. Philemon, Sr.'s brother, Williamson, is once again listed near Philemon, and received two draws.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
