2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Carter-7639
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters of the American Revolution
2 CONT Joseph Carter is a DAR Patriot [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A019999 Ancestor, A019999] 
2 CONT Joseph Carter is a proven Rev. War Patriot.
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpts from Miller, Campbell, _The descendants of Capt. Thomas Carter of "Barford", Lancaster County, Virginia, 1652-1912_.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Carter, second son of Thomas and Arabella Williamson Carter, born in 1696-1697 at "Barford," Lancaster, died in April 1751, in Spotsylvania. .... He lived in his native county until 1738, when he removed to Spotsylvania, wh
2 CONC ere he had a grant of 215 acres of land, to which he added 89 acres in 1739, one hundred acres in 1749, another hundred in 1749, and a hundred and ninety in 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1724-1725 until 1738, Jos. Carter was Tobacco Inspector at the port of Corotoman; and from correspondence relative to the manner in which he performed his duty, we get the only insight we have of his character, from which we 
2 CONC may draw the conclusion that he was a man who had a strength of character and purpose sufficient to do his duty as he saw it, even in the face of strong opposition and unpopularity.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1719 Joseph Carter married Catharine Stevens, daughter of James Stevens, of King and Queen county .... Joseph Carter, of St. George's parish, Spotsylvania, made his will Feb. 19, 1750, probated May 7, 1751. .... Catharine Carte
2 CONC r was still living in 1771, when she made a deed to her son, John Carter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Thomas Williamson Carter, born May 8, 1720; killed by the accidental discharge of a gun Christmas week, 1738.
2 CONT # Mary Elizabeth, born Dec 2, 1721, in King and Queen County, married James Davis of "Broadfield," Spotsylvania.
2 CONT # Edward Dale, born Jun 2, 1723, died prior to 1750.
2 CONT # John, born Jun 8, 1725.
2 CONT # George, born Dec 18, 1728.
2 CONT # Elizabeth, born Sep 20, 1731
2 CONT # Joseph and 
2 CONT # Catharine, twins, born May 3, 1733
2 CONT # Robert, born Aug 12, 1735
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * 1749-1759 Spotsylvania County, Virginia Will Book B; [William Armstrong Crozier];
2 CONT * CARTER, JOSEPH, St. George's Parish, d. Feb. 19, 1750, p. May 7, 1751. Wit. Robert Huddlestone, Wm. Pruitt, James Younger, Robert Durrett. Ex. wife, Catharine Carter; Mr. John Minor and my son, John Carter. Leg. wife, Catharine;
2 CONC  son, Joseph Carter, the tract of land bought of Mark Wheeler; son, John, tract of land bought of Benj. Matthews; daughter Mary Carter; daughter, Elizabeth Carter; son, George Carter; son, Robert Carter, the land where I now live 
2 CONC after his mother's decease; daughter, Caty Carter. Page 64)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * CARTER, Thomas. Will. 24 Apl. 1728. Rec. 10 Oct. 1733. Wife Arabella; sons: Thomas, land where I now live;. Peter, land in King George County, James, Dale, Charles, Edward, Joseph and Daniel. Gr.sons Jesse Carter and Thos. Carte
2 CONC r. Extrs. Wife and son Peter. Wits. John Harry and Job Carter. W.B. 12, p. 279
