2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Daniel Carter''', Daniel Carter, third son of Captain Thomas Carter, Jr., of "Barford," and his wife, Arabella Williamson, was born in 1700 and died in 1759 in his native county. He owned a farm of about 350 acres and eight ser
2 CONC vants.
2 CONT
2 CONT He seems not to have held any official position in his county and parish, and appears but three times in the county records. First, May 17, 1725, when he was the attorney for his friend, Robert Briscoe, at court; second, in his fa
2 CONC ther's will in 1728, when he received a negro woman and a share in the residency estate ; and last, when his own estate was appraised and divided between his wife and seven of his nine children. One son had had a disagreement with
2 CONC  his father and left home and was lost sight of before Daniel Carter died. The eldest son is supposed to have had his portion previously to his father's death, so did not appear in the division.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Elizabeth Pannill (daughter of Thomas & Sarah).  9 children
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/carter/18712/
2 CONT
2 CONT Child(ren) of Daniel of St. Mary's Carter and Elizabeth Pannill (daughter of Thomas Panbell)  married Abt 1720, Lancaster County, Virginia.  She was born about 1704 and died about 1785.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Patriot William Pannil Carter M.1.ca. 1723-- Lancaster Co VA1794-- Prince William Co VA
2 CONT * 2. Patriot Thomas Carter M.1.1725-06-04 Lancaster Co VAGA or SC
2 CONT * 3. Patriot John Carter M.1.ca. 1727-- Lancaster Co VA ca. 1775-- VA
2 CONT * 4. Patriot Joseph Carter M.1.ca. 1729-- Lancaster Co VA
2 CONT * 5. Patriot Robert Carter M.1.1731-08-12 Lancaster Co VA1792-02- Sumter Co SC
2 CONT * 6. Margaret Carter M.1.ca. 1733-- Lancaster Co VA
2 CONT * 7. Mary Elizabeth Carter M.1.ca. 1735-- Lancaster Co VA
2 CONT * 8. Frances Carter M.1.dspca. 1737-- Lancaster Co VA1830-- Lancaster Co VA
2 CONT * 9. Patriot Daniel Carter M.1.1738-- Lancaster Co VA1794-10-01 Lancaster Co VA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources state that Daniel left Virginia for Kentucky and that is where he died in 1759.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/carter/messages/16931.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel's estate was inventoried 16 November 1759. (LVA has Wills & Administrations for a Daniel Carter of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 17 May 1725, Daniel served as an attorney for Robert Biscoe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Carter, Sr.'s personal estate amounted to £343 2s. 4d. and included eight negroes, a sword, books, and the usual furniture. It was returned to court in Lancaster on Nov. 16, 1759.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources of Information: ''The Descendants of Captain Thomas Carter'' by Joseph Lyon Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT CARTER, Thomas. Will. 24 Apl. 1728. Rec. 10 Oct. 1733. Wife Arabella; sons: Thomas, land where I now live;. Peter, land in King George County, James, Dale, Charles, Edward, Joseph and Daniel. Gr.sons Jesse Carter and Thos. Carter.
2 CONC  Extrs. Wife and son Peter. Wits. John Harry and Job Carter. W.B. 12, p. 279.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
