1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/13620317/peter-carter
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A Patriot of the American Revolution for  VIRGINIA.    [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A020037  DAR Ancestor #  A020037]
2 CONT
2 CONT Info copied from [http://www.tonycoxhome.com/cox2005-p/p7.htm#i330 Anthony W. Cox Geneology].  See also ''[http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofcap00mill#page/n7/mode/2up The Decendents of CAPT Thomas Carter]''
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Carter served in the revolutionary war. He inherited half of his father's five hundred acre plantation in King George County where he lived until late in his life when he moved to Fauquire County with his son George -- ''Ame
2 CONC rican Genealogical Research Institute, A History of the Carter Family, p 221''
2 CONT
2 CONT On his date of death: This profile previously had May 15, 1765, but that would have made it impossible for him to have served in the war. Contrarily, [http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofcap00mill#page/n633/mode/2up The des
2 CONC cendants of Capt. Thomas Carter of "Barford", Lancaster County, Virginia, 1652-1912] page 225 puts his year of death as Dec 1789 or Jan 1790, which seems more plausible.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/13620317/peter-carter Find-A-Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Carter, Sr. was born May 23, 1706, in Lancaster county, Virginia and at the time of the American Revolution was residing in Fauquier County, Virginia created in 1759. In 1783, in Fauquier County, Peter paid supply tax to the
2 CONC  newly formed United States of America. [1] This tax was used to create the First Census of the United States published in 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Carter, Sr. is honored for his Patriotic Service by the Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution as DAR Ancestor #A020037. DAR records indicate that Peter died in December, 1789, in Fauquier county, Virginia and t
2 CONC hat his wife was Judith Norris. [2] Peter and Judith were married May 1, 1730 [3]
