2 CONT === !Charles was under twenty years of age w ===
2 CONT !Charles was under twenty years of age when his father made his will in 1728, and was left in the care of his brother Peter until he reached that age. He inherited a good plantation of several hundred acres of land in Stafford fro
2 CONC m his father, who at one time owned twenty-four hundred acres of land in that county.  His will dated 21 June 1766, was probated 1 Dec 1766. He died 2 Nov 1766. He left to each of his five children two negroes and the rest of his 
2 CONC estate to "loving wife Lucy" during the rest of her lifetime.
