1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It might be interesting in these days of equal rights for women, to mention an ancestress, Sarah Shelton, daughter of Charles Shelton, a commander in the British Navy, who was lost with his ship, the Coronation, in
2 CONC  the English Channel, in September, 1691. Tradition says that Sarah came with her brother, William, to Virginia, where she married Richard Gissage, a merchant from London, who settled in New Kent, now King William county. She must
2 CONC  have been a most impressive person, as her second son, Ralph, took as his surname, the maiden name of his mother, being known as Ralph Shelton, of St. Mary's Parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/ga/baldwin/history/other/gms293historyo.txt
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/a/r/James-D-Garrett/BOOK-0001/0006-0041.html
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT M i Ralph Gissage SHELTON
2 CONT
2 CONT F ii Mary GISSAGE
2 CONT
2 CONT F iii Christian GISSAGE 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
