1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Buckner was born ABT 1689 in , Gloucester Co., Virginia, and died 1731 in , Gloucester Co., Virginia. She was the daughter of 6. Richard Buckner and 7. Elizabeth Sampson.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT # 2.	Mordecai Cooke was born ABT 1660 in , Gloucester Co., Virginia, and died 1718 in , Gloucester Co., Virginia. He was the son of Thomas Cooke and Mary Hubbard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Buckner and Mordecai Cooke are:
2 CONT # Mordecai Cooke,   b. Abt 1709, 'Wareham' Gloucester County, Virginia, d.  . 5 Apr 1751. Married Elizabeth Whiting.  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Cooke was born ABT 1712 in , Gloucester Co., Virginia, and died 1800 in Hamilton Parish, Fauquier Co., Virginia. She married William Pickett 1728 in Cople Parish, Westmoreland Co., Virginia, son of John Pickett and Mar
2 CONC y. He was born ABT 1700 in ,, Virginia, and died 1766 in Hamilton Parish, Fauquier Co., Virginia.
2 CONT # Jemima Cooke. She married Thomas Chilton 1723, son of John Chilton II. He was born 1699, and died 1765/1775 in , Fauquier Co., Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Buckner  married ... Elizabeth Sampson, the daughter of Thomas Sampson and his first wife, Elizabeth Johnson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Buckner died before 7 May 1734 when the Inventory of his estate was submitted before distribution could take place. Richard's wife, Elizabeth, she died after 7 May 1734, and before 1735. Richard and Elizabeth had the follo
2 CONC wing children validated and proven:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Buckner died before 7 May 1734 when the Inventory of his estate was submitted before distribution could take place. Richard's wife, Elizabeth, she died after 7 May 1734, and before 1735. Richard and Elizabeth had the follo
2 CONC wing children Ã¢ÂÂ validated and proven. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Buckner married 1st, William Bernard, Jr. - married 2nd, William Thornton, Sr. - Issue with both husbands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Buckner, born 1684, died after 1727 - married Ann Robinson - we have no proof of issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Buckner married Mordecai Cooke, son of Thomas Cooke and his wife, Mary Hubbard'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Buckner, Sr. married Jane Aylett, daughter of William Aylett Sr. and his wife, Ann Woodward Taylor. Ann was the widow of Christopher Robinson who died 1728. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Buckner, married Sarah Hubbard, daughter of Robert Hubbard and his wife, Jane Buckner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although he owned two small parcels of land in Caroline County, Richard and wife, Elizabeth Sampson, never lived there. He resided in Stafford County in 1691 and in Spotsylvania County before 1721, when it was formed. We can prove
2 CONC  three land grants to Richard in Spotsylvania County. We have Road Orders that prove his residency there from 1722 through 1734, the year of his death. The records presented below were compiled from the Spotsylvania County Road Or
2 CONC der Book 1722-1734. The following proofs read exactly as written without editing.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
