2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/147720374/hannah-anne-moore?_gl=1*1j7wbbv*_gcl_au*ODcxODEwNjI1LjE3MDE2MTg3NjU.*_ga*MTQ1NDM0Mjg2NS4xNjUzMjYwODQ4*_ga_4QT8FMEX30*Y2Y3ZGJkNDAtYTBiZi00NTM4LTk1OTEtZTZiODgxZjM5MDQzLjU5LjEuMTcwNDgzMzU
2 CONC zOC41OS4wLjA.*_ga_LMK6K2LSJH*Y2Y3ZGJkNDAtYTBiZi00NTM4LTk1OTEtZTZiODgxZjM5MDQzLjU3LjEuMTcwNDgzMzUzOC4wLjAuMA..
2 CONT HANNAH "ANNE" RANSDELL MOORE
2 CONT
2 CONT = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Ransdell was born October 22, 1758, in Fauquier County, Virginia, the daughter of William and Mary (Chilton) Ransdell. She married William Grant Moore on January 8, 1779, in Fauquier County, Virginia. Hannah's father was al
2 CONC ready deceased at the time of her marriage so her brother Wharton Ransdell was the bondsman. William was born March 5, 1753, in Louisa County, Virginia, the son of Samuel and Charity (Courts) Moore. Hannah and William had the foll
2 CONC owing known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hannah Ransdell Moore (1780-1863)
2 CONT 2. William H. Moore (1781)
2 CONT 3. Sarah Moore (1781-1860)
2 CONT 4. Henley William Moore (1782-?) Married Jane J. Russell
2 CONT 5. Wharton Ransdell Moore (1783-1850) Married Mary Elizabeth Browning
2 CONT 6. William Grant Moore (1785-1818)
2 CONT 7. Thomas Ransdell Moore (1785-1844) Married Evaline Hockaday
2 CONT 8. Anne E. Moore (1786-1898)
2 CONT 9. John Whitney Moore (1787-1844) Married Mary Grant
2 CONT 10. Mary Elizabeth Coates Moore (1788-1836 or 1851) Married James S. Gray
2 CONT 11. Charles Chilton Moore (1789-1860) Married May Ann Harrison Stone
2 CONT 12. Margaret J. Moore (1790-?)
2 CONT 13. James Moore (1790-?)
2 CONT 14. Elizabeth G. Moore (1791-1840) Married Henry Brite
2 CONT 15. Aaron Jackson Moore (1792-1855)
2 CONT 16. Nancy Ann Moore (1792-1851) Married Benjamin Young
2 CONT 17. Stephen Moore 1792-?)
2 CONT 18. Samuel Turner Moore (1794-1833)
2 CONT 19. Ann Chilton Moore (1795-1896)
2 CONT 20. Mary Margaret Moore (1796-1815)
2 CONT 21. Henry Moore (1798-?)
2 CONT 22. Charles Moore (1800-?)
2 CONT
2 CONT William was an officer in the Revolutionary war, he was a Sergeant and a Lieutenant in the Virginia line in the company of John Chilton. They moved to Fayette County, Kentucky about 1790 to claim William's bounty land where they l
2 CONC ived the rest of their lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah died October 1810 in Fayette County, Kentucky. She was buried on their Poplar Hill farm which is located 8 miles north of Lexington, Fayette County, Kentucky. William then married Margaret L. Browning and they one one son. 
2 CONC William died May 1818, in Fayette County, Kentucky and he was buried with Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
