1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rawleigh TRAVERS was born ABT 1622 in England, and died BEF 14 MAY 1670 in Richmond Co., VA. He was the son of 2. Mr. TRAVERS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Raleigh Travers, patented land on Rappahannock river in 1653; justice of the peace for Lancaster county in 1656; burgess for Lancaster in 1651, 1661, 1665, 1666 and 1669. He was lieutenant-colonel of the Lancaster militia. He died
2 CONC  before 1674, as in that year his widow Elizabeth married Robert Beckingham. He was brother of Colonel William Travers, of Richmond county. Virginia Biography, pg 344.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT # unknown 
2 CONT # Elizabeth 17 NOV 1654 in Lancaster Co., VA. She was born ABT 1637 in England, and died AFT 14 JUL 1703 in Lancaster Co., VA. perhaps Hussey, widow Stephens
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT * William, by 1st wife 
2 CONT *1. John Travers b. 1656, Lancaster County, Virginia 
2 CONT *2. Elizabeth Travers, b. Bef 1660, Lancaster County, Virginia , d. 5 Mar 1692/93, Christ Church Parish, Middlesex County, Virginia - Probate 
2 CONT *3. Rawleigh Travers, b. 1660, Northumberland County, Virginia d. 1701, Stafford County, Virginia  (Age 41 years)
2 CONT *4. Million Travers b. 1660, Lancaster County, Virginia d. 8 Jun 1727, North Farnham Parish, Richmond County, Virginia - Probate
2 CONT *5. Giles Travers b. Abt 1661, Lancaster County, Virginia d. 11 Sep 1717, Stafford County, Virginia - Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT !7 Aug 1654: Elizabeth and Raleigh Travers deeded to John Chynn of Lancaster Co. VA one forth right in Traver's Mill.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
