1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Francis-Tyler/6000000027239328012?through=6000000009216219330 and his wife Rebecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A John Tyler lived at Falmouth in Stafford County, but he appears to have been too old a man to have been John Tyler, third son of I Francis Tyler.  His will was made November 4, 1755, and proved in King George County, June 2, 175
2 CONC 7. By his wife Mary Downman, he had one child, '''Margaret''', who married first, William Waugh, September 10, 1738, and had issue: ... She married 2ndly, Daniel Royalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of the Waugh-Tyler Marriage
2 CONT # John Tyler Waugh was born on 28 February 1739 in Overton Parish, Virginia. He married 1) Margaret Mauzey (1738-1773) c. 1760 and 2) Mary Crump (c. 1750- ) on 25 August 1773 in Fauquier County, Virginia. Tyler died on 27 December
2 CONC  1776 in Overton Parish, Virginia, United States.
2 CONT # Priscilla Waugh was born on 22 October 1741 in Overton Parish, Virginia. She married Peter Mauzy (1730-1799) on 15 May 1763 in Overwharton Parish, Stafford, Virginia. Priscilla died c. 1801.
2 CONT # Million Waugh, daughter, was born c. 1745 in Prince William, Virginia.
2 CONT # William Waugh was born in 1747 in Virginia.
2 CONT # Thomas Waugh
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no record found for her death. She may have died in 1769 with the birth of her last child to Royalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from Familysearch under collaborate tab for Margaret Tyler.
2 CONT
2 CONT Register of Overwharton Parish--Margaret Tyler was the only child of John Tyler of Brunswick Parish, King George County, who died in 1756. William Waugh died in 1748 and his widow married Daniel Royalty of Overwharton Parish. The 
2 CONC last will and testament of JOHN TYLER mentioned his five grandchildren--Tyler, William, Thomas, Priscilla and Million Waugh. He also decreed that Daniel Royalty should not enjoy any part of his estate..  (this seems to prove to me
2 CONC  John Tyler, NOT Henry Francis Tyler was father of Margaret Tyler who married William Waugh and Daniel Royalty.
2 CONT Contributor
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LVFK-WLP
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage of Daniel Royalty & Margaret Tyler
2 CONT 5 February 1752
2 CONT Stafford, Virginia, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Last child born to Margaret and her first husband was in 1748, and the history's ["The Waugh Way West", and family group sheets from J Abrams [1989] and J Henry [1999] [I'm no longer sure which of these second which parts of the i
2 CONC nformation I have]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/sources/LVFK-WLP
2 CONT
2 CONT On Feb. 5, 1752 Margaret Tyler Waugh was involved in proving her dower rights of property of her previous husband William Waugh who had died in 1748. Daniel was named as her present husband in those proceedings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret had the following children by William Waugh: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla, Thomas, Million, and William. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his marriage, Daniel went to Albermarle Co. and enlisted in the Virginia Militia under Col."s Byrd and Washington for 5 years from 1754 to 1759, he took up land in Amherst Co. in 1761 and lived there until his death in about
2 CONC  1810. Daniel apparently had two brothers, John and Isham who seemed to follow him from place to place. Isham was in Albermarle at the time Daniel was serving in the militia during the French and Indian war. He and John later are 
2 CONC found in Amherst Co. after Daniel took up land there. John and Isham later married sisters Sally and Patsy Muse in Amherst Co. on the same day in 1797. Daniel is found on a list of Amherst Co. surveys with 65 acres of land on May 
2 CONC 3, 1766. He is later listed as a witness to a deed in 1791. He is found in the 1810 census for Amherst Co and probably died about that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disproved
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of FRANCIS TYLER and REBECCA [NO] are:
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. MARGARET TYLER, b. Abt. 1720, VA; m. WILLIAM WAUGH, September 10, 1738, Stafford County, VA; b. Abt. 1718, VA. More About WILLIAM WAUGH and MARGARET TYLER: Marriage: September 10, 1738, Stafford County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT
