1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Thomas Pinkard
2 CONT * aka Pinckard
2 CONT * Born about 1660 [uncertain] in Lancaster County, Colony of Virginia 
2 CONT * Died about 1740 [uncertain] at about age 80 in Lancaster County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT * Son of John Pinkard and Elizabeth Jones
2 CONT * Husband of Margaret (Swan) Pinckard — married before 12 Mar 1709 (to before 22 Apr 1727) in Lancaster County, Colony of Virginia at age 49
2 CONT * Husband of Elizabeth (Downman) Pinkard — married 22 Apr 1727 in Richmond County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT ”Pinkard Family,” from ''William & Mary College Quarterly Magazine'', p.262 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Captain Thomas2 Pinkard (John1) was justice of Lancaster in 1702. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, first, Margaret, daughter of Captain Alexander Swann * (will of Capt. Swann proved in Lancaster, 1709.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, second, Elizabeth Downman (Hayden, Va. Genealogies, 74), daughter of William Downman, who names his “daughter Elizabeth Downman” in his will, proved in Richmond county, June 8, 1727. Her mother was Million Travers (dau
2 CONC ghter of Capt. William Travers.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue named in his will proved Oct. 10, 1740, 14 
2 CONT *Thomas 3, 15
2 CONT *John3, 16 
2 CONT *Eliza, married, 1721 (i.) Major Charles3 Lee (Charles2, Richard1) ; married (ii.) Brent. 17 
2 CONT *Margaret, married John Ball.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstract of the Will of Thomas Pinckard 1740 (From Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia Wills from 1653 to 1800, by Ida J. Lee, p 182) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Pinckard, Thos. 29 Aug 1740, Rec 10 Oct 1740 
2 CONT *Wife. Elizabeth.
2 CONT *Sons: Thos., all land I now live on; John.
2 CONT * Daus: Eliza Brent and Margaret Ball.
2 CONT *Exors: Sons and cousin Wm. Stepto.
2 CONT *Wits: Thos. Stepto and Thos Bridgford.
2 CONT *"That my daughter Margaret Ball may be maintained out of my estate as long as she behaves herself well and lives from her husband John Ball." 
2 CONT *WB 13, pg 183
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ulrich800&id=I1768 (dead link)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pinkard's (only) child by his third wife Elizabeth Jones Haynes was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Pinkard who married 1st Margaret Swan & 2nd Elizabeth Downman
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT >thomas appears to have two daughters named Elizabeth, one married Charles Lee in 1721 and the other to William Brent abt 1735.; refer to his son' John's 1743 will. (??)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT
2 CONT #”Pinkard Family,” from ''William & Mary College Quarterly Magazine'', p.262 ("Eliza, married, 1721 (i.) Major Charles3 Lee (Charles2, Richard1) ; married (ii.) Brent.") < [https://archive.org/details/williammarycolle1219will/page
2 CONC /262/mode/1up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT # http://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I058129&tree=Tree1
