1 NAME Mary /Smoot/
2 GIVN Mary
2 SURN Smoot
2 _MARNM Gilbert
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1646
2 ADDR
3 STAE Maryland Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 3 SEP 1707
2 PLAC North Farnham Parish
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Mary Smoot
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1646 - St. Mary's County, Maryland
2 CONT * Death:	From Sep 3 1707 - North Farnham Parish, Rappahannock, Virginia, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Husband:	James Gilbert
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary stated she was upwards of 61 years in 1707. which would give her a birth date of about 1646. This fits the fact that she wasn't listed as one of the children that William Smoot brought to Maryland in 1646; she was born after 
2 CONC the Smoot family's arrival. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy and Thomas Durham. Dorothy and Thomas Durham also received from Mary (Smoot) Gilbert a gift of deed of 50 acres which adjoined the land given by William Smoot. The recording of the deed is listed: "At a court held for Rich
2 CONC mond County the third day of September 1707 ... this day Mary Gilbert acknowledged a deed for land to Thomas Durham which is ordered to be recorded. This day WILLIAM SMOOT acknowledged a release of his right and title of a parcell
2 CONC  of land sold by Mary GILBERT to Thomas DURHAM, and on motion of said Thomas the same is ordered to be recorded” [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The relationship between William Smoot and Dorothy Durham and Mary Gilbert is unknown but William's release of his right to land sold by Mary Gilbert does indicate some type of family relationship that needs further research.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Smoot-350
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy, wife of Thomas Durham and mother of his three youngest children, was the daughter of Mary (Smoot) Gilbert, youngest sister of William Smoot. This relationship is based on speculation as there is no documented proof of thi
2 CONC s relationship.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was often speculated that Dorothy was a daughter of William Smoot Jr., who was actually Dorothy's maternal uncle. William Smoot Jr. conveyed property to Dorothy Durham in 1700 "with love and affection." Based on the various rec
2 CONC ords there does appear to be a family relationship of some type. The relationship between Dorothy and William Smoot is based on speculation as there is no documented proof of the relationship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Various records prove that Dorothy Durham, Thomazin Goodridge, and Alice Chinn were all sisters[11] However, the women are only recorded by their married names. The maiden name has not been proved.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no Documents which prove that Mary, wife of James Gilbert was a Smoot and there are no documents which prove she was the mother of Dorothy Durham, or Dorothy's sisters, Alice and Thomasin. There was a family relationship
2 CONC  of some type but there are no Documents which prove what the relationship was. See: https://dna-explained.com/2017/06/25/dorothy-durhams-parents-and-the-mysterious-william-smoot-52-ancestors-165/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Research Found on the Smoot/ Gilbert Connection
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I21565&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Solved by Janean Ray
2 CONT
2 CONT In going through old papers.. I've come across something of interest.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is alleged that the 3 girls in question.. Alice, Thomasin and Dorothy are the daughters of Mary Smoot Gilbert sister to William Smoot.
2 CONT
2 CONT William acknowledged a deed by Mary to Thomas Durham and wife Dorothy to wit: 50 acres of Buory Swamp (which is how someone transcribed it dated 1707)
2 CONT
2 CONT On 29 Apr 1700 North Neck Grants 2:315 Richmond Co. William Smoot Sr. 262 acres in Richmond Co. adj. his other land, Bryary Swamp, James GILBERT, Mr. Lueson, etc. line,
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This would make perfect sense that Mary Gilbert and William Smoot were brother and sister... that this land Bryary Swamp was bequeathed to them by their father.. And Mary Smoot Gilbert could therefore be the wife of the above Jame
2 CONC s Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a will of James Gilbert of North Farnham Parish 31 Jan 1701/2 - 7 June 1704 but wife's name not given.
2 CONT
2 CONT So if Mary Smoot was the wife of James Gilbert (him passing before her as she was listed in the indenture to Thomas and Dorothy dated 1707 as Widow.. They most likely appear to be the parents of Dorothy. therefore also Alice and T
2 CONC homasin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Dorothy Durham had son Thomas that DID marry... Mary Smoot... daughter of William and Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT William then made a bequeath to Dorothy... 02 Aug 1700. Richmond Co, VA DB03:057. William SMOOT, Sr. of North Farnham Parish to Dorothy DURHAM, wife of Thomas DURHAM; for love and affection for Dorothy and her children, 62 acres i
2 CONC n Richmond County; if Dorothy should die, land to her eldest, Thomas DURHAM; if Thomas should die, to John DURHAM; if he should die without issue, land to Mary DURHAM, daughter of sd. Dorothy. Wits: Jno: SIMMONS, Tho: MACKEY. Jane
2 CONC  SMOOT, wife of William, relinquished dower. (DNFP)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Dec. 1702 Richmond Co. Order Book 4 p. 38... nonsuite is granted to Thomas Durham and Dorothy his wife for the non appearance of Wm Smoot Jr. which is ordered to be paid with cost of suit asl Exo. (Exo iss. 8th December 1702)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1704 OB4p 107.. Ordered that Charles Dodson, William Smoot and George Devenport or any two of them .... do meet at the house of James GILBERT, dec'd and do inventory the estate.... Capt. John Tarpley is requested to administer an 
2 CONC oath to Mary, the wife of said James.etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond Co. Order Bk 4 p 5 Nov. 1. 1704.. Pursuant to an order of court the 3rd day of Aug 1704 granted upon the petition of Mary GILBERT .. of the last will and testament of James GILBERT dec'd to prove the will.. Etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Feb 1704 NN Grants William Smoot of Richmond Co. possessed 409 a in said Co part of 1156 a granted Samuel Griffin. etc... on Briery Swamp of Farnham Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Nov 1704 Richmond Co. Misc Records Bk 1 pp 26-28 depositions respecting the will of James Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Sept 1707 Mary Gilbert acknowledged a deed for land to Thomas Durham which is ordered to be recorded..and on this day William Smoot acknowledged a release of his right and title of a parcel of land sold by Mary Gilbert to Thomas
2 CONC  Durham.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Nov. 1708 - 6 July 1709. Will of Abraham MARSHALL wife Thomasin use of plantation and lands and after her death to daughter Mary Campbell.. etc etc.. son in law Alexander Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Durham's 1711 will made reference twice to that 50 acres trying to ensure the property stayed within the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomasin m. William Goodridge and he m. provision that Rawleigh Chinn have the care of his 3 children, William, Moses and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1714/15 Dorothy Durham widow m. Jeremiah Greenham
2 CONT
2 CONT 1725 Will of Ann Chinn daughter of sister ALICE mentions her Aunt Dorothy Greenham wife of Jeremiah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Alice Stretchley mentions sisters Dorothy Durham and Thomasin Marshall as well as cousin (neice) Mary Dodson who was the daughter of Thomas Durham and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT This "Compilation of Smoot Records" is about 30 pages of records/abstracts like this. I believe this is enough evidence..to consider that the scenario is this:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Smoot and Mary Smoot were sister and brother
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Smoot m. James Gilbert and they had daughters Alice
2 CONT Gilbert.(Chinn/Stretchley) Dorothy Gilbert.(Durham/Greeham) and Thomasin Gilbert.(Marshall/Goodrige)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
