1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Montague''', ''of Jamaico'', [fn1] was born Abt. 1670 in Middlesex Co. VA, Christ Church and died Bef. 10 May 1710 in Middlesex Co. (in "Jamiaco"), VA
2 CONT * Parents:  Peter Montague III b: ABT 1634 in Nansemond County, Virginia and Maria Minor b. 1642 Married:
2 CONT # about January 03, 1702/03 to Lettice Lidford, daughter of Abraham Weeks and widow of the Rev. Matthew Lidford. [fn2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Montague and Lettice Lidford:
2 CONT # Elizabeth Montague b: 1699 in Essex County, Virginia [fn3][link 2](see "Discussion")
2 CONT # Abraham Montague b: 28 SEP 1701 in Middlesex County, Virginia
2 CONT # Mary Montague b: ABT 1702
2 CONT # William Montague b: 1706 in Virginia
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT  * [http://www.kykinfolk.com/clark/family/fr058-montague.htm Clark County KyGenWeb]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 11. WILLIAM3 MONTAGUE (Peter2,Peter1), born about 1670, married Lettice (Weeks) Lidford, daughter of Abraham Weeks and widow of the Rev. Matthew Lidford (died 22 March 1692/3), whom she had married 6 Jan. 1691/2. William3 Montag
2 CONC ue was called "of Jamaico" to distinguish him from his uncle; it was presumably the name of his plantation. It was presumably his estate on which Robert Bird was granted administration, 10 May 1710.
2 CONT
2 CONT * iii. Wlliam Montague, born Abt. 1670 in Middlesex Co. VA, Christ Church; died Bef. August 04, 1761; married Lettice Weekes January 03, 1702/03; born Abt. 1670; died 1704 in Middlesex Co. VA, Christ Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Issue: 21 Abraham4, baptized 28 Sept. 1701, left will 3 May 1740 - 16 Sept. 1740, married Charlotte Latane, left will 25 Jan. 1746/7-22 July 1747, daughter of the Rev. Lewis Lantane; 22. Mary4, baptized 23 Feb. 1703/4; 23 Willia
2 CONC m4, married, 3 Dec. 1729, Jane Price. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Discussion==
2 CONT
2 CONT re: daughter Elizabeth from Rootsweb source - can anyone verify?  25 Feb 2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Montague and Maritje Meinerts were the parents of the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Mary Montague, b. 1662 (m. Thomas Payne).
2 CONT * 2. Peter Montague, b. 1666 (m. Elizabeth Merry).
2 CONT * 3. William Montague, b. 1670 (m. Lettice Weekes).
2 CONT * 4. Elizabeth Montague, b. 1673.
2 CONT * 5. Catherine Montague, b. 1676 (m. 1. George Twyman and 2. Philip Warwick).
2 CONT * 6. John Montague, b. 1682. (died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Adventures of Purse and Person, Virginia by John Frederick Dorman.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT # http://www.kykinfolk.com/clark/family/fr058-montague.htm
2 CONT # http://worldconnect.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=wrwoodwa&id=I688
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=tcM40zgdAZgC&lpg=PA652&ots=xKBzoXxj2d&dq=Adventurers%20of%20Purse%20and%20Person%20%3A%20Virginia%20montague&pg=PA652#v=onepage&q&f=false Dorman, John F. Adventurers of Purse and Person, Virgini
2 CONC a, 1607-1624/5.] Baltimore: Genealogical Pub. Co, 2004. Print. p. 657
2 CONT # Pace Family History, Frankfort Genealogical Library, Kentucky Historical Society, Frankfort, Kentucky, 40601-1931
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Footnotes==
2 CONT # William Montague was called "of Jamaico" to distinguish him from his uncle; it was presumably the name of his plantation. It was presumably his estate on which Robert Bird was granted administration, May 10, 1710. Adventures of 
2 CONC Purse and Person pg. 454 LOC
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Montague, born abt 1670, married Lettice Weeks Lidford, daughter of Abraham Weeks and widow of the Rev. Matthew Lidford (died March 22, 1692/3) whom she had married Jan. 6, 1691/2 [49324py.FTW] (KyKinfolk website)
2 CONT ========================
2 CONT * from http://worldconnect.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=wrwoodwa&id=I675
2 CONT * R. Malone, 151 Massachusetts Ave. Congers, NY 10929 advised the Pace Society of America that the Montague line was researched by genealogist, Mrs. R. C. Richardson, and is accurate as indicated in the list of Magna Carta Barons.
2 CONC ..which included William de Montacute (old spelling). The Montagues enter the Pace line and all Paces descended from John Pace II and Elizabeth Montague are of Royal blood. The Montague line goes back to Sir Simon Montacute, Baron
2 CONC  of Shepton who married Anfricia, Daughter of Fergus, King of the Isle of Man in 1300. The Isle of Man is a crown possession of the United Kingdom and lies in the Irish Sea 30 miles west of England, 221 square miles, capitol is Do
2 CONC uglas.
2 CONT * A reprint of the original book "Montague", compiled by G. W. and W. L. Montague, 1886, can be purchased from: Higginson Books, 14-GH Derby Square, Salem, MA per ad in the July/August issue of "The Genealogical Helper". It lists 
2 CONC a sale price of $67 and an original price of $117.
2 CONT
