1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''His wives and children on Geni need a lot of work.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dr. Andrew Robertson''', "a surgeon and physician of great eminence, b. Inverness, Scotd., 1716; grad., Edinburgh, Univ.; entered the army in Flanders; was in battle of Fontenay, 1745; with Braddock in Pa., 1755; escaped with r
2 CONC emnant of his Regt., 20 in number, living for days on acorns; returned to Eng., resigned his com'n, and em. to America with wife and son. Landing at Indian Banks, Rich'd Co., Va., he was entertained most kindly by a Scotch mcht., 
2 CONC Mr. Glasscock [whose daughter he later married]; settled in Lanc. Co, Va.; became leading physician in the No. Neck. A gentleman in feeling and manners, a man of intelligence and of enterprise, his influence was great; uniting wit
2 CONC h Col. Jas. Gordon he contributed not a little to the prosperity of the Presby. ch. in his region, being also an elder. He d. Mar. 1, 1795, ae. 79. He had James Monroe and Margaret McIntosh." (Hayden, 347n., citing Foote S. I. 368
2 CONC ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT This last statement is controversial because there is no other evidence to support it. The idea seems to have originated because Andrew Robertson had a wife with the unusual maiden name Roysdon, while [https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC James-Roberson/6000000011139499142 James Monroe Roberson] gave one of his sons the name Roysdon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Robertson was married four times. The only reference to any of his children by his first wife Ann ? [maybe Munro] is in the diary of Dr. Gordon from Lancaster Co who mentions "Dr Robetson and his poor children." However, Dr
2 CONC . Robertson left many accounts, court records, cases, and a very detailed will. There are references to each and every child except James Monroe Roberson.  
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Horace Edwin Hayden, ''[http://books.google.com/books?id=SJcsAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA347&ots=z5H8Xcn05E&dq=andrew%20robertson%20%22landing%20at%20indian%20banks%22&pg=PA347#v=onepage&q=andrew%20robertson%20%22landing%20at%20indian%20bank
2 CONC s%22&f=false Virginia Genealogies: A Genealogy of the Glassell Family of Scotland and Virginia]'' (1891)
