1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hannah Bushrod  b: ABT 1704. Married 1) Joseph Heale 2) Adam Crump
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I041213&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills of Westmoreland County, Virginia , Page 106
2 CONT * COOPER, HANNAH, 26 Dec. 1738; 29 May 1739.
2 CONT * Bushrod Thomas;
2 CONT * William Sanford son of my sister Elizabeth decd. of Richmond Co. 2500 lbs. of tobacco;
2 CONT * my dau. Elizabeth Meriwether a gold ring;
2 CONT * dau. Sarah Berryman a gold ring;
2 CONT * son John Bushrod a ring;
2 CONT * dau. Hannah Heale;
2 CONT * my late husband Col. Willoughby Allerton who gave his bond for my dau. Hannah Neale, by name of Hannah Bushrod;
2 CONT * son in law William Fauntleroy and his wife Apphia;
2 CONT * son Richard Bushrod land purchased of John Jewel and his wife Elizabeth;
2 CONT * I desire my son Richard Bushrod to bury me between his father and Mr. Cooper and put pedestals to Thomas Bushrod's grave stone;
2 CONT * son Richard exr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I029526&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/L2VN-PQ5
2 CONT
2 CONT When Hannah Bushrod was born about 1708, in Westmoreland, Virginia, British Colonial America, her father, Colonel John Bushrod, was 47 and her mother, Hannah Keene, was 33. She married Joseph Heale after 17 January 1723, in Westmo
2 CONC reland, Virginia, British Colonial America. She died on 22 February 1774, in Lancaster, Virginia, British Colonial America, at the age of 67, and was buried in Mount Holly, Westmoreland, Virginia, United States.
