1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p. 86
2 CONT Capt. Daniel McCarty "of the Parish of Cople, in the Co. of Westmoreland, Esqr.," b. 1679.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 1st Mrs. Payne, widow of James Payne, probably Sarah Payne.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 2nd Ann (Lee) Fitzhugh, dau. of Richard and Lettice or Laeticia (Corbin) Lee, son of Richard, of VA., 1641, and widow of Col. Wm. Fitzhugh of "Eagle's Nest,"King George Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - LEE OF VIRGINIA 1642-1892 Edited & Published by Edmund Jennings Lee, p. 83
2 CONT He died 4 May, 1724, will dated Mar. 29, 1724; pro. Westmoreland Co., May 27, 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - SOME PROMINENT VIRGINIA FAMILIES, VOL II, p. 561 by Louise duBellet
2 CONT His tomb is still to be seen at Old Yeocomico Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. McCarty was Burgess, Justice and Sheriff of Westmoreland, in 1715-20; he was speaker of the Assembly.  - Ibid
