1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Porter (d. 1800) and his wife Sarah, a daughter of William Ramsay (1716-1785) (of Ramsay House, the Alexandria Visitors Center at 221 King Street), may have owned this frame flounder house.  Sarah was a brid
2 CONC esmaid at the Mount Vernon marriage of Fanny Bassett (Martha Washington’s niece) to George Augustine Washington (George Washington’s nephew) in 1785.  George Washington attended the Porter’s wedding on February 5, 1788.  Mr. and M
2 CONC rs. Washington dined (probably at another location) with the Porters on March 14, 1788.  Thomas Porter was a merchant with Porter & Ingraham, which was located where the Stabler Leadbeater Apothecary Shop is today at 105-107 South
2 CONC  Fairfax Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Adapted from Robert Madison’s Walking with Washington, available in Alexandria museum gift shops.) http://www.localkicks.com/community/news/Sarah_and_Thomas_Porter_412_South_Fairfax_Street
