1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I believe that the father of my Sarah McCarty was also the father of Dennis 1784, Daniel 1786 and Michael also about 1784 and a James H McCarty also about that same time frame. James H 1781 married Elizabeth Funder
2 CONC burgh, daughter of Isaac Funderburgh. Michael McCarty was born 16 FEB.1854 in Edgefield District, South Carolina  per his Rev. War Record. A Dennis McCarty, per 8 May 1769 • BERKLEY COUNTY, SOUTH CAROLINA, received a tract of land
2 CONC  containing 100 acres surveyed on this date in the four holes Swamp in Berkley County.. Michael eventually moved to Jefferson County, Alabama where he died in 1850'''. '
2 CONT
2 CONT "The History Of Edgefield County From the Earliest Settlements" gives this account:
2 CONT
2 CONT "There were other early settlers in that part of Edgefield bordering on Big Saluda and Persimmon Creek, not yet mentioned. These were the Perrys, Colemans, Trotters, Berrys, Nunns, Summerses, Rileys, and McCartys, to say nothing a
2 CONC s yet of the Brookses."
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael was in Craven County, S. C. on Dec 31, 1762 for a "chain of Title to a Grant from Mark Jones, 300 acres on Wateree Creek. In April 22, 1769 Craven County, his name is on an Index for a Memorial for 250 acres located on Ced
2 CONC ar Creek in Craven County, Wateree Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1778 Camden District, he is listed on a South Carolina, Compiled Census and Census Subsitutes Index, 1790-1890.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgefield County was established in 1785 from part of Ninety-Six District (96 District). In this case he would have been born in the 96th District.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael states in his 1832 Pension Record that he was born 16 Feb, 1754 in Edgefield District, South Carolina. He also says he left there in the Fall of 1827 and moved to Jefferson County, Alabama. He can be found in the 1830 & 18
2 CONC 40 census for this county. Dennis Sr also was in in the area per a land Transaction on 8 May 1769 • BERKLEY COUNTY, SOUTH CAROLINA
2 CONT
2 CONT There are now indications of four distinct families in the Edgefield area in 1790.
2 CONT Dennis McCarty, b. 1784, Daniel McCarty, b. 1786, Thomas McCarty b. 1800 South Carolina, are 37 marker matches therefore have a 98.26 % probability that they are indeed brothers. Who was their father is yet to be established. Base
2 CONC d on 1790 and 1810 census records of Edgefield and Newberry, SC and land records of Dennis McCarty, it suggests most strongly that their father was a Daniel McCarty received land in Newberry for his service in the Revolutionary Wa
2 CONC r. Albert McCarty, b. 1807 Edgefield, married Martha Gentry, the daughter of Levi and Ruth Gentry. Albert is not a match with the others but his family is very closely tied to that of Dennis McCarty for several generations. This i
2 CONC s a real mystery. Michael J. McCarty, b.c.1784 and thought to have died about 1825 leaving a widow Margaret Byrd and several orphan children. The widow and family moved to Georgia and received land in the Georgia Lottery. Michael 
2 CONC J. McCarty is a 37-marker match with Daniel Sterling McCarty. This match indicates that there is a 98.26% probability that they shared a common ancestor within 180 years. They appear to be uncle and nephew.
2 CONT
2 CONT John McCarty, b. c. 1813 is also a perfect match of 37-markers. John McCarty married Caroline Raiford of Edgefield, moved to Covington Co., Alabama by 1850 then Macon Georgia by 1855.
2 CONT
2 CONT James H. McCarty, b. 1784, Edgefield is also a 37-marker match. With this pattern of perfect matches, two generations of these families have taken shape.
2 CONT
2 CONT An important addition to this group is that of descendants of Edward McCarty b.1773, who is also 37 marker match with all of these men. These results support the popular belief that all of these men were children or brothers of Mi
2 CONC chael McCarty b. 1754 Edgefield, South Carolina, since paper research indicates that the father of Edward McCarty was, indeed, Michael McCarty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thompson McCarty, b. 1821 Jefferson Co., Alabama who is thought to the son of William McCarty, b. 1787 Edgefield, SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE:From the South Carolina Department of Archives & History there are numerous records for McCarty's.
2 CONT This first date of June 5th, 1753 is the earliest I have found for "a" Michael and puts him in the same area as Isaac Funderburg(h) and Sarah (McCarty) of Craven County. So we can place them here in Craven County 1753, 1762, 1769,
2 CONC  1770, 1771, 1772, and in Edgefield County, 1809 and 1811. And I do believe this is a brother of Sarah. Michael & Dennis are living close to each other on Edgefield, South Carolina in 1790.
2 CONT *Note that these early dates, especially 1753, would mean that there had to be an older "Michael" as ours was not born until 1754 plus the "1762" date would make our Michael only 8 years old.
2 CONT *
