1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Elizabeth Rousby
2 CONT * Born 1712 in Calvert County, MD
2 CONT * Died abt 14 August 1744 in St. Mary's County, MD
2 CONT * Daughter of John Rousby II and Anne (Burford) Rousby
2 CONT * Sister of George Plater II [half], Anne (Plater) Carroll [half], Gertrude (Rousby) Henry [half], Ann (Rousby) Lloyd [half], John Rousby III [half] and Araminta (Thompson) Biscoe [half]
2 CONT * Wife of Abraham Barnes Jr. (1710-Dec 1777) — married 1742 in St. Mary's County, Maryland
2 CONT *Mother of John Barnes and Richard Barnes
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT The second wife of Abraham Barnes was Elizabeth, daughter of Col. John Rousby of Calvert Co. whom he married sometime between 1740 and 1742. They had two sons, namely John Barnes (1743-1800) and Richard Barnes (ca1745-1804). Both 
2 CONC sons died unmarried and without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
