2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I077592&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT >1687-1699 Order Book Part 2 - Northumberland Co Va; Hamrick: Pg 708 Northumberland County Court August 22, 1695 Upon the motion of JANE WILKINS Administratrix of JOHN WILKINS deceased JOHN BAYLY, RICHARD SMYTH, ANTHONY HAYNIE and
2 CONC  THOMAS PINIFY or any three of them being first sworn by the nearest Justice are appointed sometime before the next Court with the next conveniency to meet at the house of the said JANE and appraise the Estate of the said JOHN WIL
2 CONC KINS deceased, and ordered that the said JANE deliver an Inventory thereof unto the next court
2 CONT
2 CONT >273/1: 17Nov1703: Whereas Col Sam'll Griffin by deed of gift did give Jane Wilkins now Jane Barnes one red cow and cow calfe and their increase, it is ordered that Thomas Barnes deliver and pay unto Thomas Wilkins son of the sd J
2 CONC ane a heifer and calfe & Two yeare old steer due him this said Thomas for the said Encrease.
2 CONT
2 CONT >807: 18Feb1713: The last will and testament of Thomas Barns deceased ws presented in court by Jane Barns his relict who mae oath thereto and being proved by the oaths of Richard Robinson, John Had[d]ock and Peter Wilkins witnesse
2 CONC s thereto it's admitted to record and on the motion of said Jane Barns and her performing of what is usual in such cases Certificate is granted for obtaining a probate thereof in due form.
