1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Judith [Surname Unknown] (c. 1690 – 1748) was a resident of Lancaster County, Virginia, and the widow of William Payne Jr. (c. 1685–1726). While frequently subject to speculative identification in secondary literature—often appear
2 CONC ing as "Merryman," "Davenport," or "Mitchell"—her maiden name and parentage remain unproven in the primary record. She is best documented through her widowhood, during which she managed the interests of her children until her deat
2 CONC h in 1748. Her probate records serve as the definitive link confirming her motherhood of the children born to William Payne Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Born: c. 1690, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1748, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Dated: 1748 (Proved in Lancaster County).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: [Unknown/Unproven]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: [Unknown/Unproven]
2 CONT
2 CONT Researcher’s Note: There is no primary record (will, marriage bond, or land grant) that provides conclusive proof of Judith's maiden name. Hypotheses linking her to the Merryman, Davenport, or Mitchell families are based on associ
2 CONC ative naming patterns or secondary compilations rather than direct documentary evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: William Payne Jr. (c. 1685–1726)
2 CONT Marriage: c. 1710 in Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (Documented in Probate):
2 CONT 1. Merryman Payne (c. 1713–1773)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Susannah Payne Johnson (c. 1715 – after 1758); Married Major James Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Judith Payne Ball (c. 1717 – after 1747); Married George Ball.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William Payne (c. 1719 – after 1758)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Rachel Payne Smith (dates unknown)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Inventory & Record Analysis===
2 CONT 1. Primary Probate Evidence
2 CONT Document: Will of Judith Payne, Lancaster County Will Book 14, Page 241 (1748).
2 CONT Significance: This document is the anchor for her identity as the widow of William Payne Jr. and confirms the identities of her surviving children, allowing for the correct reconstruction of the family unit.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Genealogical Distinction
2 CONT Analysis: It is crucial to distinguish Judith from the grandmother, Susannah Merryman (wife of William Payne Sr.). The repetition of the name "Merryman" as a given name for her son, Merryman Payne, is a common colonial practice of
2 CONC  honoring a paternal grandmother, not necessarily a claim of the mother's maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources===
2 CONT 1. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 14, Page 241. (Will of Judith Payne, 1748).
2 CONT 2. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 10, Page 505. (Will of William Payne Jr., 1726).
2 CONT 3. Fleet, Beverley. Virginia Colonial Abstracts, Vol. 22: Lancaster County.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * PAYNE, Judith. 29 Mar. 1747. Rec. 9 Sept. 1748.
2 CONT * Sons: Merryman & William Payne. Dau.: Judith Ball. Gr.dau.: Judith Ball. Dau.-in-law: Catherine Payne. Extr.: Son Merryman Payne. Wits: John Taylor, Jesse Ball. W.B. 14, p. 212
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * PAYNE, William, of Parish of St. Mary's White Chappell. 27 Aug. 1726. Rec. 14 Sept. 1726.
2 CONT * Wife: Judith.
2 CONT * Sons: Merryman and William Payne.
2 CONT * Daus: Susanna and Judith Payne.
2 CONT * Dau.-in-law: Katherine, wife of Mark Bannerman.
2 CONT * Brothers: John and George Payne.
2 CONT * Brother; Robert Mitchell.
2 CONT * Friend: Charles Burgess.
2 CONT * Mother: Susanna Laidner.
2 CONT * Exors: Wife and brother, Robert Mitchell; son-in-law Mark Bannerman and Charles Burgess.
2 CONT * Wits: Jo. Chichester and John Flint. W.B. 10, p 505.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I023027&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
