1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT William Payne Jr. (c. 1685 – 1726) was an established landholder and resident of St. Mary’s Whitechapel Parish in Lancaster County, Virginia. As the son of William Payne Sr. and Susannah Merryman, he operated within the social and
2 CONC  economic circles of the Northern Neck’s landed families. His life and the composition of his immediate family are definitively anchored by his 1726 Last Will and Testament, which serves as the primary record for his heirs. He was
2 CONC  survived by his wife, Judith, and their five children, who maintained the family’s presence in Lancaster County through the mid-18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Born: c. 1685, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: September 1726, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Will Dated: August 27, 1726 (Proved September 14, 1726).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: William Payne Sr. (c. 1654–1700)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Susannah Merryman (c. 1666–1726)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: Judith [Surname Unknown/Hypothesized] (c. 1690 – 1748)
2 CONT (Note: While frequently identified in secondary genealogies as "Merryman" (due to the naming of her son, Merryman Payne), "Davenport," or "Mitchell," no primary document (marriage bond or probate of her father) confirms her maiden
2 CONC  name. It remains unproven.)
2 CONT Marriage Date: c. 1710 in Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Documented Children (Per 1726/1748 Probate):
2 CONT 1. Merryman Payne (c. 1713 – 1773)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Susannah Payne (c. 1715 – after 1758); Married Major James Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Judith Payne (c. 1717 – after 1747); Married George Ball.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William Payne (c. 1719 – after 1758)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Rachel Payne (dates unknown); Married [Unknown] Smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Inventory & Record Analysis===
2 CONT 1. Primary Probate Evidence
2 CONT Document: Will of William Payne Jr., Lancaster County Will Book 10, Page 505.
2 CONT Significance: This is the anchor record for the family. It legally documents the existence of his children and the identity of his widow, Judith.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Naming Pattern Analysis
2 CONT Context: The son "Merryman Payne" is often used as "proof" that his mother was a Merryman. However, it is equally possible the name was chosen to honor his grandmother, Susannah Merryman (wife of William Payne Sr.), rather than in
2 CONC dicating his mother's maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources===
2 CONT 1. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 10, Page 505. (Will of William Payne Jr., 1726).
2 CONT 2. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 14, Page 241. (Will of Judith Payne, 1748).
2 CONT 3. Fleet, Beverley. Virginia Colonial Abstracts, Vol. 22: Lancaster County.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT *Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * PAYNE, William, of Parish of St. Mary's White Chappell. 27 Aug. 1726. Rec. 14 Sept. 1726.
2 CONT * Wife: Judith.
2 CONT * Sons: Merryman and William Payne.
2 CONT * Daus: Susanna and Judith Payne.
2 CONT * Dau.-in-law: Katherine, wife of Mark Bannerman.
2 CONT * Brothers: John and George Payne.
2 CONT * Brother; Robert Mitchell.
2 CONT * Friend: Charles Burgess.
2 CONT * Mother: Susanna Laidner.
2 CONT * Exors: Wife and brother, Robert Mitchell; son-in-law Mark Bannerman and Charles Burgess.
2 CONT * Wits: Jo. Chichester and John Flint. W.B. 10, p 505.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I022658&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
