1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Do not confuse, conflate or merge with https://www.geni.com/people/Susannah-Carter/6000000003615801961?through=6000000003999734222. 
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Susannah Payne Johnson (c. 1715 – after 1758) was a member of the established Payne family of Lancaster County, Virginia. She is well-documented in regional probate records as the daughter of William Payne Jr. and Judith Mitchell.
2 CONC  Her marriage to Major James Johnson is confirmed by the testamentary records of her mother, which differentiate her from other women named Susannah in the same parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Born: c. 1715–1720, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: After 1758 (date of mother’s will).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: William Payne Jr. (1685–1726)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Judith Merryman (c. 1690 – 1748)
2 CONT
2 CONT Researcher’s Note: She was the granddaughter of the elder William Payne and Susannah Merryman. Her identity as the daughter of the younger William Payne and Judith Merryman is supported by the 1758 will of her mother, which lists 
2 CONC "Susannah Johnson" as an heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: Major James Johnson (c. 1715–1787)
2 CONT Marriage Date: c. 1736 in Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Judith Johnson (documented in DeJarnette and Allied Families)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Note: Other children are often cited in secondary sources, but remain unverified due to the prevalence of the name "James Johnson" in colonial records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Inventory & Record Analysis===
2 CONT 1. Primary Probate Evidence
2 CONT Document: Will of Judith Payne, 1758 (Lancaster County, Virginia).
2 CONT Significance: This is the "Anchor Record." It explicitly identifies the testator’s daughter as "Susannah Johnson," legally separating her from all other contemporary individuals named Susannah in the area.
2 CONT 2. Genealogical Distinction
2 CONT Analysis: This profile is distinct from the Susannah [Unknown] who married Captain John Carter. By verifying this Susannah as the daughter of William Payne Jr. and Judith Mitchell, we confirm she is not the same person often erron
2 CONC eously linked to the Carter lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources===
2 CONT 1. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book: Will of Judith Payne (1758).
2 CONT 2. DeJarnette, D. DeJarnette and Allied Families in America (1699–1954).
2 CONT 3. Fleet, Beverley. Virginia Colonial Abstracts, Vol. 22: Lancaster County.
2 CONT 4. Lunenburg County, Virginia, Will Book 3: Page 295, the Last Will and Testament of James Johnson (dated October 11, 1787).
2 CONT 5. Historical Register of Virginians in the Revolutionary War: (Gwathmey) Reference to Major James Johnson of Lunenburg.
