1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert, son of the 1st Robert Howson. Married Sarah; she married Robert Hewitt 2nd.  children: Anne m Rice Hooe lll, Mary m Charles Calvert.  Frances.  Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: A Nathl. JONES is listed on the 1723 Stafford Co, VA 1723 Rent Roll (Census Index Colonial America, 1607-1789). According to a King footnote in OPR: "Charles CALVERT, Gentleman, (circa 1664-1733) moved from MD to Stafford Co
2 CONC unty and married Mary HOWSON, daughter of Robert HOWSON who possessed a handsome landed estate in the Northern Neck of Virginia. They had two daughters, viz: (1) Anne wife of Thomas PORTER (16??-1740) and Sarah HOWSON wife of Nath
2 CONC aniel JONES (1696-1754). (Ella Foy O'Gorman's Descendants of Virginia Calverts, 1947, pp. 64-5, 68-73.)" (OPR)(1)
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I035489&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia's Eastern Shore, Ralph T. Whitelaw, Picton Press, Camden, Maine, 1989, page 200
2 CONT R 1720 Robert Howson bequeathed 200 acres in N52 to John Custis Matthews. (Whitelaw, 334)
2 CONT ===
2 CONT Mar 30, 1714. Deed between Sarah Howson Calvert, Thomas Porter and Anne his wife (which Sarah, Thomas and Anne are of the County of Stafford) to John Pratt 200 acres in West Moreland County, part of a patent granted to Robert Hows
2 CONC on for 450 acres, April 15, 1667. (Ibid, p. 253.)
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Howson’s daughters were named in the will of Robert Hewitt, 1689, Stafford County:
2 CONT
2 CONT ... “Also it is my will intent & meaninge that if ye said Lande fail to my Daughter SARAH that then MARY HOWSON, ANNE BEHETHLAND & SARAH HOWSON shall have ye next foure tents after MR. SANDERSON everyone haveinge accordingle to th
2 CONC eir age begininge wth MARY first, ...”
2 CONT
2 CONT ... “and in case of r mortality before my two children then to bee divided amongst ye Daughters of Mr ROBERT HOWSON deced equally”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *Genealogies of Virginia Families, from the Virginia Magazine of History & Biography. Volume lV - Healy - Pryor [https://msa.maryland.gov/megafile/msa/speccol/sc3500/sc3520/000600/000669/pdf/drews.pdf link] page 70
2 CONT *“Charles Calvert and some of his Descendants.”  John Bailey Calvert Nicklin.  Maryland Historical Magazine Summer 1929 Page 127 - 128 [https://archive.org/details/msa_sc_5881_1_94/page/n33 Archive.Org]
