1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === John Turberville
2 CONT * Born 1650 in Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT * Died 9 Oct 1728 at about age 78 in Lancaster, Virginia
2 CONT * Husband of Unknown (Unknown) Turberville — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT * Husband of Elizabeth (Lee) Turberville — married 1689 in Westmoreland, Virginia
2 CONT * Father of Edward Turberville, James Turberville and George Turberville
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Turbevil-of-Craven-County/6000000086231314857
2 CONT
2 CONT Betsy Lee and her second husband had one child, George Turberville (1694–1742), who lived at Hickory Hill in Westmoreland County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT 1687-1698 Northumberland County, Virginia Order Book, Part 2; [Hamrick]; Page 695/8 At a Court held for Northumberland County June 18, 1695
2 CONT
2 CONT >In obedience to his Excellency Sir EDMUND ANDRES' Commission to JOHN TURBERVILLE Gentleman for that purpose the said TURBERVILLE was this day sworn High Sheriff of this County, and JOHN SHARP his Sub-sheriff.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Property 
2 CONT
2 CONT URL (Click on link) http://lvaimage.lib.va.us/cgi-bin/GetLONN.pl?first=63&last=&g_p=G3&collect ion=NN Grant
2 CONT Title Turberville, John.
2 CONT Publication 4 December 1704.
2 CONT Other Format Available on microfilm. Northern Neck Grants, reels 288-311.
2 CONT Note Location: Lancaster County.
2 CONT Description: 78 acres adjoining the land of Thomas Coxe crossing Tarr-kill Cove. On a sandy point by the bay side at the mouth of Fleets Bay Creek or Nantepoizon Creek so called by some people.
2 CONT Source: Northern Neck Grants No. 3, 1703-1710, Page 63 (Reel 288).
2 CONT ===
2 CONT http://image.lva.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/GetLONN.pl?first=95&last=&g_p=G3&col lection=NN Grant
2 CONT Title Turbervile, John.
2 CONT Publication 18 April 1705.
2 CONT Other Format Available on microfilm. Northern Neck Grants, reels 288-311.
2 CONT Note Location: Richmond County.
2 CONT Description: 798 acres upon the head of a run called Horsepenn Run about five miles above the falls of Rappahannock.
2 CONT Source: Northern Neck Grants No. 3, 1703-1710, Page 95 (Reel 288).
2 CONT ===
2 CONT http://image.lva.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/GetLONN.pl?first=104&last=&g_p=G4&co llection=NN Grant
2 CONT Title Lee, Issac.
2 CONT Publication 30 July 1712.
2 CONT Other Format Available on microfilm. Northern Neck Grants, reels 288-311.
2 CONT Note Location: Richmond County.
2 CONT Description: 223 acres between the lands of John Waugh, John Tuberville, Hancock Lee, and Thomas Knight above the falls of Rappa. River.
2 CONT Source: Northern Neck Grants No. 4, 1710-1712 , Page 104 (Reel 289).
2 CONT
