3 NOTE Thank you Erica Howton for reading some of my sources I uploaded regarding the parents Col Richard Lee, I appreciate it very much.
4 CONT https://photos.geni.com/p13/56/74/1c/1a/5344485f54b39abf/col_ricahr...
4 CONT https://leesofvirginia.org/Col_Richard_Lee.html
4 CONT
4 CONT Genealogy has grown in 'Leaps and Bounds" since the internet now allows documentation and primary sources at our finger tips, not like earlier days of genealogy when much had to be written, mailed requests if lucky enough to find 
4 CONC a location or contact to query or go to the source location oneself.
4 CONT
4 CONT Much more documents are able to be found in the UK Parishes records as well as globaly nowadays.
4 CONT
4 CONT Again,thank you for posting what I tried to highlight as a valid historic publishing with sources for Richard Lee and Elizabeth Bendy as parents of (Col) Richard Lee the Immigrant. I appreciate it as it was myself that was able to
4 CONC  prove Thorndale in error without question.
3 NOTE Parents of Richard Lee the emigrant are seen here as Elizabeth Bendy and Richard Lee (living in 1621), with a birth date for the son as 1613, “more consistent with a portrait painted in 1661.”
