4 CONC eabouts" being capable of an under- as well as overestimate.
3 NOTE Deposition says he was in Virginia in January 1653/4, at Jeremiah Harrison's plantation on Queen's Creek, York River, in company with Mr. Harrison and (the plaintiff) William Morton. Does not specify whether he lived in Virginia o
4 CONC r was on a business trip. Perhaps the original documents in the case (since this is just an abstract) have more information.
3 NOTE Is this Richard Lee in London likely to also be Richard Lee in Virginia?
3 NOTE Direct screencap of Coldham abstract of deposition from a "Richard Lee of London, gent., aged 34". No "or thereabouts", as often erroneously reported. Implies a birth date between mid-September 1619 and end August 1620, which does
4 CONC  not accord with any of the proposed identities for Col. Richard Lee.
