4 CONT Your welcome Erica - as I pointed out the direct link has been on my material (website) for years now and on the PDf's I uploaded from compiling sources for my argument that these were Col Richard Lee's parents (Richard of Coton a
4 CONC nd Elizabeth Bendy) as some may not have ancestry accounts, etc., to view ... but the Rootsweb link needs no account.
4 CONT
4 CONT BTW - the genealogy.com Book link for me that you had posted https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/f/i/n/Jacqueli-C-Finley/BOOK-0001/0002-0021.html#CHILD263684 
4 CONT I cannot take credit for that as it was actually Jim's Lawlers research - it was Jim's correspondence and email address on his research he gave me back in 2005 (re:John Leyes, Jane Hancock ...) he had asked me to include it with m
4 CONC y own (our correspondence documented as well) so I would not want to be credited for what he did - I just included his work with mine in onto my GED and research per his requests/permission. Thank you for understanding..
4 CONT
4 CONT If he was still with us I am sure he would want me to clarify.
4 CONT
4 CONT Although - He would have gotten a big chuckle on confusing his work for mine thinking how my research had evolved since then ... he was actually known for giving symposiums for the Lee Society on the LOV family based on his resear
4 CONC ch!!! :D
4 CONT He was my mentor, always grateful for that.
