1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vital Statistics'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''William  Lee''', Capt. Born ca 1650 in Charles City, Virginia.  Died ca 1696 in Northumberland County, Virginia, unmarried.  
2 CONT * son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Colonel-Richard-the-Immigrant-Lee/6000000002700598061?through=6000000003289947894 Colonel Richard "the Immigrant" Lee] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Lee/6000000003908169132?through=600
2 CONC 0000003289947894 Ann Constable]
2 CONT * The middle name “Constable” is speculative. Middle names were rare in this century, unless you were royalty. It is probably a genealogical shortcut to identify his branch of the family tree, from before computers were commonly u
2 CONC sed.
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Schriever/6000000011024139374 is seen as daughter or widow of https://www.geni.com/people/Captain-William-Lee-Esq/6000000003289947894?through=6000000011024139374 but there is no documentation pro
2 CONC ving this.  Mary Schriever, formerly Heath, “friend or companion,” was named executrix and heir in William Lee’s 1696 will.  That inherited estate was reverted back to the Lees in a court battle.  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stratford Hall Historic Preserve: The Lees of Virginia: An American Legacy < [https://leefamilyarchive.org/the-lees/ link] > accessed 28 December 2025.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >https://www.geni.com/people/Colonel-Richard-the-Immigrant-Lee/6000000002700598061?through=6000000003289947894’s children shared in their father’s good fortune. John, the eldest, attended Oxford University, where he obtained a deg
2 CONC ree in medicine. Richard, the second born and his father’s namesake, also attended Oxford. Francis, the third born child, became the family’s factor in London. '''The fourth son, William, died in his mid-forties, apparently withou
2 CONC t marrying or issue.''' The fifth son of the family founder, Hancock, married (the second time) Sarah Allerton, a granddaughter of Isaac Allerton, who was a passenger on the Mayflower. Charles, the youngest of all the children, in
2 CONC herited the part of his father’s Dividing Creek lands that came to be known as Cobbs Hall, the name also given to Charles’s line of descendants. Hancock Lee built a mansion house called Ditchley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
