2 CONT ===DNA Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT >Recent advances in DNA studies indicate that William  Lee was most likely not the father of a son named William, and if he did have a son named William,'' that'' William was not the person we know here on Geni as "William Lee of 
2 CONC (Ulster &) Richmond." The Lee family of Stratford Hall - the famous "Lees of Virginia" -  all carry the I1A y-DNA haplogroup while descendants of William Lee of Richmond carry the R1B or R1B1 y-DNA haplogroup.  [https://www.geni.c
2 CONC om/people/William-Lee-of-Ulster-Richmond/6000000028281399108] appears to be the son or grandson of an Ulsterman.
