1 CHAN
2 DATE 25 JAN 2026
3 TIME 13:43:50
0 @I6000000012062852380@ INDI
1 NAME Hancock /Lee/
2 GIVN Hancock
2 SURN Lee
2 _MARNM Lee
2 NICK The Honourable Hancock Lee
2 NICK The Honourable Captain Hancock William Lee
2 NICK Hancock Captain LEE
2 NICK Hancock         Captain Lee
1 NAME Hancock Lee, of Ditchley
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1652
2 PLAC Dividing Creek (?)
2 ADDR
3 STAE VA
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 MAY 1709
2 PLAC Ditchley
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 BURI
2 DATE 25 MAY 1709
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ditchley Plantation
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU Captain & A Burgess, justice, burgess, naval officer, Landowner; planter; statesman, Military, Captain, Justice, Burgess, Landowner, Planter, Statesman
1 TITL Hon.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vital Statistics'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Hancock Lee, son of Richard Lee and Ann Constable, was born "1645 in Northumberland Co., Virginia.  Possibly in Dividing Creek.  Died 1714 in Isle Wight, Virginia." 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Miles Files version: born 1653, Ditchley, Northumberland County, VA; died 25 May 1709, Ditchley, Northumberland County, VA.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Lee of Virginia version: born 1653, probably Dividing Creek, Northumberland County, VA; died between 20 May and 20 July 1709, Ditchley.)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: 1) Mary Kendall (1651 - 1694); 2) Sarah Allerton (ca. 1669 - d. 17 May 1731)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children w/Mary Kendall'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # William b Bet 1678-1682 [''m 1703 Dorothy Taylor.  Death inventory, Feb. 5th 1717/18 in Wills of Richmond County VA.'' No children.  Died possibly before 1706.]  Wrong William - did ''not'' marry Dorothy Taylor,did ''not'' live 
2 CONC in Richmond County. Did die young without issue, probably before 1706.
2 CONT #  Anna, “the elder,” born prior to January 5, 1682, and was living as late as October 1754 married William Armistead
2 CONT # (from Miles Files) Kendall , b bet 1682-1684, probably d. shortly after 1685. Mentioned in will of her grandfather Col. William Kendall, but nowhere else.
2 CONT # Richard born August 18, 1691
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children with Sarah Allerton:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Ann Lee, “the younger,” born after October 25, 1702; died after September 03, 1739.  Married William Eustace.
2 CONT # Isaac Lee, born 1707 in  Northumberland,  Virginia; died 1727 in Stepney, Middlesex, England, will probate.  No children.  Buried Rappahannock, Virginia ?
2 CONT # John Lee, born ca 1709 in Northumberland, , Virginia; died 11 Aug 1789 in Orange, Co, Va.  Not married.  No children.
2 CONT # Hancock Taylor Lee, born 1709 in Ditchley, Northumberland, Co, Va; died Nov 1763 in Warrenton, Fauquier, Va, will; married Mary WILLIS.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Lee, born 1709 in Ditchley, Northumberland, Co, Virginia; married (1) Swan Jones born ca. 1708 in of Westmoreland Co., Virginia.; died 1734 in Virginia; married (2) Zachary Taylor; born 17 Apr 1707 in Rapidan. Orange, 
2 CONC Co, Virginia; died 01 Mar 1768 in Orange, Co, Virginia.   Elizabeth Lee and Hancock Taylor Lee were twins.  They were christened in 1709 after their father's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes and Sources'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: There were two different daughters of Hancock Lee, the elder named Anna Lee, daughter of his 1st wife, Mary Kendall. She married William Armstead.  The other named Anne Lee, the younger, was a daughter of 2nd wife, Sarah All
2 CONC erton. She married William Eustace. A very well-written article by James R. Hancock, using primary documents, has solved the question of Anna and Anne Lee. He shows they are two different women, half-sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hancock I LEE was born in 1650/1653 in Of, Northumberland, W. Moreland, Va. He was christened in 1677 in Of, Ditchley, Northampton, Va. He died on 25 May 1709 in Ditchley, Northumberland, Virginia. He was buried on 20 Oct 1709 in 
2 CONC Ditchley, Northumberland, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occup: Captain - "Build Ditchley Estate" Ditchley, Northumberland, Westmorland, Virginia Occup: 1677 Just
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Ditchley" Line
2 CONT
2 CONT >(2)Hancock Lee (#2)1653-1709 m. 1.Mary Kendall<br/>
2 CONT
