2 CONC d {color:purple; text-decoration:underline;} span.EmailStyle17 {mso-style-type:personal-compose; font-family:Arial; color:windowtext;} @page Section1 {size:8.5in 11.0in; margin:1.0in 1.25in 1.0in 1.25in;} div.Section1 {page:Sectio
2 CONC n1;} --> Today I am tracking Alice Felton, I have found nothing on her in Virginia, and if she had married Thomas Felton she would have been 7 years old. From what I have found below she must have came to Virginia as a servant met
2 CONC  William Lee (the rogue that he was) and married him. Still found nothing on marriage though. I have been doing census on Williams and Richards (Tax list) (census) WM would have to be in Maryland; that is where his father left him
2 CONC  a home and land. I found Col Richard Lees will he made in England when he and his family were in their home there, he went to sell all and give up England for good. He had made many trips back and forth over the years and owned 1
2 CONC /8 of 3 ships for transporting goods back and forth and people. Francis Lee went back to England lived, raised his family and died there in 1714. Col Lee left the ownership of the 3 ships to (Elizabeth-Mary-& Susan 1/8th eh.) to F
2 CONC rancis and if he dies first it goes to Charles and the two sisters, Elizabeth and Ann. Jim, how do I go about getting Edmond Jennings Lees book? Did you find anything in there on Alice? Talk to you two later Ellie
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Francis Lee: Record Change: 31 Mar 2002
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Tamak or Tamar: Record Change: 31 Mar 2002
2 CONT
2 CONT 		iii.	William Lee4,4, born Abt. 1650 in Charles City, Co, Virginia, Colony; died Abt. 1696 in 1696/1703 estate suit, King and Queen, Va; married Alice Mrs FELTON; born Abt. 1644 in of, Richmond, Co, Va; died Abt. 1703 in St Steph
2 CONC en Parsh, King and Queen, Co, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for William Lee: 3. William Lee b. 1678 or 1682, Northampton, Northumberland Co, VA
2 CONT      m. Dorothy Taylor, ca 1703, Westmoreland Co, VA d/o Thomas Taylor & Elizabeth Harwood b. 1681, Surry,
2 CONT      King and Queen Co, VA
2 CONT      Information on Dorothy Taylor comes from "Log Cabins to White House" by Brewer. 13 Apr 1745
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy was witness to will of Henry Williams in Richmond Co.,VA. signed as Dorothy Croucher. Dorothy and her brother Thomas were administrators of her husband William Lee's estate. She was left wearing apparel in her mother's wil
2 CONC l. "Dorothy to have my Coyas" d. 1717, Richmond Co, VA (Source: Amelia Co. Order Book 7, p. 226, Letters of Administration of Estate of William Lee to Dorothy Lee, relict of William Lee on 12/4/1717.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Documentation from "Log Cabins to White House" by Brewer. On page 275 "On 19 Jan 1668 William and wife Alice acknowledged debt of 250 acres of land to William Heath. On 5 Sep 1668 William and wife Alice sold their plantation to Th
2 CONC omas Adams (Surry Co. records p.54).
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Log Cabin" book on p.276 it gives William Lee( who married Dorothy Taylor) as one of his children. On p.273, Richard Henry Lee and Anna Constable are given as the parents of William (husband of Alice) but other sources state
2 CONC  that Richard Lee's son William did not marry. Other sources say he married and had a daughter Mary who married a Heath and that he left his estate to her -- which was contested by his brother and returned to the Lee family.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a William Lee and Mary Lee, witnesses in Richard Jesper's will, dated 1698 in North Farnham Parish, VA. Need to identify them. Dorothy and brother Thomas Taylor were administrators of his estate. They left to William's gr
