2 CONC MHB GE (Magazine of History and Biography.)  gives the following:    THOMAS LEE:  "The first reference in the records is when he was a witness with Cuthbert Potter and Wiliam Brett to a deed for land made by Bertram Obert, Dec 3rd
2 CONC , 1662 (Lancaster Co. Deed Book II, p . 255).  In 1665 he is charged with 4 titables and in 1666 with 5 tithables (Lancaster County, Book III).  He evidently resided in that part of Lancaster County which became Middlesex, for in 
2 CONC 1677 hi s name appears seventh on a list of prominent men who would equip a soldier of horse.  There are many references to him in the court records from 1665 until the probate of his will March 8th, 1709 i n Middlesex County.  hi
2 CONC s will, probabted by his son Charles, mentions wife Elizabeth; son Charles; daughters Mary Jones and Ann Gardner; grandsons Thomas Lee and Charles Lee;  granddaughter Elizabet h Mullins.  He left a considerable plantation.    the 
2 CONC maiden name of Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Lee is not known.  His daughters:  (1) Mary (no record of birth in Christ Church Middlesex County, Parish register ) married William Hones and left issue :  (2)  Ann (no record of birth in 
2 CONC parish register) married William Garnder and left issue; (3)  Elizabeth, bron Aug 11, 1678, married William Mullins, and left a daughter Elizabeth.  The son Charle s Lee continued to live in Middlesex County."    1709 Will probate
2 CONC d in Middlesex Co. by son Charles.  Will Book A. p. 222.  Item - I give and bequeath unto my Grandchild Thomas Lee one feather bed and furniture whereon I now sleep, on cow with her increase, my chest, one mare with all her increa
2 CONC se, on pig from Dagg to hi m and his heirs forever.    Item - I give and bequeath to my Grandchild Charles Lee on cow with all her increase to him and his heirs forever.    I give unto my Daughter Mary Hones one steer and on cow w
2 CONC ith all her increase to her and her heirs forever.    I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Anna Gardner on bullock and on cow and all her increase to her and her heirs forever.    Item - I guve unto Mary the daughter of William Mu
2 CONC llins decd. one cow yearling with all her increase to her and her heirs forever.    Item - I give unto my Dear Wife Elizabeth Lee all the rest of my household goods to enjoy the rest of her life and after her death I give and bequ
2 CONC eath the same to my above mentioned two daughters an d my son Charles Lee to be equally divided between them share and share alike.    Item - I give and bequeath unto my said wife my horse Toby and my mare to my son Charles with a
2 CONC ll her increase.    Item - I give and bequeath all the rest of my stock (excepting one two year old heifer) which now belongs to my said wife and son Charels Lee to be equally divided between them.    Item - I lend unto my said wi
2 CONC fe the plantation at which I now live during her life.  After her death I give and bequeath the same to my son Charles Lee and his heirs forever.    Item - I give and bequeath unto my said grandchild Thomas Lee all that certain pi
2 CONC ece of land which I bought from Anthon slaughter situated on the north side of the plantation whereon I now live to hi m and his heirs forever.    Lastly, i do hereby nominate my son John Charles Lee Whole and sole Executor of thi
2 CONC s my Last Will and Testament.  IN WITNESS WHEREOF I have hereunto set my hand and seale this 13th day of February, 17 09.  In the presence of John Owne, Elizabeth (X) Mullins and Ringing R. Gardner.  Thomas J. Lee (SEALE)    EARLY
2 CONC  VIRGINIA IMMIGRANTS, 1623 - 1666.  Greer gives the following:  Lee, Thomas, 1648, by Lewis Burwell & Thos. Haws, York River Co.    LEE, Tho., 1652, by John Meredith, Lancaster Co.    LEE, Eliza., 1652, by Anthony Dorey and Enock 
2 CONC Hawker, Lancaster Co.  Thomas and Eliza may be the Thomas Lee listed here.
