1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Kenner Family" - The William and Mary Quarterly, Vol. 14, No. 3 (Jan., 1906), pp. 173-181.
2 CONT
2 CONT RODHAM KENNER3 (Francis,2 Richard') was probably Rev. Rodham Kenner, to whom the St. Bees Grammar School register, date after 1686, referred to by Mr. Winder' as a scholar there, describes, "born at Cherry Point, Virginia, went to
2 CONC  Glasgow and thence to Virginia as minister." He was born Sept. 28, 1707, and in 1728 was recommended to St. George's Parish, Spotsylvania county. (Meade, Old Churches, &c.) In 1730 he married Judith, daughter of Harry Beverley. D
2 CONC r. James Blair referred to him as " a very good man,"' and in March, 1734-35, he was reported as "dead or dying." (Perry, Papers relating to the church in Virginia).
2 CONT
