2 DATE 16 MAR 1759
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Keene-431
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Keene (daughter of William Keene Jr. and Ann Therriott) was born 02 May 1701, and died 16 Mar 1759. Her Grandparents were William Keene Sr. and Elizabeth Rogers.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married first husband Thomas Lee 01 Nov 1716, son of Charles Lee and Elizabeth Medstand, and he died in 1735. She married second husband James Scrosby 15 April 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the Mother of William Lee, Thomas Lee, Richard Lee, John Lee, Lucy Lee, Leanna Lee, Charles Lee, Elizabeth Lee and James Scrosby.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Removed John James Lee Sr. <[https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lee-3391  Wikitree]> as son as dates do not match up.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Garner-Keene families of Northern Neck, Virginia'', by Ruth Ritchie and Sudie Rucker Wood. (1952). Page 203.  <[https://archive.org/details/garnerkeenefamil00ritc/page/203/mode/1up Archive.Org]>
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Elizabeth4 Keene (Wm.3 Wm.2 Thos.1), born May 2, 1701, married Thomas Lee of Lancaster County. His will (Lan. W. & C. B. 12, p. 342), dated June 16, 1733 and proved June 11, 1735, did not mention his wife by name, though she wa
2 CONC s appointed one of his executors. His brother, Major Charles Lee, was mentioned, also the following chil¬ dren: (1) William5 Lee; (2) Thomas5 Lee; (3) Richard5 Lee; (4) Charles5 Lee; (5) John5 Lee; (6) another as yet unborn, proba
2 CONC bly Elizabeth5 Lee. Thomas5 Lee died in Lan¬ caster County in 1759. His will (Lan. D. & W. B. 16, p. 47) mentioned his wife, Lucy, brothers Richard, John and Charles, sister, Elizabeth, and the following children: (1) Mary6 Lee; (
2 CONC 2) George6 Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lee and Elizabeth Keene had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Lee 1717-1742,
2 CONT # Thomas Lee 1718-1759,
2 CONT # Richard Lee 1719-1758,
2 CONT # John Lee 1725-,
2 CONT # Lucy Lee 1729-,
2 CONT # Leanna Lee 1730-,
2 CONT # Charles Lee 1731-1792,
2 CONT # Elizabeth Lee 1731-.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/t/a/y/Daniel-M-Taylor-HI/GENE3-0013.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lee died just before Elizabeth was born but she was included in his will as the child his wife goes with now. She was later listed in the wills of her brother Thomas Lee in 1745 and her sister Lucy Lee in 1758. In her broth
2 CONC er's will she was listed as "Betty." Their mother married James Scrosby on April 15, 1737. It appears from records that he treated the children of his wife fairly in the distribution of all property. Their home was in Urbana, York
2 CONC  County, Virginia. It has been recorded that Elizabeth along with two of her other sisters went to live with Leeanna and her husband for a time before Elizabeth's marriage. The two sisters, Leeanna Fearn and Elizabeth Dibrell woul
2 CONC d remain close throughout their lives. According to records the terms of a gift by James Scrosby upon the marriage to their mother, both Leeanna and Elizabeth would each receive one negro boy or girl when they either reached the a
2 CONC ge of twenty-one or were married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Records include
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * LEE, Thomas. 16 June 1733. Rec. 11 June 1735.
2 CONT * Name of wife not given.
2 CONT * Sons: William, Thomas, Richard and Charles to whom is given "the land I now live on." Child unborn.
2 CONT * Son: John.
2 CONT * Exors: Wife, brother Charles Lee and Nicholas Martin.
2 CONT * Wits: Ezekiel Gilbert, Isaac Currell. W.B. 12, p. 342. Inv. returned by Elizabeth Lee his Extrx. W.B. 12, p. 243.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * LEE, Thomas. Division of estate. Rec. 12 Nov. 1742.
2 CONT * James Scrosby & Eliza. his wife, Exors. Estate divided between Elizabeth & her children Leanna, Elizabeth, Thomas, Richard, John, Charles, & Lucy Lee. W.B. 13, p. 303.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * LEE, Richard, orphan of Thomas Lee, Gent. Ezekiel Gilbert his guardian. 12 Aug. 1743. Rec. 12 Aug. 1743. W.B. 13, p. 341
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee}
2 CONT * LEE, Lucy, one of the daus. of Thos. Lee, dec. Rec. 2 Dec. 1746. Division of estate. Legatees: John Lee, Thomas Lee, Leana Fearn, Betty Lee, Richard Lee, Charles Lee, John Lee. W.B. 14, p. 147.
2 CONT * 24 Mar. 1745. '''John Lee and Lucy Lee, orphans of Thomas Lee'''. W.B. 14, p. 104.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Garner-Keene families of Northern Neck, Virginia, page 203:
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000185377457870&size=large}}
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
