1 NOTE {geni:about_me} While in England, Fleete married Sarah Burden, a widow and brought her to Virginia. They had one son, Henry Fleete." (p.66) He left his widow so well provided for that she could twice remarry respectably, first Col
2 CONC . John Walker, a member of the King's Council and later, Dr. John Stone. She could also send for her daughter in England, and bequeath young Henry (not yet of age) a deed of gift to all his father's lands. Even after remarriage sh
2 CONC e always signed her name on legal documents as "Widow Fleete". (pp.72-3)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Adventurers of Purse and Person" Vol. 1, (p.972) has more:  "Rather late in life Henry Fleete married a widow, Sarah (  ) Burden, who had a young daughter Mary Burden.  Sarah married third, bef 28 Oct 1661, Col. John Walker of Gl
2 CONC oucester County (died 1668/9) and had two daughters by him, Sarah Walker and Hester Walker, and married fourth, by 2 Nov 1672, Col John Stone, by whom she has no children.  As Sarah Walker she left a will, 28 Jan 1668/9 - 29 Dec 1
2 CONC 679." A footnote says: She named her son Henry, daughters Mary Burden,Sarah Walker and Hester Walker and Colonel Walker's six daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Henry Fleet was an early pirate/explorer who settled in Jamestown after voyaging on Lord Rich's ships, the Warwick and the Tiger, that sailed down the West African coast and to the West Indies in the 1620s and later. Upon 
2 CONC his death, his widow, Sharin [SIC: Susan] Fleet married Lieutenant Colonel John Walker of Virginia and brought into that marriage a number of enslaved Africans, including Edward Mozinga (Mozingo).
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 28 Jan 1668/9 his widow, Mrs. Sarah Walker, wrote a deed giving six slaves to Col. John Walker's six daughters, Anne Payne, Frances Walker, Jane Walker, Elizabeth Walker, Sarah Walker and Esther Walker; to Anne Payne, a filley and
2 CONC  a mare to each of her five sisters; to Frances Walker, five cows when she marries; similar gifts to four other daughters; to Anne Payne, Frances Walker, Jane Walker and Elizabeth Walker, the plate that was their father's; to son 
2 CONC Henry, silver and household effects when he comes of age; and to daughter Mary Burden, silver and household effects. This deed was recorded 29 Dec 1679. Mrs. Sarah Walker married Col. John Stone of Rappahannock Co. after the above
2 CONC  deed was written. Jane Walker married John Deane 1679; he married Elizabeth, daugher of Silvester Thatcher. Sarah Walker married Col. Edwin Conway 1685 and had Mary who married her first cousin John Daingerfield first then marrie
2 CONC d Maj. James Ball in 1707. Col. Conway married Elizabeth Thompson; they were the great grandparents of President James Madison Hester or Esther Walker married Thomas Moss first then married Capt. Edmond Crask, Clerk of the Court. 
2 CONC Henry Fleet, Jr. died in Lancaster Co. leaving a will dated 1729 (1733). ...Vivian
2 CONT
2 CONT
