2 CONT
2 CONT 13 February 1992
2 CONT
2 CONT p 16 Edward (I) MOZINGO, an illegitimate non-white, was indentured to
2 CONT Col. John WALKER. Col. WALKER married Sarah, widow of Henry FLEET, and
2 CONT had two daughters. After his death, Sarah married Col. John STONE, and
2 CONT had one daughter Anne STONE.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.angelfire.com/mt2/genealogy/html/fam1127.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah WALKER STONE reacted rather negatively to this lawsuit [to free
2 CONT Edward Mozingo]. Emphasis has been added: TO ALL CHRISTIAN PEOPLE to whom these presents shall come &C KNOW yee that I Sarah STONE Alias WALKER of the County of Rappa did in the time of my widowhood but before I had proved the wil
2 CONC l of Colonel John WALKER my Late Husband deceased did set apart certaine young Negroes Certaine Cattle Some Plate and Household Stuff which I did intend to give to the children of Coll� John WALKER deceased as also to some of my o
2 CONC wne had by him and to that Intent Richard FOX did make a writing of the Particulars soe Intended upon Consideration that I might oblige them the more to Love and Respect me and stir up filial affection in them unto me but finding 
2 CONC contrary to Expectation I am for my good will and Affection to them Contemned & despised and Rewarded with Contumelious words and approbious actions and my loving husband John STONE molested by Litigious Lawsuits and daily threate
2 CONC ned by more suits of Law doe by these presents of Wrighting Annulling Revoaking and making void all and Every the said Premises Part Parcell or Gifts therein Contained in the said Wrighting as if there Never was or had been such G
2 CONC ifts by writing made interesting and giving them fully to the disposing of my own loving husband and do further declare that I the said Sarah STONE alias WALKER did never subscribe the said Writing but what is there subscribed is 
2 CONC the act and subscription of Richard FOX and doe moreover with the consent of my loving Husband John STONE make ordaine Constitute and appoint Mr. Henry CLERK [CLARK] my true and lawful attorney to acknowledge this as my act and de
2 CONC ed in Court. IN WITNESS whereof I have sett my hand and Seale this 2nd day of November Anno 1672. Signum: Sarah (X) STONE (Seale). Signed Sealed and Delivered in the presence of Thomas BLISSED and Henry CREIGHTON. I acknowledge my
2 CONC  Consent to this as Witness my hand and Seale the day and year above written: John STONE There is no documented cause and effect relationship between the lawsuit in which Edward MOZINGO won his freedom and the revocation of Sarah 
2 CONC WALKER STONE. Nonetheless, Edward MOZINGO sued Doctor STONE, who married Col. WALKER�s widow, and she in turn revoked her gifts to WALKER�s children in part because her �loving husband John STONE� was �molested by Litigious Lawsui
2 CONC ts.� The sequence of events strongly suggests a connection between the two events.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Wills 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geocities.com/Yosemite/5273/lorna.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Will Records from Old Rappahannock County, VA.: Sarah Stone's lst Will was written before she married Col. John Stone:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Will of Sarah Walker. Dated 18 1668/9 and probated Dec. 29, 1679. "I
2 CONT Sarah Walker Doe give and bequeath unto Coll. John Walker's six daughters as Followeth: unto Annie Paine one negro boy called Richard and one young filly. To Frances Walker one negro boy called Peter and one young filly. To Jane W
2 CONC alker one negro girl named Deborah and one young filly. To Elizabeth Walker one negro girl named Susannah and one young filly. To Sarah Walker, one negro girl named Mareay (sic) and one young filly. To Easter (sic) Walker one negr
2 CONC o boy called Palmer and one young filly. To Frances, Jane, Sarah and Easter Walker 5 cows at marriage. To Anne Paine, Frances, Jane and Elizabeth Waler all the plate that was their father's to be equally divided among them. To my 
2 CONC son Henry Fleete one Silver Buckle and one Silver spoon at my decease. To my daughter Mary Burden one Silver Tankard and onw Ailcwe spoon at my decease. To my daughter Sarah Walker one Great Silver Salt cellar and one Silver spoon
2 CONC  at my decease. To my daughter Esther Walker one Silver Bason and one Silver spoon at my decease. To Frances, Jane and Elizabeth Walker ten pewter dishes at marriage. I give unto my son Henry Fleete when he cometh to age one feath
2 CONC er bed and Boulster, one Rugg, one paire blankets, one paire pillows and pillowbeeres and one paire of sheets. I give unto my daughter Mary Burden one feather bed and Boulster, one paire of blankets, one paire of sheets with a cou
2 CONC ple of pillows at her marriage. Test: Francis Settle and Richard Fox. (W.B. #2 p 142)." Evidently only two of his daughters, Col. John Walker, viz: Sarah and Esther Walker, were hers also, the other four daughters having been by C
2 CONC ol. Walkers first wife Elizabeth.......While this is called and listed as her Will, it was evidently an entirely different document, as she was later to marry again and to die as the wife of Col. John Stone of Rappahannock, later 
2 CONC Richmond County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Stone 2nd Will: "TO ALL CHRISTIAN PEOPLE to whom these presents shall com & CKNOW yee that I SarahStone, Alias Walker of the County of Rapp did in the time of my widowhood but before I had proved the Will of Colonel John Wal
2 CONC ker my Late Husband Deceased did set apart certaine young negroes Certaine Cattle Some Plate and household (goods) which I did intend to give to the children of Coll John Walker deceased as also to some of my owne had by him and t
2 CONC o that Intent Richard Fox did make a writing of the Particulars soe Intended upon Consideration that I might oblige them the more to Love and Respect me and stir up filial affection in them unto me but finding contrary to Expectat
2 CONC ion I am for my good will and affection to them Contemned and despised and Rewarded with Contumelius words and opprobrious actions and my loving husband, John Stone molested by Litigious Lawsuits and daily threatened by more suits
2 CONC  of Law doe by these presents of Wrighting Annulling Revoking and making void all and Every the said Premises Part Parcell or Gift therein Contained in the said Wrighting as if there never was or had been such Gifts by writing mad
2 CONC e interesting and giving then fully to the disposing of my own loving husband and do further declare that I the said Sarah Stone alias Walker did never subscribe the said Wrighting but what is there subscribed is the act and subsc
2 CONC ription of Richard Fox and doe moreover with the consent of my loving husband John Stone make ordaine Constitute and appoint this as act and deed in Court. IN WITNESS whereof I have sett my hand and Seale this 2nd day of November 
2 CONC Anno 1672. Signum: Sarah (X) Stone (Seale). Signed Sealed and Delivered in the presence of Thomas Blissedd and Henry Creighton. I acknowledge my Consent to this as Witness my hand and Seale the day and year above written: John Sto
2 CONC ne. Test: Thomas Blissed and Henry Crighton. (Book 5, 1671-1676, pg 10).
