2 _MARNM Conway
1 NAME Francis CONWAY (s/o Edwin); Francis CONWAY Sr
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 APR 1696
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE APR 1733
2 PLAC King George, Virginia, British Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 APR 1733
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Francis Conway, I 
2 CONT * BIRTH: 15 Sep 1696 Richmond County, Virginia, USA 
2 CONT * DEATH: 12 Apr 1733 (aged 36) King George County, Virginia, USA 
2 CONT * BURIAL	Non-Cemetery Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/81731419/francis-conway
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Thornton gave his grandson, Francis Conway his "Snow Hill" plantation in Caroline County.  His home "Mount Sion"  was built on property acquired by gant to his father Edwin.  He built up a substantial tobacco business as o
2 CONC wner of one of the first 2 chartered warehouses.   As a county magistrate he and his 2 brothers-in-law John and Thomas Catlett wer instrumental in developing rolling roads on  which tobacco could be transported to his warehouses o
2 CONC n the Rappahannock River.   
2 CONT
2 CONT He petitioned to take up 10,000 acres on the Rapidan River (The original document is at the Alderman Library a gift from Julia Conway Clark).  He was granted 5000 acres was granted to Francis Conway and Anthony Thornton (1st. cous
2 CONC ins?) on the branch of the "Raperdan River" at the Great Montains.   The land was divided by Zachary Taylor.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He also received a grant in Orange County, which would become "Hawfield" where his grandson Catlett lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was presented to the Caroline Court by his wife Rebecca Conway and was proved April 12, 1733.  She had considerable acumen and carried on the business until her son Francis Jr. was able to take over.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A son of Edwin Conway (ca. 1642–1698) and his wife, Elizabeth Thornton, was Francis Conway (1697–1733). Rebecca Catlett (d. 1760), whom Francis married about 1718, was the granddaughter of Elizabeth Underwood and John Catlett, kil
2 CONC led by Indians in a fort at Port Royal on the Rappahannock River in 1670, and a daughter of John’s son of the same name (1658–1724) and his wife, Elizabeth Gaines. Nelly Conway (1732–1829), one of the children of Francis and Rebec
2 CONC ca Catlett Conway, married James Madison, Sr., on 15 September 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * '''Military service''': Colonel
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-644658958/francis-conway-i-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 4 2020, 9:57:54 UT
2 CONC C''
2 CONT * “Conway Family.” The William and Mary Quarterly, vol. 12, no. 4, 1904, pp. 264–267. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/1915587. Accessed 10 Sept. 2020.
2 CONT *”A Genealogy of the Glassell Family of Scotland and Virginia : Also of the Families of Ball, Brown, Bryan, Conway, Daniel, Ewell, Holladay, Lewis, Littlepage, Moncure, Peyton, Robinson, Scott, Taylor, Wallace, and Others, of Virg
2 CONC inia and Maryland.” Horace Edwin Hayden E.B. Yordy, printer, 1891 - Virginia - 759 pages.  Page 231: [https://books.google.com/books?id=SJcsAAAAYAAJ&vq=Conway&pg=PA231#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * “The Madison Family Tree,” Founders Online, National Archives, https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Madison/01-01-02-0063-0001. [Original source: The Papers of James Madison, vol. 1, 16 March 1751 – 16 December 1779, ed. Will
2 CONC iam T. Hutchinson and William M. E. Rachal. Chicago: The University of Chicago Press, 1962, pp. 4–6.]
