1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p.341
2 CONT Dr. James Craik was born in 1740 in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Mariamne Ewell on Nov. 13, 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died in Fairfax Co.,VA in Feb. 6, 1814.
2 CONT He lived in Alexandria until age compelled retirement from practice, when he removed to Vaucluse, a part of the Ravensworth estate, where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Craik came to VA in 1750; was commissioned Surgeon in Col. Fry's VA. Regiment March 7, 1754 which regiment Washington commanded after Col. Fry's death.  He served in the provisional army during the French and Indian Wars; was 
2 CONC at Braddock's defeat, and dressed the wounds of that General after the battle.  He settled later at Port Tobacco, MD., but was persuaded by Washington to remove to Alexandria.  In 1777 he was appointed Ass't Director General in th
2 CONC e Hospital Dep't of the army.  He served through the war, and received from VA. 6,000 acres land for his services, March 12, 1832.  He was a member of the Society of the Cincinnati of MD. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT TOMBSTONE INSCRIPTIONS OF ALEXANDRIA, VA. VOL I by Wesley E. Pippenger, p. 101
2 CONT CRAIK, Dr. James.
2 CONT In Memory of JAMES CRAIK
2 CONT Chief Physician and Surgeon
2 CONT of the Continental Army
2 CONT Born 1727 Near Dumfries, Scotland
2 CONT Died February 4, 1814
2 CONT At his residence in Fairfax Co.
2 CONT Near Alexandria, Virginia
2 CONT In the 84 year of his age
2 CONT (Note:  This is a modern monument.  Many years ago it was claimed that the remains of Dr. James Craik lie near the wall of a dwelling house adjacent to the Presbyterian grave yard, the monument (a table stone) disappeared during t
2 CONC he Civil War.)
