2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 DEC 1831
2 ADDR
3 STAE Kentucky
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Calvert-1498
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezekiel "Zeal" Calvert was born on February 7, 1755, in Prince William, Virginia, his father, William, was 29 and his mother, Hannah, was 28. He married Mary Ewell in 1780 in Virginia. They had 12 children in 20 years. He died on 
2 CONC December 25, 1831, in Mason, Kentucky, having lived a long life of 76 years, and was buried in Lewisburg, Kentucky.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedigree Chart from Church of Latter-day Saints 1987,1990 lists spouse as Nancy Ewell. http://www.ewellfamily.org/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I19160&tree=ewellcombo Notes spouse as Nancy or Mary Ewell. Same birth year so like
2 CONC ly same person.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Conflated profile
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendents of Virginia Calverts by Ella Foy Gorman gives Zeal / Zealy Calvert, son of william, she never mentions his name being Ezekiel or anything other than various spellings of Zeal / Zealy - 
2 CONT
2 CONT Four of the daughters currently attached to this profile for Ezekiel have marriage bonds, with signatures of an assumed father
2 CONT -Dorothy in 1806, signed Zeal, in his own hand
2 CONT -Nancy in 1806, signed Ezekiel, in his own hand
2 CONT -Betsy/Elizabeth in 1807, signed Zeal, with his mark
2 CONT -Catharine in 1814, signed Zelia, with his mark
2 CONT
2 CONT All in Mason county, but this is very likely atleast two different men
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War soldier DAR Record - problems found with this ancestor
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor Comments:
2 CONT 1) FAMPCL-THE MOTHER OF THE PATRIOT’S CHILDREN HAS BEEN QUESTIONED. NO PROOF
2 CONT 2) THAT MARY NANCY EWELL WAS ONE PERSON OR THAT HER MAIDEN NAME WAS EWELL.
2 CONT 3) SEE DATACF. 8/2017
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Book: Five Generations of the Family of Burr Harrison of Virginia, 1650-1800
2 CONT Author: John P. Alcock, Heritage Books, 2008. Page 228
2 CONT
2 CONT >Quote: “William Calvert m. (1?) Caty Korn, (2) Hannah ---. Children: Elisha (1758-1784), Basil (1760-1833), John (1762-1824), Landon (1764-1809), Gerrard (1765-1840), and William b 1768. William Calvert bought 117 acres on the no
2 CONC rth side of the North Run of Neabsco in 1779. He and hs wife, Hannah, sold that land plus 65 acres given him by his father, George, to Arrington Wickliff in 1796. (12)"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
