1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Lee'''  was born c.1724 in Westmoreland County, Virginia. Most likely, he was born at Lee Hall. He was the son of  Henry Lee and wife Mary Bland. He married the widow Mary (Smith) Ball. They had no children
2 CONC . John died in 1767 at his home at Cabin Point, along the Potomac River in Westmoreland County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As the eldest son of Henry and Mary, John ordinarily would have inherited the home plantation, but John had established himself in Essex County before his father's death. Lee Hall, instead, went to brother Richard, while John inhe
2 CONC rited other property.
2 CONT
2 CONT John served in his local militia, rising to the rank of colonel. Which outfit he actually commanded is no long known, but the rank and title of colonel was not used freely in this era of Virginia history. If he was known as "Col. 
2 CONC John Lee," he earned the title. John became Clerk of the Courts for Essex County in 1745 and held that position until 1762, when he was elected Burgess for Essex County. His cousin John, son of Phillip Lee of Maryland, became the 
2 CONC next Clerk of the Courts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Smith was the daughter of Capt. Philip Smith, of Fleets Bay. Her first husband's name was Jesse Ball. After John's death she married a third time, to John Smith of Shooter's Hill,", described as "old John Smith, the Innoculat
2 CONC or" in family correspondence. Mary died in 1802. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John left a will, dated September 23, 1765, which was probated in February 2, 1767 in Westmoreland County, Virginia.After Mary's death, the bulk of John's property went to the male heirs his brothers Richard and Henry. As Richard 
2 CONC had no male heirs, the estate went to the sons of Henry Lee.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''The Bland Papers: Being a Selection from the Manuscripts of Colonel'' ...By Theodorick Bland.  Page 13 < [https://books.google.com/books?id=_kZ2AAAAMAAJ&pg=PR13#v=onepage&q&f=true link] >
2 CONT
2 CONT >”Mary Bland, eldest daughter of Richard Bland, of Jordans, Gent., was born 21st August, 1704, and married Colonel Henry Lee of Westmoreland, and by him has four children, viz.: John, Richard, Lettice and Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
