1 NOTE !BIRTH - SOME PROMINENT VA FAMILIES VOL 4, p. 38 by Louise Du Bellet
2 CONT Philip Smith, youngest son and child of John Smith of "Purton" and Mary Warner was born June 1, 1695 and died in 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Mary Mathews, daughter of Baldwin Mathews, Justice of York Co.,
2 CONT grandson of Governor Samuel Mathews in Feb. 19  1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Philip Smith died June 4, 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Smith was vestryman, Petsworth Parish 1714-1722.  He inherited "Fleet's Bay" estate in Northumberland County, VA. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 11, 1743 the will of Philip Smith was proved.  He gave 200L to each of his daughters and the residue of his estate to his son, Baldwin Mathews.  He made his brother, Augustine Warner Smith, his nephew, James Smith and his 
2 CONC son, Baldwin Mathews Smith, his executors. - Ibid p. 39
