1 NOTE !BIRTH - SOME PROMINENT VIRGINIA FAMILIES, VOL 4 by Louise duBellet, p. 41
2 CONT Baldwin Mathews Smith was the son of Philip Smith and his wife, Mary Mathews.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Fanny Burgess.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - GENEALOGICAL ABSTRACTS FROM 18TH CENTURY VIRGINIA NEWSPAPERS by Robert K. Headley, Jr., p. 313
2 CONT SMITH, Baldwin Matthews Smith of Lancaster Co., deceased, some of his slaves to be sold at Lancaster Court House by his administrator, John SMITH (VIRGINIA GAZETTE 4 Nov 1763)
2 CONT Note:  Because of no date of death, he probably died sometime in 1763. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT LANDHOLDERS & LANDHOLDINGS, CHRIST CHURCH PARISH, Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT LANDOWNERS 1720-1750 PRECINCT F
2 CONT F-7 - Baldwin Mathews Smith (absentee) 50 acres
2 CONT Absentee owner Baldwin Mathews Smith possessed this tract by virtue of his marriage to the daughter and heir of Col. Charles Burgess of Saint Mary's White Chapel Parish.  The 50 acres had a succession of many owners, most of whom 
2 CONC were absentee, including Edward Nicken, a free black, who purchased it in 1714 (DB 9:478) and soon thereafter sold it to Col Burgess.  Before Smith, the land had also been listed under the name of Jesse Ball, who had married the w
2 CONC idow of Col. Burgess.
