1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 17 DEC 1754 AND 10 FEB 1755
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ==Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Judith Steptoe''', a daughter of John Steptoe and his wife Elizabeth, widow of John Eustace, was born on 15 April 1702 in Northumberland County, Virginia, and died there on between 17 December 1754 (date will written) and 10 Fe
2 CONC bruary 1755 (date will proved).  She was still single when she was named as a legatee in Mary Swan's Will on the 20th of January 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Steptoe married twice:
2 CONT #      Richard Lee (1691-bef.1735) - married about 1721, Northumberland County, Virginia  [1]
2 CONT #     Samuel Peachy (1699-1750) -  married on the 16th of February 1749/50, Northumberland, Virginia. [2]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family of Judith Steptoe and Richard Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1720/21, in Northumberland County, Virginia, Judith married Richard Henry Lee, a son of Hancock Lee and Mary (Kendall) Lee. [2] Judith and Richard became the parents of seven children. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Lee died before the 21st of May 1735, the date when his will was probated. Judith married, secondly, Samuel Peachy, a son of William Peachy and Phebe Slaughter, as his third wife, on the 16th of February 1749/50. [2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT The seven children of Judith Steptoe and Richard Lee were:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Elizabeth Lee (abt.1720-aft.1764) who married Major Peter Conway. [3][5] 
2 CONT #     Kendall Lee Sr (1721-1780) who married Betty Heale of Lancaster. [3][5] 
2 CONT #     Mary Steptoe Lee (bef.1722-1744) who married her cousin, Charles Lee. [3] 
2 CONT #     Judith (Lee) Galloway (abt.1725-) who married David Galloway. [3] 
2 CONT #     Lettice (Lee) Ball (1731-1811) who married Colonel James Ball. [3] 
2 CONT #     Anne Lee who married George Kerr. [3][5] 
2 CONT #     Lucy Lee, who married Baldwin Matthews Smith was the last of the seven children to be identified. [3][5]  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family of Samuel Peachey
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Peachey (1699-1750) was married three times:
2 CONT # Katherine McCarty, daughter of Captain Daniel McCarty (1 child, Elizabeth)
2 CONT # Winifred Griffin, daughter of Thomas Griffin and Elizabeth Medstand Lee (4 sons: William Griffin, Samuel jr, Thomas Griffin, Leroy, and 2 daughters: (NN) Flood and (NN) Eustace.)
2 CONT # Judith Steptoe Lee, widow of Richard Lee of Ditchley (no children)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1753-1756 Record Book #3; Northumberland Co Va, (Lewis & Booker): Page 183
2 CONT * Peachey, Judith
2 CONT * W. W. 17 December 1754---W. P. 10 February 1755
2 CONT * All my estate both real and personal to be equally divided among all my children.
2 CONT * Mr. Samuel Blackwell and my son Kendal Lee executors.
2 CONT * Witness: Betty Conway, Kendal Lee, Lucy Smith and Ann Ker.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Steptoe-9
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Genealogy room of the Library in Rogersville, Hawkins County, Tennessee there is a note that, according to the DAR, a bible belonging to Capt. Thomas LEE said that he was born on 12/3/1729 at Ditchley, Northumberland, the "
2 CONC next to youngest" child of Richard Lee and Judith Steptoe. This Bible entry is apparently a 20th-century forgery, from correspondence described at that library. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
