1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/p/a/c/Janie-H-Pace/GENE2-0001.html :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. THOMAS1 WHITE was born Abt. 1670 in England, and died Abt. 1721 in Lancaster Co, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (1) UNKNOWN Abt. 1690 in Lancaster Co, VA.
2 CONT He married (2) ELINOR ROGERS Aft. 1718 in Lancaster Co, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for THOMAS WHITE: Thomas's will was recorded August 24, 1709. His wife's name is not given. He lists his sons Richard and Isaac and his brother William. He granted freedom to his personal servant, Thomas Langley in his will.
2 CONC   Witness were John Crosted, John Mill, Mil Walters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas recorded a new will on May 9, 1711 and named Elinor his wife as appointed Extrx. WB #10, page 3  Thomas's will was executed Feb 14, 1721. John Rogers was appointed guardian of Isaac, orphan of Thomas. W.B. #10, page 361.  W
2 CONC ill Book #10, page 105 Lancaster County,VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Chuck Johnson at the LDS library in Lancaster County, comes the information on Thomas White.  1. From "Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills, 1653-1800" by Ida J. Lee, 1959, Dietz Press. Inc. Richmond, VA. Page 232, E
2 CONC state Record of 14 Feb. 1721, Thomas White. John Rogers was appointed the guardian of Isaac White, orphan of Thomas White. Will Book 10. page 361. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for THOMAS WHITE and UNKNOWN:  In a Depository Public Record Office Survey Report No.3653, there is mention of a Thomas White. It reads, " Two endorsements on the second fragment read as follows: "Ann Accoumpt (sic)
2 CONC  of the passengrs (sic) passing from the porte of gravesend from the 11th August 1677 to ye (?) of Nov 1677. and "Delivered this first day of December of 1677 into the office of H.Ms Fem. these tenne Rolles by Thomas White, Clerck
2 CONC  (sic) to Wm. Monsharst & Obadiah Clayton, gents." 
2 CONT
2 CONT In a Depostory Public Record Office Survey Report No. 763, it reads, "Sale is to be completed to Thomas White of a tract of 220 acres, and of a tract of 136 acres of moorland bought from Robert Taliaferro and his wife Margaret; bo
2 CONC th tracts are in St. Mary's Parish." 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several references to Thomas as being a clerk to Monsharst and Clayton in the Library of Virginia. Proof that this is the same Thomas White as father to Isaac has become difficult as there were several Thomas Whites' in 
2 CONC Lancaster County,Virginia at the same time. However, it is a strong possibility that this is the Thomas from whom we descend.  (Pat Shannon)  pms5s@virginia.edu 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About THOMAS WHITE: Date born 2: Abt. 1670, Scotland (possibly)
2 CONT
2 CONT More About THOMAS WHITE and UNKNOWN: Marriage: Abt. 1690, Lancaster Co, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT More About THOMAS WHITE and ELINOR ROGERS: Marriage: Aft. 1718, Lancaster Co, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of THOMAS WHITE and UNKNOWN are:  
2 CONT * 2.	i.	 	ISAAC JOHN2 WHITE, b. Abt. 1700, Lancaster Co, VA; d. Bet. 1767 - 1775, Frederick Co, VA.
2 CONT *  	ii.	 	RICHARD WHITE, b. Abt. 1699; d. Abt. 1794, Old Frederick Co, VA. 	Notes for RICHARD WHITE: It is thought that Richard White was married and had two children. However, secondary sources imply that his family was killed by
2 CONC  Indians in colonial Virginia. Pat Shannon Research Material.  More About RICHARD WHITE: Burial: Old Frederick Co, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT !11 Oct 1727: Isaac White & Mary Ann Ewell. Sec. Wm. Ballendine. Marriage Bonds in Lancaster County. William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine, Vol. 12, No. 2 (Oct., 1903), pp. 96-103. Change Date: 27 AUG 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This is not the same person as Isaac John White who was married to Catherine Lawson.  Their profiles had gotten merges but that has been corrected.  Please do not remerge!'''  It seems the bad merges were probably the result of
2 CONC  gedcom uploads from trees with incorrect connections.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record for Isaac White and Mary Ann Ewell is posted under Media tab.  They married in 1727. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One Wiki page (there is more than one for these same folks)  has that Catherine Lawson was this Isaac's 2nd wife and doesn't refer to him as Isaac John as her husband usually shows.  However, the sources that is based on is just o
2 CONC ther personal trees, no marriage record, no actual documentation.  The facts are that it is shown Isaac and Mary Ann married in 1727 and Mary Ann didn't die until 1796.  Every indication that can be documented is that Mary Ann was
2 CONC  his only wife.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Va Wills and Administrations list Isaac as recording his inventory in 1767. It is not known when the exact date of death was recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has become a strong possibility that Maryann Ewell was not Isaac's first wife. The children's birth dates indicate that perhaps Isaac was married and from that union had three children. His wife may have suddenly died and he qu
2 CONC ickly remarried to ensure a safe and maternal upbringing for his children. He and Maryann then most likely had Isabel, Isaac and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded in Old Frederick County in 1735, Isaac listed his family as Presbyterian and his country of origin as Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above date of 1735 represents the time of settlement in Old Frederick County. This sources states that several of the families later went south to the Carolinas. Some 73 families migrated south. We have proof that Isaac and Ma
2 CONC ryann remained in Frederick County as their wills registration and probate records indicate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac, Maryann, and Richard White are buried in Old Frederick County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no records of Isaac and Maryann owning any slaves at any time.
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE: Charles Ewell died before Mary Ann married Isaac. William Ballentine signed as her guardian. PAGE The Will Book Vol 10, page 361 Chuck Johnson, Researcher
2 CONT
2 CONT ABBR Va Wills and Adminstrations 1632-1800 TITL Wills recorded in local courts of Va 1632-1800, and of Administration on Estates shown by Inventories of the Estates of Intestates recorded in Will (and other) books of local courts.
2 CONC  AUTH Clayton Torrence PUBL Published through the courtesy of the National Society of the Colonial Dames of America. The William Byrd Press, Inc, Printers, Richmond, Va TEXT Listed under the heading, Frederick: Isaac 1767 i Mary 1
2 CONC 796 w
2 CONT
2 CONT page 453Given Name: Isaac JohnChange: Date: 11 NOV 2010
