2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/White-7406 WikiTree Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 20 2020, 0:52:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Va Wills and Administrations list Isaac as recording his inventory in 1767. It is not known when the exact date of death was recorded. It has become a strong possibility that Maryann Ewell was not Isaac's first wife. The children'
2 CONC s birth dates indicate that perhaps Isaac was married and from that union had three children. His wife may have suddenly died and he quickly remarried to ensure a safe and maternal upbringing for his children. He and Mary Ann then
2 CONC  most likely had Isabel, Isaac and John.  Recorded in Old Frederick County in 1735, Isaac listed his family as Presbyterian and his country of origin as Scotland.  The above date of 1735 represents the time of settlement in Old Fr
2 CONC ederick County. This sources states that several of the families later went south to the Carolinas. Some 73 families migrated south. We have proof that Isaac and Mary Ann remained in Frederick County as their wills registration an
2 CONC d probate records indicate.  Isaac, Mary Ann, and Richard White are buried in Old Frederick County,VA.  Source: pms5s@virginia.edu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no records of Isaac and Mary Ann owning any slaves at anytime. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750 Census - Lancaster Co, VA Library of Virginia, "Colonial Records Division" Author: The Library of Virginia; Text: Survey Report No. 1312. pg 2 #01190 pg 128-130.  1759 Census - Frederick Co, VA (David Ashworth, Certified Gene
2 CONC alogist) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Isaac White, Sergeant, Sep 1758, Frederick Co, VA. Virginia Colonial MIlitia, 1651-1776.  Virginia Colonial Militia, 1651-1776. Drozier, William Armstrong. Richmond, VA, USA: Southern Book Co, 1905. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for MARY ANN EWELL: Charles Ewell, her father, died before Mary Ann married Isaac. William Ballentine signed as her guardian.  Source: World Wide Genealogical Message Board Archive, Title: Latter Day Saints, pg: The Will Boo
2 CONC k, Vol 10, pg 361. Charles Johnson, Researcher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About MARY ANN EWELL: Burial: Old Frederick Co, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT More About ISAAC WHITE and MARY EWELL: Marriage: 11 Oct 1727, Lancester Co, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of ISAAC WHITE and MARY EWELL are: 
2 CONT  	i.	 	WILLIAM3 WHITE, b. 1723, VA; d. 04 Feb 1819; m. NANCY ELIZABETH UNKNOWN.
2 CONT  	ii.	 	SARA WHITE, b. 1724, VA; m. SAMUEL SMITH.
2 CONT  	iii.	 	THOMAS WHITE, b. 1725, VA; d. 1804; m. FRANCES UNKNOWN.
2 CONT  	iv.	 	ISABELL WHITE, b. 1728, Lancaster Co, VA; m. NEWSOM COOPER. 3.	v.	 	ISAAC WHITE, SR, b. 1729, Lancaster Co, VA; d. Aft. 05 Apr 1801, Union Co, SC. 4.	vi.	 	JOHN WHITE, SR, b. 1730, VA; d. 26 Oct 1819, Union District, SC.
