1 NAME Maurice /Jones/
2 GIVN Maurice
2 SURN Jones
2 _MARNM Jones
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1664
2 PLAC Fleets Bay
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 APR 1733
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maurice Jones, youngest son of Robert Jones of Fleet's Bay & his wife Martha.  Married 2nd to Judith, daughter of Capt Alexander Swann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://archive.org/stream/jstor-1915269/1915269#page/n5/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT April 18, 1733. The will of Capt Maurice Jones was presented  for probate by his widow, Mrs. Judith Jones. Mr. Swann Jones,  and Spencer Ball executors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, the will books of this time are missing, so that  the provisions of the will are gleaned only in part from the  meagre items of the Order Books. As was often the case, Capt.  Jones may have provided for his older ch
2 CONC ildren before his mar-  riage with Judith Swann. It is hardly possible that Swann was  his eldest son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When the will was probated, and probably from a provision  of the will, a deed of lease and release to 100 acres of land in  Wicomico Parish was made to Wm. Garlington, perhaps a  nephew of Capt. Jones. Power of atty. from Mrs. El
2 CONC izabeth  Jones, wife of Swan Jones, was given to Charles Jones and  proved by Mrs Judith Jones & Spencer Ball. Mrs Judith Jones  relinquished her right of dower in this 100 acres, and Mr. Charles  Jones, atty. for Elizabeth, wife 
2 CONC of Swann in her behalf, relin-  quished her right of dower in sd. land. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Judith Jones, widow of Capt Maurice, died 1742. 
2 CONT
2 CONT April 13, 1742, Spencer Ball petitioned for administration  upon her estate in behalf of his four children, Judith, Mattrom,  Betty and William Ball. 
2 CONT
2 CONT May 10, 1742, Spencer Ball agreed to surrender certain prop-  erty to Zachary Taylor gent, of Orange Co, present husband of  Elizabeth, the mother of John Jones and orphan of Swan Jones,  gent., deed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the records the children of Capt. Morris Jones probably  were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Mary Quarterly 269 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Chas., b. before 1700, d. 1759 m., first, Elizabeth (possibly  Lee), second, Mary Lampkin, widow of Theo (?) Lampkin, six  children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Swann, b. after 1700, d. before 1742, m. Elizabeth, who  m., second, Zachary Taylor of Orange Co. Child, John Jones. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 Betty, m. Smith, before 1721. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Judith, b. 171 m. Spencer Ball; children: (a) Judith b.  1730, died April 30 1759; m. Jan 17, 1750 John Cralle. (b)  Mattrom (c) Betty m William Roane, had Spencer & Thomas  (d) William. For further account see Hayden's Genealo
2 CONC gies. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Mr. Chas. Jones, Sr. (Capt Maurice, 2 Robert 1 ) born pro.  before 1700, d. 1755, m. 1st, Elizabeth, 2nd, Mary Lampkin,  widow. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Maurice Jones' will is missing, but various records  make it seem probable that Chas. Jones, Sr. was his son. Chas.  Jones, Jr., son of William and Leanna (Lee) Jones was born in  St. Stephen's Parish in July, 1710, and died
2 CONC  before 1739, leaving  one child, an infant dau., Ann, named in her grandfather's will,  1741 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT From www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I024310&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT >1699-1706 Order Book Part 1 - Northumberland Co Va; Hamrick: Pg 300 Northumberland County Court - 22d day of June An'o 1704
2 CONT
2 CONT >M'r JOHN CARNEGIE & WINIFRED his wife late WINIFRED HEWLETT ag't Capt. MAURICE JONES Exec'r of ROBT JONES dec'ed Cont'd till next Court at the Prts Moc'on
