2 CONT Another Harding descendant:
2 CONT
2 CONT  From: Bbaughn <Bbaughn@aol.com>
2 CONT
2 CONT  Date: Sun, 24 May 1998 00:04:14 EDT
2 CONT
2 CONT  Subject: Arledge Connection
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pam,
2 CONT
2 CONT  I have enjoyed your web page on the Arledge family. My possible connection is
2 CONT
2 CONT  thru Clement Ardridge and Mary Tilles' daughter, Mary Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT  My line is:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Henry Harding (1666-1698 VA) md. Jane Arledge.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) William Harding (1690 VA- 1752) wife Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Thomas Harden (1716 VA - bef 25 May 1809 NC) md. Unknown 1st wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT     If this Thomas Harden is the father of Jane Harden has not been proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Jane Harden (c1750 NC - 1 Jun 1832 MO) md. William Hornbuckle.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Sarah Jane Hornbuckle (c1772 NC - prob. before 1810 KY) md. Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT  Overstreet.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Martha Overstreet ( 2 Oct 1797 KY - 7 Jul 1864 KY) md. Joseph Baughn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) James Henry Baughn ( 22 Feb 1834 KY - 2 Feb 1898 KY) md. Elizabeth Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT  Walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8) Otis James Baughn (23 Apr 1877 KY - 11 Feb 1948 AZ) md. Mary Holman
2 CONT
2 CONT  Fairhurst.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9) Alfred Fairhurst Baughn (1 May 1912 AZ - ) md. Barbara Doris Hobbs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10) Brent Fairhurst Baughn ( 27 Jun 1941 CA - )    --- ME ---
2 CONT
2 CONT The Harding connections were by correspondance with Lee Pound. He did this
2 CONT
2 CONT thru deeds, wills and court records. He has Henry Harding md. to Jane Arledge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maybe this is your Mary Jane.  Henry Harding (1666-1698) is the son of Thomas Harden and Anne Mosley. He is  the immigrant ancestor. The Hardings are from London, ENG. and the early  family is in Tyler's Quarterly Magazine "Hardin
2 CONC gs of London and Virginia" by  Mrs. O. A. Keach.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Brent Baughn     < Bbaughn@aol.com >
2 CONT
2 CONT ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
2 CONT
2 CONT The latest on the subject casts doubt that any of these were children of Jane Arledge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Subject: Re: Hardin-Arledge
2 CONT
2 CONT Date: Wed, 26 Aug 1998 22:59:45 EDT
2 CONT
2 CONT From: LEPound@aol.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Pam,
2 CONT
2 CONT I won't try to get into a lot of detail, however, I now believe that the Henry Harding lines that have been thrown around for so many years are incorrect, including much of what you have in your chart.
2 CONT
2 CONT In late June I decided that there were so many contradictions in the Harding lines that I needed to see just what could be proven and what could not be proven and was I surprised.
2 CONT
2 CONT It's taken about two months to copy out all the Harding references in Northumberland County, VA and in other Northern Neck counties up to Loudoun,
2 CONT
2 CONT resulting in hundreds of entries and about 75 pages of material.
2 CONT
2 CONT That said, here are my new comments on your chart:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Henry Harding and Jane Arledge have no provable children.  All sources
2 CONT
2 CONT list four children, Henry, John, Thomas, and William.  This is from a
2 CONT
2 CONT speculative comment in an article written by Mrs. Keach in the 1920's in
2 CONT
2 CONT Tylers Quarter, which is the basis for the structure of the family as
2 CONT
2 CONT currently accepted.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  Henry Harding who married Jane Arledge was still under 21 in August 1691
2 CONT
2 CONT per court records.  He most likely married within the next year or two. He
2 CONT
2 CONT died in August 1697 when his wife filed for probate, not May 1698.  Jane is
2 CONT
2 CONT the only name Jane Arledge is known under in the records.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  Henry Harding II, supposed son of Henry Harding  and Jane Arledge, was
2 CONT
2 CONT married by early 1708 in Northumberland Co., VA, proven by a court record
2 CONT
2 CONT where Henry and Anne, widow of William Beltcher Jr, probate his estate, not
2 CONT
2 CONT 1714-15.  If Henry II was the son of Henry and Jane, he would have been 14-15
2 CONT
2 CONT years old at marriage.  Not likely.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  Henry and Jane's other listed sons are figments of the imagination.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas does not exist and was never assigned a family by any researcher. John is most likly the son of William Harding, Henry's brother, proven by a
2 CONT
2 CONT Westmoreland Co. court order.  William was invented and the dates of his
2 CONT
2 CONT children were changed by 10 years from parish registers to make him fit the
2 CONT
2 CONT family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  The only proven child of Henry Harding II is Henry III.  All others are
2 CONT
2 CONT speculation.  Charles belongs in neither position that you have him in. If
2 CONT
2 CONT you look carefully you will note you have him twice, under Henry and under
2 CONT
2 CONT William, both times married to Rachel Lunsford.  William may belong in this
2 CONT
2 CONT family but there is nothing to connect him.  George may belong here too but
2 CONT
2 CONT there is no proof.
2 CONT
2 CONT I need to e-mail Sue Harris and Brent Baughn with the results of myresearch
2 CONT
2 CONT since it is such a radical change.  Ironically, I keep coming back to my
2 CONT
2 CONT original idea of Brent's ancestry, which also mine, the more I research, and
2 CONT
2 CONT not the line he sent you, which is now clearly incorrect.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following are my basic charts.  I have details for each individual amounting
2 CONT
2 CONT to dozens of records in some cases.  I don't know how much interest you have
2 CONT
2 CONT in this line since it is now my belief that Henry and Jane Harding had no
2 CONT
2 CONT children.  The numbering system is generational, that is 1132 is the second
2 CONT
2 CONT child of the third child of the first child.  Hopefully the e-mail does not
2 CONT
2 CONT screw it up too much.  Let me know if you are interested in a full copy of the
2 CONT
2 CONT work I've done.  There are five different families, not one as in most
2 CONT
2 CONT sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lee Pound
2 CONT
