1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Pope, 1722:
2 CONT
2 CONT > I give and bequeath unto Isaac Basie my gray broad cloth coat, vest and breeches.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Pope and Isaac Basye are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. Isaac Basye was born ABT 1692.
2 CONT * ii. William Basye was born ABT 1693. He married Rebecca Martin, daughter of Nicholas Martin and Jane Rogers.
2 CONT * iii. John "IB" Basye was born 1695 in Northumberland Co. VA, and died 13 Nov 1769 in Northumberland Co. VA. He married Hannah Taylor, daughter of Benjamin Taylor and Elizabeth Waters. She was born in VA.
2 CONT * iv. Jesse Basye was born ABT 1700. He married Martha Sutton, daughter of John Sutton and Elizabeth Lunceford. She died AFT 20 Jul 1816.
2 CONT * v. Winifred Basye was born ABT 1705. She married Marsh.
2 CONT * vi. Judith Basye was born ABT 1710.
2 CONT * vii. Elisha Basye was born ABT 1718.
2 CONT * viii. Edmund Basye was born ABT 1720 in Northumberland Co. VA, and died 1804 in Culpeper County, Virginia He married Winnifred Taylor 1749, daughter of Benjamin Taylor and Elizabeth Waters. She was born 1732 in Culpeper County, 
2 CONC Virginia, and died Jan 1805 in Culpeper County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Basie and Thomas Pitman, named as estate executors along with wife Ann Pope, seem to have been sons in law of married daughters, not named in Will.  Since the 4 named sons were underage, it seems likely there had been a firs
2 CONC t, unnamed wife, mother of daughters already married in 1722.  Ann Pope was born about 1703, and https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Basye/6000000005664874200 was supposedly having children by 1692.  Was she a sister of John Pop
2 CONC e; a more distant relative; a second wife?
2 CONT
