2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I083521&tree=Tree1
2 CONT * http://www.reynoldspatova.org/histories/Dameron%20Pedigree.pdf
2 CONT * https://www.familyhistory.bryantdameron.com/plantations.html Guarding Point was likely built before the Civil War by the Harding family. The home sets on land purchased by Lawrence Dameron in 1655 and held in the Dameron family 
2 CONC for over 200 years. The property was also known as Garden Point and Dameron Marsh. A home known as Gascony borders the property and is said to have been burnt by the British during the Revolution, it also came into the possession 
2 CONC of the Harding family and was rebuilt in 1848. Dameron Marsh is now a 316 acre Natural Area Preserve
2 CONT *http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~kyjohnso/LawDameronFT.htm
