1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/44489327/lazarus-dameron
2 CONT
2 CONT Lazarus Dameron probably was born Wicomico Parish. His parents George Dameron & Elizabeth Bunbury/Bumbury/Bunberry. More proof needs to be found to confirm Elizabeth's maiden name. She did marry a John Dennis before George Dameron
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The Elizabeth Dameron (Unknown) was married also to John Dennis.  She was not a Dennis by birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000191712351844&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-34360
2 CONT *THE DAMERON-DAMRON GENEALOGY, Compiled by Helen Foster Snow, p 13, https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=oU0ZAQAAMAAJ&hl=en&pg=GBS.PA13
2 CONT *Kirk, Robert, Married Well and Often: Marriages of the Northern Neck of Virginia, 1649-1800, Genealogical Publishing Company, 2003
2 CONT *U.S. and International Wedding Records, 1560-1900
2 CONT *Marriages of the Northern Neck of Virginia, 1649-1800
2 CONT
2 CONT '''See an excerpt from a document of Dameron marriages under Media / Document where she is referred to as the widow of John Dennis when she married George Dameron.'''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "GEORGE, son of above Lawrence, who married Elizabeth Dennis, widow of John Dennis, in 1679 or 1680. He inherited the manor at Guarding Point in Wicomico Parish, which was kept by his descendants until 1819 when land was deeded by
2 CONC  Robert J. Dameron to John Hopkins Harding and William Harding, brothers. Robert made deeds to both Hardings and Jennie Harding Cornelius says: 'All William's brothers inherited much property and money from him and it is likely th
2 CONC is property was bought by William Harding and given to his brother J. Hopkins or his children.' The old Dameron house was torn down about 1819 . George Dameron died 1698 and his brother Bartholomew administered the estate April 15
2 CONC , 1702. The children of George Dameron were Elizabeth, Thomas, George and Lazarus."
2 CONT
2 CONT Quoting The Damerons of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *Mary Elizabeth DAMERON b: BET 1675 AND 1681 in Wicomico Parish, Northumberland Co., VA
2 CONT *Thomas DAMERON b: 1683 in Northumberland Co., VA
2 CONT *George DAMERON b: 1685 in Northumberland Co., VA
2 CONT *Grace DAMERON b: 1687
2 CONT *Lazarus DAMERON b: ABT 1690 in Wicomico Parish, Northumberland Co., VA
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FIRST HUSBAND
2 CONT *John Dennis,  CHILD  
2 CONT *Joseph Dennis
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary' maiden name might have been Appleford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Dennis, 3rd, son of John Dennis, Sr, and Barbara………………b. about 1649 in Virginia) [Birth: Virginia Colonial Abstracts, Vol. 1, Northumberland County, Virginia]. John died before March 19, 1679 in St. Stephen’s Parish, Northumb
2 CONC erland County, Virginia. He married Elizabeth (maiden name unknown). Elizabeth was born in 1645 in Wicocomoco, Virginia and died 1725 in St. Stephen’s Parish, Northumberland, Virginia. On March 19, 1679 Mr. George Bledsoe was appo
2 CONC inted as one of the appraisers of the estate of John Dennis of which Elizabeth Dennis, the widow, administered his final will. Elizabeth Dennis afterwards married George Dameron. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John and Elizabeth Dennis included: 
2 CONT *John Dennis, 4th, b. 1667 in St. Stephen’s Parish, and d. 1687 or 1700; and 
2 CONT *Sarah Dennis, b. 1677, and d. April 18, 1716, she married Phillip Tignor on September 25, 1699.. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Cher, Centre, France
