1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac Coppedge[55] was born in 1737 in Northumberland, Virginia, United States. He married Elizabeth Dameron in 1763. He died on 10 Feb 1807[56].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~sharprm/genealogy/coppage.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ISAAC COPPEDGE (ca. 1737 - 1807) of Fauquier & Scott Co., Kentucky. Subject of Chapter Nine.
2 CONT pg 37
2 CONT
2 CONT ISAAC COPPEDGE (ca. 1737-1807) of Northumberland, Prince William and Fauquier Cos., Va. and of Scott Co., Ky., next younger bro. of Moses Coppedge, soldier of the French and Indian War. Isaac was a road surveyor in 1761 in Prince 
2 CONC William and Fauquier Cos. When his cousin John Coppedge died about 1760-3 he married the widow, Elizabeth Dameron Coppedge, dau. of Christopher Dameron (d. 1764) and his wife Sarah Ball, dau. of Capt. George Ball (1683-1746) of "B
2 CONC ay View" in Northumberland by his wife Gracie Haynie, dau. Anthony Haynie and Sarah Harris, dau. Major John Harris (of the family of Harris of Hayne and Radford in Devon, pictured by Inglis Fletcher in Roanoke Hundred, 91 and 99) 
2 CONC and his wife Grace, widow of Richard Perse; Christopher Dameron was son of Bartholomew Dameron (son of Lawrence and Dorothy) and Elizabeth, dau. Christopher Garlington (of the ancient family of Girlington of Normanby in England) ;
2 CONC  Capt. George Ball was son of Capt. Wm. Ball (and Margaret, granddau. Col. William Underwood) son of Col. William Ball, Royalist of "Millenbeck" in Lancaster, great-grandfather of George Washington. Isaac bought 212 acres in Staff
2 CONC ord Co. in 1779 which he and Elizabeth deeded to James Leach in 1780 (See Stafford Deed Bk. S, 16 and Fauquier Will Bk. I, 240). On 16 Jan. 1786 Isaac Coppedge was granted 500 acres in Fayette Co., Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT (See W. R. Jillson, Old Kentucky Deeds and Entries) As Isaac Copige he appears on an old petition printed by the Filson Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Charles Coppage, d. 1817
2 CONT * Rodham Coppage, received tract of land purchased of William Steel under will of his father, Isaac, proved in 1807.
2 CONT *  Lucy Coppage m. KEARNS
2 CONT * Nancy Coppage, inherited house and home field until her marriage, when it should pass to Rodham Coppage.
2 CONT *  Grace Coppage m. 1792 PHILES or John P. HILL pg84
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Well and Often: Marriages of the Northern Neck of Virginia, 1649-1800 COPPEDGE (fnu) & DAMERON, Elizabeth; bef.28 Jun 1863; bride dau. of Christopher DAMERON (d. NC 1763-64); (NC RB 6:337)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Will Records of Scott County, Kentucky 1794-Feb. 1820 OS 
2 CONT * Page: 354
2 CONT *  Name: Isaac Coppedge
2 CONT * My son, Charles My son, Rollen, land which I purchased of William Steel My daughter, Lucy Kearns My daughter, Nancy My daughter, Gracy Philes My son, Rollin and Fielding Bradford, Exe.
2 CONT * Written: 10 February 1807
2 CONT * Witnesses: William Steel, Thomas Foster, and Jesse Threlkeld
2 CONT * Probated: March 1807
2 CONT
