1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Generation No. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  WILLIAM1 DAVENPORT was born Abt. 1748 in Possibly Richmond, VA, and died Abt. 1823 in Casey Co, KY.  He married COMFORT FISHER 1770 in Accomack Co, VA.  She was born Abt. 1752, and died 30 Nov 1837 in Casey Co, KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for WILLIAM DAVENPORT: More About COMFORT FISHER: Burial: South Fork Cemetery- Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of WILLIAM DAVENPORT and COMFORT FISHER are: 2.    i.    JOHN2 DAVENPORT, b. 1771, Surry Co, NC; d. 20 Jul 1835, Casey Co, KY. 3.    ii.    MARY DAVENPORT, b. 1773, Surry Co, NC. 4.    iii.    AGNES DAVENPORT, b. Abt. 177
2 CONC 4, Surry Co, NC. 5.    iv.    THOMAS DAVENPORT, b. Abt. Apr 1776, Surry Co, NC; d. Abt. 1862, Casey Co, KY. 6.    v.    SARAH DAVENPORT, b. 1778, Surry Co, NC. 7.    vi.    GEORGE P. DAVENPORT, b. Abt. 1781, Surry Co, NC; d. 14 Fe
2 CONC b 1845, Sangamon Co, IL. 8.    vii.    WILLIAM DAVENPORT, b. 1782, North Carolina; d. 16 Mar 1837, Dewitt Co, IL. 9.    viii.    MARGARET DAVENPORT, b. 1786, Surry Co, NC; d. Aft. 1860, Macon Co, IL.
2 CONT     ix.    HENRY DAVENPORT, b. 1788, Surry Co, NC; d. 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married Comfort Fisher in Accomack Co. Virginia in 1770.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1852 his fourth child, Thomas, made application for pension  in Casey County, Kentucky.  Williams 8th child, Margaret Davenport Clifton, was the only other child living on that date.  Paschal's History of North Carolina Baptist
2 CONC s, The Surry county Congregation was known as the Davenport Church in the early days.  The Church History lists William, his wife Comfort and John as early members and meetings were held in their hourse until the first church was 
2 CONC built.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
