2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT EDWARDS, Thomas. Will. 14 Nov. 1759. Rec. 15 Feby. 1760.
2 CONT * Wife (no name)
2 CONT * Son Richard.
2 CONT * Daughters Betty and Lucy, estate of my mother-in-law Mrs. Ann Ingram in Northumberland county;
2 CONT * Sons: Thomas and Robert.
2 CONT * Dau. Mary Fleet and release of her husband Maj. Fleet from my debt.
2 CONT * Dau. Sarah Keene, and release of her husband Capt. Keene, from my debt. 
2 CONT * Niece Betty Whiting;
2 CONT * Sister, Mrs. Dorothy Matthews;
2 CONT * Daus.-in-law Mrs. Judith Fauntleroy and Mrs. Ann Haynie; Col. Landon Carter, Col. Armistead Churchill, Rev. Mr. Currie; Negro man Stephen which will belong to Mr. Swann's estate at wife's death; son Robert land known as Fleet's 
2 CONC Point.
2 CONT *  Extrs. Sons Thomas and Richard Edwards. 
2 CONT *  W.B. 16, Page 80.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
