1 NOTE !MAR - LANCASTER CO., VA MARRIAGE BONDS 1652-1850 compiled by Ida J. Lee, p. 48
2 CONT 10 Feb 1734 - Opie, Lindsy of Northumberland to Sarah Heale, dau. of George Heale.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - ABSTRACTS LANCASTER CO., VA, WILLS 1653-1800 by Ida J. Lee, p.169
2 CONT Evidently 1st wife, Sarah had died and he had married again to Elizabeth ___. 
2 CONT ABSTRACTS LANCASTER CO., VA, WILLS 1653-1800 by Ida J. Lee, p. 169
2 CONT Opie, Lindsey - DEED  4 June 1763    Rec. 15 July 1773
2 CONT Deed between Lindsey Opie of Northumberland Co. and Elizabeth his wife and Andrew Robertson of Lancaster Co., physician, for 105 lbs current money land in Lancaster containing 103 1/2 acres being part of a tract devised by last wi
2 CONC ll and testament of George Heale, gent., of Lancaster Co. bearing date 13 Dec. 1697, to son Joseph, remainder to his son John, both of whom died without issue.  The 1st sd tract descended to Elizabeth, Sarah, Anne & Catherine, dau
2 CONC ghters & coheirs of George, eldest son of sd. Geo Heale, in Fee simple but being equally divided the above mentioned part descended to Lindsey Opie heir at law of sd Sarah except 1/3 part which Mrs. Hannah Crump holds as her dower
2 CONC  during her natural life.  W.B. 17, p.11
2 CONT Note:  Lindsey Opie is showing how he inherited tract of land descended to Lindsey Opie heir at law of said Sarah.  He is married to Elizabeth so Sarah was probably his first wife. - JMC
2 CONT !MAR - EARLY VIRGINIA MARRIAGES Edited by William Armstrong Crozier, p. 51
2 CONT Feb. 18, 1734 - Lindsay Opie and Sarah Heale, daughter of George Heale -
2 CONT Lancaster Co., VA.
