1 NOTE {geni:about_me} After the death of Colonel Tayloe, his widow seems to have taken up residence in Lancaster County and cohabitated with James Burne; her brother-in-law, Joseph Tayloe, Gentleman, complained to the Lancster County co
2 CONC urt that they were "vehemently disposed of fornication and incontinency" in October 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Anne Tayloe, widow, seems to have married the said James Burne shortly thereafter and he died testate in Lancaster County in 1721. Anna Catherine Tayloe Ball and Samuel Ball were administrators of the James Burn/Bourne's esta
2 CONC te.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=adgedge&id=I25503
