2 CONT
2 CONT (1) 1716, 14 Nov: At Lancaster Co., VA court, the county of Lancaster being indebted for 6,000 pounds of tobacco, ordered a levy of 5 3/4 pounds of tobacco by the poll to be collected by Capt. Richard BALL, Sheriff, from every tit
2 CONC heable person in the county, and he to pay the same to the several creditors. On Mr. Thomas CARTER's list, Jos. TAYLOE was assessed for 6 titheables, and James BURN for 1 titheable.
