2 CONT (1) "The Tayloes of Virginia and Allied Families," by W. Randolph Tayloe (Berryville, VA, 1963) p.1,79. FHL #929.273 T211t. (2) "Enclyclopedia of Virginia Biography," Vol. 5 (Lewis Historical Pub. Co., New York, 1915) p.716. (3) "
2 CONC The Parish Register of Christ Church, Middlesex Co., VA 1653-1812," p.10. FHL #873,777. (4) "The Octagon," by George McCue (American Institute of Architects Foundation, Washington D.C., 1976) p.9. (5) Tayloe family records from Mt
2 CONC . Airy, VA, extracted 29 Sep 1927 (by Cabell Gwathmey?). (6) "Genealogy of the Virginia Family of Lomax by one of the Seventh Generation in the Direct Line" (1913) p.47,50. FHL #929.273 L 8 37l.  ! Birth: (1) d/o Henry Corbin/Alic
2 CONC e Eltonhead of Buckingham House in Middlesex Co., VA. (2,5) d/o Henry Corbin. (3) 9 Feb 1664. (3,4) d/o Henry and Alice Corbin. (6) d/o Henry Corbin/Alice Eltonhead. Baptism: (3) 29 Feb 1664, Christ Church, Middlesex Co., VA. Marr
2 CONC iage to Col. William Tayloe: (1,2,5,6) (4) 1685. Death: (4,6) 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT the Northern Neck of Virginia still looks very much like it did in colonial times. Carolyn Daily O'Connor
2 CONT  took this photo of cattle grazing near Mount Airy in October 1990. The gardens behind Mount Airy were in full bloom in June 1999. John Tayloe built the home in 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Corbin, fourth daughter of Alice Eltonhead and Henry Corbin, lived at Mount Airy after her marriage to William Tayloe in 1685. She was only 30 when she died in 1694.
