1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Elizabeth Hackley (c.1694-1756)
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary
2 CONT Elizabeth née Shippey was a colonial Virginian whose life spanned the late 17th and mid-18th centuries in the Northern Neck region. Born to Richard Shippey and Eleanor Mott, she lived across Essex and King George counties as a lan
2 CONC downer's wife and matriarch overseeing family property, with her lineage anchored in the interrelated Shippey, Mott, and Hackley households of colonial Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage
2 CONT Father: Richard Shippey (c. 1650 – 1708)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Eleanor "Ellen" Mott (c. 1673 – 1741)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1694, Northern Neck, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: August 5, 1756, King George County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Colony of Virginia (Unverified exact site)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue
2 CONT Spouse: James Hackley (c. 1691 – 1748)
2 CONT Married: Circa 1711, Essex County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Ellin (Elen) Hackley (c. 1714 – c. 1790) — Married Thomas Stubblefield
2 CONT 2. John Hackley (c. 1716 – 1760) — Married Judith Ball
2 CONT 3. Joseph Hackley
2 CONT 4. Lancelot (Lot) Hackley
2 CONT 5. Mary Hackley — Married [first name unknown] Underwood
2 CONT 6. Lucy Hackley
2 CONT 7. Francis Hackley
2 CONT 8. James Hackley Jr. (c. 1742 – 1822) — Married Mary Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Factual Information and Relevance
2 CONT Northern Neck Family Lineage: Connected directly to the Shippey and Mott landholding families of Richmond and Westmoreland counties through her parents' marriage and subsequent colonial quit-claim records.
2 CONT
2 CONT King George County Residence: Resided alongside her husband James Hackley on family holdings in King George County, where they raised an established family whose members subsequently intermarried into prominent Culpeper County lin
2 CONC eages (such as the Stubblefields).
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate Context: Outlived her husband James, who died in August 1748, participating in the regional social and familial networks of the Northern Neck until her own death in the mid-1750s.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources and Records
2 CONT Colonial Deeds and Court Records: Richmond County, Virginia, Deed Book 3, page 122 (Quit-claim involving Richard and Ellen Shippey); Westmoreland County Deeds and Wills.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate and Family Records: King George County, Virginia, probate and land conveyances tracking the Hackley and Shippey family estates through the mid-18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondary References:
