1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==James Hackley (c.1691-1748)
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary
2 CONT James Hackley was a colonial Virginia landowner whose family line is established in Essex, King George, and Culpeper counties. Born in the late 17th century in Virginia, he was a son of colonist John Hackley and inherited land and
2 CONC  property in the Northern Neck region.
2 CONT His parentage and family origin are proven by his father's 1698 Essex County will, which explicitly names James as an heir. James established his household in King George County, where his estate was probated following his death i
2 CONC n 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage
2 CONT Father: John Hackley (c. 1655 – 1698)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth Bowler (Widow Ridgedale; c. 1665 – 1756)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1691, Old Rappahannock / Essex County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: August 5, 1748, King George County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Colony of Virginia (Unverified exact site)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue
2 CONT Spouse: Elizabeth Shippey (c. 1694 – 1756)
2 CONT Married: Circa 1711, Essex County, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Ellin (Elen) Hackley (c. 1714 – c. 1790) — Married Thomas Stubblefield (c. 1712 – 1758)
2 CONT 2. John Hackley (c. 1716 – 1760) — Married Judith Ball
2 CONT 3. Joseph Hackley
2 CONT 4. Lancelot (Lot) Hackley (Documented as brother-in-law and contingency appointee in Thomas Stubblefield's 1757 will)
2 CONT 5. Mary Hackley — Married [first name unknown] Underwood
2 CONT 6. Lucy Hackley
2 CONT 7. Francis Hackley
2 CONT 8. James Hackley Jr. (c. 1742 – 1822) — Married Mary Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Factual Information and Relevance
2 CONT Primary Legal Proof of Parentage (1698): Named explicitly as a surviving son and heir in the last will and testament of his father, John Hackley, executed in March 1698 and recorded in Essex County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Northern Neck Land Operations: Established homestead and land holdings in King George County, serving as the patriarch of the Hackley family branch that subsequently intermarried with the Stubblefield family in Culpeper County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate Settlement (1748): Died in August 1748 in King George County, where his estate and probate proceedings were formally administered.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources and Records
2 CONT Primary Probate (Parentage): Essex County, Virginia, Will Book 9, page 306 (Will of John Hackley, March 1698, naming son James) and page 330 (Estate Inventory).
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary Probate (Estate): King George County, Virginia, Will Book 1 (1721–1752) — Estate proceedings and administration for James Hackley (1748).
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Compilations: Bessie Henry, A History of the Henry and Hackley Families (1975), pages 137–141.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondary References:
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hackley-53
2 CONT John Hackley wrote his will in March 1698 and passed away within a year. The will mentions his wife; sons James, John and Joseph; daughters Mary, Agnes and Elizabeth; and son-in-law John Andrews (most likely a son from his wife's 
2 CONC first marriage). John's wife Elizabeth did the subsequent inventory of the estate.
2 CONT #Henry, Bessie.  ''A History of the Henry and Hackley Families''.  (1975) “John Hackley and Elizabeth Bowler” http://www.familysearch.org/library/books/idurl/1/292974.  Book page 137-141, page viewer page 150-155 http://www.family
2 CONC search.org/library/books/idviewer/292974/150 ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000223416460847 document attached]) 
2 CONT # 3. Virginia. County Court (Essex County), will book 9, page 306 Family Search < [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G9P6-3W2D?i=344&cat=413447 link] > 
2 CONT #4.   Virginia. County Court (Essex County), will book 9, page 330 Family Search < [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G9P6-3WGT?i=358&cat=413447 link] > 
