1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Ellin Stubblefield (c.1714-c.1790)
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary
2 CONT Ellin (Elen) née Hackley was a colonial resident of Virginia and a member of the established Hackley family. Her life is documented through her marriage to Thomas Stubblefield and her appointment as executrix in his 1757 Culpeper 
2 CONC County probate proceedings.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage
2 CONT Father: James Hackley (Unverified in direct primary probate records)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth Shippey (Unverified in direct primary probate records)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1714, King George County, Virginia (Secondary estimates vary)
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Circa 1790, Culpeper County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Colony of Virginia (Unverified exact site)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue
2 CONT Spouse: Thomas Stubblefield (c. 1712 – 1758)
2 CONT Married: Circa 1730s, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. George Stubblefield (Eldest son; c. 1731 – c. 1791)
2 CONT 2. James Stubblefield (c. 1735 – ?)
2 CONT 3. Younger children (Explicitly referenced as a group in Thomas Stubblefield's 1757 will, but unnamed individually)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Factual Information and Relevance
2 CONT Executrix Appointment (1757–1758): Named as the primary executrix in the last will and testament of her husband, Thomas Stubblefield, dated November 28, 1757, and proved in Culpeper County Court on February 16, 1758. She was entru
2 CONC sted with managing the real and personal estate for the support and education of the children until the eldest son came of lawful age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Associations: Designated her brother, Lot Hackley, as a contingency overseer and appointee in Thomas Stubblefield's will to assist with estate execution and child care.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources and Records
2 CONT Probate Records: Culpeper County, Virginia, Will Book A (1749–1770), pages 174–177 (Library of Virginia, Reel 31) — containing the will of Thomas Stubblefield naming Ellin as wife and executrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondary References:
