1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of Capt. Richard Taliaferro and Rose Berryman include:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter TALIAFERRO born February 12, 1740, Caroline County, Virginia; married Anne HACKLEY;
1 FAMC @F6000000000591594184@
1 FAMS @F6000000000591594174@
1 RFN geni:6000000000591488789
1 SUBM @S6000000000591388342@
1 NOTE Peter Taliaferro, son of Captain Richard Taliaferro and his wife Rose Berryman, was born Feb 12, 1740, date of death not known.  Peter inherited part of the 10,000 acres of land in Amherst County that belonged to his father.  He s
2 CONC old this land in 1767 and removed to Fredericksburg, Virginia.  Married in 1761 to Ann Hackley, the daughter of John and Judith Hackley of King George County, Virginia.  Judith was the daughter of Samuel Ball and Ann Cahterine Tay
2 CONC loe.  John Hackley was the oldest son of James and Elizabeth Hackley of King George County.
2 CONT Name: Peter TALIAFERRO Given Name: Peter Surname: TALIAFERRO 1 Sex: M Birth: 12 Feb 1740 in Caroline County, Virginia Death: 8 Feb 1792 in Orange County, Virginia Note: Died at the home of "Mr. Dade." SOURCE: "The Taliaferro Famil
2 CONC y" in GENEALOGIES OF VIRGINIA FAMILIES: Tyler's Quarterly 3:518-519; See also "Some Hackley Notes" Woodford B. Hackley to Jennie Henry Crugar, 1940, FHL film 0029884 item 1. RES: Spotsylvania
2 CONT  Father: Richard TALIAFERRO  Mother: Rose Anne BERRYMAN
2 CONT  Marriage 1 Ann HACKLEY  b: 1740
2 CONT Married: Abt 1760 in Culpeper County, Virginia
2 CONT Children of Annie HACKLEY and Peter TALIAFERRO are:
2 CONT 1.	i.	Richard TALIAFERRO was born 24 SEP 1762 in Fredericksburg, Culpepper, Va., and died ABT 1810. He married Sarah JONES  20 FEB 1786. She was born ABT 1770, and died ABT 1830.
2 CONT 	ii.	Zachariah TALIAFERRO  was born 1764 in Fredericksburg, Culpepper, Va., and died 1803.
2 CONT 	iii.	Judith TALIAFERRO was born 1766 in Fredericksburg, Culpepper, Va..
2 CONT 	iv.	Sara TALIAFERRO was born 1768 in Fredericksburg, Culpepper, Va.. She married Thomas BRAGG
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Media: Book Abbrev: Culpeper Co., Virginia Genealogies Title: Genealogical and Historical Notes on Culpeper County, VA Author: Raleigh Travers Green Publication: Southern Book Company, Baltimore, 1958
