2 CONT 5a) - 1) - 17 mar 1998 e-mail from Robert Green <rdgreen@inforum.net>
2 CONT
2 CONT I am descended from James Green's younger brother, Elijah Green (b. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Oct 1786,  Russell Cnty VA., m.  Sarah Hendrickson b.  abt 1798)   It's
2 CONT
2 CONT great to hear from you. I have Lewis Green Sr. as being born in 1724 in
2 CONT
2 CONT Culpeper Cnty., VA (from other internet responses), but I have not been
2 CONT
2 CONT able to establish him there legally yet.  I have a book about early
2 CONT
2 CONT Culpeper Cnty families (GENEALOGICAL AND HISTORICAL NOTES ON
2 CONT
2 CONT CULPEPER COUNTY, VIRGINIA by Raleigh Travers Green),  but have not found
2 CONT
2 CONT as yet direct mention of Lewis Sr. Internet sources have stated
2 CONT
2 CONT that Lewis Sr. moved to the Clinch river region around 1751 and served
2 CONT
2 CONT in the French and Indian War.   During the war, he moved his family back
2 CONT
2 CONT to Culpeper Cnty.   I found evidence of a land bounty granted to a Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT Green for service in the French and Indian war in a publication
2 CONT
2 CONT abstracted by Philip Fall Taylor.   Fifty acres of Kentucky l and was granted
2 CONT
2 CONT and surveyed in 1783 which indicates that he was a private. I don't have a
2 CONT
2 CONT clue who he married. Lewis Jr. was born at Fort Blackmore
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1751 in the Clinch river area. I understand that he served in the
2 CONT
2 CONT Continental Army, attaining the rank of Colonel.   I'm told he settled on
2 CONT
2 CONT the Cumberland river between Barbourville and Mt Pleasant.   I found an
2 CONT
2 CONT 1819 tax roll for Harlan  County that lists Lewis Green among males
2 CONT
2 CONT over 21 transferred from the tax rolls of Knox County, to the newly
2 CONT
2 CONT formed Harlan County.   My line descends through Lewis's son, Elijah
2 CONT
2 CONT through Breathitt, Floyd and Magoffin Counties until my gr grandfather,
2 CONT
2 CONT George Green (m. Mary England  in 1876 in  Salyersville) moved his
2 CONT
2 CONT family to Murray county Oklahoma.  From there, Greens spread to
2 CONT
2 CONT Arizona, Utah, Montana, Washington and California (the San Francisco Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Area is where I'm from).   I now live in the Sierra Nevada foothills about
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 miles from the 1848 gold discovery town of Coloma.
2 CONT
