1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thank you to Ed Bartolacci for the following obituaries:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Frankfort Roundabout, Frankfort, Kentucky, Aug. 24, 1901, Saturday
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATHS
2 CONT
2 CONT LILLARD-- At his home, near Lawrenceburg, on Monday morning, Mr. Ephraim Lillard, sr., aged nearly 82 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Lillard was one of the most highly respected citizens of Anderson county - - honorable, upright and kindly in all the relations of life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He leaves six daughters, Mrs. Mary Blakemore, Mrs. W. S. Farmer, Mrs. H. B. Carpenter, Mrs. W. S. Barriger, Miss Rachel Lillard and Miss Jennie Lillard, and one son, Mr. Ephriam Lillard, jr., and a large circle of relatives and fr
2 CONC iends to mourn his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral services were conducted by Rev. W. E. Gwatkin, from the family residence, on Tuesday afternoon, at 2 o'clock, after which the remains were laid to rest in the Lawrenceburg cemetery by the side of his wife, who had prec
2 CONC eded him to the grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT *********************************************************
2 CONT Morning Herald - Aug. 21, 1901
2 CONT
2 CONT COL. EPHRIAM LILLARD DEAD
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawrenceburg, Ky.,  August 20,  - Colonel Ephriam Lillard, aged eighty-two years, one of the most highly respected farmers of this county, died yesterday at his home, ten miles from here.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/me
2 CONC morial/91975590/ephriam-wallace-lillard Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 30 2021, 6:13:05 UTC''
