1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7951856/james-m-lillard Find-A-Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=7951856 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 24 2017, 13:50:20 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Canton Press (Canton, Missouri) 23 Oct 1896, Fri Page 3
2 CONT Rev. James M. Lilliard
2 CONT Died in Canton, Oct. 10, 1896.
2 CONT Born in Mercer Co., Kentucky September 29, 1896. When he was eight years of age, his father, Rev. David Lillard, moved to Boone Co., Ky. The deceased lived at home until 21 years old, and was baptised by his father and united with
2 CONC  the Baptist church when 18 years of age. When 21 he was united in marriage to Martha Cox, of Kentucky, who survives him and will be 92 years old Nov. 15. They came to Lewis county Mo., in 1833, and settled on a farm ten miles fro
2 CONC m Canton, where they remained 60 years, and then moved to Canton. Brother Lillard was ordained in Kentucky and his first preaching in Mo. was in the Gilead Baptist church the second day after its organization in 1833 and numbers m
2 CONC ade a profession of faith. From that time he preached in Northeast Missouri 60 years, and labored much in new fields. He organized 20 churchs and encouraged 30 young men to enter the ministry and baptised over three thousand perso
2 CONC ns. For 35 years he road on horseback to his preaching stations, traveling in all kinds of weather, enduring great hardships, yet always cheerful, and loved most ardently his work. His education was limited but he studied his bibl
2 CONC e, and read with zeal other books. He had a naturally good mind, and a rare gift of common sense, also a warm heart, full of love for humanity, and strong faith in God and christianity. Thus he was one of the most efficient and in
2 CONC fluential preachers of Mo. Hence he is lovingly spoken of "Uncle Jimmie Lillard". His last revival meeting was held at Overton schoolhouse, with Brother A. F. Wilson when he was 83 years of age. Since then he has been blind, hard 
2 CONC of hearing and unable to walk.  Survives son David, four daughters, and a number of grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7951856/james-m-lillard Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 30 2021, 8:14:17 UTC''
