1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Bowater'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BOWATER, John''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following information was compiled by Linda Coate [Phone: (614) 915-1243; E-mail: ancestrees@gmail.com] and retrieved from her site at http://www.ancestrees.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: Apr 25, 1630, Whitley, Coventry, Warwickshire, England 1 
2 CONT * Marriage (1): '''CROSS, Ann''' in 1654 in Coventry, Warwickshire, ENG 1 
2 CONT * Marriage (2): '''MAUNDER, Mary''' on Nov 12, 1685 in , Worcestershire, ENG 
2 CONT * Died: Jan 16, 1704/05, Spitalfields, Stepney Borough, London, ENG at age 74 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===General Notes:===
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary were from Spitalfields, a town near London, England. John married twice. He was a Quaker who actually visited but did not settle in the American colonies. He and his second wife died when Mary was a young woman. He w
2 CONC as listed as age 75 at his death. (C-1447)
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Baptism, Apr 25, 1630, Bromsgrove, Worcestershire, ENG.
2 CONT
2 CONT • death2 (conflicting), Jan 16, 1703/04.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Ann CROSS in 1654 in Coventry, Warwickshire, ENG.1 (Ann CROSS was born in 1628 in Bromsgrove, Worcester, Worcestershire, England, died on Apr 25, 1679 in Warwick North M.M., , ENG and was buried on Apr 27, 1679 in War
2 CONC wick North M.M., , ENG.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John next married Mary MAUNDER, daughter of Edward MAUNDER and Miriam WELLS, on Nov 12, 1685 in , Worcestershire, ENG. (Mary MAUNDER was born in 1649 in London, Middlesex, ENG 3 and died on Feb 10, 1703/04 in Spitalfields, Stepney
2 CONC  Borough, London, ENG.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources===
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Tango1010, The Quaker Tree (www.ancestry.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Stewart Baldwin, Quaker Marriage Certificates The American Genealogist Vol. 72, Nos. 3-4 July/Oct 1997 225-243.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 kansas2AZ, Wortman Family Tree (www.ancestry.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Middletown Monthly Meeting (Quaker) was held at the home of John Bowater during the years 1700, 1701 and 1702 and was known as "Bowater's Meeting" until 1702.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1702, he removed to Willistown (West Town?) Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in either 1704 or 1705.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: 1629, Coventry, Warwickshire, England [ALT location: BROMSGROVE, WORCHESTER, ENGLAND]
2 CONT * Marriage (1):  Ann Cross
2 CONT * Marriage (2): Mary Maunder on 12 Nov 1685 in Worcestershire, England
2 CONT * Died: 16 Jan 1705, Spitalfields, Stepney Borough, London, England at age 76
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT *  http://www.drwilliams.org/genealogy/1711.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial 82757789
2 CONT --------------------
