2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Nov 1693 Middlesex Co.,Va., Will of Elizabeth Wormeley, Rec. 5 Mar 1693:
2 CONT * Mother:Mrs. Elizabeth Spencer;
2 CONT * Sister: MillionDownman;
2 CONT * Brother: RawleighTravers;
2 CONT * Brother: Giles Travers;
2 CONT * Children of sister Million Downman: Wilmoth Downman, Million Downman the younger, Elizabeth Downman,
2 CONT * Husband: Christopher Wormeley, his children: Judith Wormeley, Thomas Wormeley, William Wormeley.
2 CONT * (Hopkins, Middlesex Wills & Inv. 1673-1812, p.54).
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT STAFFORD COUNTY VA DEED & WILL BOOK 1689 - 1693; THE ANTIENT PRESS pp. 237- 237a 
2 CONT
2 CONT * THIS INDENTURE made ye Two and Twentieth day of February 1691 Betweene ELIZABETH SPENCER of LANCASTER COUNTY of ye one part and GILES TRAVERS of County of Stafford Wittnesseth that said ELIZABETH SPENCER in consideration of twen
2 CONC ty thousand pounds of Merchandable Tobacco in Caske have sold unto GILES TRAVERS his heires for ever Six hundred twenty five acres of lande on ye North side of OCQUAON upon ye Southwest side of POTOMACK RIVER beinge part of a Divi
2 CONC dend of Iande purchased by WILLIAM HARRIS and THOMAS BAXTER by a Patent dated the tenth day of October 1670 To Have and To Hold said lande and att premises in as full manner as is ex
2 CONT * pressed in ye Pattent or as ELIZABETH SPENCER might have had In Wittnesses whereof said ELIZABETH SPENCER have sett her hande & Seale
2 CONT * In presence of JOHN JOES ELIZABETH SPENCER JOHN BEECHINGE RAWLEIGH TRAVERSE, WM. DOWNMAN
2 CONT * KNOW ALL MEN by these presents that I ELIZABETH SPENCER of LANCASTER COUNTY have made Capa. GEORGE MASON of Stafford County my lawful Attorney to acknowledge Sale of lande to GILES TRAVERS In Wiliness my hande and Seale the day 
2 CONC and yeare aforementioned
2 CONT * Wittnesses JOHN JOES ELIZABETH SPENCER RAW TRAVERSE WM. DOWNMAN
2 CONT * This above Deed was acknowledged in County Court of Stafford to Mr. GILES TRAVERS by Capa. GEORGE MASON Attorney of said ELIZABETH SPENCER on ye 9th day of March 1691/2 and was then recorded
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Richmond County, Virginia Wills and Inventories 1707-1719; {Robert K. Headley, Jr}: p.297 - Alexander DONIPHAN, will; 20 Sep 1716, 6 Feb 1716/17
2 CONT * son Alexander 250 ac. in the fork of Rappahannock bought of George JONES decd;
2 CONT * Stephen BOWEING the other 250 ac. of land joining the aforesaid tract;
2 CONT * son Mott 180 ac. out of a tract bought of Joshua DAVIS being 330 ac. lying back of my river land; if he has no heirs, to go to grson. Giles TRAVERS;
2 CONT * son Robert;
2 CONT * dau. Margaret 70 ac. bought of Joshua DAVIS;
2 CONT * dau. Elizabeth remainder of 80 ac. and her mother's wedding ring;
2 CONT * wife Susannah, having kept her est. apart, and taken it to herself and desiring nothing of mine...;
2 CONT * dau. Anne; ex. to give Mrs. Mary BELFIELD a ring of 12 shillings price;
2 CONT * ex: son Robert;
2 CONT * wits: Peter LOWD, Elias POWELL, Robert FASSAKER.
2 CONT * [Alexander DONIPHAN mar. his 2d wife, Margaret MOTT, by Nov 1691; she d. prior to Mar 1709. MAC, p.57.)
2 CONT
