1 NOTE !BIRTH - BRONAUGH FAMILY RECORD
2 CONT Mary Doniphan was born 10 July 1737 in Stafford Co.,VA
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - A HISTORY OF THE BRONAUGH FAMILY IN AMERICA by Sarah Amelia Bronaugh Benson
2 CONT William Bronaugh's 2nd wife was Mary (Doniphan) Cooke, the widow of Travers
2 CONT Cooke who was the son of Sir John Cooke, an Irish Baronet, and Elizabeth
2 CONT Travers daughter of Rawleigh Travers.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - BRONAUGH FAMILY RECORD
2 CONT She married William Bronaugh 13 Oct 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT She died 26 Dec 1781 in Loudoun Co., VA.
1 NOTE !BIRTH - SOME BRONAUGH FAMILY NOTES compiled by Ruth (Thayer) Ravenscroft
2 CONT Mary Ann Grant was born in VA
2 CONT Note:  HISTORY OF CHRISTIAN CO., KY says she was related to forebears of
2 CONT President Grant.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT She died in 1825 in Mason Co., KY
2 CONT She left a will mentioning her grandchildren, John C., Mary and Sally (Sarah)
2 CONT and another grandson, David as executor.
1 NOTE William B. Magill (his middle name probably was Bronaugh) was the son of
2 CONT Charles T. Magill and Mary Doniphan Bronaugh and was Mary Jane Bronaugh's first
2 CONT cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - He does not appear on the 1870 census and was probably dead by that
2 CONT time.
