1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p. 308
2 CONT Born "Crow's Nest", Stafford Co., VA Sep. 14, 1769
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT Married 1st Jan. 16, 1792 Maria Nivin, dau. of a Spanish merchant of Cadiz, who had a branch house at Glasgow, Scotland where Mr. Daniel met his wife.  They were married in St. John's Church, London, the banns being published.  Sh
2 CONC e died d.s.p. Dumfries, VA. Oct. 30, 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT Married 2nd Margaret Eleanor Stone Dec. 15, 1793, dau. of Hon. Thomas and
2 CONT Margaret (Brown) Stone of MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #3 - Ibid
2 CONT Married about 1810 Maria Vowles.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT From THE FREDERICKSBURG, VA HERALD of Oct. 13, 1813.
2 CONT "Died on Thursday the 7th inst. in the 42d year of his age, at the residence of Mr. Travers Daniel, Sr., Stafford Co., Dr. John Moncure Daniel, Senior
2 CONT Hospital Surgeon in the military service of the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Daniel studied medicine in Scotland; was Surgeon U.S.A. in the War of 1812, serving in the South and in Canada.  He was appointed Hospital Surgeon, U.S.A. by President Madison, July 9, 1809.  In 1797-8 he was a member of St. C
2 CONC olumbia Lodge, A.F. & A.M., Pt. Tobacco, MD. to which many of his kinsmen belonged. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT SOME WILLS FROM THE BURNED COUNTIES OF VIRGINIA and other Wills not listed in Virginia Wills and Administrations 1632-1800 by William Lindsay Hopkins, p. 127
2 CONT JOHN MONCURE DANIEL - Stafford - 28 Apr 1813/13 Dec 1813
2 CONT Wife Maria Daniel.  Children by my late wife Margaret Daniel.  Exors:  Zachariah Nowles, John Moncure, Jr., David Briggs, Jr. and Peter N. Daniel.  (Legatees and devisses of John Moncure Daniel are viz Thomas H. C. Daniel and John
2 CONC  Henry Daniel the children of Maria Daniel while John M. Daniel, Raleigh T. Daniel, Jane N. Crane wife of William Crane and Margaret E. Conway wife of Walker P. Conway are children by the first wife, Margaret Daniel.)
2 CONT U.S. Circuit Ct. VA Dist., Box 142, 1838; "Buchan vs Buchan & Seddon (File 1)
