1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Magazine of Virginia Genealogy Vol 52 Number 1 Feb 2014; Page 73.  “The Lancaster County Will of Fortunatus Davenport, First Husband of Susannah (Payne) Mitchell.” by Craig M. Kilby
2 CONT
2 CONT Craig Kilby: "Davenport's unrecorded original will in this collection names his wife Susannah. It leaves 1/2 of his "Forest" property to his nephew John Davenport, son of his brother George Davenport, and the other half to his dau
2 CONC ghter Susannah Davenport. It also leaves his 100 acres in Lancaster County bought of John Callahan to his daughter Susannah Davenport. Further, it mentions his wife "may" be with child. His will is dated 21 FEB 1713/4 an was recor
2 CONC ded (on the jacket) on 12 May 1714"
2 CONT
2 CONT In the case of Fortunatus Davenport (a not entirely unravelled mystery), we can be sure that he married Elizabeth Payne, her first husband. Her 2nd husband being Robert-2 Mitchell. By Davenport, she had one daughter Susannah who m
2 CONC arried a POPE and by whom John Pope and Elizabeth Pope who married another Davenport.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Susannah PAYNE and Robert MITCHELL are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. Sarah MITCHELL was born 10 MAR 1717 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died 31 JAN 1752 in Lancaster County, Virginia. She married Thomas CHINN 12 NOV 1735 in Lancaster County, Virginia, son of Rawleigh CHINN and Esther BALL.
2 CONC  He was born 1714 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died 21 JAN 1768 in Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT * ii. Robert MITCHELL was born 15 NOV 1724, and died 3 JAN 1758 in Richmond County, Virginia. He married Hannah BALL 7 SEP 1746 in Lancaster County, Virginia, daughter of William BALL and Hannah BEALE. She was born ABT 1708, and d
2 CONC ied 10 JUL 1769.
2 CONT * iii. Elizabeth MITCHELL was born 28 SEP 1726. She married Moore FAUNTLEROY. He was born ABT 1726.
2 CONT * iv. John MITCHELL was born ABT 1727.
2 CONT * v. Richard MITCHELL was born 2 NOV 1728 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died 10 JUL 1781 in Richmond County, Virginia. He married Anne SYDNOR 24 AUG 1752 in Richmond County, Virginia, daughter of Anthony SYDNOR and Elizabeth 
2 CONC DEW. She was born 24 JUN 1729 in North Farnham, Richmond County, Virginia, and died 1793 in Richmond County, Virginia.
2 CONT * vi. Frances MITCHELL was born 15 FEB 1730 in Lancaster County, Virginia, and died 1807 in Richmond County, Virginia. She married Anthony SYDNOR ABT 1748 in Richmond County, Virginia, son of Anthony SYDNOR and Elizabeth DEW. He w
2 CONC as born 25 DEC 1724 in North Farnham, Richmond County, Virginia, and died 1755.
2 CONT * vii. Judith MITCHELL was born 19 MAR 1732.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT * 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT * PAINE, Richard. 4 Apr. 1709. Rec. 9 Aug. 1709.
2 CONT * Brothers: Will, George and Jon. Paine.
2 CONT * Mother: Susanna Ladner.
2 CONT * Sisters: Susannah, Margaret and Katherine Paine.
2 CONT * Exor: William, brother.
2 CONT * Wits: Thomas Barker, and Thomas Cattlett. W.B. 10, Page 54.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *  (1) "The Chinn and Myers Families," by Randie Myers (http://wc.rootsweb.com, rjm66 database, 29 Apr 2007).
2 CONT *   (2) "Selvage and Peterson Families and More," by Charles J. Peterson (http://wc.rootsweb.com, selvage1 database, 26 Aug 2007). Cites: (a) Lancaster Co., VA Will Bk 16, p.184. (b) "Dr. John Mitchell, The Man Who Made the Map," 
2 CONC by  Edmund Berkeley and Dorothy Smith Berkeley (1974).
2 CONT *   (3) "Charles and Kate Carter Family Tree," by Kimball Carter (http://wc.rootsweb.com, :2157819 database, 8 Jul 2002). Cites: (a) "Abstracts, Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800," by Ida J. Lee, p.236. FHL 975.522 P2l. 
2 CONC Cites Will Bk 14, p.212.
2 CONT * Birth: (1) Abt 1692. (2) d/o William PAYNE/Susannah MERRIMAN. 1688. Leedstown, Rappahannock Co., VA. (2b) d/o William PAYNE.
2 CONT *   Marriage to Robert MITCHELL: (1,2) 1714. (2) Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT *   Death: (1) Bef. 19 Feb 1762. (2) 23 Nov 1761. Lancaster Co., VA. (2a) Will recorded 19 Feb 1762, Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT *  (3a) [1748]: Susannah, wife of Robert MITCHELL, renounced her legacy given her in will of Robert MITCHELL.
2 CONT *  (2a) 1762, 19 Feb: Will recorded, Lancastor Co., VA. Named Robert MITCHELL's children, Thomas CHINN (husband of daughter Sarah), Moore FAUNTLEROY (Elizabeth), Richard MITCHELL, John SYDNOR (Frances), and George GLASCOCK (Judith
2 CONC ). Wits. James BALL, M. SHEARMAN, Thomas STOTT.
