2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # !  (1) "The Chinn and Myers Families," by Randie Myers (http://wc.rootsweb.com, rjm66 database, 29 Apr 2007).
2 CONT #   (2) "Selvage and Peterson Families and More," by Charles J. Peterson (http://wc.rootsweb.com, selvage1 database, 26 Aug 2007). Cites: (a) "Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800," by Ida J. Lee (1959) citing 
2 CONC  Will Book 10, p.36; Will Book 14, p.212. (b) Norm McHan, Jan 2002, citing Richmond Co., VA Deed Bk 9, p.25. (c) List of Tithables, upper Precinct of St. Mary's White Chapple  Parish, Lancaster Co., VA. (d) "Dr. John Mitchell, The
2 CONC  Man Who Made the Map," by  Edmund Berkeley and Dorothy Smith Berkeley (1974), citing Lancaster Co., VA Court Deeds & Wills 1743-1750, p.212. (e) "Lancaster County, Virginia, Order Book 1736-1739," by R. & S. Sparacio, p.13.
2 CONT # !  Birth: (1) 1684. VA. (2) s/o Robert MITCHELL/Saram SMITH.
2 CONT #   Marriage to Mary CHILTON: (2) Abt 1710. VA.
2 CONT #   Marriage to Susannah PAYNE: (1) Sarah or Susanna PAYNE. (1,2) 1714. (2) Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT #   Death: (1) Bef. 9 Sep 1748. VA. (2) 8 Aug 1748. Lancaster Co., VA. Will dated 12 Jul 1748, probated 9 Sep 1748.
2 CONT #   (2) 1702, 16 Nov: Named in the will of his father Robert MITCHELL. (2d) Robert apparently inherited his father's inventory of merchandise as he also operated a store involving the exchange of tobacco for goods imported from Eu
2 CONC rope.
2 CONT #   (2d)  He and his family lived on 50 acres on Moratico Creek, leased from Anne and Bryan PHILLIPS for 30 pounds sterling and one ear of Indian corn.
2 CONT #   (2d) 1722: He was appointed Tobacco Receiver for Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT #   (2d)  1727-1730: He served as a Justice of the County Court.
2 CONT #   (2d) Served as a Burgess to the VA parliament.   (2b) 1734,  4 May: Jean LAWSON, Jno. STEPTOE Jr., and Joanna STEPTOE, John's wife, of Christchurch Parish, Lancaster Co., VA deed to Robert MITCHELL of St. Marys White Chapell P
2 CONC arish, Lancaster Co., VA, for 18,000 pounds of tobacco, 450 acres in North Farnham Parish, Richmond Co., VA, bounded on the west by a branch of Moratico Creek from the land of John MILLS, on the north side by the land of Thomas DU
2 CONC RHAM; on the northeast by the land of Abraham GOAD, on the east by the property of William KING and Anthony SYDNOR, and on the south by the land of Isaac WHITE; originally part of a patent granted to Thomas MADISON dated 1770 [sic
2 CONC ], conveyed to Capt. John  PURVIS, subsequently conveyed to Jno. OCKLEY, and lastly inherited by will by Jean LAWSON [mother of Anthony SYDNOR; Joanna who married 12 Jun 1727 Lancaster Co., VA, Jno. STEPTOE as the daughter of John
2 CONC  LAWSON].
2 CONT #   (2e) 1736, 14 Jul: Robert MITCHELL to examine and settle the estate of William PITMAN, Lancaster Co., VA.    (2c) 1745, Jun: Mr. Robert MITCHELL was in list of tithables in the upper Precinct of St. Mary's White Chapple Parish
2 CONC , Lancaster Co., VA, with 8 tithables, including Robert MITCHELL the younger and six slaves.
2 CONT #   (2d) Tobacco receiver in Richmond Co., VA.  [NOTE: His son Robert?]
2 CONT #   (2) 1748, 12 Jul: Robert MITCHELL made his will. Names son Robert MITCHELL (to receive the land and plantation in Richmond Co. purchased from William BELLFIELD; also the plantations Upper Quarters and Lower Quarters in North F
2 CONC arnham Parish, Richmond Co., and lands adjoining in Richmond and Northumberland Counties; and a number of slaves); son Doctor John MITCHELL; son Richard MITCHELL (to receive the plantation upon which he was living in Lancaster Co.
2 CONC , and his Mill in Northumberland Co.); daughter Elizabeth (5 shillings as she had already received her portion of the  estate), wife of Moore FAUNTLEROY; daughter Judith MITCHELL (200 pounds); daughter Sarah, wife of Thomas CHINN,
2 CONC  and her children Robert, Thomas, Rawleigh and Mary CHINN (50 pounds if she becomes a widow before her children come of age); daughter Frances MITCHELL (200 pounds); sister Sarah PITMAN (1000 pounds of tobacco and all the debts ow
2 CONC ed to him), with support to his wife during her widowhood. Executors John, Robert and Richard MITCHELL.
2 CONT #   (2d) 1748, 9 Sep: Will probated, Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT
