1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh McAdams who lived at Back Creek on the Haw River is first found in Orange Co. on the 1776  elections list and Capt. Tate's Company list. He was appointed constable in 1779. The following year he  was drafted, 
2 CONC but his son, John served for him. He supported the American cause and pay records show him  furnishing supplies to the American troops. He married more than once.  His widow, Catey Beard who he  married, 3 Jan 1803. was still livi
2 CONC ng in 1820. He first married Catherine Scott, d/o John Scott 11 Sept. 1761  in Luenburg Co., Va. He made his will on 3 Jan. 1809 and named 12 children. Most Hugh's children remained  in Orange County area.
