1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://kirkpatrick.com/irish24.htm
2 CONT >Major Abraham Kirkpatrick - 1749 Cecil County, Maryland - 1813 Pittsburg, PA (Abraham is son of John K ( - 1774) & Alice Tidbell). He marries Mary Ann Oldham 1761-1813).They have 4 known children:
2 CONT *John Conway K - 1790 Virginia - Mar 6, 1811 Pittsburg, PA
2 CONT *Elizabeth Maria - 1789 - July 19, 1822 Pittsburg, Pa. She marries Christopher Cowan (-1835)
2 CONT *Amelia Louisa. Marries Judge Charles Shaler.
2 CONT *Mary Ann b 1798 marries Dr Joel Lewis. They have daughter Abigail Lewis (1776-1834) who marries Benjamin Patterson Jr. They have daughter Susan Patterson who marries David Kirkpatrick MD, of Westmoreland County, PA
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Abraham Kirkpatrick was one tough son of a gun. Original research shows that the polite obituaries that were written when he died in Pittsburgh glossed over the life he had really led. He fled Maryland for Fort Pitt after killing 
2 CONC a man in a fight at 18. He was at Trenton, Yorktown, and many other battles in the Revolution. He crippled another officer in a duel. He was shot in the head by an enlisted man for seducing his wife. Blind in one eye, he stared do
2 CONC wn a mob during the Whiskey Rebellion. President Washington sent him a case of wine to say thanks.
