1 NOTE !BIRTH - OVERWHARTON PARISH RECORDS,VA 1720-1760 by Wm. G. Boogher, p. 130
2 CONT Moncure, Frances - The wife of the Rev. John Moncure was delivered of a son
2 CONT about 20 minutes after 10 at night, and was privately baptized by the Rev.
2 CONT James Scott about 2 hours after by the name of John and departed this life next morning about 6 of the clock, in the year 1744 and the month July 13. -
1 NOTE !BIRTH - OVERWHARTON PARISH REGISTER, VA 1729-1760 by Wm. G. Boogher, p. 117
2 CONT The wife of the Rev. John Moncure, was delivered of a son about half an hour
2 CONT after four in the morning, January 7, 1746-7, and baptized John, March 3, 1747 by the Rev. Jr. John Phipps; John Mercer and George Mason, Esq., his God
2 CONT Fathers and Elizabeth Brown, his Aunt, His God Mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p. 428
2 CONT He married about 1770 Anne Conway, daughter of George and Anne (Heath) Conway.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid 
2 CONT He and his wife are buried at "Dipple", Stafford Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited his father's estate of "Clermont" - SOME PROMINENT VIRGINIA
2 CONT FAMILIES by Louise Pecquet DuBellet
