2 TITL William Moncure (1774 - 1832) - Find A Grave Memorial
1 NOTE !BIRTH - OVERWHARTON PARISH REGISTER, VA. 1720-1760 by Wm. G. Boogher, p. 130
2 CONT Moncure, William, son of John and Ann, born September 21, 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - VIRGINIA GEANEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p. 428
2 CONT He married Sarah Elizabeth Henry, dau. of Hon. James Henry, of Fleet's Bay, Northumberland Co.,VA., and his wife, Sarah Scarborough, dau. of Col. Edmund Scarborough, of "Seaside," Accomac Co., VA. in 179_.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Horace E. Hayden, p. 428
2 CONT William Moncure died at his estate, "Windsor Forest," Stafford Co. in 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Moncure was a churchman and one of the original pewholders of Monumental Church, Richmond, he having bought pew 50 for $330 in 1814.  He was confirmed at Aquia Church, on Oct. 13, 1815; vestryman of same, 1816; elected to fill
2 CONC  place of E. C. Moncure, warden, 1822.
