1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Not a known son of https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-Carter/6000000006243087091?through=6000000004956195627 and https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Carter/6000000006242748510?through=6000000004956195627. John’s  pare
2 CONC nts have not been verified or confirmed. He is not listed in the will of Henry Skipwith Carter (Lancaster County Will Book 13, Page 324) identifies his children.
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT John Carter (c. 1708 – 1782) was a resident of Stafford County, Virginia. While widely featured in secondary genealogical literature and online databases, the primary record for his life is limited. He is definitively linked to St
2 CONC afford County through his marriage to Mary Butler in 1745, as recorded in the Overwharton Parish Register. Other familial connections—most notably the claim that he married a "Susannah Payne" or held the rank of "Captain"—lack sup
2 CONC port in primary source documentation and appear to be the result of conflating this individual with other men of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Born: c. 1708, presumed Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1782, Stafford County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: [Unproven]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: [Unproven]
2 CONT
2 CONT -Researcher’s Note: While often attributed to Henry Skipwith Carter and Anne Harris in secondary sources, there is no probate or land record confirming this parentage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse 1: [Name Unknown].
2 CONT -Note: The identification of this spouse as "Susannah Payne" is not supported by primary evidence. The Susannah Payne who was the daughter of William Payne Jr. is confirmed to have married Major James Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:1. John Carter (c. 1708–1782): Proven to have married Mary Butler in 1745 (Overwharton Parish Register).
2 CONT 2. William Merriman Carter (c. 1730–1818):
2 CONT
2 CONT -Attributed parents: John Carter and [Unknown/Susannah Payne].
2 CONT Status: Unproven. The link is widely asserted in DAR patriot records and online family trees, but it lacks a contemporary, primary document (like a will or deed) that bridges the two generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Spouse 2: Mary Butler.
2 CONT Marriage Date: February 4, 1745 in Overwharton Parish, Stafford County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (Verified via Parish Record):
2 CONT Documentation for his offspring is limited to those recorded in the Overwharton Parish Register with his wife, Mary Butler. Other children attributed to him in popular genealogies are unverified.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Inventory & Record Analysis===
2 CONT 1. The "Captain" Title
2 CONT Status: Unsubstantiated.
2 CONT Analysis: No record of a military commission or Revolutionary War service for this individual exists in the National Archives or Virginia state militia records. The title is considered an error stemming from the common practice of
2 CONC  applying honorifics to male ancestors in early 20th-century genealogical compilations.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The "Susannah Payne" Marriage
2 CONT Status: Disproven/Conflated.
2 CONT Analysis: This marriage is a genealogical impossibility. The Susannah Payne born c. 1715 (daughter of William Payne Jr. and Judith) is documented as having married Major James Johnson, per the 1758 probate of her mother. Linking h
2 CONC er to John Carter is a clear case of record-merging.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources===
2 CONT 1. The Register of Overwharton Parish, Stafford County, Virginia, 1720–1758. (Primary source for marriage to Mary Butler).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 14, Page 241. (Confirms the identity of Susannah Payne, wife of James Johnson).
