1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of George Harvey  w.w. Jan 8, 1764;  w.p. Feb. 13,1764
2 CONT Northumberland County Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpt from  “The Lost Pioneer” by Daniel R. Long
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Elizabeth- that tract of land in Cherry Point which I had of her by marriage, to her and her heirs, and also a third part of what other estate I may possess (the land whereon I live excepted)  during her natural life.  To my 
2 CONC dear child Nelly—the tract of land together with all my other estate, to her and the heirs of her body, but failing of such heirs, the said land to be equally divided as also the other estate among the children of Jeremiah Middlet
2 CONC on, children of Hannah Roe, and Elizabeth Middleton, that is each, to have only one third each.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Betty –negro boy James and a feather bed of ten pounds value.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister Elizabeth Middleton—shall live in my house to take care of my daugher Nelly, and that she be sufficiently supported out of my estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Exec: Thomas Jones, Matthew Neale, John Roe
2 CONT Witnesses:  Robert Clarke, Adam Menzie, George Bearcroft
2 CONT
2 CONT The phrasing  of George Harvey’s will is most significant.  He left land and his estate to Nelly, daughter by his first wife, and if she died withough heirs, to be divided in thirds:  1/3 to the children of his widowed half-brothe
2 CONC r, Jeremiah Middleton; (half-brother who married Sarah Ellin was not widowed.  KP); 1/3 to children of Hannah (Middleton) Dollins Roe (Wroe) (his half sister); and 1/3 to his half-sister, Elizabeth Middleton.  We know his second w
2 CONC ife Elizabeth (Straughan) Cralle Harvey  had land and possibly income of her own; so George Harvey could assume that daughter Betty Harvey would be amply cared for by her mother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT We find on June 11, 1764, that Griffin Lewis was a plaintiff versus John Wroes (Roe, Wroe), defendant, Executor of George Harvey, deceased, for 14-16sh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Harvey made a deed of gift to her two sons Rodham Kenner Cralle and William Taite Cralle, of 160 acres of land in Cherry Point, recorded July 10, 1764.  Guardians were appointed
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm. Taite Gentl apptd guardian of  Wm. Taite Cralle-together with Griffin Fauntleroy as Security in penalty of L2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Griffin Fauntleroy apptd guardian of Rodham Kenner Cralle-together with Wm. Taite as security in penalty of L2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Harvey appt guardian of Mary Cralle- together with Wm Taite as Security in penalty of L300.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three days following the above transactions, Elizabeth Harvey married her third husband, Jeremiah Middleton (half brother to George Harvey (half-brother to George Harvey, deceased), on July 13, 1764.  (It is my belief that the Jer
2 CONC emiah Middleton that Elizabeth Harvey married was the son of John Middleton III (half brother of George Harvey, deceased) and Ann Claughton.  George Harvey’s half brother Jeremiah Middleton was married at the time to Sarah Ellin l
2 CONC nu).KP
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Will of George Harvey w.w. Jan 8, 1764; w.p. Feb. 13,1764 Northumberland County Virginia Excerpt from “The Lost Pioneer” by Daniel R. Long. Also includes description of family relationships between George Harvey, Middletons, and
2 CONC  Wroes. ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000208954854843 document attached])
