1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of Anne AYLETT and Augustine (Austin) WASHINGTON are:
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Jane WASHINGTON was born APR 1756 (niece of Gen. George Washington) in Westmoreland County, Virginia, and died OCT 1833 in va. She married John Spotswood THORNTON 1784, son of Francis III col THORNTON and Mary Frances GREGORY. 
2 CONC He was born ABT 1739 in Spotsylvania, Virginia, and died 1822.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Augustine Washington 1756 1833
2 CONT Married John Thornton (LTC 3rd Va. Regt. C.L.), her cousin, in 1784
2 CONT
2 CONT John Thornton (c1743-1822) born at "Fall Hill," Fredericksburg, Spotsylvania County, Va. Married his 2nd cousin in 1784, Jane Augusta Washington (1756-1833) who was born at Popes Creek in Westmoreland County, Va. In place of her f
2 CONC ather, who had died, her uncle Gen. George Washington gave the bride away. He last served (1778-79) as a lt. colonel of Grayson's additional Continental regiment. Later he commanded a regiment of Virginia militia at the decisive b
2 CONC attle of Yorktown in 1781.
2 CONT
2 CONT Five children were 
2 CONT #Mary (c1785-c1806) who married c1801, Dr. Isaac Winston (1777-1867); 
2 CONT #John Augustine (c1787-1817);
2 CONT # Frances Gregory (c1789-1828) who married her 1st cousin, Dr. George Alexander Thornton (c1787-1818); 
2 CONT #Jane Washington (1795-1819/20) who married her 1st cousin, once removed, Rev. Francis Thornton IV (1795-1881); and 
2 CONT #George Washington Spotswood Thornton (c1795-1824) who married c1824, Mildred Hooe Buckner (c1800-36). The latter marriage had an only child, Jane Washington Augusta Thornton (1824-87), who married in 1848, U.S. Senator James Burn
2 CONC ie Beck (1822-90)(Transylvania Law 1846), of Kentucky.
2 CONT # Caroline R. Thornton (source needed)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Nancy-Rogers/6000000003601163931 (born about 1763) was not her child.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # http://dcodriscoll.pbworks.com/w/page/9957081/Thornton_(II)_
2 CONT # https://members.tripod.com/brian_skelton/d0002/g0000037.html#I0458
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I26913&tree=Tree1
2 CONT # Genealogies of Virginia Families Vol. I, from the Virginia Magazine of History and Biography.
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Jane Augusta (Washington) Thornton (1740-1833)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Washington-567 : accessed 08 November 2024). shows birth date as Apr 1740 and death date as 
2 CONC  18 Oct 1833 "at age 93."
2 CONT # https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67057919/jane_augusta_thornton shows middle name of "Augusta" without citation.
2 CONT # https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67058133/john_thornton cites
2 CONT #See John Augustine Washington (1920-2020), Descendants of Rev. Lawrence (c1602-52/3) and Amphyllis Twigden Washington (-1655), Five Generation Chart (Chevy Chase, Md. 1982), 11516
2 CONT #Dr. Justin M. Glenn, The Washingtons, A Family History, Volume One, Seven Generations of the Presidential Branch (Savas Beatie, El Dorado Hills, Ca. 2014), I: 85-86; 
2 CONT #James Houston Barr III, Lt. Colonel Nathaniel Pope, c1610-1660, of Virginia, Ancestor of Washington, Governors and Legislators, History of His Descendants (Louisville, Ky. 2018), 12.
2 CONT # https://services.dar.org/members/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A114864  JANE AUGUSTA WASHINGTON   (wife of John Thornton d. 1822). MILDRED, ALICE & NANCY ARE NOT CHILDREN OF THIS PATRIOT.
2 CONT #  "Will the real Francis Thornton please stand up!"  By Staff/Contributed Jul 2, 2015  < [https://www.rappnews.com/features/will-the-real-francis-thornton-please-stand-up/article_7942c821-0128-5a99-b284-cfd3a1a53854.html link] > 
2 CONC ... The western portion (which he supplemented with additional land purchases and which included “Thornton Hill”) was bequeathed to his wife and to his son George Washington Spotswood Thornton in John’s will of 1822.
2 CONT # "Orders to Captain John Thornton, 9 January 1777"  https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Washington/03-08-02-0030 John Thornton (1749–1822) of Thornton Hill in Culpeper (later Rappahannock) County, Va., a distant cousin of GW,
2 CONC  was married to Jane Washington, the daughter of GW’s half brother Augustine. Thornton commanded a rifle company in the Culpeper minutemen before being commissioned a captain in the 3d Virginia Regiment on 12 Feb. 1776. On 20 Mar.
2 CONC  1777 Thornton was appointed major of Col. Charles Mynn Thruston’s Additional Continental Regiment (see GW to Thornton, 20 Mar., and GW to George Weedon, 27 Mar. 1777), and from November 1778 to April 1779, when he left the Contin
2 CONC ental line, he served as the lieutenant colonel of Col. William Grayson’s Additional Continental Regiment.
2 CONT # https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LDYB-6B9
