1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 346
2 CONT William Augustine Washington, I (1757-1810), son of Augustine Washington, II (half-brother to George) and wife Ann Aylett; inherited Wakefield.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 1st Jane Washington, daughter of John Augustine Washington, I.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT He married 2nd Mary Lee, daughter of Richard Henry Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #3 - GENEALOGICAL ABSTRACTS FROM 18TH CENTURY VIRGINIA NEWSPAPERS by Robert K. Headley, Jr., p. 357
2 CONT WASHINGTON, Col. William Augustine, of Westmoreland Co., married Miss Sally Tayloe, dau. of the late John TAYLOE, Esq. of Mount Airy, at Mansfield the seat of Mann PAGE, Esq. in this county (Spotsylvania) (THE VIRGINIA HERALD 14 M
2 CONC ay 1799)
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - MARRIAGES AND DEATHS FROM BALTIMORE NEWSPAPERS, 1796-1816 by Robert Barnes, p. 338
2 CONT WASHINGTON, Col. William Augustine, died last Tues. at Georgetown in his 53rd year.  (Balto. Evening Post, 10 Oct 1810)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT He was buried at Mt. Vernon in Fairfax Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited Wakefield; after 1780 built at Blenheim, later at Haywood, 1783. He had in all 9 children, among them George Corbin Washington and (by his 3rd wife) Sarah Tayloe and William Augustine II.  He died in Georgetown; burie
2 CONC d at Mt. Vernon.  General Washington in his will (1799) names William Augustine Washington, "son of my deceased brother, Augustine Washington"; leaves him a sword.
