2 CONT ===Mildred Reade===
2 CONT * Birth:  Oct. 2, 1643 York County Virginia, USA  
2 CONT * Death:  Oct. 6, 1686 Gloucester County Virginia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of George and Elizabeth (Martin) Reade. Married to Augustine Warner II. Greatgrandmother to George Washington. Mother of Mary, Augustine III, Robert, Elizabeth, George and Mildred (Washington). 
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   George Reade (1608 - 1674)
2 CONT   Elizabeth Martiau Reade (1625 - 1696)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Augustine Warner (1642 - 1681)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Mildred Warner Washington (1671 - 1701)*
2 CONT   Elizabeth Warner Lewis (1672 - 1720)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Warner Hall Graveyard  Naxera Gloucester County Virginia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Kaaren Crail Vining Record added: Aug 23, 2005  Find A Grave Memorial# 11596681 
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Mildred Reade
2 CONT
2 CONT Mildred Reade was the daughter of Colonel George Reade and Elizabeth Martiau.2 She married Colonel Augustine Warner, son of Captain Augustine Warner and Mary Towneley, in 1670/71. She died in 1693/94 at Warner Hall, Virginia, U.S.
2 CONC A.  From 1671, her married name became Warner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mildred Reade and Colonel Augustine Warner
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Mary Warner+3
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Mildred Warner+1 b. 1670/71, d. 26 Mar 1701
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Elizabeth Warner+2 b. 24 Nov 1672, d. 5 Feb 1720
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Augustine Warner , II, of Warner Hall, son of Augustine & Mary (Townley) Warner , b. 3 Jun 1642, Glouchester, VA or 20 Oct 1643[iv]; d. 19 Jun 1681, Gloucester Co., VA; bur. Warner Hall Plantation, Gloucester Co., VA; m 1s
2 CONC t 1655 to Mildred Reade , daughter of Col. George Reade  {founder of Yorktown}; m 2nd Elizabeth Martian .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1658, he was sent to England by his father to be educated at Marchant Taylor's School in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine Warner  is frequently referred to in documents as Speaker Warner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine Warner  II , served as a Burgess for York Co., VA in Apr 1652; as Burgess for Gloucester Co., VA Mar 1658-59. He served as Burgess for the Council of State Marc 1659-60.  In Mar 1675-6 and Feb 1676-7, he ws the Speaker o
2 CONC f the House of Burgesses during Bacon's Rebellion.  He was a member to the Council of Virginia, 1677.  During Bacon's Rebellion Warner Hall was used by Bacon, as his headquarters, after the burning of Jamestown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Augustine  & Mildred (Reade) Warner  had four (4) children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.2.1.  Mildred Warner , d. 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.2.2.  Mary Warner ,  m.  17 Feb 1680 to Speaker John Smith  of Purton, Jr. of the Virginia House of Burgesses.  She is the "Common-denominator" to the ancestry with the British Royalty of the Cowne Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.2.3.  Elizabeth Warner , b. 24 Nov 1672 at "Chesake" , m. "Councilor" John Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.2.4.  Robert Warner , never married.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate Birth Date: 10/20/1643
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate Death Date: 1694
