1 NOTE !BIRTH - SOME PROMINENT VA FAMILIES VOL IV p. 24 by Louise P. duBellet
2 CONT Col. Augustine Warner, Jr., of "Warner Hall", Gloucester Co., VA, born June 3, 1642, according to the inscription on his tombstone.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 262
2 CONT Married Mildred Reade, daughter of Col. George Reade and wife Elizabeth Martiau or Martain before 1671.  Col. Augustine Warner, Jr. and Mildred Reade became the great grandparents of George Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid p. 262
2 CONT Col. Augustine Warner, Jr. d. June 19, 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone At Warner Hall reads:
2 CONT Here lyeth interred
2 CONT Col. Augustine Warner
2 CONT Who was born ye 3rd of Jun 1642
2 CONT And died ye 19th of June 1681
2 CONT
2 CONT COLONIAL & REVOLUTIONARY LINEAGES OF AMERICA, VOL 4
2 CONT Col. Augustine (2) Warner, son of Col. Augustine (1) and Mary Warner, was born June 3, 1642-43, at "Warner Hall," and died according to the inscription on his tombstone, June 18, 1681, at "Warner Hall."  He was enrolled at the Mer
2 CONC cchant Tailor's School of London, in 1658, as the eldest son of Augustine Warner, Gentleman, of Virginia.  After finishing his education in London, he returned to Virginia, and in 1674 was a Burgess for Cloucester Co.  In 1675-76 
2 CONC he was Speaker of the House of Burgesses and Councillor.  He was a member of the Council in 1676-77, and a colonel of the Gloucester Co. Militia in 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1658 - At age 16 he was sent to England to be educated.  Was enlisted at the
2 CONT Merchant Tailor's School in London.
2 CONT 1667 - Before this date, he married Mildred Reade.
2 CONT 1675 - Inherited Warner Hall upon death of his father.
2 CONT 1676 - Elevated to position of Speaker of the House of Burgesses.
2 CONT 1676 - Councillor
2 CONT 1677 - Contributed 10L sterling to Petsworth Parish Church, Gloucester Co.
2 CONT (Vestry Book, Petsworth Parish).  He also presented the silver service used in that church.
2 CONT 1680 -  Col. Commandant of Gloucester Co. Militia.
2 CONT From VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson p. 262
2 CONT
2 CONT SOME WILLS FROM THE BURNED COUNTIES OF VIRGINIA AND OTHER WILLS NOT LISTED IN VIRGINIA WILLS AND ADMINISTRATIONS 1632-1800 by William Lindsay Hopkins,p.45
2 CONT AUGUSTINE WARNER, II   Gloucester Co.      
2 CONT Wife Mildred Warner.  Second son George Warner.  Youngest Son Robin Warner.
2 CONT Walker Cant.  Daughters (not named).  (From a 1691 letter of William Fitzhugh to Mildred Warner.)
2 CONT VA Mag V.3, pp. 11-15
1 NOTE Speaker of the House of Burgesses, VA
