1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Augustine Warner''' was born on January 17, 1666/7 in Warner Hall, Gloucester Co. VA, son of Augustine Warner (1642–1681) and Mildred Reade (1643–>1694).
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine died on March 17, 1687 in Warner Hall, aged 21, unmarried.  He was buried in the Warner Hall Graveyard at Naxera, Gloucester County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tombstone Inscription'''
2 CONT
2 CONT "Here Lyeth interred
2 CONT Augustine Warner
2 CONT son of Coll Augustine &
2 CONT Mildred Warner born ye
2 CONT 17th of January, 1666/1667, And
2 CONT deceased ye 17th of March, 1686-7."
2 CONT
2 CONT Info from Lyon G. Tyler's 1894 article in the William and Mary Quarterly quoted in "Warner Hall Story of a Great Plantation" by David Brown & Thane Harpole 2004.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustine_Warner_Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine Warner Jr. had three sons, all of whom died unmarried, and three daughters, who inherited the Warner property and left many descendants.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT Augustine might have been born in 1671 instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # https://familyhistory.themartyns.net/familyfiles/6093.htm
2 CONT # Some Prominent Virginia Families IN FOUR VOLUMES .VOLUME IV. By Louise Pecquet du Bellet J. P. BELL COMPANY (Inc.), .Publishers, (Lynchburg, Virginia.). Page 9. < [https://archive.org/details/someprominentvir04pecq/page/9/mode/1
2 CONC up?q=Warner Archive.Org] >
2 CONT # Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7656599/augustine-warner: accessed May 21, 2025), memorial page for Augustine Warner III (17 Jan 1667–17 Mar 1687), Find a Grave Memorial ID 7656599, citing 
2 CONC Warner Hall Graveyard, Naxera, Gloucester County, Virginia, USA; Maintained by archtype (contributor 47159002). This Transcription contributed by Kim Curlin Wettroth kwet@ mindspring.com .....
