1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Elizabeth Warner
2 CONT *Birth:  Nov. 24, 1672 - Chesake, Virginia
2 CONT * Death:  Feb. 5, 1720 -  Gloucester County, Virginia
2 CONT * Burial: Warner Hall Graveyard  Naxera Gloucester County Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Parents: Col. Augustine Warner II, Mildred Reade 
2 CONT * Spouse: Col. John Lewis lll (1669-1725) - married 1692 at Warner Hall
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Tombstone Inscription 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Here Lyeth Interr'd ye Body of Elizabeth Lewis the Daughter of Col Augustine Warner and Mildred his Wife and late wife of John Lewis Esq She was Born at Chesake the 24th of November, 1672 Aged 47 years 2 Months and 12 Days, and 
2 CONC was a Tender Mother of 14 Children. She Departed this Life the 5th Day of February 1719/20."
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Augustine Warner (1642 - 1681) Mildred Reade Warner (1643 - 1686)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: John Lewis (1669 - 1725)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # John Lewis (1692 - 1754)*
2 CONT # Charles Lewis (1696 - 1779)*
2 CONT # Robert Lewis (1702 - 1765)*
2 CONT # Catherine Lewis (1702 - 1705)*
2 CONT # Ann Lewis (1712 - 1712)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Calculated relationship*
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: kimshockey (reb) (inacti... Record added: Jul 05, 2003  Find A Grave Memorial# 7656611 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Warner-685
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Born November 24, 1672 at "Chesake"[4][5] at Warner Hall, Gloucester County, Virginia  
2 CONT *     Parents Augustine Warner (1642-1681) & Mildred Reade (1643-1686)[6]  
2 CONT *     Marriage in 1692 to Col. John Lewis (1669-1725) at Warner Hall, Gloucester County, Virginia.[2][3]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Warner) Lewis, the third daughter of Augustine Warner II, became the wife of John Lewis[1][2] and inherited Warner Hall. They moved there about 1702 from Chemokins, New Kent County.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the mother of fourteen children, according to her gravestone. The "names of nine of them are known from records in Hening' s Statutes-at-Large and in the Parish Register of Abingdon Parish, Gloucester (in which Warne
2 CONC r Hall was located)."[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children cited in various sources were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #     John Lewis, born before 1694 in New Kent County.[7][8] 
2 CONT #     Charles Lewis, born before 1696 in New Kent County.[7][8] 
2 CONT #     Mildred Lewis (c1700-1733), married (1) John Howell, (2) Dr. John Brown, (3) Col. Henry Willis.[8][9] 
2 CONT #     Robert Lewis, born at Warner Hall, in August 1704.[7][8] 
2 CONT #     Catherine, baptized 2 November 1705. Twin to Elizabeth, died young.[8] 
2 CONT #     Elizabeth, baptized 2 November 1705. Twin to Catherine, died young.[8] 
2 CONT #     Elizabeth, born 6 May 1706 or 1700-1749, m John Kennon Bolling.[8] 
2 CONT #     Isabella, baptized 18 December 1707.[8] 
2 CONT #     Anne, baptized 14 February 1712.[8] 
2 CONT #     Mary[citation needed] (no baptismal or any records have been found to show that she was the daughter of John and Elizabeth Warner Lewis), married Major Throckmorten.[8]  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Lewis) Warner died February 5, 1720 at Warner Hall, Gloucester County, Virginia.[3][10] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth is buried in the Warner Hall Colonial Family Cemetery[1] with her husband, John Lewis, at Naxera, Gloucester County, Virginia.[3][11] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
