1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Bushrod Jr. married first Jane Lane Corbin. His children, according to his will, were Hannah (married John Augustine Washington) and Elizabeth (married Philip Smith). He married secondly Mildred Washington. Mi
2 CONC ldred had been married once before, and some sources cite her married name as Seaton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT from http://www.frostandgilchrist.com/getperson.php?personID=I17761&tree=frostinaz01
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) There is some uncertainty as to who John BUSHROD's wives were. His wives may have included any or all of the following women: Anne BUSHROD, Jenny (or Jane) CORBIN, and Mildred SEATON. The only wife of John BUSHROD mentioned in
2 CONC  his will was named Mildred.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Ritchie, Ruth and Wood, Sudie Rucker, Garner-Keene Families of Northern Neck, Virginia, Charlottesville, VA: Jarman Printing, 1952, pp. 208-209:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bushrod . . . inherited "Bushfield" and married Mildred Corbin of King and Queen County, a first cousin of Colonel Thomas Lee of Stratford. They had a daughter Hannah Bushrod, who married John Augustine Washington, brother of
2 CONC  General George Washington. Their son, Bushrod Washington, born June 5, 1762, at "Bushfield," was an Associate Justice of the U. S. Supreme Court and it was to him that George Washington left Mt. Vernon and all his books and paper
2 CONC s. He married Julia Anne Blackburn. As they had no children, upon his death in 1829 he left Mt. Vernon to a nephew, John Augustine Washington, son of his brother, Corbin Washington, who married Hannah Lee, a daughter of Hon. Richa
2 CONC rd Henry Lee. He in turn left it to his son, John Augustine Washington III, who was the last private owner of the estate. Thus all the private owners of Mt. Vernon after George Washington's death were descendants of Thomas and Mar
2 CONC y Keene of Northumberland County. George Washington visited numerous times at "Bushfield." The first John Augustine Washington and his wife, Hannah, who was the second mistress of Mt. Vernon, are buried at "Bushfield."
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) "The Corbin Family," Virginia Magazine of History and Biography, Vol. 29 (1921), pp. 521:
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue [of Gawin CORBIN] (which marriage uncertain): . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT Jenny, or Jane, married John Bushrod, of Westmoreland county. She is not mentioned in Gawin Corbin's will and the only evidence for her existance [sic] is the account of the family given by Bishop Meade in his Old Church and Famil
2 CONC ies of Virginia. The John Bushrod, she is stated to have married, died in Westmoreland county and his will proved Dec. 30, 1760, names a wife Mildred. As he makes Richard Corbin an executor and as the name Corbin appeared as a Chr
2 CONC istian name among his descendants, it is probable that Jenny Corbin was his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) McIlhany, Hugh M., Some Virginia Families, Staunton, VA: Stoneburner and Prufer Printers, 1903, p. 215:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bushrod lived at "Bushfield", and was a vestryman of Cople Parish in 1755, High Sheriff of Westmoreland County in 1759, and a member of the House of Burgesses, 1748-1755. He probably married his cousin Anne, daughter of Thoma
2 CONC s Bushrod; she dying, he married Jane Corbin . . . , and left two daughters, Hannah and Catherine. About 1760 Hannah married John Augustine Washington, a brother of George Washington, and had four children, - Bushrod, Corbin, Mild
2 CONC red and Augustine.
2 CONT
2 CONT (5) "Bushfield" History <http://www.bushfieldmanor.com/History.htm>:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bushrod, the younger, married first Jenny Corbin and second Mildred Seaton. He fathered a daughter, Hannah, by his first marriage, who married John Augustine Washington. At the death of John Bushrod, Bushfield was left to his
2 CONC  daughter Hannah Washington for her lifetime and then the property to go to her first born son.
2 CONT
2 CONT (6) Westmoreland County, Virginia Wills, 1654-1800 [database online], Provo, UT: The Generations Network, Inc., 2000:
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: John Bushrod Description: Decedent Date: 14 Feb. 1760 Notes: Bushrod, John, gent. 14 Feb. 1760; 30 Dec. 1760. Wife Mildred part of est.; dau. Hannah Washington 35 slaves, furniture and land; grand daus. Mary and Jenny Washin
2 CONC gton 3 slaves each; dau. Elizabeth Bushrod land and 41 slaves; to Lydia Bushrod Pettit dau. of John ??10 yearly if her father spend her est.; friends Hon. Richard Corbin and John Washington exrs. Title: Gentleman Prove Date: 30 De
2 CONC c 1760
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/bushrod/59/
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=29586667 
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=OexQCAAAQBAJ&lpg=PA324&ots=ihuLNgWGnc&dq=Mildred%20Seaton%20Bushrod&pg=PA324#v=onepage&q&f=false page 324] of Washington - 25 generations  By Jim White
2 CONT
