1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 344
2 CONT Warner Washington I (1715-1791), eldest son of John Washington (uncle to George) and wife Catherine Whiting.  His grandmother was Mildred Warner.  He was a brother to Henry of Middlesex Co., VA; was a justice of Frederick Co., VA.
2 CONC , in 1769 and 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT He married (1) Elizabeth Macon, daughter of Col. William Macon of New Kent Co.,VA.  From 1765 or thereabouts he lived at Fairfield, now Clarke Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT He married (2) in 1765 Hannah Fairfax of Belvoir on the Potomac.  Hannah is named in his will, 1789.  He then had 2 young sons, Fairfax and Whiting.  General Washington frequently visited Warner at Fairfield.  On November 11, 1799
2 CONC , Mrs. Warner Washington and son Whiting dined at Mt. Vernon.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT See Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
