2 CONC -13-8¾. Signed by John Grymes, exr. of Henry Willis, John Casper Stover, execr. to my father. Wit: Jonath. Gibson, James Porteus. 25 Nov. 1742. Returned to Court. [Orange County Virginia Will Book 1, Dorman, pg. 46]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1640 or before, Colonel Francis Willis arrived in Virginia from England. In England — clearly outlined and identified in his will of 1689 — he left an uncle John, his sister Grace, brothers William and Henry, and several nep
2 CONC hews, a Francis among them. At the same time, some assert that it was a Lewis Willis in Virginia before 1690 who was the father of the Henry Willis who married the Widow Mildred (nee Washington) Brown and helped establish the city
2 CONC  of Fredericksburg. Early details are murky, but the central points are accurate.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel Henry Willis''', born February 1691-92, died 14 September 1740. Founded city of Fredericksburg. Married (1) 2 November 1714 Ann Alexander, widow of John Smith of Purton. [Sources: Virginia Magazine of History and Biogra
2 CONC phy, vol. 4, no 2]
2 CONT * Mary Willis, born 5 August 1716, married Hancock Lee 1733
2 CONT * Francis Willis VI, born 1718
2 CONT * David Willis, born 1720
2 CONT * Henry Willis, born 1722, married Elizabeth Gregory, no male issue
2 CONT * John W. Willis, born 1724, married Elizabeth Madison
2 CONT * Robert Willis, born 1725
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (2) 30 October 1726 Mildred Howell, sister of Mary who married Charles Lewis of the Byrd and daughter of John Howell, the "widow Brown," who died November 1732.
2 CONT * John Willis, born 16 July 1728, died 5 March 1750, no issue
2 CONT * Elizabeth [Mary/Isabel] Willis, born 12 January 1729
2 CONT * Ann Willis, born 14 September 1731, married Duff Green c 1756
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (3) 5 January 1734 Mildred Washington, who died 5 September 1747, widow of Roger * Gregory, cousin of her predecessor.
2 CONT * Colonel Lewis Willis, born 11 November 1734, married (1) Anne Carter, (2) Mary Champe
2 CONT * Isabell Willis, born 10 June 1733
2 CONT * Ann Willis, born 30 January 1736 http://www.glenncourt.com/genealogy/fam_willis.php
