1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Daughters of American Revolution Ancestor #: [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A127014 A127014]
2 CONT * Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): LIEUTENANT COLONEL, PATRIOTIC SERVICE
2 CONT * Birth:  11-11-1734    FREDERICKSBURG SPOTSYLVANIA CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT * Death:  1-15-1813     FREDERICKSBURG SPOTSYLVANIA CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT * Service Source: SANCHEZ-SAAVEDRA, GUIDE TO VA MIL ORGS IN AM REV, P62 ABERCROMBIE & SLATTEN, VA REV PUB CLAIMS, V3, P855-857
2 CONT * Service Description: 1) LCOL, 10TH VA REGT; 2) FURNISHED SUPPLIES 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 3 times 
2 CONT * 1) MARY CHAMPE   
2 CONT * 2) ANN CARTER CHAMPE   
2 CONT * 3) ELIZABETH BROMFIELD   After his 1st wife Mary Champe died, he married her brother John's widow, Ann Carter Champe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is married to (1) Mary Jane Champe in the year 1751 at Lambs Creek, Virginia, United States, he was 16 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Child(ren):
2 CONT * Milly Willis  1775-1795
2 CONT * Leviva Willis  1772-????
2 CONT * William Champe Willis  1770-1843
2 CONT * Deborah Willis  1750-1842
2 CONT * Mary Willis  1755-1778
2 CONT * Henry W Willis  1755-1761
2 CONT * Jane Willis  1755-1760
2 CONT * Mildred Willis  1751-1772
2 CONT
2 CONT He is married to (2) Anne Byrd Carter in the year 1774 at Virginia, United States, he was 39 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Child(ren):
2 CONT * Byrd Charles Willis  1755-1761
2 CONT * Byrd Charles Willis  1781-1846 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a relationship with Elizabeth S Bromfield
2 CONT
