1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 335-336
2 CONT Computing age at death from death date would be 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Martha died unmarried June 19, 1773, aged 17.  She had epilepsy and died of a seizure.
2 CONT
2 CONT Washington had no children and his constant and devoted care was given to his step-children, John Parke and Martha Custis.  Mrs. Washington's daughter Martha (Patsy) Custis was subject to fits.  Persistent efforts were made to cur
2 CONC e or relieve her.  On June 19, 1773, Washington wrote in his diary:  About five oclock poor Patsy Custis Died Suddenly.  
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT She was probably buried at Mount Vernon.
