1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 177
2 CONT Col. John Lewis was born 22 March 1694, prob. in Gloucester Co.,VA
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid
2 CONT Married abt 1718 Frances Fielding, daughter of Henry Fielding.  She died 27 Oct 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT Married 2nd Priscilla (Churchill) Carter, the widow of Robert Carter II of
2 CONT Nomini, son of Robert "King" Carter.  Her two children by her first marriage
2 CONT went with her to Warner Hall to live.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT John died 17 Jan 1754.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT Buried at Warner Hall, Gloucester Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. John Lewis as eldest son of "Councillor" Lewis and Elizabeth Warner inherited under the English system of primogeniture the Warner Hall home with all the surrounding estate and he made his home at Warner Hall his entire life.
2 CONC   His wife, Frances Fielding lived on 13 years after her marriage during which time 7 children were born to her and she died soon after the birth of her youngest child and namesake who probably also died about the same time as her
2 CONC  mother.  Col. Lewis married (2) Priscilla (Churchill) Carter, the widow of Robert Carter II of Nomini, son of Robert "King" Carter.  Her 2 children by her first marriage, Robert "Councillor" Carter and Elizabeth Carter went with 
2 CONC her to Warner Hall to live.  In 1748, Col. John Lewis III was appointed to the Council.  It is certain he held at one time the rank of colonel in the Virginia Militia as that title is always attached to his name.  He inherited the
2 CONC  3,000 acre estate of Warner hall and so had the responsibility of the operation of this large plantation.  He was also considerably engaged in the shipping business and was owner of a number of vessels engaged in trade with dista
2 CONC nt parts. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. John Lewis and Robert Bruce Carter are 1st cousins, 7 generations removed.
