1 NOTE !BIRTH - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 178
2 CONT Col. Charles Lewis was born 25 Feb 1729 in Gloucester Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married about 1750 Lucy Taliaferro.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died about 1770 in Port Royal, Caroline Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Charles Lewis entered the VA Militia at an early age and served as a Captain in the Royal VA Regiment comanded by Col. Wm. Byrd against the Indians; was company commander in Royal Virginians and later the regimental adjutant.
2 CONC   Along with his uncle, Lt. Col. George Washington, he accompanied the ill-fated Braddock expedition which resulted in Braddock's defeat and death.  That expedition began its march on 10 Oct 1755 and Col. Lewis kept a journal of h
2 CONC is experiences during this time.
