2 PLAC Warner Hall, Glouchester County, Virginia
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 MAR 1777
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family legend has her as the wife of George Yates (IV) but is only substantiated by dates and names of children much similar to that of Lewis. It is believed that she was living at her husband's death as the Court 
2 CONC Order Book spoke of executrix and executors. John (eldest son) and Michael Yates (brother)were the ultimate executors with no mention of a third party.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the nine children credited to her four have Lewis family names. The first son was normally named after the paternal grandfather but since George did not really know his father this would have been unlikely. Instead the first so
2 CONC n was named John, possibly after her father. Then there was Frances which was her mother's name. A Charles Lewis followed which could have been named after her closest brother. Warner was her grandmother's maiden name. This seems 
2 CONC to be more than a coincidence. Frances could certainly have had the opportunity to meet George in Fredericksburg while visiting her brothers, Fielding Lewis and Charles Lewis, as George lived nearby. Sorley in "Lewis of Warner Hal
2 CONC l" stated that Frances undoubtedly died at a young age but this was based on family records as court records are not available. There is no record of her death in the Abingdon Parish Book, where all other deaths in the family were
2 CONC  recorded. If she married outside the parish this would be the case.The circumstantial evidence is there and we may never find any more.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
