1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Lewis/6000000173130382871?through=6000000008596524362 & not the husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Frances-Lewis/6000000008596524362
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Samuel Lewis 
2 CONT *Birth:	November 11, 1780 Berryville, Culpeper County, Virginia
2 CONT *Death:	November 28, 1842 (62) ‘Shellfield‘, Westmoreland County, Virginia, United States
2 CONT *Son of George Lewis and Catherine Daingerfield.
2 CONT *married 1) Sarah Attaway Miller 2) Maria Turner Baylis 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 children  of Sarah Attaway Miller and Samuel Lewis
2 CONT # Judge George Washington Lewis (1804 - 1879) m 1) Jane Brockenbrough Lewis, 6 children 2) Lucy Ann Robb, 2 children 
2 CONT # Thomas Lewis (1806 - 1833) died unmarried 
2 CONT #Eliza Airess Lewis (1809 - 1832) m James William Finnie, 1 child 
2 CONT # John Bankhead Lewis (1810 - 1879) m Elizabeth Briggs, 7 or 8 children 
2 CONT # Mary Willis Lewis (1812 - 1886) m Col. John Casey, 6 children 
2 CONT # Sarah Attaway Lewis (1814 - 1872) m John G. Putnam, 6 children 
2 CONT # Capt. Henry Howell Lewis, CSN (1817 - 1893), of Baltimore; m Ann Ogle Tayloe, 3 children 
2 CONT # Catherine Dangerfield Lewis (1820 - 1849) m her cousin Fielding Lewis as his first wife  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 children of Maria Turner Baylis  and Samuel Lewis
2 CONT # Janette Gibson Lewis 
2 CONT # William Lewis 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT The other Samuel Lewis married Frances Pulley, children include John Henry Lewis.  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.fold3.com/page/91802613/samuel-morgan-lewis/stories
2 CONT
2 CONT “.... I went to Kenmore Plantation in Fredericksburg over a year ago and saw a geneaology chart and saw the name Samuel Lewis, but no John Henry Lewis. I am thinking that perhaps Samuel Morgan Lewis had two wives and our family co
2 CONC mes from the second wife, who was Frances Pulley. [SIC - NO]. The first wife seems to be Sarah Attaway in the book "Lewis of Warner Hall" by Merrow Egerton Sorley. I think there also may be a genealogy chart at Woodlawn Plantation
2 CONC  (near Mount Vernon) where Lawrence Lewis and Nellie Custis-Lewis (George Washington's adopted grand-daughter) lived. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth dates 1780 vs 1785 and locations, Berryville vs. Jamestown seem to diverge for Samuel Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * *”Lewis Family of Warner Hall.” The William and Mary Quarterly, vol. 10, no. 1, 1901, pp. 48–54. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/1919805. Accessed 28 Feb. 2021. (Page 50 - 51)
