1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 201
2 CONT Eleanor Parke (Nelly) Custis was born March 21, 1779 and was adopted by George Washington as her father had died in 1781.  She was born at "Abingdon", her father's residence on the Potomac about midway between Alexandria and the F
2 CONC ederal City, on land acquired from the Alexanders, for whom Alexandria was named.  She grew up with her grandmother, Martha Washington, at Mt. Vernon and was married there.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT On February 22, 1799, Washington's birthday, Eleanor married Lawrence Lewis, the General's nephew, son of Betty Washington Lewis, late of Fredericksburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid p. 209
2 CONT She died in 1852 and her will was admitted to record at Berryville on Monday, August 23, 1852.  After her husband died in 1839, she lived at Audley, near Berryville, in Clarke Co.,VA., with her son, Lorenzo Lewis, and his family w
2 CONC here she died in 1852.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT The body of Nelly Custis Lewis was carried to Mount Vernon for interment.
1 NOTE She was married in the presence of George and Martha Washington on his last birthday.
1 NOTE THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 201
