2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://edu.lva.virginia.gov/online_classroom/shaping_the_constitution/people/william_woodford Education at Library of Virginia]
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM WOODFORD (1734–1780)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Woodford to the President of the Virginia Revolutionary Convention, December 9, 1775, Revolutionary Government, Papers of the Fourth Convention, Record Group 2, Accession 30003, Library of Virginia, Richmond, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Woodford was a Revolutionary War general from Caroline County. The son of William Woodford Sr. and Anne Cocke, daughter of William Cocke, secretary of the Virginia colony, he grew up on his father's plantation, Windsor, te
2 CONC n miles outside of Fredericksburg on the Rappahannock River. In 1762 he married Mary Thornton. They had two children. 
2 CONT ----
