2 CONT * 1779 Virginia Court Reports
2 CONT * Chapman v. Chapman
2 CONT * Nathaniel CHAPMAN, died intestate 1760 in Maryland.
2 CONT * Survived by his widow (who besides her legal interest in his estate, possessed, in her own right, lands and slaves of considerable value).
2 CONT * Issue: Nathaniel (eldest) died intestate and without issue;
2 CONT * Issue: Pearson, deceased, Will dated in 1771, survived by a son, George;
2 CONT * Issue: George;
2 CONT * Issue: several daughters.
2 CONT * The estate of Nathaniel Chapman, the elder was considerable and included lots in Alexander, acerage in Fairfax County, "Pignut" tract in Fauquier County, etc. as well as lands in Maryland.
