1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_Richard_Fendall_I Philip Richard Fendall I]
2 CONT
2 CONT .... Fendall returned home in 1780 and married another cousin''', Elizabeth Steptoe Lee''', the widow of Philip Ludwell Lee of Stratford Hall. Elizabeth brought significant land holdings to the marriage, including the 6,595 acres 
2 CONC at Stratford Hall. Philip lived with Elizabeth, her two daughters, Flora and Matilda, and her son-in-law Col. "Light Horse Harry" Lee at Stratford Hall in 1784. In that year, Fendall bought a half-acre lot at the corner of Washing
2 CONC ton and Oronoco Streets in Alexandria, Virginia from Light Horse Harry for ₤300. He constructed the Lee-Fendall House, a large family home on the lot in 1785.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1787, Fendall's wife Elizabeth had contracted a cancer-like disease. She died unexpectedly in May 1789, while on a trip to Stratford Hall to visit her daughter. Two years later, in 1791, Fendall married a third Lee lady, Mary L
2 CONC ee ...
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: daughter of Dr. James Steptoe, Col. and Anne Steptoe (Ashton)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # Philip Ludwell Lee
2 CONT # Philip Fendall 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_Ludwell_Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Ludwell Lee (February 24, 1727 – February 21, 1775) increased his landholdings in 1763 by marrying his heiress ward, but they had no children that survived their parents. Elizabeth, daughter of James Steptoe of Westmoreland
2 CONC  County, survived him and remarried to Philip Richard Fendall. Their children were:
2 CONT *their son died as an infant.[5]: 104 [b] 
2 CONT *Matilda would marry her cousin Lighthorse Henry Lee (whose financial profligacy caused difficulties for later generations) and 
2 CONT *Flora married her cousin Ludwell Lee.[1]: 72 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://www.leefendallhouse.org/?p=217 Lee-Fendall House - Museum & Garden]
2 CONT
2 CONT Confused yet? It gets worse: '''Philip R. Fendall''' married three Lee ladies. His cousin Sarah Lettice, of the Blenheim Line, came first. Then he married '''Elizabeth Steptoe''', who was the widow of '''Philip Ludwell Lee''' of t
2 CONC he Stratford Line. Philip Ludwell Lee and Elizabeth Steptoe’s daughter Matilda, was married to Light Horse Harry Lee, which means that Elizabeth Steptoe was Light Horse’s mother-in-law. Finally, Philip R. Fendall married Mary Fend
2 CONC all, Light Horse Harry’s sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=tlIEAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA72&lpg=PA72&dq=elizabeth+steptoe+lee&source=bl&ots=L1GVQufYnv&sig=pTdt_xd8fWkwNR6g_xbYNqZBCFo&hl=en&sa=X&ei=HCMHUZq-I4j4rAGRtYGIDg&ved=0CEAQ6AEwAg#v=onepage&q=elizabeth%20stept
2 CONC oe%20lee&f=false Stratford Hall and the Lees Connected with Its History:] Biographical .... Page 72
2 CONT # ^ Fairfax County Deed Book. Fairfax County, Virginia. pp. 270, 486.
