1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE LEES OF VIRGINIA: A SELECTIVE GENEALOGY by Paul C. Nagel
2 CONT Elizabeth Steptoe was born about 1741 in Westmoreland Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - GLEANINGS FROM MARYLAND NEWSPAPERS 1786-1790 by Robert W. Barnes, p. 20
2 CONT FENDALL, Mrs., died in Baltimore, consort of Philip Richard Fendall, Esq., or Alexandria. (BMJ, 19 May 1789)
2 CONT Note:  Elizabeth Steptoe Fendall must have been the Mrs. Fendall who died in 1789 as he remarried by 1791. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT In that year, Mrs. Fendall died, which meant that her portion of the Stratford property, which included title to the manor house and outbuildings, reverted to Matilda as Col. Phil's eldest daughter. - See Birth Ref. p. 165
