1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Jane "Jenny" Lane CORBIN 
2 CONT * Birth:  1712 VA 
2 CONT * Father:  Col. Gawin CORBIN 
2 CONT * Mother:  Jane LANE
2 CONT
2 CONT 20—3.  Jane Lane, b. 1710-17; m. Col. John Bushrod, of "Bushfield," Westmoreland Co., Va., who served as a Burgess, 1748-55; son of Hon. John and Anne (Bushrod) Bushrod, gr.-dau. of Hon. John and Hannah (Keene) Bushrod, of Glouces
2 CONC ter Co., Va., and of Hon. Thomas Bushrod.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT * 21—1.  Hannah, m. John Augustine Washington, of Westmoreland Co., Va., son of Augustine and Mary (Ball) Washington, of "Bridges Creek," and had issue.  (See Washington and Ball lineage.)
2 CONT * 21—2.  Elizabeth; untraced...
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT By Jane Corbin John Bushrod had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hannah Bushrod m. abt 1760 John Augustine Washington [brother of George Washington] Issue: Bushrod, Corbin, Mildred and Augustine.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Catherine Bushrod m. abt 1762 William Taylor d. 1816; WP 1 Apr 1816 Frederick Co. VA. Settled at "Green Hill" Frederick County, near Berryville, which estate remained in the possession of his descendants until after 1870. Issue
2 CONC : 6.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bushrod married 2nd to Mildred Washington, daughter of John Washington & Mary Massey; her 4th husband.  
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT * http://dgmweb.net/FGS/B/BushrodJohn-JaneLaneCorbin.html
2 CONT **1.  Stella Pickett Hardy.  1911.  Colonial Families of the Southern States of America.  T.A. Wright, New York, NY (republished 1958, Southern Book Co., Baltimore, MD; republished 1965, Genealogical Publ. Co., Baltimore, MD; onli
2 CONC ne at books.google.com). 
2 CONT * http://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I038673&tree=tree1
