2 CONC  Edwin Hayden
2 CONT
2 CONT >a. John Bushrod, b. Glouc'r Co., Jan. 30, 1663; d. Feb. 6, 17*9, ittpra: m. Hannah, dau. of Wm. and Elizabeth Keene, North'd Co.; had—4. '''John, m. Anne, dau. of Thomas Bushrod''', and pro. had Col. John, Burgess West'd, 1748-17
2 CONC 55; m. Jenny, dau. of Col. Gawin Corbin, and had Hannah, m. John Augustine Washington, and had Hon. Bushrod W. 5. a son 6. Apphia, m, 171a o), Wm. Fauntleroy, &c , &c. (Va His. Mag., I., w)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Stella Pickett Hardy.  1911.  Colonial Families of the Southern States of America.  T.A. Wright, New York, NY (republished 1958, Southern Book Co., Baltimore, MD; republished 1965, Genealogical Publ. Co., Baltimore, MD; onlin
2 CONC e at books.google.com). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >20—3.  Jane Lane, b. 171017; m. Col. John Bushrod, of "Bushfield," Westmoreland Co., Va., who served as a Burgess, 1748-55; son of '''Hon. John and Anne (Bushrod) Bushrod''', gr.-dau. of Hon. John and Hannah (Keene) Bushrod, of G
2 CONC loucester Co., Va., and of Hon. Thomas Bushrod.  Issue: ....
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Ritchie, Ruth and Wood, Sudie Rucker, Garner-Keene Families of Northern Neck, Virginia, Charlottesville, VA: Jarman Printing, 1952, pp. 208-209:
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Bushrod . . . [son of John Bushrod] inherited "Bushfield" and married Mildred [sic: Jane] Corbin of King and Queen County, a first cousin of Colonel Thomas Lee of Stratford. They had a daughter Hannah Bushrod, who married Jo
2 CONC hn Augustine Washington, brother of General George Washington. Their son, Bushrod Washington, born June 5, 1762, at "Bushfield," was an Associate Justice of the U. S. Supreme Court and it was to him that George Washington left Mt.
2 CONC  Vernon and all his books and papers. He married Julia Anne Blackburn. As they had no children, upon his death in 1829 he left Mt. Vernon to a nephew, John Augustine Washington, son of his brother, Corbin Washington, who married H
2 CONC annah Lee, a daughter of Hon. Richard Henry Lee. He in turn left it to his son, John Augustine Washington III, who was the last private owner of the estate. Thus all the private owners of Mt. Vernon after George Washington's death
2 CONC  were descendants of Thomas and Mary Keene of Northumberland County. George Washington visited numerous times at "Bushfield." The first John Augustine Washington and his wife, Hannah, who was the second mistress of Mt. Vernon, are
2 CONC  buried at "Bushfield."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
