1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Bushrod''', the younger daughter of John Bushrod and his first wife, Jane Corbin, was born about 1744 at Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia, and died there after 1782.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Philip Smith about 1771.  He was born before 1749, and died between July 1781 and March 1782. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=JBlCAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA93&ots=wFk467AlCF&dq=Elizabeth%20bushrod%20Philip%20smith&pg=PA93#v=onepage&q&f=false page 93] of William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine, Volume 6
2 CONT
2 CONT >... This last couple had two sons, Philip and Edward, who were students at William and Mary College. There is in Westmoreland county a deed made March 2, 1782, from '''Elizabeth Smith''', relict of Philip Smith, of Washington par
2 CONC ish, to John Augustine Washington in behalf of her three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Baldwin Bushrod Smith, 
2 CONT #Frances Burgess Smith and 
2 CONT #Hannah Bushrod Smith. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Burgess Smith married Rev. John Mathews, of Essex, son of John Mathews, Of Mathews county. Their issue was John, William B., Thomas, Philip Smith, Virginia, Mollie and Fanny Burgess.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
