1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Henry Lee Washington, son of Corbin Washington and Hannah Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/161949947/richard-henry_lee-washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of
2 CONT Corbin Washington and
2 CONT Hannah Lee Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned Prospect Hill, cottage and 900 acres,
2 CONT Mt. Vernon, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Walnut Farm,
2 CONT Westmoreland County, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at the age of 29 years,
2 CONT at Mount Vernon, Fairfax County, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Henry Lee Washington's Estate was
2 CONT divided between his siblings, John Augustine
2 CONT Washington, Bushrod Corbin Washington, and
2 CONT Mary Lee Washington Herbert.
2 CONT Also sister, Jane Mildred Washington died 1807.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LD8H-15M/richard-henry-lee-1732-1794
2 CONT When Richard Henry Lee was born on 20 January 1732, in Stratford Hall, Westmoreland, Virginia, British Colonial America, his father, Thomas Lee, was 42 and his mother, Hannah Ludwell, was 30. He married Anne Aylett on 5 December 1
2 CONC 757, in Virginia, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 2 daughters. In 1784, at the age of 52, his occupation is listed as 4th, president of the confederation congress. He died on 19 June 1794, in
2 CONC  Chantilly, Fairfax County, Virginia, British Colonial America, at the age of 62, and was buried in Coles Point, Westmoreland, Virginia, United States.
