2 NOTE https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/pdf_files/SpecialCollections/RA-016_Historic_AE_Rappahannock_County_2003_Traceries_Report.pdf
3 CONT
3 CONT Architectural Survey Report of Rappahannock County, Virginia
3 CONT E.H.T. Traceries, Inc., May 2003
3 CONT Page 39
3 CONT
3 CONT Figure 20: Thornton Hill (078-0050)
3 CONT
3 CONT The Dutch Colonial style is represented by one dwelling in Rappahannock County, Thornton Hill
3 CONT (078-0050). The wood-frame dwelling measures one-and-a-half stories in height, sits on a stone
3 CONT foundation, and is capped by a standing-seam metal gambrel roof. A central projecting gambrel,
3 CONT flanked by two added gabled dormers, dominates the dwelling. Other detailing includes
3 CONT decorative wood shingles, which cover beaded weatherboard, 9/9, 6/6, and 4/4 wood windows, a
3 CONT molded wood cornice with returns, and interior-end brick chimneys. A three-bay portico is
3 CONT supported by Tuscan columns. The dwelling was built for Colonel John Thornton, the son of
3 CONT Francis Thornton, who was one of the original landholders in Rappahannock County, and owned
3 CONT 40,000 acres of land granted by the king. 
