1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Hammond was born in Ireland. He sailed to Baltimore as a teenager for a six-year business apprenticeship. Hammond then moved to Charles Town (in what is now the easternmost county of West Virginia), opened a
2 CONC  mercantile business, and served as captain of a Berkeley County militia company. In 1792 he married Mary Lewis "Polly" Tapscott.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT "The Ownership of Happy Retreat by the Hammond Family, 1800–1837," The Rising Sun (Friends of Happy Retreat newsletter), May 2021, 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hammond, Thomas (ca. 1770–ca. 1826)," in Holly C. Shuman, ed., The Dolley Madison Digital Edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hammond in Virginia Compiled Marriages, 1740–1850 (Ancestry.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hammond at Early Colonial Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck Counties.
2 CONT
2 CONT CPT Thomas Hammond at Find a Grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hammond at FamilySearch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Author
2 CONT
2 CONT From Thomas Hammond, 6 June 1807
