1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/baldwin/6935/ <- Also (Another site) "JOHN MOORE, A Merchant Marina From Bristol Eng., who settled in "Isle of Wright" in 1640; Father of Thomas, George, and Katherine MOORE;
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sallysfamilyplace.com/robert-flake-katherine-moore/
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Barry Hayes  says that the wife of Robert Flake was Katherine Moore daughter of John Moore, the burgess in 1640 based on strong circumstantial evidence & analysis.  The records show that Katherine had been previously married a
2 CONC nd had had three daughters by this first husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bennett Boddie in Vol 8 of HSF gives this list of children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Katherine Moore and 1st husband: [some say George Wyatt]
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Mary ? [ca 1630 re deposition] ca 1632 – aft 1696 married 1st John Burgess
2 CONT *2. Susannah ? ca 1631 – ca 1691 married 10 Sept 1669 Thomas Atkinson died 1688
2 CONT * 3. Joyce ? ca 1633 – 9 June 1679 no children married aft 1650 Capt Francis England 1609 – 9 June 1677 married ca 1678 George Cripps who died 1787 Isle of Wight Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Katherine Moore and Robert Flake:
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Flake ca1653 – married ca 1669 Peter Hayes
2 CONT * 2. Mary Flake ca 1650/55-aft 1717 married bef. 25 Oct 1670 John Clarke ca 1636 – 1722 he had married 1st 7 May 1666 Katherine Gwaltney ca 1630 – ca 1669
2 CONT * 3. Robert Flake Jr. ca 1660-1724 married bef. 1702 Margaret Marriott
2 CONT * 4. Katherine Flake ca 1667 – ? married 1st 1689 William Evans married 2nd bef. 1692 Thomas Pierce
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From < [https://www.scribd.com/doc/31681229/Moore-Williams “MOORE-(WILLIAMS) EXCERPT”] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT >George Moore probably lived in England briefly—perhaps first pursuing an education and then on family business interests.  On 29 July 1650, when he was only 18, he and his future father-in-law Charles Barcroft were on the headrig
2 CONC ht list of John Munger (Nugent, I, 191). As noted above in the material on Barcroft, Moore and his '''purported brother-in-law Richard Williams''' witnessed the assignment of Barcroft’s effects in 1654 to his third wife Magdalen a
2 CONC nd son William, probably a year or so before his marriage to Barcroft’s daughter Jane. On 25 September 1663, George Moore was a headright, along with several Blackwater people, including Ann Wombwell and Joseph and Thomas Poole, o
2 CONC f John Harvey who was patenting along the Carolina frontier (Nugent, I, 191, 427). Joseph Poole is noted above as the second husband of Moore’s purported aunt, '''Mrs. Elizabeth Moore Champion Poole Walton'''.  John Harvey was the
2 CONC  son-in-law of James Tooke whose will was witnessed by Thomas Carter, # 8, on 1 February 1659. Concerning the Harvey-Tooke connection, see William Carter, # 2, the note at “ca. 1625/29. A settled career in Isle of Wight probably b
2 CONC egan for George Moore when his '''purported brother-in-law Robert Flake''' conveyed to George Moore land at Blackwater from Flake’s 2,700-acre patent on 20 August 1666 (Boddie, Seventeenth Century, p. 558). Flake and wife Katherin
2 CONC e deeded George Moore additional land on 18 October 1669 (Isle of Wight Wills and Deeds, 1662-1715, Vol. I, p. 201).  Neither the amounts of land nor any consideration are mentioned. Robert Flake and George Moore were the bondsmen
2 CONC  for '''Mary Skinner, daughter of Katherine Flake by her first husband, name unknown,''' as administratrix for Mary’s husband Richard Skinner on 9 April 1677 (Chapman, Wills, p. 104). George Moore had already added to his holdings
2 CONC  in 1669 when he patented 1,400 acres on the “2d Swamp” of the Blackwater adj. Captain Wombwell and the Beaver Dam Branch, from whence came part of the plantation of son-in-law his Thomas Carter; one of his headrights was John Col
2 CONC lins who became the third husband of the aforementioned Mary Skinner, evidently George Moore’s niece.  See Nugent, Vol. 2, p. 57.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://sallysfamilyplace.com/maple-lawn/george-moore-jane-barcroft/
2 CONT
2 CONT >George Moore (ca 1634 – 1714)  |his parents/ & Jane Barcroft (ca 1641 – ), daughter of Charles Barcroft  (ca 1610 – 1666) & Maudlin [relict]  of Isle of Wight County, Virginia. George Moore married Jane, daughter of Charles Barcr
2 CONC oft.  This George Moore was the brother of Thomas Moore 1643 – 1696 married ca 1665 Elizabeth [widow of Samuel Eldridge]. They probably also had a sister.    From Dr. Barry Hayes.   “The circumstantial evidence is strong that Mrs.
2 CONC  '''Priscilla Champion''' was…. a sister of the proved brothers a.'''Thomas Moore''' and b. '''George Moore'''…… e. –?– '''Moore''' and his wife ''Mrs. Anne Rogers Moore Baron Matthews Davis'', whose only Moore son was yet another
2 CONC  John Moore, f. '''Elizabeth Moore''' who married 1st Thomas Barlow and 2nd William Baldwin, and g. '''Katherine Moore''' who married 1st unknown and 2nd '''Robert Flake'''.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
