1 NAME Matthew /Rodham/
2 GIVN Matthew
2 SURN Rodham
2 _MARNM Rodham
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 SEP 1620
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 MAR 1672
2 PLAC Chiacone
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Some believe the parents of Matthew Rodham are Edmund and Margaret (Grey) Rodham. More evidence needs to be found. If these are Matthew's parents, he has older brothers Ralph (d. 1615), John, Edward, and Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodham came to America with a group of men who were servants c. 1634, '35, or '36 on the ships James and Revenge. He worked as a servant for about 5 years. It was recorded on 28 Oct. 1639 that Matthew had served his full time for 
2 CONC William Clobery & Company of London, England, Merchants. Part of his time as a servant was spent with the Hale family.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1648[3], he married Elizabeth Hewitt in either Northumberland, Virginia or Kent Island, Maryland, and the couple had four [sic: five] daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # - Hannah Rodham m. Christopher Neale
2 CONT # - Elizabeth Rodham m. Richard Kenner
2 CONT # - Susannah Rodham m. Robert Mason
2 CONT # - Mary Rodham m. Richard Rice
2 CONT # - Sarah Rodham m. Claudius Tullos
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the offices of Commissioner, Juror, Justice, and Vestryman.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1663, he had acquired 393 acres of land from Hugh Lee[5].
2 CONT
2 CONT His date of death is alternately given as 1665 or 20 March 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1674-1677 Northumberland County, Virginia Order Book, Part 3; [Antient Press]; Page 219
2 CONT * Northumberland County Court 3d of February 1674/5
2 CONT * - Probate Mr. RHODUM's Will
2 CONT * Upon ye Petition of Mr. ROBERT MASON, Executor of the Will of MRS. ELIZABETH RHODUM, ye Executrix of Mr. MATTHEW RHODUM deceased, a Probate of the Will of ELIZABETH RHODUM is granted Mr. ROBERT MASON ye Will being proved by the 
2 CONC Oaths of MORGAN LEWIS and JOHN WILLIAMS, wittness to the Will
2 CONT
2 CONT
