1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John FOXALL and Martha BUTLER had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 i. Mary FOXHALL.  Mary Foxhall had 5 husbands: abt 1672 Robert Vaulx, bef 26 Nov 1686 Alexander Gorges, bef June 1688 Edward Duddleston, bef Feb 1697 Caleb Butler, and aft 19 Dec 1711 John Bagg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Mary FOXHALL was born in 1665 in ENGL. She signed a will before 27 Aug 1713. Mary's will was proved 27 Aug 1713. She died before 27 Aug 1713. Mary and Caleb had a daughter, Jane, who married Augustine Washington and had a son, 
2 CONC Lawrence, half-brother to George Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Caleb BUTLER before Feb 1697 in WestmorelandCo, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb BUTLER signed a will on 16 Feb 1708/9 in WestmorelandCo, VA. BUTLER, CALEB, 16 February 1708-9; 25 May 1709. 3 negroes to wife Mary; daughter Jane 6 negroes; son in law Robert Vaulx and his deceased Uncle John Foxhall 5000 l
2 CONC bs. tobacco, 1 negro, furniture etc; Sarah Elliott daughter of Sarah Elliott and her deceased uncle John Foxhall ?30 Sterling; son in law James Vaulx gun, sword, and 5000 lbs. of tobacco; my sister Ann wife of Joseph Bayley ?25 St
2 CONC erling; to Thomas Robins clothing; to Mary daughter of John Butler deceased 3000 lbs. tobacco; to Thomas Clayton Sr. tobacco he owes me; to Thomas Boyleston tobacco he owes me; sister Sarah Elliott, widow, debt to me; to Jenny wif
2 CONC e of Thomas Shaw 1000 lbs. tobacco; to Elizabeth wife of Captain Richard Craddock ?12 Sterling; friend James Taylor one mourning ring
2 CONT
2 CONT He died after 16 Feb 1708/9. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary FOXHALL and Caleb BUTLER had the following children:
2 CONT * +5i.Jane BUTLER.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Robert Vaulx about 1681 in WestmorelandCo, VA. Robert Vaulx was born in 1651 in CumberlandCo (of), ENGL. He obtained a land grant on 9 Jun 1665 in Half of 6,000 A., WestmorelandCo, VA. William Gooch and Robert V
2 CONC aulx were granted 6,000 A. of land in WestmorelandCo. "on the South Side of Potomack River behind Cliffs of Corowoman in the Woods beginning on the Westward Side of a great deep runn being the head of great Rapppahannock Creek" fo
2 CONC r the transportation of 120 persons.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1657 [sic], Robert Vaulx was granted another 2,000 A. in the same County. He served as a Justice in 1679 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He died before 27 May 1685 in WestmorelandCo, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Alexander Gorges before 20 Nov 1686 in WestmorelandCo, VA. Alexander Gorges died before Jul 1688 in WestmorelandCo, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Edward Duddleston before Jul 1688 in WestmorelandCo, VA. Edward Duddleston died before Feb 1697 in WestmorelandCo, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Rev. John BAGG after 19 Dec 1711.
2 CONT ===========
2 CONT Mary Foxhall (John Foxhall, Ambrose Foxhall) was born ABT 1667 in England, and died BEF 5 Sep 1713 in Westmoreland Co. VA. She married Caleb Butler. He was born ABT 1665. She married Alexander Gorges. She married Edward Duddleston
2 CONC e. She married John Bagge. She married Robert Vaulx, son of Robert Vaulx and Elizabeth Burwell. He was born 1651, and died 1685 in Westmoreland Co. VA.
2 CONT  	  Child of Mary Foxhall and Caleb Butler is:
2 CONT * +	6	  i.	Jane Butler was born 14 Oct 1699 in Westmoreland Co. VA, and died 24 Nov 1729 in Bridges Creek, Washington Pa. Westmoreland Co. VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Mary Foxhall and Edward Duddlestone is:
2 CONT *  	7	  i.	John Duddlestone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Mary Foxhall and Robert Vaulx is:
2 CONT * +	8	  i.	Robert Vaulx died 1721 .======================
2 CONT The article appeared in the Virginia Historical Magazine, Vol. 44. 1936. Mary Foxhall had 5 husbands: abt 1672 Robert Vaulx, bef 26 Nov 1686 Alexander Gorges, bef June 1688 Edward Duddleston, bef Feb 1697 Caleb Butler, and aft 19 
2 CONC Dec 1711 John Bagg.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Jane BUTLER was buried in Nov 1728 in Washington family vault, Bridges Creek, WestmorelandCo, VA. She died on 24 Nov 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT SECOND GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Caleb BUTLER signed a will on 16 Feb 1708/9 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He died after 16 Feb 1708/9. He was married to Mary FOXHALL before Feb 1697 in WestmorelandCo, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mary FOXHALL was born about 1656 in ENGL. She signed a will before 27 Aug 1713. She died before 27 Aug 1713. Caleb BUTLER and Mary FOXHALL had the following children:
2 CONT * 1 i. Jane BUTLER.
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. John FOXALL was born in 1633 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He was christened on 9 Jun 1633 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He immigrated on 27 Jul 1665 to MD. He obtained a land grant on 20 Oct 1666 in St. Mary'sCo,
2 CONC  MD (Province of). He was a Merchant, WestmorelandCo, VA from 1667 to 1686 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He purchased land after 1667 in E. of Montross, Westmoreland, VA. He sold land on 10 Oct 1667 in St. Mary'sCo, MD (Province of). He 
2 CONC obtained a land patent on 31 Dec 1667 in Oak Grove, Westmoreland, VA. He gave a power of attorney on 23 Dec 1668 in Pope's Creek, WestmorelandCo, VA. He leased Maj. William Underwood's mill for 99 years in 1670 in WestmorelandCo, 
2 CONC VA. He made an apology to the County Commissioners on 1 Nov 1670 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He sent an adventure in 1675 to New England. He obtained a land grant before 10 Jan 1677 in S. of R. Hill patents, WestmorelandCo, VA. He serv
2 CONC ed on a jury on 14 Jun 1682 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He signed a will on 10 Feb 1697 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He died after 10 Feb 1697. He had an estate probated on 30 Mar 1698 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He was married to Martha BUTLER a
2 CONC bout 1660 in ENGL.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Martha BUTLER was born about 1645 in ENGL. She gave Small black stone horse to daughter Mary ffoxhall on 9 May 1673 in Pope's Creek, WestmorelandCo, VA. She died in WestmorelandCo, VA. John FOXALL and Martha BUTLER had the foll
2 CONC owing children:
2 CONT * 3 i. Mary FOXHALL.
2 CONT *  ii. Sarah FOXHALL was born in 1665 in America. She was sued in Aug 1711 in WestmorelandCo, VA. She signed a will on 26 Jul 1739 in WestmorelandCo, VA. She died after 26 Jul 1739 in WestmorelandCo, VA.
2 CONT *  iii. John FOXALL was born about 1675 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He was a Planter in 1696/97 in Pope's Creek, WestmorelandCo, VA. He signed a will on 10 Feb 1697 in Washington Parish, Westmoreland, VA. He had an estate probated on 3
2 CONC 0 Mar 1698 in WestmorelandCo, VA. He died betw feb 1697-March 1698 in VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOURTH GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Ambrose FOXALL was born before 1613 in Birmingham (of), Warwick, ENGL. He was a Tanner from 1640 to 1670 in Birmingham, Warwick, VA. He signed a will on 26 Oct 1668 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He died in 1670 in ENGL. He was
2 CONC  married to Mary WILSON on 26 Jan 1630 in St. Mary, Stafford, ENGL.
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. Mary WILSON was born about 1605 in St. Mary, Stafford, ENGL. She signed a will on 13 Nov 1685 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. She died in 1686 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. Ambrose FOXALL and Mary WILSON had the following childr
2 CONC en:
2 CONT *  i. Elizabeth FOXALL was born about Apr 1631 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. She was christened on 10 Apr 1631 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL.
2 CONT * 6 ii. John FOXALL.
2 CONT *  iii. Ambrose FOXALL was born about Jan 1636/37 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He was christened on 8 Jan 1636/37 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL.
2 CONT *  iv. Mary FOXALL.
2 CONT *  v. Abraham FOXALL was born about Mar 1642 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He was christened on 3 Apr 1642 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He signed a will on 21 Dec 1671 in Dublin, IREL. He died after 21 Dec 1671.
2 CONT *  vi. Sarah FOXALL was born about Oct 1644 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. She was christened on 10 Oct 1644 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL.
2 CONT *  vii. Deborah FOXALL was born about Nov 1645 in Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. She was christened on 30 Nov 1645 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL.
2 CONT *  viii. Hannah FOXALL.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIFTH GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. John FOXALL was born about 1585. He died in Mar 1637 in ENGL. He was buried on 25 Mar 1637 in St. Martin's, Birmingham, Warwick, ENGL. He was married to Margaret ? on 16 Nov 1609 in Worfield, Shropshire, ENGL.
2 CONT
2 CONT 25. Margaret ?. John FOXALL and Margaret ? had the following children:
2 CONT *  i. William FOXALL was born before 1611. He signed a will on 6 Oct 1653 in Stafford, Stafford, ENGL. He died after 6 Oct 1653 in Stafford, Stafford, ENGL.
2 CONT * 12 ii. Ambrose FOXALL.
2 CONT *  iii. John FOXALL signed a will on 2 May 1655 in Hardwick. Lattingham, Stafford, ENGL. He died after 2 May 1655 in StaffordCo, ENGL.
2 CONT *  iv. Bridgett FOXALL was living in 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT 26. ____ WILSON. ____ WILSON had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 i. Mary WILSON.
2 CONT *  ii. Elizabeth WILSON died after 1653.
2 CONT *  iii. John WILSON.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
