1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married 1) Richard Cradock 2) Daniel Porten 3) George Eskridge 
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, Rebecca, he married Elizabeth Vaulx, (1700-1744) (daughter of Robert Vaulx and Mary Foxal) in 1716. They had one daughter, Elizabeth Eskridge, born in 1717 in Sandy Point, Westmoreland Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT Wills of Westmoreland County, Virginia , Page 118
2 CONT Note: ESKRIDGE, ELIZABETH, 20 Oct. 1744; 27 Nov. 1744.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Widow of George Eskridge.) To Craddock Butler 1 negro etc.; dau. Elizabeth Aylett; Goddau. Judith Newton 1 negro girl; to Mary Luck 900 lbs. of tobacco; exx. dau. Elizabeth Aylett; widow rest of estate; Mrs. Bray her bed
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I023817&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hello: Based on the information found in records such as Vaulx-35 (will of James Vaulx, brother of Elizabeth Vaulx of this profile, in which he names his sister and her first husband Richard Craddock) and the marriage records of 
2 CONC Virginia, U.S., Marriages of the Northern Neck of Virginia, U.S., 1649-1800 for Elizabeth Vaulx and Richard Craddock, it seems that Elizabeth should be connected as a daughter of Robert Vaulx (Vaulx-34) and Mary Foxhall Vaulx. As 
2 CONC well, her date of birth is closer to 1680, (as given in some records) and this would fit the ages of her first two husbands (otherwise she was considerably older than they were) and also the births of her children (1714 and 1716) 
2 CONC would also fit her being a younger woman at the time of their birth. What do you think?
