1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1. Rebecca Willoughby, emigrated to Rappahannock, Virginia, with her father, Henry Willoughby, in  1675-76, mar. (2) Richard Hull, of the Potomac River, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # Sarah HULL b: 18 DEC 1680 in Richmond Co, VA married 1) Henry Brereton 2) William Woodbridge
2 CONT # Mary HULL b: 12 DEC 1682
2 CONT # Richard HULL b: 14 APR 1685. Married ?? Gaskins " !17 Jun 1713: Thomas Gaskins executed a gift deed to his granddaughter, Sarah Hull, daughter of Richard Hull."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT >21 Dec 1686: WILLOUGHBY, HENRY, Gent., 28th day of Per, 1685; 21 December, 1686. All my lands in Virginia to my daughter Rebecca Hull during her life and after her decease to my two grandaughters Sarah and Mary Hull. The rest of 
2 CONC my estate I give to my daughter Rebecca Hull whom I make executrix of this my will. No witnesses. Decemr: 21st. 1686. Mr Charles Harris & Edward Nelbett did in Court upon Oath declare that Mr: Henry Willoughby did in their hearing
2 CONC  owne that this was his Will & Testamt. & died before he could signe the same. Vera Copia Test Tho : Hobson Jun Cl Cur North Test Wm COLSTON CL Cur. William Montgomery Sweeny, Wills of Old Rappahannock County, Virginia, p. 76.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT *Burke, John (1831), A General and Heraldic Dictionary of the Peerage of England, Ireland and Scotland, London: Henry Colburn and Richard Bentley.[https://archive.org/stream/ageneralandhera02burkgoog#page/n591/mode/2up link]
2 CONT * "Willoughby of Parham, Baron (E, 1547 - 1779)". Cracroft's Peerage. [http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/willoughbyp1547.htm link]
2 CONT * http://www.europeanheraldry.org/united-kingdom/families/families-s-z/house-willoughby/
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=thamm&id=I188886
