1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Hull was born ABT 1644, and died BEF 1696. He was the son of John Hull and Anne Webb. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT # Rebecca WILLOUGHBY, daughter of Henry WILLOUGHBY. She was born ABT 1650. "Rebecca Willoughby, mar. (2) Richard Hull, of the Potomac River, Virginia". She and her father emigrated to Virginia about 1675
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT #  Sarah HULL b: 18 DEC 1680 in Richmond Co, VA
2 CONT #  Mary HULL b: 12 DEC 1682
2 CONT #  Richard HULL b: 14 APR 1685.  Married ?? Gaskins " !17 Jun 1713: Thomas Gaskins executed a gift deed to his granddaughter, Sarah Hull, daughter of Richard Hull."
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Beverley Fleet, Virginia Colonial Abstracts, p. 550.
2 CONT >!4 May 1667: Will of John Hull of Fairfields par. dated 4 May 1667, date of probate not shown. Dau. Maryann Hull. Dau. Anne Hull. Son Thos Hull under 17. Wife Anne Hull. My two sons Richd and John Hull. Wit: Wm Griffin, Robt Webb
2 CONC . Codicil 16 Apr 1668. His son John is dead. Wife with child. Wit: Joseph Dowlen, Joane Dewell. 16.97. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~bush22031/chapter1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >Elizabeth Gaskins Hull, whose husband was Col. Richard Hull (m. Mar. 1738-9). The Hull family arrived in Virginia in the mid-1600s and settled (probably) on Hull Creek in St. Stephen's Parish on the Northumberland County bank of 
2 CONC the Potomac. The father of Col. Richard Hull, also named Richard, had married a daughter of Thomas III.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
