2 CONT
2 CONT ===will===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1656-1692 Old Rappahannock County, Virginia Will Book; [William Montgomery Sweeny]
2 CONT * 15 February, 1682; 4 March, 1684/5.
2 CONT * EDRINGTON, (or ETHERINGTON), MARGARET, widow, of the Parish of Sittingburne.
2 CONT * To my three sons John Jennings, William Jennings and Christopher Edrington all my hogs sheep and household goods to be equally divided according to quantity and quality.
2 CONT * To sons William Jennings and Christopher Edrington all my mares & homes to be equally divided between them. To son Christopher Edrington all my cattle and if either of my sons William or Christopher die that all that I give shou
2 CONC ld goe to either of them. It is my will that my sons should be of age at sixteen.
2 CONT * Wit. FFRAN: STONE, ELIZ. X STONE. Page 43
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills of Old Rappahannock County, Virginia [William Montgomery Sweeny]
2 CONT 15 February, 1682; 4 March, 1684/5.
2 CONT
2 CONT EDRINGTON, (or ETHERINGTON), MARGARET, widow, of the Parish of Sittingbourne
2 CONT
2 CONT To my three sons John Jennings, William Jennings and Christopher Edrington all my hogs sheep and household goods to be equally divided according to quantity and quality. To sons William Jennings and Christopher Edrington all my ma
2 CONC res & homes to be equally divided between them. To son Christopher Edrington all my cattle and if either of my sons William or Christopher die that all that I give should goe to either of them. It is my will that my sons should be
2 CONC  of age at sixteen.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT BEE IT KNOWNE UNTO ALL MEN by these prsents that I MARGARET JENNINGS of the County of Rappa, and Prish of Sittingbourne Widdow Relict & Executrix of my late deced Husband JOHN JENNINGS doe hereby give graunt & confirme & by these 
2 CONC psents doth bind & make over from me my heires and successors parte of my Estate of the wch my aforesd Husband JOHN JENNINGS did make me Executrix unto sevrll. of our children as therein specified Imprs. I give unto my Eldest Sonn
2 CONC  JNO. JENNINGS the first mare fold that falleth of Either of my mares next and immediately after she doth hereof with all the Increase both male & female to him & his heires for Ever 2dly I give unto my Daughter GRACE JENNINGS the
2 CONC  next or second mare fold that falleth of Either of my mares with the female increase thereof until the said GRACE JENNINGS shall be full twelve yeares of age and after shee shall have all the Increase male & female for Ever to he
2 CONC r & her heirs for Ever. 3dly I give unto my Daughter JEAN JENNINGS the third mare fold of either of my mares with the increase thereof until my said Daughter GRACE is twelve years of age & after the male & female increase to her &
2 CONC  her heires for ever 4thly I also give my younger Sonn WM, JENNINGS the fourth mare fold that falleth of either of my mares wth the female Increase thereof to him & his heirs forever (then entry becomes too faded but JNO. JENNINGS
2 CONC  appears to be given foure Sows & four barrows to be delivered to him when he reaches the age of Sixteene; the same given to her younger son WM. JENNINGS at his being sixteene years of age; also provision is made if either of her 
2 CONC sons dyes before they reach the age of sizteene yeares as well as her two Daughters and if the said MARGARET shall joyne in Marriage before each of her children JNO., GRACE. JEAN or WILLIAM JENNINGS shall be sizteene yeares of age
2 CONC  then my children shall have mayntenance thereof the rest of my Estate until! they shall be each Sixteen yeares of age) â As Witness my hand and seale this 18th day of 8br 1670
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
