2 CONC hannock River and GEN: the Potomac River. Her death occured between the date of her will in l5 of Feb GEN: 1682 and the court action on it on the 4 Mar 1684/5. The introduction of her GEN: will in 1682 is also the source indicatin
2 CONC g the death of her husband, GEN: Christopher Edrington. GEN: Margaret remarried after John's death in l670. She married Christopher GEN: Edrington and bore him one child, also named Christopher. His death date is not GEN: known bu
