1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=kmcmahan&id=I14210 ID: I14210 View Post-em!  •Name: William (parent theory) Thacker  •Sex: M  •Change Date: 18 FEB 2012  •Birth: ABT 1690 in England 1 2  •D
2 CONC eath: 1767/1768 in Hanover Co., VA 1  •Occupation: Military Colonel 3  •Note:  Virginia Bannister refers to PASSENGER AND IMMIGRATION LISTS INDEX by Filby & Meyer as her source for the immigration of William Thacker to Virginia in
2 CONC  1714. Bannister refers to page 341 of the RECONSTRUCTED VIRGINIA 1760 CENSUS, published by T.L.C. Genealogy, as her source for William Thacker being recorded in the 1760 census of Hanover Co., VA. Bannister gives THE VESTRY BOOK 
2 CONC OF ST. PAUL'S PARISH, Hanover County, Virginia 1706-1786, transcribed and edited by C.F. Chamberlayne (1940), as her source for the death of William Thacker in 1767 or 1768 at Hanover Co., VA. However, I don't see any evidence pro
2 CONC vided by Bannister that the subject William Thacker had sons Benjamin, Pettis, William, Reuben, Nathaniel, John, and Joel, as she proposes. Linda Klave has that William Thacker has also been found in 1700's records in the Virginia
2 CONC  counties of New Kent, Louisa, and Hanover, but she gives no sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mahey has the subject William Thacker as b. ABT 1690 in England as a son of John Thacker and as the father of only sons John, Benjamin, William, Nathaniel & Joseph Thacker. Mahey is my only source placing Joseph as a son of W
2 CONC illiam.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/237185177/william-thacker
2 CONT
2 CONT I suspect that the placement of the children of the subject William Thacker is based on speculation without any solid evidence that connects them. There may well have been more than one William Thacker if that name was found in mo
2 CONC re than one county during the same period. For example, my correspondent Clarence Coley saw a transcription of a Louisa Co. court order ABOUT 1763 that ordered churchwardens to bind out William Thacker's sons, Benjamin and Joel. C
2 CONC larence speculated that the sons were POSSIBLY under age orphans and, IF SO, could not have included Benjamin Thacker Sr. b. ABT 1720 in my database. So, I am tentatively making the connections to the children of William Thacker i
2 CONC n my database as theoretical.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarence said he also found a William Thacker Jr. with a Louisa Co. land patent (or grant) ABOUT 1760 for 400 acres on branches of Roundabout Creek. No record for a William Thacker SR. has been found there yet. Clarence also found
2 CONC  a 1764 Louisa Co. land sale of 400 acres on Roundabout Creek from William Thacker (no Jr. or Sr.) and wife Mary to John Thacker. Clarence then found a William Thacker in 1771 Hanover Co. who was given merchandise from John Thacke
2 CONC r in Louisa Co., and this gift was witnessed by a Mary Thacker. Clarence wonders COULD they be the same William Thacker. Clarence notes that IF they were William Thacker of the ABOUT 1763 Louisa Co. court order, then he was still 
2 CONC alive in 1764 and his children could NOT have been orphans and MAY have been bound out for another reason.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John Thacker b: 1613 in Arundel, Sussex, England
2 CONT
