1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lengthy family history at [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=63341134 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah's maiden name is unknown, but she married Barnabus Wilcox in 1665/6 in Bristol, England. She, Barnabus and their five children were members of The Society of Friends, and emigrated to America in 1683. They settled in Philade
2 CONC lphia and had one more child.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnabas and family came to North America in 1683, and settling at Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. There he was a merchant, and a member of the Colonial Assembly of 1685. He later became a Justice of the Peace (1686-1690).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnabas and Sarah had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Wilcox, 1667 - 1694
2 CONT # Joseph Wilcox, 1669 - 1721
2 CONT # Esther Wilcox, 1673- 1724
2 CONT # Hannah Wilcox, 1679 - 1710; she married John Rhodes
2 CONT # Abigail Wilcox, 1679 - 1713; she married Samuel Powell
2 CONT # Ruth Wilcox, 1681 - 1681
2 CONT # Rachel Wilcox, 1685 - 1760; she married Elisha Gatchell
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT April 20, 1692. September 30, 1692. A. 216. Being the sole Administratrix of my deceased husband, Barnabas Willcox - estate to children George and Joseph, who are the Executors, daughter Rachell the youngest child, Hester, Hanah a
2 CONC nd Abigall. Willm. Clayton is mentioned in connection with a mill property. Overseers: John Bristoe of Chester, Paul Sanders of Schoolkill. Witnesses: Paul Sanders, John Roades, James Fapell.
