1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-2079
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT 30th day of 6th month 1660, (old style) Ripley, Derbyshire, England as reported at the Chesterfield Monthly Meeting of the Society of Friends [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 4th day Ninth month (November) 1691 Adam Roads and Katherin Blunston registered their marriage intention at the Darby Monthly Meeting. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Residencies and other events
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1687 Adam Roades was one of those selected for jury duty in a Chester County court case involving one Thomas Colborne who was bound over by the last Court for "Selling ye Indians Rum...". [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1689 "'Adam Roades'" was again called for jury duty for the Chester County courts. [3] This case may have involved a debt issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the twenty-fifth day of March 1696 John Bunstone, Attorney for John Roads acknowledged a deed to Adam Roads for one hundred acres of land lying in Darby [Chester County] the deed bearing the date 25 March 1696.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 March 1745, Darby, Chester County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Rhodes (Rodes, Rhoads) of Winegreaves, Derbyshire, England, and Elizabeth his wife, had children, Adam, b. 1660, Mary, John, Elizabeth, Jacob, Abraham, Sarah, Hannah and Joseph. Of these Adam and John came to Pennsylvania in 
2 CONC 1684, and the father, with Jacob and Joseph, some years later (about 1665).
