1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT ''Last updated 8 August 2025''
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-7648 and then edited 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Rhodes''' was the daughter of John Rhodes/Roades (d. 1701) and his wife Elizabeth, [NOT Elizabeth Jessop] born on 30 Jan 1662 in Derbyshire, England, and died the “6th day of the twelveth mo.” (February) 1706 at the family
2 CONC  residence in Spring Mill, Whitemarsh, Philadelphia (now Montgomery) County, Pennsylvania. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT She followed the Quaker faith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Rhodes or Roades first married on the 9th day of the 9th month [November] 1689 in Chesterfield, Nottinghamshire, England to William Maltby or Maulsby of Orston, Nottinghamshire, England. [2] The distance between Orston and Ri
2 CONC pley is about 34 USA miles (55km). Between the two is the town of Nottingham, County Nottinghamshire a large area inhabited by many Quakers and where they conducted their Monthly Meetings.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1698 William and Mary Maltby emigrated from Nottinghamshire, England alledgedly on the ship "Bristol Merchant" because their son Merchant was born at sea as recorded in the Philadelphia Arch Street Monthly Meeting. [3] Their ne
2 CONC xt and final child, David, was born in 1699/1700 in Philadelphia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary second married David Rhys Williams on 30 Jan 1704 at the Philadelphia Meeting House.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died at the family residence in Spring Mill, Whitemarsh, Philadelphia County (now Montgomery), Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary and William Maulsby had the following children:
2 CONT * John Roades Maulsby Sr, 1690 – 1758, m. Mary Anthony
2 CONT * Mary Maulsby, 1692 – 
2 CONT * Elizabeth Maulsby, 1694 – 1759, m. Rees Williams
2 CONT * William Maulsby Jr, 1695 – 1779, m. Rose Rees
2 CONT * Merchant Maulsby, 1698 – 1785, m. Elizabeth Parker
2 CONT * David Maulsby, 1699 – 1764, m. Mary Laugharne
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary and David Williams had one son:
2 CONT * Joseph Williams, 1705-1755, m. Sarah Griffith
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Rhodes (Rodes, Rhoads) of Winegreaves, Derbyshire, England, and Elizabeth his wife, had children, Adam, b. 1660, Mary, John, Elizabeth, Jacob, Abraham, Sarah, Hannah and Joseph. Of these Adam and John came to Pennsylvania in 
2 CONC 1684, and the father, with Jacob and Joseph, some years later (about 1665).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
