2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Mary (Rhodes) Williams (1662-1709)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-7648 : accessed 08 August 2025). Cites 
2 CONT ##England and Wales Non-Conformist Record Indexes 1588-1977 on FamilySearch.org citing RG#6; Public Record Office in London, England; Nottinghamshire Monthly Meeting; p38; for Mary Rhodes, b: 30 Jan 1662 Chesterfield, Derbyshire, 
2 CONC England; father: john Rhodes; Text: "Mary. daughter of John and Elizabeth Rhodes was born on the 30th day of the 11th month (January) 1662"
2 CONT ## England & Wales, Quaker Birth, Marriage and Death Registers 1578-1837 on ancestry.com compiled by Society of Friends:c iting Derbyshire, Nottinghamshire, England; Chesterfield Monthly Meeting; reg#1381; Marriages from 1669-1760
2 CONC ; Births from 1669-1765; piece#1487; Marriage Intention, Text: "Upon the 13th day of the 4th month [July] 1689 at our monthly meeting at _____ house, William Maltbe of Orston in the County of Nottingham and Mary Roades of Ripley i
2 CONC n the County of Darboy [Derby] tho having in good order declared their intention and we have unity with them ..."; witnesses: John Roades, Will Wooley, Will Day, Luke Rank, Thomas Witbe, Edward Dawes, John Dawes, Phillip Taylor, M
2 CONC artha _____, Dorothy ______; Sarah Taylor, Eliz. Dennis, Marg Farquor(?) ...; & Marriage, Text: "William Maltby of Ors[t]on, County Nottingham and Mary Roades of Ripley in the County of Darby were married on the 9th day of the 9th
2 CONC  month [November] 1689"
2 CONT ## "An Abstract of the Record of Births of Philadelphia Monthly Meeting 1688-1826" by Spencer Bonsall; on ancestry.com citing Historical Society of Pennsylvania; transcribed by Gilbert Cope; Philadelphia MM birth register; p68; Ma
2 CONC ry & William Maltby of Eastwood, Nottinghamshire, England had childrens' births registered at Philadelphia (Arch Street) MM
2 CONT ##Philadelphia Monthly Meeting, Births, Deaths and Burials 1688-1826 on ancestry.com citing "U.S. Quaker Meeting Records 1681-1935: "An Abstract of the Record of Births, Deaths and Burials of Philadelphia Monthly Meeting 1688-1826
2 CONC ; for husband, William Maulsby
2 CONT ##Will of her husband dated 5th of November 1699; image attached here; which mentioned that he expected his beloved wife Mary, to care for their children; and asked that her brother, Adam Rhodes, "to be an Assistant" to Mary as so
2 CONC le Executrix; additionally, her brother, John Rhodes, attorney, wrote his name in the witness section; estate appraisers: Richard Roades with William Philpot
2 CONT ## "Quaker Arrivals at Philadelphia 1682-1750: Being a List of Certificates of Removal Received at ..." compiled by Albert Cook Myers; Ferris & Leach (1902); citing p35-6; Certificate of Removal on 29th day 10th mo. (Dec) 1704 Hav
2 CONC erford MM for "David William (widower) who is to marry the widow, Mary Malsby of Philadelphia, on the 11th day 11th month (January) 1704 at the [Arch St.} Philadelphia Monthly Meeting
2 CONT ##Find A Grave: Memorial #140875594 for Mary Williams
2 CONT ## "Chesterfield, Darbyshire MM #379; Marriages 1661-1795; Births 1641-1720; Burials 1659-1700" compilation by Society of Freinds consisting of 10 Books #379-388; Registers not indexed Non-parochial Registers; reprinted; on ancest
2 CONC ry.com "Source text quoted verbatim"
