1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-2084
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, daughter of John and Eizabeth Rhodes was born the 7th day of the 11th (January) month 1667 to parents John Rhodes and Elizabeth Jessop as recorded in the Chesterfield, Derbyshire/Nottingham Monthly Meeting (MM). [1] [2]
2 CONC  Her parents were "of Ripley, Derbyshire, England".
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT As recorded in the Chesterfield [Nottingham/Derbyshire] MM "Elizabeth Rhodes of Eastwood, Nottinghamshire, England married Edward Daws of Graisly, Nottinghamshire on the 14th day of the 5th month (July) 1692." [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT [1696]
2 CONT
2 CONT [She died in 1741, based on a record found for her burial, 24 Mar 1741].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Conflicting death date 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dawes-57
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Dawes was born in 1662, the son of Adrian Dawes and Anna Tirpin. In 1692, Edward married Elizabeth Rhodes who passed away in 1696. Subsequently, Edward married Sarah Kassel/Cassel in 1709. He passed away in 1714. His Death 
2 CONC record has not yet been found, however his Will was proven 13 Dec 1714.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the book referenced below "Descendants of William and Mary Maltby" about the Dawes families, Edward emigrated to Pennsylvania about 1698. In 1709, he married Sarah Cassel, at which time it is believed that Edward was 
2 CONC a widower.
