1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of John Rodes/Rhodes/Roades and Elizabeth, who came to PA with the initial William Penn group.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-2090
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhodes, as a surname, is quite common in Philadelphia and Montgomery counties in the 18th and 19th centuries. For this reason I include this profile in the Norriton project.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT When Jacob Roads was born on 16 February 1670, in Ripley, Derbyshire, England, United Kingdom, his father, John Roades, was 45 and his mother, Elizabeth, was 31. He married Margaret Warner on 26 March 1703, in Darby Monthly Meetin
2 CONC g, Delaware, Pennsylvania, United States. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 3 daughters. He died on 15 October 1740, in Pennsylvania, British Colonial America, at the age of 70.
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LR7Z-JMF/jacob-roads-1670-1740
