1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rhodes-1416 and then edited.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Rhodes was born on 5 Apr 1680 in Ripley, Derbyshire, England to parents John Rhodes and Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Abigail Bonsall on 2 Jul 1702 in Darby, Chester, Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Rebecca, Jane, Joseph, Abigail, Benjamin, Rebecca, John, Mary, Elizabeth, Abigail, James. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 29 Nov 1732 in Marple, Chester, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Business History of J. E. Rhoads and Sons: In 1702 Joseph Rhoads established a tannery on his 100 acre farm in Marple Township, Pennsylvania. Rhoads, who probably learned tanning .in.his.native England, typified the farmer-turned-
2 CONC tanner so prevalent in colonial America. In 1732, Joseph died. His wife, Abigail, operated both the farm and tanyard until 1743 when their youngest son, James, came of age and received:. . .a grant of land containing 65 acres, 52 
2 CONC perches (rods). . . with the buildings, including the tannery, improvements and all rights, privileges and appurtenances involved. . .
2 CONT
2 CONT … Joseph Rhoads married another English Quaker, Abigail Bonsall, in 1702, and founded the tannery the same year. "He cleared a little land, built a vat or two, dug a few pools and started tanning leather for neighboring settlers i
2 CONC n the county," the account reads. "Apparently, it was very successful," Lucas said. But in 1732, Joseph Rhoads died when his oldest son, James, was only 10 years old. He left behind six other children as well. And so his wife (Abi
2 CONC gail) took over the business and ran it for 11 years, until 1743, when James reached the age of 21. "She was one of the premier businesswomen of the country," Lucas said. The tannery stood at Sproul Road (Route 320) and Reed Road.
2 CONC  A fifth Rhoads house once stood on the present-day site of the Don Guanella School, Lucas said. [1]
2 CONT ----
