2 CONT ----
2 CONT George Custer/Kuster was born about 1705, in Germantown, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He was the son of Arnold Kuster and Rebecca Nuzom. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Rhodes, 28 Jun 1731, in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. [1] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT George was killed by Indians, 01 Nov 1755, near the Gap of the Blue Mountians, Northampton County, Pennsylvania. (This area is now Carbon County, Pennsylvania). [1] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Kuster Name Study]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT George Custer/Kuster was born about 1705, in Germantown, Philadelphia,Pennsylvania.  He was the son of [[Kuster-43 | Arnold Kuster]] and [[Nuzom-2 | Rebecca Nuzom]].  <ref name="White">White, Jean M., Editor; [[Space:The_Descendan
2 CONC ts_Of_Paulus_And_Gertrude_Kusters | The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Pennsylvania the first four generations]];  Castor Association of America, Mennonite Press, Newton, Kansa
2 CONC s, 1991; 303 Pages, Indexed; Pages 119-124. </ref> 
2 CONT He married [[Rhodes-1646 | Mary Rhodes]], 28 Jun 1731, in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.  <ref name="White">White, Jean M., Editor; [[Space:The_Descendants_Of_Paulus_And_Gertrude_Kusters | The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kuste
2 CONC rs of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Pennsylvania the first four generations]];  Castor Association of America, Mennonite Press, Newton, Kansas, 1991; 303 Pages, Indexed;  Pages 119-124. </ref>   George was killed by India
2 CONC ns, 01 Nov 1755, near the Gap of the Blue Mountians, Northampton County, Pennsylvania.  (This area is now Carbon County, Pennsylvania).  <ref name="White">White, Jean M., Editor; [[Space:The_Descendants_Of_Paulus_And_Gertrude_Kust
2 CONC ers | The Descendants ofPaulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown,Pennsylvania the first four generations]];  Castor Association of America, Mennonite Press, Newton, Kansas, 1991; 303 Pages, Indexed;  Pa
2 CONC ges 119-124. </ref> 
2 CONT
