1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William is the son of Richard Thomas and Elizabeth Walton of Bucks Co.,PA. He was a Loyalist "Torrey" who lost all his lands etc when the British lost the Revolutionary War. He along with his brothers, Joshua and E
2 CONC van had to flee PA. for New York and adventually settled in Nova Scotia and New Brunswick where the English provided land grants for American lands lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married twice, he was but 19 years of age when he first married the Widow Mary Wilcox (Rhodes) Custer, she being 46 years old. She was the widow of George Custer who was killed by the Indians in the "Gap" in Bucks Co.,PA. 
2 CONC He left also a daughter Martha who along with her mother went to live with a relative in Philadelphia, Thomas Paschall, rather then move to Nova Scotia. William and Mary had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Thomas-George Crosley
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha must have died shortly after 1774 as William married the second time to Elizabeth Waters, whom he married 18 Nov 1775 in Trinity Parish, Digby, Digby, NS. They are parents of eleven children all born in Digby or Clementvill
2 CONC e, Nova Scotia.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Thomas,Capt.-1777
2 CONT James Thomas-Abt 1779
2 CONT Daniel Thomas-Abt 1781
2 CONT William Thomas,Yoeman-Abt 1783
2 CONT Elizabeth "Betsy" Thomas-Abt 1785-Johann George Apt
2 CONT Girl Thomas-Abt 1786
2 CONT Boy Thomas-Abt 1787
2 CONT Robert Thomas-1789
2 CONT Joshua Thomas-1791
2 CONT Joseph Thomas-Abt 1795
2 CONT Evan Thomas-Abt 1797
