1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Beersheba Church Book (p.76):
2 CONT
2 CONT "19. Departed August 19, 1824; buried August 20, 1824. JOSEPH RHOADS, a married man aged 68 years, and about 3 months. He was born in May 1756, day unknown, in Bucks County, Pennsylvania. In the Year 1773 he was married to Rosanna
2 CONC h Edmonds; their married state was blessed with 10 children; 3 sons and 7 daughters; one son and 3 daughters departed this world before him. In the year 1785 he became a member of the Brethrens' Congregation by Holy Baptism, and s
2 CONC hortly after was admitted to Holy Sacrament. In the month of October 1790 he became a widower; on the 16 of May, 1791 he entered the second time into the Holy state of matrimony with the present widow, Catharine Riedy, their marri
2 CONC ed state was blessed with 3 children: 1 son and 2 daughters. One daughter has departed this world before him. In June 1814 he moved with his family to this place.
