1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ribecca Or Rebecca Nuzan, Nuzom Or Nuysom. or maybe Elizabeth Rebecca Sell. Or Sellen. Also has three different listed death dates. I think this is a pretty muddy trail...
2 CONT
2 CONT >",,,Arnold Kuster is believed to have come to America with his parent and married Rebecca. His wife's last name is variously reported as Nuysum, Nuzam, and Schulzer, but there is no known documentation for any of these names." [3
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ~• There is a revealing passage in the <journals> of the Rev. H.M. Mühlenberg of [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011394700&view=1up&seq=622&skin=2021&q1=Jenkin%20Davis Aug.19th. 1784.] She, as wife of the deceased
2 CONC , is termed ''"the grandaughter of the late Superintendant Sproegel"''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known of Rebecca, even her maiden surname is uncertain. Rebecca's birth in Pennsylvania is listed as 1671 which is before Germantown and Philadelphia were settled in 1683.  She might have been born topre-Penn settlers, b
2 CONC ut her place of birth may be wrong.
2 CONT
