1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/pedigree/landscape/LH71-HZX
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21548294/nicholas-custer
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Custer was baptized as an adult on the 12 Feb. 1745 by Henry Melchior Muhlenberg. Also served as an Elder and Deacon in his church. Henry Melchior Muhlenberg gave a detailed eulogy of Nicholas. His remains are buried at t
2 CONC he Augustus Lutheran Church Cemetery beside his wife Susannah in an unmarked grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Paulus joined the congregation just across the Perkiomen: Saint James Episcopal Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is Nicholas' line that gave rise to the Civil War  and Indian Wars figure [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Armstrong_Custer '''George Armstrong Custer''']  
2 CONT
2 CONT ~• possibly: ~• Non-Associator (1779) The term Non-Associators was applied to American colonists who refused to support and sign "military association" charters. They were not affiliated with associators, or would choose instead, 
2 CONC to pay a fine and suffer possible retaliation. (see pg.24-25 of book w/list; url in in <journals> project
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas and the Rev. Dr. Henry Melchior Mühlenberg bid each other farewell > [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011394700&view=1up&seq=562&skin=2021 July 2, 1783 in Trappe] Mühlenberg had baptized Nicholas.
2 CONT Before he died he hosted a grown grandson, son of Johann George Marsteller. See [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011394700&view=1up&seq=598&skin=2021&q1=Jenkin%20Davis March 16th, 1784] in <journals>; by [https://b
2 CONC abel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011394700&view=1up&seq=621&skin=2021&q1=Jenkin%20Davis August 15th, 1784 he is lying ill from "the dropsy"]  ; see also: [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011394700&view=1up&se
2 CONC q=622&skin=2021&q1=Jenkin%20Davis August 19th, 1784] 
2 CONT -------------------- 
