1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Helene was not married to https://www.geni.com/people/Peter-Foster-of-Wendover/6000000016670862342. Peter Foster and her actual spouse, https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Foster-of-Wing/6000000225887903929, along
2 CONC  with her children, https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Foster-of-Wing/6000000225887985900?through=6000000225887903929 and https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Foster-of-Wing/6000000225887985922?through=6000000225887903929 were con
2 CONC flated together.
2 CONT *Not to be confused with https://www.geni.com/people/Ellen-Foster-of-Wendover/6000000225887581997?through=6000000016670862342
2 CONT -Her middle name wasn’t “Newton”. She had no middle name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helene Foster Greenway (often recorded as Helene Greenway) is a documented historical figure from late 16th-century Buckinghamshire, England.
2 CONT However, her biographical details are frequently distorted because online public family trees have accidentally combined her records with those of Ellen, the wife of the Wendover fuller Peter Foster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Factual Biographical Profile
2 CONT Birth: Estimated circa 1556 in the Borough of Wing (Wyng) Buckinghamshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parent Profiles
2 CONT Father: William Greenway (born c. 1526–1528). He was a resident of Buckinghamshire, England, and raised his family in the region surrounding the parish of Wing.
2 CONT Mother: Elnor Birch (born c. 1527–1529). Her surname is sometimes transcribed in early English regional records as "Burch."
2 CONT
2 CONT True Spouse: She married a man named Patrick Foster (not Peter Foster).
2 CONT
2 CONT Documented Children: Her verified children with Patrick Foster include:
2 CONT 1. Agnes Foster (Baptized December 17, 1577)
2 CONT Documented Fact: She is the only child whose primary baptism record is widely preserved and explicitly verified.
2 CONT The Record: The parish register of All Saints Church in Wing, Buckinghamshire reads that Agnes Foster was christened on December 17, 1577, explicitly naming her parents as Patricke Foster and Helene Greenway.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Katherine Foster (Estimated c. 1579–1582)
2 CONT Documented Fact: Regional historical indices and local family reconstructions place Katherine as a younger daughter born into the Wing household.
2 CONT -The Confusion Note: In unverified, crowdsourced databases (like MyHeritage), Katherine is often erroneously merged with Katharen Foster of Wendover (the daughter of Peter and Ellen). Because of this widespread data corruption, ge
2 CONC nealogists treat details regarding Katherine of Wing's exact birth year or adulthood with high caution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Childhood Baptisms: The parish register of Wing, Buckinghamshire explicitly documents the baptisms of their children. For example, a primary entry notes: “Agnes Foster was christened on 17 December 1577, in Wing, Buckinghamshire, 
2 CONC England, as the daughter of Patricke Foster and Helene Greeway”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Residency: Her household was established in Wing, Buckinghamshire, a parish located roughly 13 miles north of the town of Wendover.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: She passed away in 1609 in Wing, Buckinghamshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Verifiable Historical Documentation
2 CONT Unlike the sparse records for the family in Wendover, specific primary church records confirm Helen’s actual family unit in the parish registers of Wing:
2 CONT The Marriage Record: Diocesan records trace the marriage of Patrick Foster and Helene Greenway in Buckinghamshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Internet "Child Theft" Error
2 CONT If you view algorithmic, crowdsourced family trees on platforms like Ancestry or MyHeritage, you will often see up to 8 or 9 children assigned to Patrick and Helen. These typically include Thomas, Richard, Margery, Elizabeth, and 
2 CONC Isabel.This is a significant genealogical error. Those children belonged to Peter and Ellen Foster of Wendover, who lived 13 miles away. Because internet databases combined "Peter" and "Patrick" into a single fictional entity name
2 CONC d "Peter Patrick Foster," the algorithms stripped Peter's children from his 1609 will and pasted them into Patrick and Helen's family profile. No surviving historical records connect those children to the parish of Wing or the Gre
2 CONC enway family.
2 CONT Updated: 06/2026
