2 CONT 	7.	MARTHA TOMPKINS (RALPH) was born about 1636. She deposed 1670 ae about 34 but she was probably older.31  Martha Tompkins may have married Richard Adams after the death of her husband John Foster  A deed dated 16 Nov. 1688 conv
2 CONC eyed land to Martha, relict of John Foster, deceased, my intended wife. Richard’s whole estate to go to Martha provided she has issue with him, if not estate to her children 32 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Foster, among others, was presented to the church for the purpose of receiving  communion in 1667.33 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha is probably the daughter of Ralph's second marriage but this is conjectural.  Ralph's first wife Katherine Foster was living in 1636 but would have been past the child bearing age to have a daughter born 1636 or later. Ralp
2 CONC h's second wife Hannah Aborne may have been a much younger than her husband and  within the child bearing years but again this is conjectural.
2 CONT
2 CONT MARTHA married (1) JOHN FOSTER in 1648 .34  John was born  c1618.35 He died in 1687/1688. John's will was dated 16 Nov. 1687 and proved at Ipswich 14 Mar 1687/88. He left land to sons John, Samuel, David, Joseph, Jonathan & Ebenez
2 CONC er; daughters Mary, Elizabeth & Martha received 4 pounds each to be paid to them by their brothers after the decease of John's wife. The three sisters also to receive 20 shillings apiece seven years after their father's decease.  
2 CONC John's wife received all the movables and stock of the estate to be divided among the children after her decease.  Son David and wife were executors of   the estate.36 
2 CONT
