2 CONT                 PHILIP KNIGHT OF TOPSFIELD MASSACHUSETTS  
2 CONT
2 CONT                           First Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT 	1.	PHILIP KNIGHT was born about 1614.113  He died in 1668 in Topsfield, Essex Co., MA114
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Knight, cooper, came to New England probably from England before 1637 when he resided in Charlestown, MA.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of widow Mary Knight of Wapping Co. Middlesex, England dated 10 Nov. 1644 mentions her mother-in-law Sarah Knight residing in New England, who if she was still living received 20 pounds; her brother Robert Knight residing
2 CONC  in Holland her late husband's wearing apparel excepting sea clothes; her brother Philip Knight her husband's sea clothes and instruments plus 5 pounds.115This may refer to Philip Knight of Salem MA but this is  conjectural. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip Knight was in Lancaster, MA in 1654 when he purchased 20 acres of land from Stephen Day.  He was also granted 20 more acres on the east side of the Penicook River.116 Philip sold this land to John Tinker "being the second l
2 CONC ott from Goodman  Prescotts.117Philip first appears in Charlestown where he was keeper of the ferry in 1651 and called planter and he & wife Margurite were voted a house and barn, and a piece of cow common and marsh meadow which h
2 CONC e sold to  John Cloyes, mariner on 15 Apr 1656.118  Philip then removed to Essex County Massachusetts.      
2 CONT
2 CONT The administration of the estate of Philip Knight of Topsfield, MA was granted on 24 Nov. 1668 to widow Margarey Knight.  The Court ordered to the eldest son (Jonathan) 20li, and 10li each to Philip, Rebecca, Elizabeth and Mary, a
2 CONC t age or upon marriage.119  The widow was bound for the children's portions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT PHILIP married MARGERY. Margery was born about 1621. She died on 18 Apr 1709 in Concord, Middlesex Co., MA.120 Margery married2 THOMAS BATEMAN 27 Jan. 1668 Concord, MA121 Thomas died 6 Feb. 1669 Concord, MA 122  Margery married3 N
2 CONC ATHANIEL BALL  7 Feb. 1670 Concord, MA123 Nathaniel Ball died 14 Jan. 1705/6 Concord, MA.124
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery Knight was admitted to the church in Charlestown 7 (3) 1650125
2 CONT
2 CONT PHILIP and MARGERY had the following children:126
2 CONT
2 CONT +	2	M	i.   JONATHAN KNIGHT was born about 1642 and died in 1683/1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	3	M	ii.   PHILIP Jr. KNIGHT was born about 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	4	F	iii.   REBECCA KNIGHT was born about 1651 and died on 8 Jan 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	5	F	iv.   MARY KNIGHT was born about 1654 and died on 5 Mar 1737/1738.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	6	F	v.     ELIZABETH KNIGHT was born c1655 and died on 6 Nov 1742.
2 CONT
2 CONT                            Second Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT 	2.	JONATHAN KNIGHT (PHILIP) was born about 1642.127 He died in 1683/1684.128
2 CONT
2 CONT Administration of the estate of Jonathan Knight was granted to his widow Ruth in 1685.  The eldest son (Jonathan Jr.) was to receive 11-1/2 acres of land  that Jonathan Sr. had purchased from his brother Philip Jr. Knight ,widow R
2 CONC uth Knight petitioned the estate to allow her to sell various properties and she mentions sons Enos & Ebenezer Knight and their sister Deborah 129
2 CONT
2 CONT JONATHAN married RUTH WRIGHT on 31 Mar 1663. 130Ruth, daughter of  JOHN WRIGHT was born on 23 Apr 1646 in Woburn, MA.131 She died on 17 Oct 1715 in Concord, MA.132  Ruth (Wright) Knight m2 THOMAS BATEMAN Jr.133
2 CONT
