1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isabel Foster was a daughter of Peter and Ellen Foster of Wendover, Buckinghamshire, England, whose historical existence is verified primarily through her father’s probate record.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Factual Documentation (The Primary Source)
2 CONT The single piece of direct historical evidence for Isabel is the last will and testament of her father, Peter Foster, dated April 20, 1609, and proved on July 13, 1609 (Archdeaconry of Buckingham, Wf/18/37A).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Legal Entry: In the text of the will, Peter Foster explicitly names her as "my daughter Isabel Foster".
2 CONT
2 CONT Marital Status in 1609: Because she is legally recorded under her maiden name (Isabel Foster), she was unmarried at the time the will was drafted.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Record Deficit: Her exact burial and baptism dates do not exist because the 1609 Bishop’s Transcripts (and surrounding late-16th-century register pages) for the parish of Wendover are permanently lost or destroyed.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Biographical Details & Timeline Analysis
2 CONT Because primary birth records are missing, her timeline is constructed logically based on her sibling order and her status in 1609:
2 CONT Estimated Birth (c. 1593): Genealogists frequently place her birth year around 1593. This is because she is typically listed as the youngest or one of the youngest daughters in the family tree order, born well after her older sibl
2 CONC ings (like Katheren, who was married and had a child by 1609).
2 CONT
2 CONT Age of Majority Context: If born in 1593, Isabel would have been roughly 16 years old when her father died in 1609, perfectly explaining why she was still living at home and unmarried when the will was finalized.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Tree Discrepancies and "Matches" to Avoid
2 CONT When adding Isabel Foster to your genealogy databases, it is critical to filter out two massive errors that frequently pollute online family trees:
2 CONT The 1616 Ellesborough Marriage Trap: Many automated hints on sites like FamilySearch claim that this Isabel Foster married a man named John Toffield on October 13, 1616, in Ellesborough, Buckinghamshire. While Ellesborough is geog
2 CONC raphically close to Wendover, this is a distinct, unproven match that lacks a documented paper trail linking her back to Peter the fuller.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Parental "Greenway" Myth: As noted with Alice, any record attaching Isabel to parents named "Peter Patricke Foster" and "Helene Newton Greenway" is a fabricated genealogy lineage. Her true mother is documented strictly as Elle
2 CONC n, whose maiden name is unrecorded in primary English sources.
