2 CONT ————————
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN WARD JR., son of JOHN of Terrell, was also a resident of Beaufort and then Pitt counties. His wife was HANNAH, the daughter of JAMES and ELIZABETH SWAIN, his will having been proved in 1762 in Tyrrell and hers after 5 May 177
2 CONC 7 in Martin Co. which was cut off of Tyrrell in 1774. In her will of this 1777 date, she names her daughter, HANNAH WARD, and her grandson, SWAIN
2 CONT
2 CONT The relationship to JOHN WARD, his wife HANNAH and son, SWAIN, is further established by a deed from "JOHN WARD SR. of the county of Pitt to SWAIN WARD for the natural love and affection which JOHN WARD SR. hath and beareth to SWA
2 CONC IN WARD and for the better maintenance of said SWAIN WARD, 400 acres on the S. side of Flat Swamp adj. DENNIS GLISSON." d. 15 Oct. 1797 (D. Bk. 0. pp. 61 and 62)
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN WARD JR., added to his holdings in that area 21 Oct. 1782 when he received from the State of N.C. 500 acres in Pitt Co. on the north side of the Tarr R. and of Grindall's Creek and on the south side of Flat Swamp beginning at
2 CONC  JOSIAH BULLOCK'S line, between said WARD and ARCHIBALD KNOX. (Grant Bk. G p. 155 No. 271).
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct. 11, 1785 WARD added another fifty acres on the N. side of Tarr R. and S. side of Flatt Swamp bounded by WATER (or WALTER) SESSONS at WARD'S and GLISSON'S line. This land was surveyed on the date given above but finally gra
2 CONC nted on 26 Nov. 1793. (Grant Bk. K. p. 338, State of N.C. Grant No. 989)
2 CONT Source: Family - Sutherland - "We cousins" (Virginia to Texas): a genealogy of several of the families comprising the Alabama settlement of Austin's Colony, 1830 and 1831, now Texas, and including the other Virginia lines of the S
2 CONC utherland family - Florence Hudson - Strawberry Point, Iowa: Press-Journal Publishing Company, 1958.
2 CONT vol 2: page 111.
