1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT After William Thompson's death in 1816, the family began to move west. Widow, Charity, was dismissed by letter at Beech Branch in 1834 when the last of the family in Burke moved to Houston County occurred. She apparently went with
2 CONC  them and died before Dec. 1834. Son Anthony M. handled her estate. Newspaper-Houston Co. GA Thurs Dec 4, 1834 "Will be sold before the courthouse doors in said county on the first Tuesday in February next between the legal hours 
2 CONC of sale, all the property belonging to the estate of Charity Thompson, late of said county, deceased. Sold for the benefit of the heirs and creditors of said estate. (Signed) Anthony M. Thompson, Administrator." Note: also one dau
2 CONC ghter drowned as a child, one daughter, Sarah Thompson b. c1784 Burke Co. GA d. 8 Dec. 1871 Screven Co. GA m George Robbins; son, William Thompson Jr.12 Sept. 1788 Burke Co. GA d. 1861 m 2nd 17 Apr 1817 Elizabeth Eiland 
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
