1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Hollingsworth, son of Stephen, received his first land grant 
2 CONT in Duplin County (then New Hanover) in 1741. He married Mary Murrah (Murray) of Duplin County. Henry Hollingsworth was a vestryman of St. Gabriel's Parish, Duplin County. Henry and Mary Hollingsworth had the 
2 CONT following children: 
2 CONT Nancy who married a Mr. Wright; 
2 CONT James who married Betsey Merritt; 
2 CONT Zebulon who married Elizabeth Chesnutt; 
2 CONT Elizabeth who married Alexander Chesnutt; 
2 CONT Mary (1753-1822) who married James Faison; 
2 CONT Charity who married Cannon Faison; 
2 CONT Sarah who married David Chesnutt; 
2 CONT Lydia who married Hardy Carroll; and
2 CONT Henry who married Elizabeth Griggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Maryland
