2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === !MARRIAGE: surety William Arthur !DEED:  ===
2 CONT !MARRIAGE: surety William Arthur !DEED: Assignment of land Barnabus Arthur was by the late will and testament of William Arthur his father deceased seized of land... said Barnabas departed this life intestate leaving William Arthu
2 CONC r, Matthew Arthur, Martha Arthur, Jane Rowder wife of John Rowder, Talbet Arthur, Lucy McCroy wife of James McCroy, his children; and his wife Martha.
2 CONT === Work has been done. ===
2 CONT Barnabas Arthur son of William A. Arthur and Ann Murray born in 1735 in Campbell County, Virginia, United States. Temple work for this person has been done. 242-5403-17810
2 CONT === !MARRIAGE: Barnabas Arthur m. Nancy Will ===
2 CONT !MARRIAGE: Barnabas Arthur m. Nancy Williamson surety William Arthur, by John Ayers on Jan 3 bond Jan 3 1811 !MARRIAGE: Barnabas Arthur m. Nancy Vaughn on Aug 1 1811 by John Harper bond Jul 26 1811 Washington Co KY. !WILL: dat Mar
2 CONC  2 1815 pro Apr 24 1815. wife Nancy, grandsons James Maxy, Barnabas Maxy, land bought of Benjamin Williamson to negroes George and Betty, equally to children John Arthur, William Arthur, Lewis Arthur, Barnabus Arthur, Caleb Arthur
2 CONC , Elizabeth Bowls, Fanny Pratt, Lucy Green and Rhody White decd's children.  exec. friends John Arthur and Samuel Clayton (jr) witness J. Leftwich, James Floyd, John Clayton. Accounts: to children John Arthur negro Bob, Lewis Arth
2 CONC ur tract of land, William Arthur land and cash, Lucy Green cash (in addition to inheritance). !DEED: Barnabas Arthur and Elizabeth sell to Stephen Hale 57 acres on Craddocks Creek Jul 26 1768 Bedford Co DB 4 p 172. !DEED: Barnabus
2 CONC  Arthur of Halifax Co bought 175 acres of land on the north side of Staunton from John Talbot of Bedford Co 27 Apr 1761 Bedford Co DB 1 p 407.
2 CONT === !FamilySearch (AFN:KWZG-57) Ancestral Fi ===
2 CONT !FamilySearch (AFN:KWZG-57) Ancestral File - downloaded 5/22/02 jdb
2 CONT === Served in the 5th Virginia Regiment as E ===
2 CONT Served in the 5th Virginia Regiment as Ensign & Lt under George Washington from the VA magazine of history vol2 pg250 relinquished the rights to his land to William Arthur of Wilkes County Ga There are two marriage dates for this 
2 CONC couple. the one shown and 26 May 1755 William Arthur was Surety on this listed marriage. After the death or before the death of Barnabus, his family has moved to Georgia. Son Mathew sells 504 acres on Flat creek. Mathew is listed 
2 CONC as resident of Georgia. Rev war patriot, There apparently were two Barnabuses. Look at the other Barnabus who was here about the same time and you will see a cross link on Marriages. This Barnabus was supposed to be married to Mar
2 CONC tha Talbot and Nancy Williamson. The other Barnabus was supposed to be married to Elizabeth and Nancy Williamson. One or the other is incorrect as far as second wife, but is likely OK as a person who exists.
2 CONT === According to Will of Barnabas (4th child ===
2 CONT According to Will of Barnabas (4th child of John & Rebecca of Goose creek) his wife was Nancy; from Bedford Cnty Deeds we find a Barnabas with a wife named Elizabeth who was still living in 1802. It is believed by some that Barnab
2 CONC us married 2nd to Nancy Williamson, 3 Jan 1811 as per marriage rec of Bedford Cnty Va. Others have stated that his second wife was Nancy Clayton. Nor proof either claims, so all that can be stated for sure is that Barnabas was mar
2 CONC ried first to Elizabeth who died after 1802 and them married second to Nancy. Since there are numerous Barnabas Arthurs around Bedford, Campbell, and Franklin Counties at the same time, making it very difficult.
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT In the name of God Amen, I Barnabas Arthur of the county of Bedford being weak in body but of sound and disposing memory. Item: I give and bequeath unto my wife Nancy one third part of my whole estate for and during the term of na
2 CONC tural life, of which then it is my will that the tract of land I now live do constitute a part. Item: I bequeath unto my grandsons James Maxey and Barnabas Maxey the sum of five pounds each to be their full share of my estate. Ite
2 CONC m: In consequence of long and faithful service of my negro man George and my negro woman Betty, it is my desire that they be emancipated, whenever the laws of this state will allow it and they have the tract of land I purchased of
2 CONC  Benjamin Williamson for and during the term of their natural lives; to live upon and maintain their idiot daughter Amy and until they can be so emancipated it is my will that they shall live upon said land and maintain their said
2 CONC  daughter and have all the profits of their labor, under the direction of my son Lewis and moreover that they be furnished with one year provision out of my estate whenever they leave it in consequence of this article and the said
2 CONC  negroes are not to be considered or appraised as part of my estate. Item: The residue of my estate both real and personal, I give and bequeath in equal shares unto my children John Arthur, William Arthur, Lewis Arthur, Barnabas A
2 CONC rthur, Caleb Arthur, Elizabeth Bowles, Fanny Pratt, Lucy Greer, and the children of Rhody White, deceased, my Staunton tract of land being first sold for the purpose of said division.  I request my friends John Arthur and Samuel C
2 CONC layton to act as my Executors of this my last will and testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnabas signed by his mark. The will was probated 20 Apr 1815.
2 CONT === Batch #: 7836304, Sheet #: 57, Source Ca ===
2 CONT Batch #: 7836304, Sheet #: 57, Source Call #: 1126459 !MARRIAGE: from Marriage Bonds of Bedford, Va, 1755-1800 p.1 !DEATH: IGI Va 1992, will pb 7/26/1815 Bedford Co, Va !EVENT: father's will dtd 1/9/1778 pd 1/28/1793 !MILITARY: In
2 CONC  Sep 1758 drew pay for service in the Bedford Co., Va Militia. from Henning's Statutes of Virginia Vol 7 p.205 !From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 2 January 1996.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
