2 CONT ** Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=234170351-1-997&action=showRecord MyHeritage Family Trees] via wife [http://www.geni.com/profile-34671545225 Jane Morton (born Peden)]
2 CONC  by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 23 2015, 19:56:42 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT DAR marker - Revolutionary Soldier - Robert Morrow 1776-1780, placed by Dripping Springs Chapter.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Morrow (David Morrow5, David Morrow4, Alexander Morrow3, David Morrow2, David Morrow1) was born 1740 in Maryland, and died 1820 in Morgan County, AL. He was buried in Morrow Cemetery #1, Somerville, Morgan County, AL. He ma
2 CONC rried Jane Peden ABT 1774 in SC, daughter of John Peden and Margaret Patience "Peggy" McDill. She was born 1740 in  County Antrim, Ireland, and died 1830 in Morgan County, AL. She was buried in Morrow Cemetery #1, Somerville, Morg
2 CONC an County, AL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Morrow and Jane Peden are:  +
2 CONT 2  i. Samuel Morrow was born 8 NOV 1775 in SC, and died 7 JUN 1845 in Morgan Co., AL.
2 CONT 3  ii. William Morrow was born 5 NOV 1777 in Maryland. +
2 CONT 4  iii. David Morrow was born 23 MAR 1783 in Greeneville, SC, and died AFT 1838 in Prob. Fayette Co., AL.
2 CONT 5  iv. Mary Morrow was born 1780. She married William White. 
2 CONT 6  v. Janet Morrow was born 1782. +
2 CONT 7  vi. Thomas Morrow was born 29 SEP 1785 in Greenville Co., SC, and died 2 MAR 1870 in Anderson Co., TX.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 South Carolina Regt, Revolutionary War
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to Alabama in 1817.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR marker - Revolutionary Soldier - Robert Morrow 1776-1780, placed by Dripping Springs Chapter.
2 CONT =========================================================
2 CONT Part of the Morrow y-DNA Project Family #1
2 CONT
2 CONT  NOTE: This reseracher uses Y-DNA testing results as part of my research and yes on some of my families lines the information is different from research done before y-DNA testing. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~amorrow/morrowdnalines.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=morrowdna&id=I3074
2 CONT
2 CONT Info below copied from Morrow. y-DNA Project.
2 CONT Morrow DNA Project Matched Lines For background information go here.
2 CONT
2 CONT We currently have seven sets of matches.
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Sam/Alexander Matches (Group I) These participants originally thought they were descended from "Old Samuel of Spartenburg" (d. 1796 in Spartenburg, SC) so I use that as shorthand for the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander is generally considered the forefather (Old Sam's grandfather.) Alexander is the son of David Morrow who wrote his will in 1692 in Norfolk, VA. This is the "Norfolk, VA Morrows" line that nearly all southern Morrows assu
2 CONC me they are descended from. The DNA results show most people are wrong!
2 CONT
2 CONT There are nine matching participants in this line. There are descendants of Robert Morrow m. Jane Peden, Thomas Morrow m. Janet McCarter, David m. Margaret Kelso, Maj. Samuel m. Janet Nelson, Lt. John m. Mary Kelso, Joseph m. Jane
2 CONC  Wylie, and Adam m. Isobel. Except for Adam, these men are all the same generation. Researchers have in varying configurations shown them as brothers or cousins - the sons of Old Samuel and his cousin David m. Agnes White.
2 CONT
2 CONT Documentary evidence shows that Maj. Sam and Lt. John are brothers (pension applications reference each other) and that Maj. Sam is the "nephew" of Old Sam (from a deed). Based on that, we had a theory that Sam and John were sons 
2 CONC of David and Agnes (along with David 1762-1843) and that Robert and Thomas were the sons of Old Sam.
2 CONT
2 CONT HOWEVER, DNA testing has shown a variation between the men at one particular marker that splits them up: Thomas and David descendants have one value, the other three have a different value. 
2 CONT This discovery sparked another round of research, and the discovery of a document showing David and Mary Morrow of Spartenburg listed with sons Robert, Samuel and John in a visitation listing in 1774. 
2 CONT This is "David of Spartenburg," a man not listed in Ray's book, but easily the right age and location to be the brother of Old Samuel. 
2 CONT (Ray did list a David as a brother of Old Samuel - David Morrow m. Elizabeth Catlett. 
2 CONT We have replaced that David with David of Spartenburg.) As a result of DNA testing and further research, we hypothesize the following relationships: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wayne N.Parker  I am Robert Morrow 4th Great-grandson.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=31649888 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 15 2018, 9:35:13 UTC''
2 CONT ----
