2 CONT '''Morrow, John''' in ''Roster of South Carolina Patriots in the Revolution,'' page 704 (online at Ancestry.com):  He died 30 November 1781.  Was married to Mary Kelsey (Kelso), 1774.  He enlisted, while residing in Chester Distri
2 CONC ct, and served during 1780 and 1781 under Capt. John Mills, Cols. Edward Lacey, Henry Hampton and Gen. Sumter.  He was in the battle at Fish Dam Ford and was killed in the skirmish at Dorchester on 30 Nov. 1781.  At some time, he 
2 CONC was under Col. Roebuck.  An annuitant (pension) claim was filed in SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''DAR Ancestor #: A081257''': Served with Mill's Troops, Sumter's Brigade.  A Patriot of the American Revolution for South Carolina with the rank of LIEUTENANT. 
