1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Margaret Morrow
2 CONT * FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT * Birth:	1760 - Orange, North Carolina, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Death:	Oct 5 1841 - Davidson, Tennessee, USA
2 CONT * Parents:	William P Morrow Sr, Jane Morrow (born Parks)
2 CONT * Spouses:	Steel, Samuel Bryan
2 CONT * Children:	Jane Pinkerton (born Bryan), Sarah Webb (born Bryan), Henry Morrow Bryan, Elizabeth Pinkerton (born Bryan), Mary Orton (born Bryan), Margaret Campbell (born Bryan), William Park Bryan, and names of 6 more children
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT SAMUEL BRYAN (2) is son of John Bryan (1) and Sarah Bryan. According to the 1830 census, Samuel Bryan (2) was born between 1750 and 1760. In 1772, Samuel Bryan is listed with his father, John Bryan (1) in a Rowan County, North Car
2 CONC olina tax list. During this time period, a white male would have been at least sixteen years of age to be taxable and usually left home by age twenty, therefore, Samuel Bryan would have been born between 1752 and 1756. Samuel Brya
2 CONC n married Margaret (Morrow) Steel in 1784 (a second marriage for Margaret resulting in a marriage date that would a little later than most marriages). Margaret (Morrow) Steel was estimated to be around twenty-four years of age whe
2 CONC n she married a second time to Samuel Bryan and therefore Margaret (Morrow) Steel was born around 1760. Samuel would have been around twenty-four to twenty-eight years of age (born 1756 to 1760) when he married Margaret. From thes
2 CONC e two sources, it is estimated that Samuel Bryan was born around 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # “Bryan Family History: Descendants of John and Sarah Bryan of Rowan County, North Carolina; Samuel and Margaret Bryan of Davidson County, Tennessee; Samuel and Charlotte Bryan of Maury County, Tennessee;  Finus and Caledonia Bry
2 CONC an of Hill County, Texas.”  By Robert Brooks Casey and Bernice (Brooks) Casey (2004). < [http://www.rcasey.net/acrobat/bryphoto0305a.pdf PDF] >. Page 8-110.
2 CONT
