1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A055400 DAR Ancestor #: A055400]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://sarpatriots.sar.org/patriot/display/181156 SAR Patriot #: P-181156]
2 CONT
2 CONT HIGHSMITH, DANIEL
2 CONT Service:  NORTH CAROLINA    Rank(s): SOLDIER
2 CONT Birth:  CIRCA 1739    NORFOLK CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Death:  POST 2-19-1807     NEW HANOVER CO NORTH CAROLINA
2 CONT Service Source:  NCDAR, ROSTER OF SOLS FROM NC IN THE AM REV, P 388; NC REV WAR PAY VOUCHERS, # 5002, ROLL # S.115.87
2 CONT Service Description:  1) MILITIA, WILMINGTON DIST
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Thomas was also a Rev War soldier.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL HIGHSMITH, JR. / Circa 1737 - Circa 1807
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel and Lucretia were members of the Beltail Burch of the Old Kehukee Baptist Association in New Hanover Co., NC (now Wells Chapel Baptist Church of the Wilmington Baptist Association), with their names appearing in the minutes
2 CONC  in 1796 and 1803. The Church minutes reveal that Daniel was excommunicated in "January 1796 for disobeying gospel rule and government of the Church," and that in Mar. 1796 Lucretia was "excommunicated for censuring the Church for
2 CONC  dealing with her Husband by order of the Conference." The Church minutes also record that "Old friend Highsmith came forward and was restored again to fellowship in December, 1803." Daughter of Thomas PARKER and Martha MAPLES .
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Highsmith, Jr. passed away, appr. age 80, circa 1807 in New Hanover County, North Carolina.  Daniel Highsmith, Jr. is interred at the Wells Chapel Baptist Cemetery in New Hanover County, North Carolina.  While spouse Lucret
2 CONC ia (Parker) Highsmith is presumably also interred at the Wells Chapel Baptist Cemetery, no documentation is emergent to validate this intuitive presumption.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment record per Find A Grave Memorial #184519426 / Created October 22, 2017 by Allan Brem, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Inferred Death year is 1813.  Will dated 19 Feb 1807.  Probate dated Nov 1813. (Photo attached).
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Unverified relationship to Thomas Highsmith, son.
