1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Partridge-of-Olney/6000000003968396807?through=6000000039603731090
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Partridge-44
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the profile of John Partridge of Navestock, Essex, England. He is not he same man as John Partridge of Olney, Buckinghamshire, whose son William and daughter Jane immigrated to Lynn and Salisbury, Massachusetts. None of th
2 CONC e children of John of Navestock left England.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was baptized at St. Thomas the Apostle on 14 September 1578, the son of Bartholmew and Purnell Green Partridge.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Jane Hogg in London on 11 May 1619.[2] Their children were John, William, Jane and Margaret. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT John wrote his will on 1 October 1652.[4] Only Margaret and John were alive at that time. His daughter Jane had married John Lake and died shortly after childbirth in 1650, and son William had died as a young boy.[5] His wife Jane
2 CONC  wrote her will in 1666, leaving bequests to her grandchildren, it seems only her daughter Margaret was living. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disambiguation 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Partridge-of-Olney/6000000003968396807 whose widow was Frances.
2 CONT *There was a family of Partridges that lived in London and Navistock, Essex who descended from Bartholomew Partridge and his wife Pernell. These men were also Citizens and Cutlers in London. They are not related to the Olney, Buck
2 CONC inghamshire Partridges. [4]
2 CONT *John Partridge of Olney was not married to Jane Hogg in London.
2 CONT *John Partridge of Navestock, Essex; not the ancestor of John Partridge of Medfield or William Partridge of Salisbury. Many people believe that John Partridge who immigrated from England and lived in Medfield, Massachusetts was th
2 CONC e son of John and Jane (Hogg) Partridge of Navestock, Essex, England. This is not correct. The origins of John of Medfield and his siblings is unknown.
2 CONT * The Visitation of Essex had the family tree of Bartholomew Partridge and includes his son John who married Jane Hogg. [1] The visitation shows that John Partridge had four children: John (age 14 in 1634), William, Jane and Marga
2 CONC ret.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Take due notice
2 CONT
2 CONT John Partridge & Jane Hogg are not known to have had children emigrating to the American Colonies. So not - their - children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Mary (Partridge) Kibbe
2 CONT *William Partridge, Sr., of Salisbury
2 CONT *siblings John Partridge, of Medfield , Margaret (Partridge) Stacy & William Partridge, Sr., of Medfield
2 CONT *William Partridge, of Hadley
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Stamper/6000000176005370999
2 CONT
