2 DATE 26 MAY 1693
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stocking-4
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was the daughter of George Stocking and presumably his wife Anne.[1] Sarah was born about 1637, probably at Hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 November 1659, John Winthrop treated "Stockin Sara 22 years".[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Samuel Olcott by about 1664. On 29 August 1667, Winthrop treated their three year old daughter.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah and Samuel Olcott were both named in her father's 1673 will, and Sarah was bequeathed £10.[4] This will was later declared to have "no value" and that "the wife of Samuel Olcott" was to instead receive £41 (like her sisters)
2 CONC ,[5] which was later revised to £42.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Olcott's will was dated 1 December 1703, naming their children, and proved 12 April 1704. Sarah was not named and had likely died by this time.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah and Samuel Olcott were married by 1664. They had (order uncertain):[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah, m. William Williams
2 CONT # Mary, m. Jonathan Bigelow
2 CONT # Elizabeth
2 CONT # Thomas
2 CONT # George
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT A previous version of this profile had her death date as "26 May 1693" without source.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archive.org/stream/stockingancestry00stoc/stockingancestry00stoc_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts from this link: 1. Wife Anna and 4 children sailed from England in the ship Griffin and landed in Boston 1633. 2. Wife Anna and his 4 children named in his will dated 15 Jul 1673. 3. Married Agnes (Shotwell) Webster widow of
2 CONC  John Webster after Anna's death. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stocking-4 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 6 2017, 2:38:40 UTC''
