2 CONT ! Birth: (1a,b) d/o John Olcott of Hartford, CT. (2) 28 Oct 1701, Hartford, CT, d/o Mary (BLACKLEACH) OLCOTT.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1b) 1722, 26 May: At Court of Probate held at Hartford, CT, Mrs. Mary Wadsworth, alias Olcott, administratrix on the estate of Mr. John Olcott, late of Hartford, decd., now exhibited an account of her administration, and the cour
2 CONC t ordered distribution to the widow her thirds, and the residue of said estate, including the relict's thirds after her decease, in housing and lands, to be distributed as follows: To Mary Ffarnsworth, Rachel Olcott, and Abigail O
2 CONC lcott, daughters of the deceased, 104.08.00, which is their equal part of said estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1a) 1722, 25 Jun: Aaron Cooke and John Pratt distribute the estate of John Olcott of Hartford, CT. To Rachel Olcott, 1/2 of the homelot with the little house thereon, valued at 100 pounds. The land in the south meadow formally be
2 CONC longing to Timothy Hide, now in the possession of Mr. Watson, and the reversion of which belongs to the heirs of the said John Olcott, we distribute to each of the said heirs an equal part thereof when the reversion thereof return
2 CONC s to them, the widow then to have 1/3 thereof. Test: Hez. Wyllys, clerk. We whose names are underwritten have agreed, divided and received our parts of the moveable estate of John Olcott, late of Hartford, deceased, the full porti
2 CONC on of our part thereof according to the order of the Court of Probate. Signed Joseph Wadsworth, Mary Wadsworth, Joseph Farnsworth, Mary Farnsworth, Rachel Ollcot, Abigail Olcot. Wits. Aaron Cooke, John Pratt. (1b) An agreement for
2 CONC  dividing the moveable estate was exhibited in Court under the hands and seals of Capt. Joseph Wadsworth, Mrs. Mary Wadsworth, Joseph Farnsworth and Mary Farnsworth, Rachel Olcott and Abigail Olcott, which agreement was accepted b
2 CONC y the court.
2 CONT
