1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Not''' the father of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Polk/6000000007141462232
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''WILLIAM BRUCE POLK'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/174653642/william-bruce-polk
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Ann Nancy Knox
2 CONT
2 CONT - - -
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his wife lived at "White Hall," on the eastern shore of Maryland
2 CONT
2 CONT According to county records he died between 23 Jan and 24 Feb 1739/40.
2 CONT
2 CONT Documentation indicates that this William Polk Sr (1672-1739) is NOT the father of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Polk/6000000007141462232 (1695-1757).
2 CONT
2 CONT William Polk Jr. (1695/1705-1757) is the earliest proven anscestor of the "Mecklenburg" Polks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill Polk Tree http://ftm.genealogy.com/users/p/o/l/Billy-F-Polk/GENE13-0001.html
2 CONT
2 CONT An argument against the "accepted" genealogies. http://ftm.genealogy.com/users/p/o/l/Billy-F-Polk/FILE/0019text.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT '''194. A Genealogical Tree of The Polk Family, 1849. This tree is incorrect in that it shows John Polk, son of Robert Bruce Polk, as the progenitor of the southern branch of the Polk Family. Research after the publication of the 
2 CONC 1849 tree revealed the proper line from Robert Bruce for the southern branch was through his son William, and then William's son William, who married Margaret Taylor.''' There is another Polk tree being sold by the James K. Polk M
2 CONC emorial Association of Columbia, TN. which shows the southern Polks (the descendants of William Polk and Margaret Taylor) as being of Robert Bruce Polk, then John Polk, then William Polk. The text about origination of this tree is
2 CONC  printed on the face of the tree and is: "The original drawing was partially updated in 1966 in respect to the family of Governor E. Louis Lowe (the "Fearless Lowe" of James R. Randall's lyrics of Maryland My Maryland) and his wif
2 CONC e Esther Winder Polk Lowe. This copy was made for James G. Stahlman of Nashville for presentation to the Polk Memorial Association, June 1967." And there is still another Polk tree, this one an updated version of the 1849 tree, wh
2 CONC ich shows the southern Polk line as coming from Robert Polk of Maryland, through his son William, and through his son William who married Margaret Taylor. The bottom of this Polk tree (which is sold by the James K. Polk Memorial A
2 CONC ssociation, also) states: "Revised and reproduced from a tracing of an original which was published in 1849 -- by the Polk Genealogical Committe ---Nashville, Tenn. in 1952." Copies of all these trees are in the possession of Bill
2 CONC  Polk of Kansas City, MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT 195. Mrs. Frank M. Angellotti, The Polks of North Carolina and Tennessee, (Originally published by the New England Historical and Genealogical Soc., 1923-1924; republished for the James K. Polk Memorial Association, Columbia, TN.,
2 CONC  1984, by Southern Historical Press, Easley, SC.), pp. 3-4, "William Polk (Robert 1), born probably in co. Donegal, Ireland, about 1664, died probably near the end of 1739, as his will was proved 24 Feb. 1739/40."
2 CONT
2 CONT 196. William Harrison Polk, Polk Family and Kinsmen, (1912, by Bradley and Gilbert Inc. of Louisville, KY.), pg. 28, "William Polk" mentioned as a child of Robert and Magdalen Polk. Pages 30, 31, 32, 33, mention William Polk. See 
2 CONC notes for information from page 34, and 203-209 of this source.
2 CONT
2 CONT 197. Miss Mary Winder Garrett of Williamsburg, VA., "Pedigree of the Pollok or Polk Family From Fulbert the Saxon (A. D. 1075) to the Present Time," The American Historical Magazine,The University Press, 208 N. College St., Nashvi
2 CONC lle, TN. April 1896 issue begins the series and concludes with Vol. 4, 1899: October 1897 issue, Vol. II, No. 4, pg. 383, Mary Garrett has the wrong William as the progenitor of the southern Polk family in her genealogy. She appea
2 CONC rs to have taken the same path as those who published the 1849 Polk tree. Garrett shows the line as Robert Bruce Polk, then John Polk, then William Polk, who (she shows) married twice, first to Priscilla Roberts and second to Marg
2 CONC aret Taylor. .
2 CONT
2 CONT 198. Burke's Peerage, Burke's Presidential Families of the United States, (Burke's Peerage Limited, 1975, London; distributed in America by Arco Publishing Co., Inc., NY, NY.), pg. 243, William Polk is shown as son of "Robert Poll
2 CONC ok (or Polke)," of "White Hall, Maryland, b probably in co Donegal ca 1664, m 1st, Nancy, widow of ---Owen, and dau of ---Knox; and 2ndly, ---Gray, widow, and d (will pr 24 Feb 1739), leaving issue..."
2 CONT
2 CONT 199. Will, Robert Polke (Robert Bruce?? Polk), MD. Archives, Perogative Court (Wills), 11, pp. 416-418; Accession No. Md. HR 1289-2; Location 1-11-1-12; Will dated 6 May 1699, proven 5 Jun 1703, "I leave to my sons John and Willia
2 CONC m Polke to each of them twelve pence."
2 CONT
2 CONT 200. Compiled by Emory Murphy, Moreland, GA., The Polk Family Supplement One, (November 1981), pg. II-7.
2 CONT
2 CONT 201. Compiled by Gary Boyd Roberts, Santa Clara, CA., Ancestors of American Presidents, (1989), pg. 18, William Polk is shown as "William Polk, prob. Co. Donegal, Ireland c. 1664-Md. c. 1739 (will proved 24 Feb. 1739/40." His wife
2 CONC  is shown as "Mrs. Nancy Knox Owens, widow." William's father is "Robert Pollock or Polk..." His mother is "Magdalen Tasker,...."
2 CONT
2 CONT 202. Will, William Polk, son of Robert Bruce? Polk, Somerset Co., MD., Officer of the Register of Wills, Bk. 9, pp. 211-212, "In the name of God Amen I William Polk of the County of Somerset and Province of Maryland....."
2 CONT
2 CONT 203. Compiled and edited by Jane Baldwin (Jane Baldwin Cotton), Maryland Calendar of Wills, Wills from 1685 to 1702, Vol. II, (1968, Genealogical Publishing Co., Baltimore, MD.), pg. 181, "Owens, William, Somerset Co., 27th Mch., 
2 CONC 1698; To 2 sons, William and John, equally, 'The Widow's Choice,' sons Robert and Samuel, personalty. Wife (unnamed), extx. Overseers: Jno. Polk, Wm. Knox. Test: Wm. Polk, Archibald Smith, Jno. Goldsmith, Jno. Browne. 6. 280."
2 CONT
2 CONT 204. F. Edward Wright, Citizens of the Eastern Short of Maryland, 1859 - 1750, (Family Line Publications, Silver Springs, MD.), pg. 42, "William Poalke" registered his cattle marks, 1703.
2 CONT
2 CONT 205. Somerset [MD.] Judicial Records, 1707-1711, Maryland Hall of Records, Accession 9169, MSA C 1774-18, Loc. 1/48/2/42], SOMERSET JUDICIAL RECORDS 1707-11 [Accession 9169, MSA C 1774-18, Loc. 1/48/2/42] JUNE COURT 1708 101 Willi
2 CONC am Polk petitions Justices for guardianship of the orphan children, William and Anne, of his brother John, deceased. To the worshipfull the Justices of Somerset County now in Court sitting Wm. Polk humbly showeth that when your pe
2 CONC titioner’s brother John Polk late of this county dec’d left two children behind him, to wit Wm. and Ann Polk who upon his deathbed he requested that your petitioner and his wife to take care of them to see them educated and brough
2 CONC t up Christian like and also to bring up the boy to learn a trade which your petitioner humbly craves that he may have the children ordered unto him per your Worships shall in your prudence and discretion think fit to be done (rea
2 CONC sonably) for the orphans and petitioner as in duty bound shall ever pray. Court grants request. William Polk is to give good security that he is to teach the said Wm Polk a trade and to read and write. James and William Polk enter
2 CONC  into recognizance for sum of L10 on behalf of said orphans, condition being that William Polk do his best to prepare what parts is delivered to him of their portions left by their deceased father till of age and then to return th
2 CONC eir increase if any and do take care to learn the said William Polk a trade and to read and write and do allow the said William and Anne Polk all necessary and convenient till they come of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT 206. Somerset [MD.] Judicial Records, 1730-1733, Maryland Hall of Records, [Accession 9177 MSA C1774-30, Loc. 1/48/3/4], Mr. William Polk aged about fifty eight years or thereabouts being sworn on the Holy Evangelists of Almighty 
2 CONC God deposeth and saith that at the time Francis Roberts was married to his sister that the deponent with the said Roberts and severall others was coming from his fathers to a fort hous which stood on a tract of land called Elliott
2 CONC s Choice belonging to the said Roberts and this deponent further saith that the afsd Roberts pointing to a large pine which stood by the marsh side about one hundred and fifty yards from the fort hous and said that the pine was th
2 CONC e first bounder of Elliotts Choice and further saith not. William [W] Polk.
2 CONT
2 CONT  William Harrison Polk, Polk Family and Kinsmen, (1912, by Bradley and Gilbert Inc. of Louisville, KY.), pg. 203, "William Polk, the second son and child of Capt. Robert Bruce Polk and his wife Magdalen (Tasker-Porter) Polk, was b
2 CONC orn about 1664-7 in the County of Donegal, Ireland, a short distance from Londonderry and Coleraine."
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Peerage, Burke's Presidential Families of the United States, (Burke's Peerage Limited, 1975, London; distributed in America by Arco Publishing Co., Inc., NY, NY.), pg. 243.
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiled by Emory Murphy, Moreland, GA., The Polk Family Supplement One, (November 1981), pg. II-7, birth date and place given is "1664," in "Donegal, Ireland."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Polk-73 WikiTree Genealogy] via father [http://www.geni.com/profile-128932662 Capt. Robert Bruce Polk] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 23 2015, 0:13:0
2 CONC 5 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Information Cite:  The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, "Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:3C5T-9S7 : accessed 2016-06-20), entry for William Whitehal /Polk/.
2 CONT
2 CONT AFGS 1 UID 94A2C0EC343D4D86B048E8A3496F2ED05FB5
2 CONT
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT
2 CONT "That William Polk, son of Robert and Magdalen. was mixed up with the Owens' in lousiness transactions, the records clearly show, for he purchased the old homestead of Wm. and John Shores. That William's wife's name was Anne, (or 
2 CONC Nancy ) the records also show."
2 CONT - Quote from Polk Family and Kinsmen, 1912, page 27
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wm. Polk Sr., was twice married, first to Nancy (Knox) Owens, and second to a widow Grey, who had a son Allen Grey. Both wives died before Wm. Sr., executed his will in Jan. 1T39-40.  - Quote from Polk Family and Kinsmen, 1912, p
2 CONC age 34
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  William Polk
2 CONT
2 CONT  in the Millennium File
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: 	William Polk Gender: 	Male Birth Date: 	1664 Birth Place: 	Donegal, Ireland Death Date: 	1739 Death Place: 	Maryland, USA Father: 	Robert PolkePollok Mother: 	Magdalen Tasker Spouse: 	Nancy Knox Children: 	William Jr Polk
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT When William Bruce Polk was born on 20 October 1662, in County Donegal, Ireland, his father, Robert Bruce Pollock II, was 37 and his mother, Magdalen Tasker, was 35. He married Mrs Jane Polk in 1693, in Somerset, Maryland, British
2 CONC  Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 1 daughter. He died on 10 March 1707, in Somerset, Maryland, United States, at the age of 44, and was buried in All Saints Monie Cemetery, Princess Anne, Somerset, Ma
2 CONC ryland, United States.
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LBC3-QCW/william-bruce-polk-1662-1707
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
