2 TITL The Probable Origins and Ancestry of John Crandall, of Westerly, Rhode Island (1618-1676
1 NOTE Jailed 1651 arrested with John Clarke, et al, at Lynn.
1 NOTE There were other children born to this marriage, but due to space I am only naming my direct line ancestor from this family.
1 NOTE Jailed 1651 arrested with John Clarke, et al, at Lynn.
1 NOTE "Tradition states that he first appears in Salem, MA in 1634/35 andremoves to Providence with Roger Williams about 1636. However, thefirst real documentation of Elder John is as a grand juror in Newport,RI 8 Sep 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT "(Extensive research in both civil and church records of Salem, Lynn,Rehoboth, and Swansea, MA as well as in early Providence and Newport,RI show absolutely no record of Elder John until 1643, even thoughthere is frequent mention 
2 CONC of Roger Williams, Obadiah Holmes, and JohnClark.)
2 CONT
2 CONT "He is one of the six purchasers of Misquamicutt (Westerly), RI in1661, and builds his homestead there on Pound Road circa 1665.
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was perhaps the first Baptist Elder in the U.S. (according totradition), later converting to the Seventh Day Baptist faith, holdingmeetings at his home in Westerly, RI.
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed to Newport because of the dangers of the King Philip Warsin 1676, and, while there, he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT "He is buried in the family burial ground on the Homestead (HistoricalCemetery #15). His monument was erected by Crandall Family Association27 May 1991.
2 CONT
2 CONT "There is absolutely no docuementation for the tradition that he isthe son of a Sir John Crandall & Elizabeth Drake of Monmouthshire,Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The township of "Westerleigh" is certainly very circumstantialevidence, since he was one of the founders of "Westerly", RhodeIsland."
2 CONT
2 CONT (all above from Crandall Internet Genealogy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Crandall Internet Genealogy has John Crandall & Mary Opp as parents ofSarah Crandall, who m. Josiah Witter.
1 NOTE !Information on the Crandall families comes from these sources.  The
2 CONT Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island, John Osborne Austin, Genealogical Pub Co, Baltimore, 1969. New England Families, Genealogy and Memories, William Richard Cutler, Vol I-IV, New York, Lewis, 1915.
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled in Providenc, Rhode Island as early as 1637.  Had settled first in
2 CONT Mass.  Moved to Newport by 1651.  He was conservator of the peace in Westerly
2 CONT in 1670, and deputy to the general assembly again in 1670-71.  He was arrested by the Connecticut authorities 2 May 1671, but declined to give bond on the advice of Rhode Island authorities who eventually paid his expenses.  He mo
2 CONC ved to Newport because of King Philip's war in 1676.
