1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eber Crandall was married 3 times and had nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #1 ___________________, unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT #2 Patience Lamphere, dau. of George Landphere * Jane Anne Hulet
2 CONT
2 CONT #3 Mary Cottrell, dau. of Nicholas and Dorothy Pendleton Cottrell.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children by second wife (Patience) Lamphear''':
2 CONT
2 CONT John, Eber, Samuel and Joseph. No birthdates known.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children by third wife Mary Cottrell:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, Nathaniel, Johnathan, Ebenezer, and Jeremiah.
2 CONT
2 CONT He becamee a Freeman June 29, 1702 at Westerly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died Aug. 22, 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was proved Sept. 15, 1727. His wife is dead in 1727 as well, and the executors of his will discuss putting his children out as apprentices.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of a branch of the Crandall family by Crandall, A. P. (Arovestus Pardee) page 15 _______________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Eber_Crandall_%287%29_
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Name  Eber Crandall'''
2 CONT * '''Gender'''  Male
2 CONT * '''Birth'''?  1676  Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT *  '''Marriage 1'''  ABT 1696 Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT **  to Mary
2 CONT * '''Marriage 2'''  ABT 1700  Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT **  to Patience Lanphere
2 CONT * '''Marriage 3'''  1708 , , Rhode Island
2 CONT **  to Mary Cottrell
2 CONT * '''Death'''?  1727 Westerly, Washington, Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT * '''Will'''?  22 Aug 1727  Westerly, Washington, Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT ** Dated Aug. 22, 1727; proved Sept. 25, 1727 Westerly Vol. 2, p 227-228. 
2 CONT *** Unnamed former wife; Wife: Mary; 
2 CONT *** Sons: John, Eber, Samuel & Joseph by my 2nd wife; 
2 CONT *** children my now wife hath living: Mary, Nathaniel, Jonathan, Ebenezer & Jeremiah. 
2 CONT *** Brother [in-law] Nathaniel Cottrill of North Kingstown & friend Nicholas Cottrell of Westerly exors. 
2 CONT *** Witnesses: James Covey, James Pendleton, George Stillman & Nathaniel Stillman. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''' 
2 CONT * 1  Abstracts of Westerly Wills, in Alden G. Beaman. Rhode Island Genealogical Register. (The Rhode Island Genealogical Research Institute), 216, April 1984.
2 CONT * 2   MISC:          
2 CONT **  -Will of '''George Lanphear''' living but incapable Oct. 31, 1726; Jan. 31, 1726/7; March 30, 1726/7; April 27, 1717 [dates need clarification] divided his real estate among his children including '''a daughter who was wife of
2 CONC  Eber Crandall'''. [Westerly Probate Vol. 2, pps. 114, 136, 195-196]         
2 CONT **  -Sept. 25, 1727 Nathaniel Cottrell of North Kingstown appeared ... to the last will & Testament of Eber Crandall of Westerly decd. [Westerly TCP 2:228]         
2 CONT **  -Mary Crandall ... widow Eber ... petitioned Counsel ... Witnesses: Samuell Cottrell & George Stillman. [Westerly TCP 2:229]        
2 CONT **  -Nathaniell Cottrell of North Kingstown was given L.A. on estate of Eber Crandall. [Westerly TCP 2:256]         
2 CONT **  -April 27, 1730 An account of debts out of estate of Eber Crandall late of Westerly lists many names including: John Ayres, Sarah Potter, Stephen Wilcox, George Stillman, Tobias Brand, Eliza. Cottrell, Samuel Cottrell, Deborah
2 CONC  Stillman Jr. [Westerly TCP 2:136]
2 CONT
