1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John Cottrell
2 CONT * Birth: Abt. 1652	Westerly, Kings County, Rhode Island
2 CONT * Marriage	1678	Kingstown, Washington, Rhode Island  to Elizabeth
2 CONT *Death	1704 Kingstown, Washington, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cottrell was born about 1650, [1] or 1652 [2] in the Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations. He is the son of Nicholas Cottrell and an unknown wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT John is thought by some to have married firstly Elizabeth/Penelope, but this marriage is doubtful. The John Cottrell in the transcribed marriage record is shown to have died in 1721, which is the death date of John's son John Cott
2 CONC rell II, and the record itself is unsure whether his wife's given name is Elizabeth or Penelope, showing her name as Elizabeth/Penelope (?). [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # John might have married (1st or 2nd) to  Hannah Gaylord Crandall, though her identity is also uncertain. John's son-in-law's mother was also called Hannah (Gaylord) Crandall.  Married afterc1676 to Hanna Taylor Crandall/Gaylord,
2 CONC  who  d.  Aug. 8, 1678/79 (Gregorian or Julian Calendar) per Crandall genealogy page 3 (Austin Crandalls "Elder John Crandall and his descendats" ) What did Hanna Gaylord Cottrell die of at age 32? (disputed marriage)
2 CONT # By 1679 to Elizabeth/Penelope, B: 30 Jan 1647, Windsor, CT D: unknown, Westerly, RI
2 CONT "John Crandall mentioned in his father's will was of Westerly and Kingston, Rhode Island. He owned the land in Kingston in 1680 which was laid out by Rev. John Crandall. His first wife's name is not known. His second wife might be
2 CONC  Hannah Gaylord Crandall. If this is so, it might explain how he came in possession of the Crandall land." [4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT John had the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hannah (Cottrell) Utter; Hannah Cottrell b. 1679 (Gregorian or Julian Calendar) named after her mother
2 CONT # John Cottrell II;
2 CONT # Samuel Cottrell;
2 CONT # Nathaniel Cottrell;
2 CONT # Mary (Cottrell) Crandall [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cottrell was named as son and heir in Nicholas Cottrell's Will probated in February 1680 in Plymouth County, Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Last will and testament of Nicholas Cottrell, Sen., living by Taunton River, taken Feb. 1680, as followeth: … I give and bequeath unto my son John Cottrell, one hundred acres of land which he now liveth upon, at Skonomicutt by Na
2 CONC rragansett. ..." [6] John Cottrell "died in early 1704, leaving a Will, of which his son John Cottrell II was Executor". [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave states that John Cottrell died in 1721, but this is the death year of his son, also called John Cottrell. Perhaps Find A Grave has conflated their identities. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cottrell, mentioned in his father Nicholas' will, was of Westerly and Kingston, Rhode Island. He owned the land in Kingston in 1681 which was laid out to Rev. John Crandall. His wife's name is not known. John may have been ma
2 CONC rried secondly to Hannah Gaylord Crandall, which may explain how he came into possession of the Crandall land.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the John Cottrell who is mentioned in the Newport Church Record as having neglected his duties and separated off from the church on Oct. 1, 1693, Oct. 5, 1693, again on Sept. 17, 1698. He died early in 1704 leaving a will.
2 CONC  The executor of his will was his son John. John Crandall and John Maxson were chosen as messengers to deliver reprimands from the Sabbatarian Church in Newport. His will was destroyed in a fire in 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record: John Cottrell & Elizabeth/Penelope, Nicholas Cottrell & Martha, Nicholas Cottrell & Ann Peabody, Nicholas Cottrell & Dorothy Pendleton
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000205791270821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: New England Marriages prior to 1700
2 CONT -----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #North Kingstown Town Council Probate 6:57-58. I give & bequeath to Elizabeth Cottrell [burn]ether Bed... moveable estate I give to my two [burn] Cottrell & Hannah Cottrell ...son John Cottrelll ...appoint cusen Nicholas Cottrell 
2 CONC of Westerly overseer. Witnesses: Capt. John Eldred, Jeremiah [burn]
2 CONT #  LAND: -June (Jan.) 11, 1715/16 Nicholas Cottrell of Westerly, husbandman, to brother John Cottrell of Westerly, husbandman, 150 Acres. Witnesses: Thomas Burdick, Edward Saunders. [Westerly Land 5:6]
2 CONT #"Rhode Island Births and Christenings, 1600-1914," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:V2HH-C6J : 10 February 2018), John Cottrell in entry for Hannah Cottrell, 1679; citing NORTH KINGSTOWN,WASHINGTON,
2 CONC RHODE ISLAND, reference ; FHL microfilm 908,270.
2 CONT #HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 325
2 CONT #"International Genealogical Index (IGI)," database,(https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:1:MQFK-RP6 : accessed 2016-08-05), entry for John Cottrell.
2 CONT #Bierce, Thurber Hoffman, 1900- . ''Ancestors in the United States of Byron H. Bierce and his wife Mary Ida Cottrell of Cortland County, New York''  Page 95-96.  < [https://archive.org/details/ancestorsinunite00bier/page/95/mode/1
2 CONC up?q=Ancestors+in+the+United+States+of+Byron+H.+Bierce+and+his+wife+Mary+Ida+Cottrell Archive.Org] >
2 CONT #http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Cottrell_%2810%29
2 CONT # http://mytreewebsite.com/cccottrell/cottrelltree.html
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cottrell-10
2 CONT # Crandall, John Cortland, 1881- .  ''Elder John Crandall of Rhode Island and his descendants'' (1931) < [https://archive.org/details/elderjohncrandal00cran_0/page/3/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] > Elder  John  married  secon
2 CONC d,  Hannah  Gaylord,  b.  30 Jan.  1647;  d.  3  Aug.  1678.  After  the  death  of  Eld.  John  his  widow  married,  second,  John  Cottrell,  Jr.  Hannah  Gaylord  was  the  dau.  of  William  (William,  John, Nicholas)  and  A
2 CONC nn  (Porter)  Gaylord. 
