1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Birth
2 CONT * “Joanna, b. 7 Nov. 1670.” – ''Vital Records from the New England Historical and Genealogical Register'' at [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/vital-records-from-the-new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/Reco
2 CONC rdDisplay?volumeId=21069&pageName=359&rId=1426569551 AmericanAncestors.org]. Early '''Records of Windsor, CT''', Copied and arranged by Samuel H. Parsons, Esq.
2 CONT * “Joanna, d. [John, Jr. & Joanna], b. Feb. 7, 1670” – ''Connecticut: Vital Records (The Barbour Collection), 1630-187''0 at [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/connecticut-vital-records-the-barbour-collection-1630-1870/R
2 CONC ecordDisplay?volumeId=12316&pageName=239&rId=138421871 AmericanAncestors.org], '''Vol. Name: Windsor CT'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marriage: Windsor, Connecticut
2 CONT * "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QP71-JMJW FamilySearch] (Sun Mar 10 19:13:24 UTC 2024); Entry for Joanna Porter and Peter Mills, 21 July 1692.
2 CONT * "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:78XZ-K7PZ FamilySearch] (Thu Mar 07 19:36:02 UTC 2024); Entry for Peter Mills and Joanna Porter, 21 July 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Death and Burial
2 CONT * Connecticut, U.S., Hale Collection of Cemetery Inscriptions and Newspaper Notices, 1629-1934 at [https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/2900/records/607493?tid=174604283&pid=132537272605&ssrc=pt Ancestry.com]:—
2 CONT ** "Mills, Jehannah, widow of Peter Mills, late of Windsor, died Dec. 2, 1760, age 90 yrs."
2 CONT ** [https://images.findagrave.com/photos/2009/236/40283457_125124672682.jpg FindAGrave¢®] Headstone Inscription: "In memory of Mrs Jehannah Mills. She Deceased this Life Decmbr ye 2 1760 Aged 90 years Being Late Widow of Mr Peter 
2 CONC Mills Late of Windsor for Deceased"
2 CONT '''—————————————————————————————————'''
2 CONT Much data about Joanna's life differs from the various sources available. Some say she was born in Hatfield, CT, some say Hatfield, MA, and others say Windsor, CT. Even her name. Her middle name is from her mother's family and is 
2 CONC sometime believed to be Gaylar. Her Christian name, Joanna, is how it is written today, but on her tombstone it's spelled Jehannah.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna married Peter Mills Jr. 21 Jun 1692 in Windsor. Although his father changed his name from the Dutch to be the first Peter Mills, Peter Jr. begins the Dutch line of Mills in this country. There is also branch from England as
2 CONC  well. The couple raised eight of their ten children in Windsor all boys but one. Two boys died in infancy. Three of their sons graduated Yale College and were ministers, one son was a lawyer, and several of them fought in the ski
2 CONC rmishes leading to the Revolutionary War as well as the French and Indian Wars. A number of her grandsons followed in the ministry and attended Yale; others were actives in the War for Independence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna's ancestors on her father's side were from England and instrumental in settling the country known as the Colonies. She preceded her husband in death. She was 90 years old when she died.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.c
2 CONC om/memorial/40283457/joanna-gaylord-mills Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 29 2020, 17:23:49 UTC''
2 CONT
