1 NOTE From “A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England, Vol. 3,” by James Savage, p. 114: TIMOTHY, Windsor, son of the first John, m. 20 Mar. 1689, Rebecca Porter, had Timothy, born 22 Feb. 1691; Ichabod, 25 Jan. 169
2 CONC 3; Lois, 15 Aug. 1695, died next yr.; Ann, 15 June 1698; Rebecca, 24 May 1700; Uriah, 8 May 1703;  and Obadiah, 4 Aug. 1705. Ten of this name had, in 1834, been graduated at the New England college chiefly at Yale.
