2 FORM png
2 TITL Person Details for Nathanell Loomys, "Connecticut, Births and Christenings, 1649-1906" — FamilySearch.org
1 NOTE From “A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England, Vol. 3,” by James Savage, p. 113: NATHANIEL, Windsor, prob. son of the first John, married 28 Nov. 1689, Ruth Porter, had Nathaniel, b. 7 Mar. 1695, Charles, 20
2 CONC  Feb. 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early Connecticut Probate Records, Vol. 3, p. 80
2 CONT                                 Page 261-2-3.
2 CONT         Loomis, Ensign Nathaniel, Bolton. Invt. £86-08-01. Taken 2 October, 1732, by Timothy Olcott and Daniel Griswold of Bolton. Will dated 6 January, 1729-30.
2 CONT         I, Nathaniel Loomis of Bolton, in the County of Hartford, do ordain this my last will and testament : I give unto my wife Ruth the use of 1-2 of my dwelling house and half of my improved land during her natural life; also 
2 CONC so much of my moveable estate as shall be necessary for her comfortable subsistence. I give to my son Nathaniel Loomis 1/2 of my right in the common and undivided land in Windsor besides what I have already given him by decd. I gi
2 CONC ve to my son Charles Loomis 1-2 of a parcell of land in Bolton I took as part of a 2nd division (the whole parcell is 16 acres, bounded east on Coventry). I give to my son Roger Loomis my 2nd division arising from my land. I give 
2 CONC to my son Jerijah Loomis my homelott I now live on, with the buildings and appurtenances thereof, as it is bounded west on the highway, south on land I have given to Roger Loomis, east on common land, and north on Charles Loomis a
2 CONC nd Col. Allyn, 1-2 of which after my wife's decease. Also I give him 1-2 of about 20 acres in Hebron I had in exchange with John Bishop ; also 1-2 of 15 acres of swamp north of John Bishop's land. I give to my daughter Ruth £80 to
2 CONC  be paid her by my son Jerijah Loomis when she is 18 years of age. The other half of my lands in Windsor Town Commons to be equally divided amongst my sons. I appoint my son Nathaniel sole executor.
2 CONT Witness : John Bissell,                        NATHANIEL LOOMIS, LS.
2 CONT Samuel Brown, John Bishop.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Court Record, Page 84 - 6 March, 1732-3: Will exhibited by Nathaniel Loomis, executor.
2 CONT                         Page 313-14.
2 CONT         Loomis, Lt. Nathaniel, Windsor. Invt. £517-05-03. Taken 21
2 CONT October, 1733, by William Wolcott, Hezekiah Porter and Samuel Ban-
2 CONT croft. Will dated 26 May, 1729.
