1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Howell-161
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Howell immigrated to New England as a child during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT "MAJ. EDMUND HOWELL (EDWARD1) was baptized January 26, 1633-4[1] in Marsh Gibbon, Buckinghamshire, England, and died before 3 Dec 1697 in Cape May County, New Jersey. 
2 CONT '''He married (1) SARAH JUDSON 11 Nov 1664''' in Southampton, Suffolk County, New York, daughter of JOSEPH JUDSON and SARAH PORTER. She was born 02 Mar 1644/45 in Stratford, Connecticut, and died 29 Aug 1688 in Southampton, Suffol
2 CONC k County, New York. 
2 CONT '''He married (2) KATHARINE BARWICK 29 Jun 1696''' in Lewes, Delaware."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Edward Howell and Eleanor [Maier?]. He passed away about 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # "Corrections and Additions: Howell" New York Genealogical and Biographical Record Volume 106 (1975) page 218
2 CONT # The Howell Family website http://edwardhowellfamily.org/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=6&Itemid=4
2 CONT # Jacobus, Donald Lines. The Judson Family of Stratford and Woodbury, Conn., The American Genealogist (The American Genealogist, Barrington, RI, 1944) Vol. 21, Page 269. https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Space:TAG
2 CONT # The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records (NEHGS, Boston, 2011) Vol. Stratford. https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Space:The_Barbour_Collection
2 CONT # Edmund Howell in the Connecticut, U.S., Town Marriage Records, pre-1870 (Barbour Collection)
2 CONT # The Anderson, Perrine, Barbour-Smith, Howell-Clark, Porter and Savery families
