1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married: 18 August 1680 (geni.com research).
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=14954540
2 CONT
2 CONT Field  	Main Profile  	Alternate Data
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Location 	Stratford, Fairfield, Connecticut, USA 	Wethersfield,Hartford,Connecticut,USA 	Wethersfield,Hartford,Connecticut,USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Date 	11/3/1717 	2/25/1717 	2/25/1717
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Location 	Stratford 	Stratford,Fairfield,Connecticut,USA 	Stratford,Fairfield,Connecticut,USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The descendants of William and Elizabeth Tuttle, who came from old to New England in 1635, and settled in New Haven in 1639, with numerous biographical notes and sketches : also, some account of the descendants of John Tuttle, of 
2 CONC Ipswich; and Henry Tuthill, of Hingham, Mass. (1883)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil01tutt#page/n303/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT William Tuttle & Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hannah Tuttle, b. England, 1632-3; d. in Hartford, Conn., Aug. 9, 1683, a. 50; bu. in the old Center chh. graveyard on Main st., where her memorial stone is still standing, among others of the Welles family; its inscription qui
2 CONC te plain;* m. 1619, John, only s. of William and Margaret Pantry (Pantree), b. abt. 1629; freeman of Harft., 1650; will dated Sept. 1, 1653; inv. taken Nov. 25, same yr.; chil., John and Hannah --Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Gen. Dict. of New Eng. sup. her dau. of Richard Tuttle of Boston, on what ground I have been unable to discover. Circumstances all point to the dau. of William Tuttle of New Haven, and the gravestone establishes the identity
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT * William Pantry came over in 1635; wealthy and advanced in years; selectman of Hartf., 1640, again in 1645; constable in 1648.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil01tutt#page/n305/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT not named, prob. posthumous; m. (2) June 23, 1654, Thomas, s. of Thomas and Elizabeth (Deming) Welles, jr., b. abt. 1627; Quartermaster under Maj. John Mason, 1658; Dep. Mag. at Hartf., 1662-3, and is said to be named as a grantee
2 CONC  in the Royal Charter of Conn. (prob. his f.) He was rep. May 1663, assistant 1668, and was killed sm. yr. by a fall from a cherry tree. Inv. taken in Hartf. Aug. 20, 1668, (english pound)1090 19s. 6d.; chattels, (english pound)59
2 CONC 0. Adm. given to wid. Hannah. He was the largest and tallest man of his time in Hartf.; of strong mind and estimable character. Inv. of est. of Mrs. Hannah Welles exh. Sept. 6, 1683; divided by the court, to John Pantry double por
2 CONC tion, and to all the rest of Mrs. Welles' chil. equal portions. Mrs. Bidwell and Mrs. Meeks to receive each a piece of gold and a gold ring that their mother before her sickness did allot and give them; the two younger ss. to be c
2 CONC lothed out of the est. before distribution. 10. chil. b. in Wethersfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT I. John, bap. March 17, 1659; m. Abigail Mix.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Hannah, b. Aug., 1652; d. unm. 1672, according to Savage; 1675, according to W. S. Porter; but Miss Mary N. Talcott says she d. before Aug., 1671, as an account of the est. of Hannah Pantry was exh. to the court of probate in 
2 CONC Hrtf. in Aug., 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Mary, b. prob. after Sept. 1, 1653, when the f. made his will; m. Nathaniel Mix.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. REBECCA WELLES, b. May, 1655; m. Aug. 13, 1680, Capt. JAMES JUDSON.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Thomas, b. Oct., 1657; m. 1689, Mary Blackleach.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Sarah, b. April, 1659; m. Nov. 7, 1678, John Bidwell, jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Ichabod, Nov., 1669; m. Sept. 4, 1684, Sarah Way.
2 CONT
2 CONT VIII. Samuel, Oct., 1662; m. Ruth Judson, sis. to James Judson.
2 CONT
2 CONT IX. Jonathan, b. Sept., 1664; d. s. i. abt. 1690; killed by piece of block falling on his head. Thomas Welles adm. his est., which the court of assistants, on petition of all but the admr., ordered distributed, Nov., 1690, to Thom
2 CONC as, Ichabod, Samuel and Joseph Welles, John Bidwell, for his wf. Sarah and James Judson, for his wf. Rebecca; Thomas appealed, May 1691, claiming te est. of his bro. according to the English law, without avail.
2 CONT
2 CONT X. Joseph, b. Aug., 1667; d. 1698; m. Elizabeth, dau. of Eleazer Way. 1. John, d. y. 2. Joseph, d. y. 3. Joshua, d. y. 4. Elizabeth, b. 1696; m. William Powell of Hartf. 1. Elizabeth, m. Nov. 4, 1750, Fletcher Ranney of Mid., Conn
2 CONC ., who d. Dec. 14, 1772, a. 47. She d. June 14, 1785, a. 60.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil01tutt#page/n343/mode/2up page 102
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. REBECCA WELLES, b. May, 1655; d. Nov. 5, 1717; m. Aug. 13, 1680, JAMES JUDSON, b. April 24, 1650, s. of Lieut. Joseph and Sarah (Porter) Judson of Windsor, Conn. He was a deputy to the gen. court. Lieut. of dragoons, and Capt;
2 CONC  res. Stratford, Conn. He d. Feb. 25, 1721; m. (2) Nov. 20, 1718 (a cous. of his 1st wf.), Ann, dau. of Samuel Wells and wid. of James Steel of Wethersfield; s. i.
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Hannah, b. May 30, 1681; m. Capt. James Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Sarah, b. Feb 16, 1683; m. Oct. 12, 1708, Rev. Natahaniel Chauncey.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Rebecca, b. Feb. 25, 1684; d. Feb. 26, 1698, a. 14 yrs.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. William, b. Jan. 4, 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Joseph, b. June 10, 1687; m. March 14, 1709, Hannah, dau. of Henry and Deborah Hawley of Stratford, b. Oct. 7, 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. James, b. April 3, 1689; m. Dec. 18, 1727, Martha Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Phebe, b. Oct. 12, 1691; m. June 19, 1714, Joseph Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT VIII. David, b. Aug. 7, 1693, m. March 29, 1713, Phebe Stiles.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
