1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Capt. David Judson'''  August 7, 1693-May 5, 1761
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents: '''Capt. James Judson April 24, 1650-Feb. 25, 1721 and Rebecca Welles May 1655-Feb. 25, 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wife '''Phoebe Stiles March 25, 1698-May 20, 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children: '''
2 CONT # Phoebe d.1758
2 CONT # David 1715
2 CONT # Abel
2 CONT # Agur 1726
2 CONT # Ruth 1726
2 CONT # Daniel 1728
2 CONT # Sarah 1730
2 CONT # Abner 1733
2 CONT # Betty
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain David Judson House''' was built by David Judson, a resident of Stratford, Connecticut, in 1723 . The 1723 house was built on the stone foundation and incorporates part of the chimney of the original house built in 1639 
2 CONC by Judson's great grandfather William. The first floor, now the cellar, is above ground level and contains a massive central stone chimney which was built with lug poles. It is believed that the cellar was used as slave quarters d
2 CONC uring the early 18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain David Judson House was listed on the National Register of Historic Places on March 20, 1973. It is also included in the Stratford Center Historic District, which was listed on the NRHP in 1978.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources:'''
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_David_Judson_House
2 CONT * http://www.stratfordhistoricalsociety.com/
2 CONT * http://historicbuildingsct.com/?p=5639
