2 CONT According to "Deacon George Clark(e) of Milford, Connecticut and Some of His Descendants," by George Clarke Bryant, 1949:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Clark filed a plea in the New Haven County Court on 7 Aug 1690 that the will of his father ("Deacon" George Clark) was void in law by the death of the exectutrix (wife Sarah) before the death of the testator, and also that 
2 CONC it was defective and imperfect in sundry respects.
2 CONT
2 CONT A transcript of Thomas Clark's will can be found in the above mentioned book.
