1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr03/rr03_115.html#P40974 Family of Sergt. John Curtis (1795) & Elizabeth] [Curtis]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Curtis. Born on 30 Sep 1652 in Stratford, CT.64 Benjamin died bef 4 Oct 1733 in Stratford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin first married Sarah [Curtis].
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Benjamin and Sarah Curtis:
2 CONT *     i. Sarah, b. 24 May 1679 at Stratford.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 Mar 1680/1 when Benjamin was 28, he second married Esther Judson, daughter of Lieut. Joseph Judson (ca 1618/9-8 Oct 1690) & Sarah Porter (ca 1624/5-16 Mar 1696/7), in Stratford, CT.64 Born on 20 Aug 1660 in Stratford, CT.64 
2 CONC Esther died in Stratford, CT, on 27 Aug 1713; she was 53.64
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Benjamin and Esther (Judson) Curtis:
2 CONT *     i. John Curtis, b. 18 Feb 1681/2, d. between 3 Sep 1745 and 19 Sep 1745, m. 1st at Stratford 19 Feb 1706/7 Margaret Pickett (b. 14 Aug 1686, d. 8 Oct 1714 at Stratford, dau. of Daniel & Mary Pickett), m. 2nd at Stratford 3 N
2 CONC ov 1715 Hannah Johnson (b. 6 Dec 1689, dau. of Ebenezer Johnson of Derby), m. 3rd after 1734 Rebecca Blackleach (dau. of Richard Blackleach, widow of John Allyn & Benjamin Rumsey);
2 CONT *     ii. David Curtis, b. Nov 1682, m. 1st at Stratford 26 Nov 1719 Dinah Wakeley (d. Jun 1725 at Stratford, dau. of James & Hannah (Gifford) Wakeley);
2 CONT *     iii. Ruth Curtis, b. 11 Jan 1683/4, d. 23 Apr 1721, m. at Stratford 15 Nov 1705 John Thompson (d. 20 Jul 1765);
2 CONT *     iv. James Curtis, b. 4 May 1686, d. 1 Nov 1765 at Durham, CT, m. ca. 1708 Hannah Coe (b. 14 Apr 1679, dau. of John Coe);
2 CONT *     v. Dinah Curtis, b. Oct 1689, m. at Stratford 26 Jun 1718 Nathan Beardsley (b. 7 Oct 1686 at Stratford);
2 CONT *     vi. Anna, b. ca. 1697;
2 CONT *     vii. Hester Curtis, d. 26 Aug 1701; and
2 CONT *     viii. Esther Curtis, bp. 10 Feb 1706
2 CONT
2 CONT Married on 1 Dec 1714	Stratford, Fairfield, Connecticut to Bathsheba Tomlinson.  She was widow of Ephraim Stiles, and dau. of Henry Tomlinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Benjamin_Curtis_%287%29 WeRelate]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Curtis, in Jacobus, Donald Lines. History and Genealogy of the Families of Old Fairfield. (New Haven, Conn.: The Tuttle, Morehouse & Taylor Company, 1930-1932), 1:172-73.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Curtis, Benjamin, s. of John. Deputy (Stratford), Oct. 1697, Jan. 1698, Oct. 1700, Oct. 1703, May 1705, May 1706, May, Oct. and Dec. 1707, Oct. and Nov. 1711, Oct. 1712, Oct. 1714, May and Oct. 1721, Oct. 1722; Naval Officer, Por
2 CONC t of Stratford, May 1714.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Born at Stratford, 30 Sept. 1652; d. there in 1733. Adm'n was granted, 19 June 1733, to John Curtis and Zachariah Booth. Married (1) at Stratford, 23 Mar. 1680/1, Esther Judson. She was dau. of Joseph, b. 20 Aug. 1660. Mrs. Heste
2 CONC r, wife of Benjamin, d. 27 Aug. 1713. Mr. Benjamin m. (2) at Stratford, 1 Dec. 1714, Mis't Bathsheba Stiles. She was widow of Ephraim Stiles, and dau. of Henry Tomlinson, b. 3 Jan. 1661/2. A prenuptial agreement with her, dated 27
2 CONC  Nov. 1714, appointed Samuel Walker trustee, and gave her power to dispose at her own will of personal estate and negroes. She d. 9 Feb. 1735 ae. 74 (g. s.).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography == Benjamin Curtis, son of John Curtis was born September 30, 1652 at Stratford, Connecticut. His last name at birth is shown in the records asCurtis.<ref name=BCStratford>[http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/c
2 CONC onnecticut-vital-records-to-1870-the-barbour-collection/image/?volumeId=12612&pageName=41&rId=143357204 ''Connecticut Vital Records to 1870''], (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England HistoricGenealogical Society, 201
2 CONC 1.) From original typescripts, Lucius BarnesBarbour Collection, 1928. Reference Stratford Volume, page 41</ref><ref name=Cothren3>Cothren, William. History of Woodbury Vol III Historyof Ancient Woodbury, Connecticut From the First
2 CONC  Indian Deed in 1659 to 1879. Woodbury, Conn.: Publ by William Cothren, 1879.  [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=hvd.hxtdf7;view=1up;seq=696 Deaths pp 689/90]  [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=hvd.hxtdf7;view=1up;seq=
2 CONC 664 Children’s births p. 658]
2 CONT </ref>
2 CONT Benjamin married (1) Esther JUDSON on 22 Mar 1681 in Stratford, Fairfield, CT.<ref name=Cothren3 /><ref name=BCStratford /> daughter of Joseph<ref name=FoOF /> He married (2) Mrs Bathsheba Stiles 1 Dec 1714.<ref name=Cothren3 /><r
2 CONC ef name=BCStratford /> widow of Ephraim Stiles and daughter of Henry Tomlinson.<ref name=FoOF />  He died in Stratford 1733; administration of his estate was granted 19June 1733.<ref name=FoOF />    Stratford deeds volume 5 shows 
2 CONC that on19 Sept 1733, John and David Curtiss, John Thompson, Zachariah Booth,Nathan Beardslee and Dinah his wife, and Daniel Beach and Esther his wife, all of Stratford, and James Curtiss of Durham, and Ephraim Hawley and Phebe his
2 CONC  wife of New Milford, made mutual distribution of the estate of their father Mr. Benjamin Curtiss, and stated "we are the only heirs." He was a Deputy from Stratford on several occasions and was a naval officer at the Port of Stra
2 CONC tford May 1714.<ref name=FoOF>Donald Lines Jacobus, History and Genealogy of the Families of Old Fairfield, CD-Local and Family Histories: CT, 1600's - 1800's, (Produced in collaboration with the Genealogical Publishing Company, 2
2 CONC 000), vol 1, pp 170, 171,585.</ref>
2 CONT
