2 CONT == Biography ==*Additional daughter, Anna (Curtiss) Booth [[Curtis-1975|(Curtis-1975)]], who married [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Booth-953 Zechariah Booth], had a profile with different parents. Her parentage is not 100% certai
2 CONC n.*Josiah CURTIS <ref>Donald Lines Jacobus, Families of Ancient New Haven ([CD]Baltimore, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1981[originally]Rome, N.Y. and New Haven, Conn., 1922-1932), vol 1, p 148.</ref><ref>Genealogical Notes o
2 CONC r Contributions to the Family History of Some of theFirst Settlers of Connecticut and Massachusetts, Hartford, 1856; Reprinted by Genealogical Publishing Co., p. 137.</ref> was born <ref><span id='Curtiss'></span>Curtiss, Frederic
2 CONC  Haines. ''[[Space:A Genealogy of the Curtiss Family|A Genealogy of the Curtiss Family]]'' (Rockwell and Churchill, Boston, 1903-1953), p. 5.</ref> 30 Aug 1662 in Stratford, Fairfield, Connecticut, British Colonial America. *He di
2 CONC ed <ref>Frederic Haines Curtiss, The Curtiss Family, p. 5.</ref>1745 in Stratford, Fairfield, Connecticut, British Colonial America. 
2 CONT *Josiah married Mary BEACH.*BIRTH: Town of Stratford, Fairfield County, Connecticut Volume 1 (1650-1684), page 28, Josiah Curtiss the sonne of William Curtiss was borne the 30th day of Agust 1662:*MARRIAGE: Town of Stratford, Fair
2 CONC field County, Connecticut Volume 2, part 2 (1684-1729), Curtis, Josiah and Abigail Judson were married July 1692*BIOGRAPHY: A Genealogy of the Curtiss Family [Boston: Rockwell and Churchill Press, 1903], page 12. Josiah Curtiss' w
2 CONC as appointed Captain of the Train Band in May 1714, by the General Court of Stratford. In 1716, he was deputy to the General Court. On 29th of December 1725, liberty was granted to Josiah Curtiss and John Wilcoxson Jr to erect a s
2 CONC awmill on the halfway river.*WILL: Probated at Fairfield County, Connecticut on the 20th of November 1745
2 CONT * Fact: Residence   Stratford
2 CONT
