2 CONT # Death: 14 AUG 1723
2 CONT
2 CONT # Education: 1714 Yale College
2 CONT
2 CONT # _DEG: 1723 Honorary degree of A.M. from Harvard
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Willard supplied the church at Norwich, Conn., a short time in September, 1716. He was settled minister of the church at Sunderland January 1, 1718/9, where he remained about three years. He sold his lands there May 4, 1722. H
2 CONC e had in the meantime removed to Rutland; began to preach there July 2, 1721. But when he was about to be installed there he was slain by Indians in one of their swift attacks, August 14, 1723. For details, see "Willard Memoir."
2 CONT
2 CONT His estate was settled first by his wife as administratrix, then by his brother Samuel Willard.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man of earnestness and devotion; beloved and honored by the people of his two parishes, and the death of such a man was a great loss to the infant state.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: WILLARD GENEALOGY, SEQUEL TO WILLARD MEMORIAL MATERIALS GATHERED CHIEFLY BY JOSEPH WILLARD AND CHARLES WILKES WALKER EDITED AND COMPLETED BY CHARLES HENRY POPE;    PRINTED FOR THE WILLARD FAMILY ASSOCIATION, BOSTON, MASS.,
