2 CONT
2 CONT # ID: I23722
2 CONT
2 CONT # Name: Joseph Willard 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sex: M
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: 23 JUL 1696 in Saybrook, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Death: 14 AUG 1723
2 CONT
2 CONT # Education: 1714 Yale College
2 CONT
2 CONT # _DEG: 1723 Honorary degree of A.M. from Harvard
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mr. Willard supplied the church at Norwich, Conn., a short time in September, 1716. He was settled minister of the church at Sunder and January 1, 1718?9, where he remained about three years. He sold his lands there May 4, 172
2 CONC 2. He had in the meantime removed to Rutland; began to preach there July 2, 1721. But when he was about to be installed there he was slain by Indians in one of their swift attacks, August 14, 1723. For details, see "Willard Memoir
2 CONC ."
2 CONT
2 CONT     His estate was settled first by his wife as administratrix, then by his brother Samuel Willard.
2 CONT
2 CONT     He was a man of earnestness and devotion; beloved and honored by the people of his two parishes, and the death of such a man was a great loss to. the infant state.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Source:
2 CONT
