2 CONT Name: Joseph WILLARD 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Reverend 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 23 JUL 1696 in Saybrook, Saybrook, Connecticut 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 14 AUG 1723 in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Number: 2/592a/313
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Samuel WILLARD b: 19 SEP 1658 in Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Sarah CLARK b: 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Susanna LYNDE b: 11 APR 1700 in Saybrook, Saybrook, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 17 AUG 1718 in Sunderland, Franklin, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT  William WILLARD b: JAN 1720 in Sunderland, Franklin, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joseph WILLARD b: 1723 in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Joseph Willard was the son of Samuel Willard and Sarah Clarke. His father was town clerk and in 1696 had command of the fort in Saybrook.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Willard graduated Yale College 1714 and Master of Arts, Harvard College in 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Willard settled first at Sunderland. When his relationship with the church in that town was dissolved, he removed to Rutland, NH where he had previously sold his inherited estate. He purchased another "on the Meeting-house Hill
2 CONC " in January 1722, After preaching in Rutland for a considerable time, he was invited to settle there in the ministry, which he accepted. On the 23rd of August 1723, before the time appointed for his induction into office, there w
2 CONC as a sudden and furious Indian attack upon the town and they fell upon Mr. Willard who was engaged in hunting a good distance from his house. He put up a brave resistance but was overpowered by numbers, slain and scalped. His scal
2 CONC p was taken to Quebec.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Willard left Susanna a widow with one son, William. A posthumous son Joseph was born three months later. The governor granted each of his sons 300 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1760, Joseph and Susanna's son Joseph was captured by Indians, along with his wife and children.
