1 OCCU Shoemaker. Elected Deacon of the First Church of Hartford, Connecticut March, 1734. Held office until his death. A weaver by trade. In May, 1721 Appointed Ensign of the North company or train band of Hartford.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1669 Hartford Hartford County Connecticut, USA Death: 	Nov., 1747 Hartford Hartford County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of William & Susannah Goodwin, he was a deacon of the church in Hartford and married Mehitabel, daughter of Samuel Porter of Hadley. Their children: Hezekiah d. Jan. 14, 1776* aged 87. Isaac d. Dec. 28, 1773 aged 82. Abrah
2 CONC am d. Jan. 6, 1771 Litchfield, CT Stephen d. Dec. 5, 1785 Simsbury, CT Eleazer m. Hannah Easton, d. Jan. 19, 1766  Mehitabel m. Joseph Goodrich Dec. 23, 1714 Bennedicta m. Jacob Goodrich Sept. 12, 1717.
2 CONT *Death date for Hezekiah Sept. 5, 1768 (from "Goodwins of Hartford", p. 144 Joanna Ruth m. ____ Bird Alice m. ____ Caldwell. (Goodwin's "Gen. Notes"), p. 15 
2 CONT
