1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69542312/nathaniel-porter Nathaniel Porter - Find A Grave - MEMORIAL ID	69542312]
2 CONT -----
2 CONT Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW HAMPSHIRE.<br/>
2 CONT  http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A091187<br/>
2 CONT DAR Ancestor # A091187
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Porter and Elizabeth Storrs, daughter to Mr. Samuel Storrs, deceased, m. September 10, 1730  Pre the = BIRTHS, BAPTISMS MARRIAGES AND DEATHS FROM THE RECORDS OF THE TOWN AND CHURCHES IN MANSFIELD, CONNECTICUT 1703-1850<b
2 CONC r/>
2 CONT http://dunhamwilcox.net/ct/mansfield_m3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT Nathaniel Porter Born: 26/Aug/1709 Hadley, Hampshire, MA <br/>
2 CONT   Died: 05/Nov/1779 Hatfield, Hampshire, MA <br/>
2 CONT      FATHER Experience Porter MOTHER Abigail Williams<br/>
2 CONT WIFE Elizabeth Storrs<br/>
2 CONT CHILDREN:<br/>
2 CONT # Samuel Porter b. 16/Jun/1731
2 CONT # Eunice Porter b. 23/Jun/1733
2 CONT # Hannah Porter b. 26/Apr/1735
2 CONT # Nathaniel Porter b. 18/Apr/1737
2 CONT # Theoda Porter b. 16/Sep/1739
2 CONT # Martha Porter b. 09/Nov/1741
2 CONT # Mehitable Porter b. 22/Dec/1743
2 CONT # Elizabeth Porter b. 02/Jul/1746
2 CONT # Nathaniel Porter b. 24/Nov/1748
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~brookefamily/porternathaniel.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ===========================         
2 CONT Descendants of the Porter Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Elizabeth Porter, relict of Lieut. Nathaniel Porter, she died July 19, 1808, aged 99 years 11 months; next the grave of this almost centenarian there still stands a headstone the inscription wholly illegible. It doubtless mar
2 CONC ks the grave of her husband, Nathaniel Porter, son of Experience3 and Abigail (Williams) Porter (Samuel,2 John1), born Aug. 16, 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT The Porter and Storrs genealogies give the pedigree of all born to those names whose epitaphs were found.  Lieut. Nathaniel4 Porter (Experience,3 Samuel,2 John1), born Mansfield, Conn., Aug. 16, 1709; died Lebanon [Grafton County]
2 CONC , N. H.; married, Sept. 30, 1730, Elizabeth Storrs, daughter of Samuel,2 Samuel,1 emigrant from England; born Mansfield, Aug. 1, 1708; died Lebanon, July 19,1808. Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Samuel,5 b. June 16, 1731. <br/>
2 CONT ii. Eunice, b. June 23, 1733.<br/>
2 CONT   iii. Hannah, b. Apr. 26, 1735. <br/>
2 CONT iv. Nathaniel, b. Apr. 18, 1737; d. ___, 1747. <br/>
2 CONT v. Theoda, b. Sept. 16, 1739; m. Joseph Estabrook.<br/>
2 CONT   vi. Martha, b. Nov. 9, 1741; m. Jedediah Hubbard, <br/>
2 CONT vii. Mehitable, b. Dec. 22, 1743. <br/>
2 CONT viii. Elizabeth, b. July 2, 1746; m. John Griswold. <br/>
2 CONT ix. Nathaniel b. Nov. 24, 1748; m. Olive Hall... <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.accessgenealogy.com/newhampshire/cemeteries/descendants_of_the_porter_family.htm
2 CONT -----
2 CONT other info:<br/>
2 CONT Gender: Male<br/>
2 CONT Birth: August 16, 1709<br/>
2 CONT   Mansfield, Tolland, Connecticut<br/>
2 CONT Death: November 04, 1779 (70) <br/>
2 CONT Lebanon, New Hampshire<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Porter of Lebanon N. H.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a native of this town from whence his father Dea. Experience Porter removed in 1725 with his family to Mansfield, Con. In 1764 he settled in Lebanon N. H. Returning from a visit to his friends in Con. he died suddenly in Ha
2 CONC tfield, Nov. 4, 1779, and was interred here by his relative, Hon. Eleazer Porter, AE 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69542312/nathaniel-porter
