1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Desc of John Porter, Vol. I, pp 56-57: [255.] James Porter, son of Ichabod Porter (50) and Dorcas Marsh, married July 4, 1737, Hannah Waite. [BENJAMIN WAITE, of Hatfield, Mass., 1663, married June 8, 1670, Martha L
2 CONC eonard, born February 15, 1649, daughter of Capt. JOHN LEONARD, of Springfield, Mass., from England, who married September 4, 1640, Sarah Heald, born in England, daughter of JOHN HEALD, who came from Berwick-on-Tweed, England, wit
2 CONC h his wife Dorcas, to Concord, Mass., in 1639-40, and died May 24, 1662. Capt. John Leonard was killed by Indians in 1676; his widow died November 23, 1711. Benjamin Waite was killed by Indians in the attack on Deerfield, February
2 CONC  29, 1704. Mrs. Martha Waite was carried prisoner to Canada, where she died January 22, 1678. Second Generation, Joseph Waite, born November 11, 1688, married (first wife) November 19, 1713, Hannah Billings. (RICHARD BILLINGS came
2 CONC  from England to Hartford, Conn., in 1639, with his wife Margery. He removed, in 1659, to Hatfield, Mass., where he died March 23, 1679. Mrs. Margery Billings died December 5, 1679. Second Generation, Samuel Billings, born about 1
2 CONC 640, married November 8, 1661, Sarah Fellows, born about 1642, daughter of RICHARD FELLOWS, from England to Hartford, Conn., with his wife Ursula, and who removed in 1659, to Springfield, Mass., and thence to Northampton, Mass., i
2 CONC n 1660; Hatfield, Mass., in 1663, and was killed by Indians August 25, 1675. Samuel Billings died February 1, 1678. Mrs. Sarah Billings married (second husband) October 9, 1678, Samuel Belding, Jr., of Hatfield, Mass., and died Fe
2 CONC bruary 5, 1713. Third Generation, Samuel Billings, born January 8, 1665, married November 8, 1686, Hannah Wright. (THOMAS WRIGHT came from England in 1636; removed to Weathersfield, Conn., 1639, and died April --, 1670. Second Gen
2 CONC eration, Samuel Wright, born in England, married September 29, 1659, Mary Butler, born (???), 1663, daughter of RICHARD BUTLER, from England to Cambridge, Mass.; who removed to Hartford, Conn., 1640; representative 1656, and died 
2 CONC August 6, 1684. Samuel Wright died February 1, 1690. Third Generation, Hannah Wright, born (???), 1667, married November 8, 1686, Samuel Billings. She died July 15, 1716. Fourth Generation, Hannah Billings, born (???), 1687, marri
2 CONC ed November 19, 1713, Joseph Waite. She died July 15, 1716. He died (???), 1780. Third and Fifth Generations, Hannah Waite, born July 8, 1716, married July 4, 1737, James Porter. Mrs. Hannah Porter died, (???), 1740. He married (s
2 CONC econd wife) Eunice Belding. (RICHARD BELDING (or Belden) came from England to Cambridge, Mass. in 1632; removed to Hartford, Conn., in 1640; representative 1656 to 1660; deacon; and died August 6, 1684. Second Generation, John Bel
2 CONC ding, born (???), 1630, married April 24, 1657, Lydia (???). Third Generation, Samuel Belding, born (???), 1658, married (???), 1688, Elizabeth Seymour. (RICHARD SEYMOUR came from England to Hartford, Conn., in 1639; Farmington, C
2 CONC onn., in 1652; removed to Norwalk, Conn., in 1656, where he died. Mrs. Mercy Seymour died (???). Second Generation, Zechariah Seymour, born --, 1642, married --, 1666. Third Generation, Elizabeth Seymour, born (???), 1670, married
2 CONC  (???), 1688, Samuel Belding. Fourth Generation, Gideon Belding, born (???), 1693, married (???), 1713, Eunice Butler. (RICHARD BUTLER came from England to Cambridge, Mass., in 1632. He removed to Hartford, Conn.; representative 1
2 CONC 656 to 1660; deacon, and died August 6, 1684. Second Generation, Joseph Butler, born (???), 1648, married (???), 1667, Mary Goodrich, daughter of WILLIAM GOODRICH, from England. Joseph Butler died December 10, 1732, aged eighty-fo
2 CONC ur. Mrs. Mary Butler died June 1, 1735. Third Generation, William Butler, born (???), 1670, married May 23, 1695, Hannah Hills, daughter of WILLIAM HILLS, of Hartford, Conn. Fourth Generation, Eunice Butler, born June 12, 1696, ma
2 CONC rried (???), 1713, Gideon Belding. Fifth Generation, Eunice Belding, born (???), 1714, married (???), 1743, James Porter. Their children were [being of the fifth generation:] 905. Hannah Porter, born November 23, 1745, married Abi
2 CONC el Allis. 906. James Porter, born (???), 1748, married Penelope Montague. 907. Jonathan Porter, born April 16, 1752, married Ruth Chapin. 908. Submit Porter, born March 15, 1754, married Seth Chapin. 909. David Porter, born July 5
2 CONC , 1757, married Sarah Nimms. 910. Silas Porter, born August 28, 1759, married Mary Graves. 
