1 NAME Capt. Ebenezer Grant
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Edwards Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY South Windsor
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 GRAD
2 DATE 1726
2 PLAC Yale University
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 OCT 1706
2 ADDR
3 CITY Windsor
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 MAR 1797
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Large ship owner and builder, innkeeper, leading citizen, surveyor, deputy sheriff, constable, selectman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1777, General Prescott imprisoned in his house. Buried at God's Acre, South Windsor, CT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Ebenezer Grant, born October 1706 at Windsor Conn.,  became a leading merchant of the vicinity, largely engaged in trade with the West Indies. He was appointed a captain in the Connecticut Militia in 1742. In 1776-77, Loyalist New
2 CONC  Jersey Gov. William Franklin (son of U.S. Ambassador Benjamin Franklin) was under confinement at Grant's house, by order of the Provincial Congress of New Jersey, as a political enemy.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Captain Ebenezer Grant was a direct descendant of Mathew Grant (1601-1681), the first person bearing the name Grant to settle in this country. After gaining his diploma from Yale on October 19, 1726, Ebenezer soon became a leading
2 CONC  citizen in Old East Windsor, serving as clerk of the Congregational Church from 1733-1767, treasurer of the committee for the new church building, 1761, town surveyor, selectman, constable, grand juror and deputy sheriff. He serv
2 CONC ed as Captain under the King during King George's War, in the French and Indian War, and against the King in the fight for Independence. Shortly after graduating from Yale, he started business in the West Indies trade, soon becomi
2 CONC ng the largest merchant in the area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Grant at age 31 married Ann Elsworth (1712-1783), daughter of Lt. John Elsworth and Ester White Elsworth of Ellington, on November 10, 1737. "She was a noble spirited lady of good estate, and well known for her beneficien
2 CONC t acts." Of their six children, only two survived childhood, Roswell (1746-1834) and Ann (1748-1838).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer married again at age 78. This time to Mrs. Jemima Ellsworth (1721-1790), daughter of Joshua and Hannah Leavitt, the widow of David Ellsworth, on June 24, 1784.
1 FAMC @F6000000011366930042@
1 RFN geni:6000000008531420376
1 SUBM @S6000000000590416963@
