1 NOTE {geni:about_me} EBENEZER DEMING, (son of John 1) born in Wethersfield, Conn.; died 2 May 1705, in Wethersfield; married 16 Jul. 1677 in Wethersfield, Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth-date of Ebenezer Deming has never been discovered. It is supposed that he was the youngest son of John Deming, and that he was born about 1659. In 1698 he received a deed of land in Wethersfield from his brother David De
2 CONC ming of Cambridge, and inherited from his father other land in the vicinity. In the record of his marriage the family name of his wife is obliterated, and it has not been discovered from any other source. In the distribution of hi
2 CONC s estate, his widow and all of his children including his two sons-in-law Talcott and Wright, are named.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BORN IN WETHERSFIELD, CONN:
2 CONT # 23. Ebenezer, b. 5 May 1678.
2 CONT # 24. John, b. 26 Jul. 1679.
2 CONT # Sarah, b. 6 Jan. 1681; m. 1 Apr. 1701 Joseph Talcott, and d. 19 Mar. 1755. 
2 CONT # Prudence, b. about 1688; m. 4 Oct. 1705 Thos. Wright, and d. 24 Oct. 1706. 
2 CONT # 25. Ephraim, b. about 1685.
2 CONT # 26. Josiah, b. about 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
