0 @N6000000000390647542@ NOTE Underwood is a Scottish and English place name that described the man who lived at the edge of the woods, from Middle English under + wood (both terms survived to modern day with the same meanings).  It is also a place name that d
1 CONC escribed the man who left any of the several settlements by that name to settle in a new location.
