1 CONT Hazel Atterbury Spraker, The Boone Family,  (1922 (reissued by Genealogical Publishing Company, 1993)), 201, "Giles Jones, a native of Wales, came to America in the British Army, and was captured at the battle of Eutah Springs.  W
1 CONC hen exchanged he sought the first opportunity to desert the British and join the American Standard.  He subsequently settled in Kentucky and later went to Missouri, where he died in Callaway County in 1838, aged 82, and his wife I
1 CONC sabella having died five years before.  Two of his children were Dr. John Jones who married Minerva Callaway (363), and Cenia Jones who married John Scholl, the above subject."  Cites Draper Mss. 22 S 269-74.  
