1 CONT [V136T0677.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Widow of Colonel Porter, daughter of Colonel Tasker, one time Chancellor of Ireland - She was relative of Countess of  Marnington, and her sister Prudence, well known figures in the aristocracy of the period. Year of birth changed
1 CONC  to 1632 from 162 7 based on data from C. RichardBugg's research. However, it should be further researched for more accuracy.[V19T1366.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Ref:
1 CONT [1] The Will of Magdalen Pollock, March ye 20th, 1727, Somerset Co., MD.
1 CONT [2] "Polk Family and Kinsmen", Revised Edition, Page 8.
1 CONT [3] "Polks of North Carolina & Tennessee".
1 CONT Magdalen Tasker was married for a short time to Colonel Porter who was in the parliamentary forces of Oliver Cromwell. After Col. Porter'sdeath, Magdalen married Captain Robert Bruce Pollok. Magdalen was theyoungest daughter of Co
1 CONC l. Roger Tasker, a Chancellor in Ireland, whose seat was Broomfield Castle, above Londonderry. Magdalen inherited from her father, a large estate called "Moneen", which embraced six hundred Cunningham acres, with a fine mansion on
1 CONC  it. It lay close to  thelittle villiage of Strabane. Magdalen emigrated to America with her husband and children.
