0 @N6000000001503913876@ NOTE
1 CONT Note: Walter Gaylord, a child of "Deacon" William, was born in England in 1617, and accompanied his parents to Dorchester and to Windsor. He was married (1st) 22 April, 1648, to Mary, daughter of " Deacon" Edward and Frances((???)
1 CONC ) Stebbings, or Stebbins, of Hartford, Conn. She died 29 June,1657, and he was married (2nd) to Sarah Rockwell 22 March, 1658. Walter Gaylord died at Windsor 9 Aug., 1689.
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: He emigrated with his father in 1630. He settledin Windsor, Ct. He was admitted as member of Windsor Church 5 May 1651, contributed 2s6d, to Connecticut Fund for Relief of Poor in other colonies, 1676. His wife gave in cloth
1 CONC  6s 3d; his sister Eliezer is6d in flax. He had an acre lot and dwelling house from Matthew Sension in the Palizade at Windsor. RTMIS00008.7
