0 @N6000000000337379625@ NOTE 5. Walter GAYLORD, (William), b. ca 1622 England, d. 9 August 1689 Windsor, CT., (Wdsr VR Vol. 1, p. 44; Col. D, p. 57), emigrated with his father in 1630. Settled in Windsor, CT., where he m. 1) Mary STEBBINS 22 April 1648 Windso
1 CONC r, CT. (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Htfd VR Vol. D, p. 23; Vol. FFS, p. 27), daughter of Deacon Edward S and Frances (Tough) Stebbins of Hartford, CT., b.c a 1630, d. 20 June 1657 Windsor, CT. (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Vol. 1, p. 56; Col. D, p. 160;
1 CONC  Vol. 1, p. 44), m. 2) Sarah ROCKWELL 22 march 1659/60 Windsor, CT. (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Vol. 1, p. 56), daughter of Deacon William and Susanna (Capen) Rockwell, b. 21 July 1638, d. 17 August 1683 Windsor, CT. (Wdsr VR Vol. 1, p. 45;
1 CONC  Col. D, p. 56)
1 CONT
1 CONT He was admitted as member of Windsor Church 5 May 1651, contributed 2s 6d, to Connecticut Fund for Relief of Poor in other Colonies, 1676; his wife gave in cloth 6s 3d; his s. Eliezer is 6d, in flax.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Walter had an acre lott and dwelling house from Matthew Sension, in the Palizade at Windsor, (now the lot of Mrs. Anson Loomis [1892])" (Genealogies and Biographies of Ancient Windsor, Henry R Stiles, p. 278/9)
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Walter and Mary (all born Windsor):
1 CONT
1 CONT 33. Joseph, b. 13 May 1649 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Vol. 1, p. 14, 44)
1 CONT
1 CONT 34. Mary, b. 19 March 1650 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Vol. 1, p. 14, 16)
1 CONT
1 CONT 35. Joanna, b. 5 February 1652 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Col. 1, p. 14)
1 CONT
1 CONT 36. Benjamin, b. 12 April 1655 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Vol. 1, p. 14; Col. 2, p. 158), d. January 1690 Windsor, CT. (has been called Samuel Benjamin, he is also the one who possible m. Ruth Williams, daughter of William and Jane William
1 CONC s and probably the father of Patience who m. Isaac Tomlinson 25 March 1712 Derby, CT (Dby VR Vol. LR3, p. 9) (see "The American Genealogist," Vol. 29, p. 254 'From a Genealogists notebook v Patience (Gaylord) Tomlinson', D.L. Jaco
1 CONC bus)
1 CONT
1 CONT 37. Isaac, b. 21 June 1657 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Col. 2, p. 161; Col. 1, p. 14), d. ca 1674. (not mentioned in will of Deacon Edward Stebbins, dated 24 August 1663)
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Walter and Sarah (all born Windsor): 
1 CONT
1 CONT 38. Eleazer, b. 7 March 1662/3 (Wdsr VR Vol. MG; Col. 1, p. 54; Vol. 1, p. 14)
1 CONT
