1 CONT !John Shelton owned "Currioman" in Westmoreland Co.; Bought Carotoman in Lancaster Co., VA 11-11-1672 from William Clapham; Built "Rural Plains" (Shelton Home) in Hanover Co., VA in 1670; Vestryman in St. Paul Church 1705. Descend
1 CONC ants are the
1 CONT Sheltons of "Rural Plains", Hanover Co., VA per Z.F. Shelton. John's will was filed in Westmoreland Co, prob. 4-29-1708, had six children living, wife Jane.
1 CONT !"Rural Plains", Shelton home in Hanover Co., in 1670 was still owned by male descendant. It was under shellfire in 3 wars. Hanover Co. records burned 1781 after being carried to Richmond for safety.
1 CONT !John's son William inherited Rural Plains; his son Capt. John Shelton, was killed in Battle of Brandywine.
1 CONT !"The Sheltons" by Z. F. Shelton furnished some of the above information.
