1 CONT  Subject: Arledge Connection
1 CONT
1 CONT  Pam,
1 CONT  I have enjoyed your web page on the Arledge family. My possible connection is
1 CONT  thru Clement Ardridge and Mary Tilles' daughter, Mary Jane.
1 CONT  My line is:
1 CONT 1) Henry Harding (1666-1698 VA) md. Jane Arledge.
1 CONT 2) William Harding (1690 VA- 1752) wife Unknown.
1 CONT 3) Thomas Harden (1716 VA - bef 25 May 1809 NC) md. Unknown 1st wife.
1 CONT     If this Thomas Harden is the father of Jane Harden has not been proven.
1 CONT 4) Jane Harden (c1750 NC - 1 Jun 1832 MO) md. William Hornbuckle.
1 CONT 5) Sarah Jane Hornbuckle (c1772 NC - prob. before 1810 KY) md. Henry
1 CONT  Overstreet.
1 CONT 6) Martha Overstreet ( 2 Oct 1797 KY - 7 Jul 1864 KY) md. Joseph Baughn.
1 CONT 7) James Henry Baughn ( 22 Feb 1834 KY - 2 Feb 1898 KY) md. Elizabeth Ann
1 CONT  Walker.
1 CONT 8) Otis James Baughn (23 Apr 1877 KY - 11 Feb 1948 AZ) md. Mary Holman
1 CONT  Fairhurst.
1 CONT 9) Alfred Fairhurst Baughn (1 May 1912 AZ - ) md. Barbara Doris Hobbs.
1 CONT 10) Brent Fairhurst Baughn ( 27 Jun 1941 CA - )    --- ME ---
1 CONT
1 CONT The Harding connections were by correspondance with Lee Pound. He did this
1 CONT thru deeds, wills and court records. He has Henry Harding md. to Jane Arledge.
1 CONT Maybe this is your Mary Jane.  Henry Harding (1666-1698) is the son of Thomas Harden and Anne Mosley. He is  the immigrant ancestor. The Hardings are from London, ENG. and the early  family is in Tyler's Quarterly Magazine "Hardin
1 CONC gs of London and Virginia" by  Mrs. O. A. Keach.
1 CONT     Brent Baughn     < Bbaughn@aol.com >
