1 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1663, St.  Stephens, Northumberland, Virginia 
1 CONT Children of  THOMAS HARDING and ANNE MOSELY  are: 
1 CONT i.   ANNE3 HARDING, b. 1663,  Northumberland, Virginia. 
1 CONT 3.            ii.   THOMAS HARDING, b. 04 September  1664, St. Stephens 
1 CONT Parish, Northumberland, Virginia; d. Bef. September 1691,  Northumberland, 
1 CONT Virginia. 
1 CONT iii.   MARY HARDING, b. 1667, St.  Stephens Parish, Northumberland, Virginia. 
1 CONT iv.   WILLIAM HARDING, b. 20 July 1669, St.  Stephens Parish, Northumberland, 
1 CONT Virginia. 
1 CONT 4.            v.   HENRY HARDING, b. 1670, St.  Stephens Parish, 
1 CONT Northumberland, Virginia; d. 19 May 1698, Stafford County,  Virginia. 
1 CONT vi.   JOHN HARDING, b. 1672,  Northumberland, Virginia. 
1 CONT vii.   GEORGE HARDING, b. 1674,  Northumberland, Virginia. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 3 
1 CONT
1 CONT 3.  THOMAS3 HARDING  (THOMAS2, GEORGE1) was born 04 September 1664 in St.  
1 CONT Stephens Parish, Northumberland, Virginia, and died Bef. September 1691 in  
1 CONT Northumberland, Virginia.  He  married (1) ELIZABETH.    He married (2)  ANNE 
1 CONT HAYNIE, daughter of  JOHN HAYNIE and JANE MORRIS.   
1 CONT Notes for  THOMAS HARDING: 
1 CONT In "Tennessee, a History,"  published in 1933 by the American Historical 
1 CONT Society, it is stated that Thomas  and Elizabeth HARDING, the parents of the 
1 CONT Thomas HARDING who married Mary GILES,  came to Virginia in 1650 and settled in 
1 CONT Norfolk County.  In a deed, this Thomas HARDING describes  himself as of 
1 CONT "Lynhaven River, Lower Norfolk," Vol. III, page  60. 
1 CONT It is almost impossible  for a couple coming to Virginia in 1650 -- and 
1 CONT presumably of age -- to have  produced a son of an age to marry Mary GILES, who 
1 CONT could not have been born until  after 1683, the date of her parent's marriage. 
1 CONT Wm. G. AMBROSE speculates  that it is more probable that this Thomas and 
1 CONT Elizabeth were married circa 1650  and were the grandparent's of the Thomas who 
1 CONT married Mary  GILES. 
1 CONT He adds that is it  possible that this is the Thomas HARDING who came to 
1 CONT Virginia prior to 1650 with  Moore Fauntleroy (Greer's "Early Virginia 
1 CONT Immigrants," page  146). 
1 CONT Page 22, Court held 2  September 1692, haying Capt. Guardian to HARDING.  Mr. 
1 CONT John HAYING, senior, petitioned  court for guardianship of Thomas HARDING, 
1 CONT 3-year old son of Thomas HARDING,  (deceased) and Mr. HAYNIE's  daughter 
1 CONT (deceased).  (daughter's name not stated) 
1 CONT * The Original Lists of  Persons of Quality 
1 CONT Lists of the Living and  Dead in Virginia, February 16th 1623 (i.e. 162xxx) 
1 CONT Thomas  HARDING 
1 CONT * Early Virginia  Immigrants; 1623-1666 
1 CONT H 
1 CONT HARDING, Sarah, 1643, by  Benjamin Harryson, Gent. James City, Co. 
1 CONT HARDING Ja., 1651, by Mr.  Rowland Burnham, -- Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Ann, 1651, by  Henry Nicholls, Lower Norfolk Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Tho., 1652, by  Henry Nicholls, Lancaster Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Joane, 1642, by  Jerimiah Grey, James City Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Mary, 1653, by  Anto. Hoskins, Northampton Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Mary, 1637, by  Richard Bennett, New Norfolk Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Tho., 1650, by  Capt. Moore Faulteroy, -- Co. 
1 CONT HARDING, Mary, 1635, by  Richard Bennett, -- Co. 
1 CONT * Colonial Records of  Virginia at Elizabeth Cittye 
1 CONT Capt. Isacke Whittakers .  . . , Thomas HARDING, . . . George Nuc
1 CONT Burwell's Bay and call it  Warnicqueack.  Stith calls it  Warrasqueake and gives 
1 CONT and interesting account of "the King of that town," and  his hospitable 
1 CONT treatment of Capt. Smith on the night of the 29th of December,  1606; page 85. 
1 CONT In particulares of land,  "McDonald Ms. above referred to it as spelt as 
1 CONT shown in the following extract:  "Warofquolacke Plantation conteyning dowewards 
1 CONT from Hoggifland, 14 miles by the  ryver side," & c., page 313. 
1 CONT Hening has it  Warrosquoiack, Vol. 1, page 149.  
1 CONT In 1634 "the country  divided into eight shires," and this being one of them. 
1 CONT  Hening ther spells it  Warrosquyoake.  Vol. L, page  224. 
1 CONT The * information was  given to me by another HARDING researcher, ?? 
1 CONT I have conflicting info  and will research the facts. 
1 CONT See "The First Seventeen  Years Virginia 1607-1624" by Charles E. Hatch, Jr. 
1 CONT Children of  THOMAS HARDING and ELIZABETH  are: 
1 CONT 5.             i.   WILLIAM4 HARDING, d. Abt. 1741,  Henrico County, 
1 CONT Virginia. 
1 CONT 6.            ii.   THOMAS HARDING, b. Abt. 1686,  Henrico County, Virginia; 
1 CONT d. Abt. 1731, Henrico County,  Virginia. 
1 CONT 4.  HENRY3 HARDING  (THOMAS2, GEORGE1) was born 1670 in St. Stephens Parrish, 
1 CONT  Northumberland, Virginia, and died 19 May 1698 in Stafford County,  
1 CONT Virginia.  He married  JANE ARLEDGE Abt. 1688 in St.  Stephens, Northumberland, 
1 CONT Virginia.   
1 CONT More About  HENRY HARDING and JANE ARLEDGE: 
1 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1688, St.  Stephens, Northumberland, Virginia 
1 CONT Child of  HENRY HARDING and JANE ARLEDGE  is: 
1 CONT i.   WILLIAM4 HARDING. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 4 
1 CONT
1 CONT 5.  WILLIAM4 HARDING  (THOMAS3, THOMAS2, GEORGE1) died Abt. 1741 in Henrico 
1 CONT County,  Virginia. 
1 CONT Notes for  WILLIAM HARDING: 
1 CONT 3 March 1717, Thomas  HARDING of Henrico County to William HARDING of same 
1 CONT for L10, upper half of  tract patented by said Thomas on E. branch of Tuckahoe, 
1 CONT bounded by land Chumbley  bought of said Thomas.   
1 CONT Witnessed by John Woodson,  Edw. Coyle. 
1 CONT Recorded 3 March  1717. 
1 CONT Mary GILES, wife of Thomas  HARDING, had relinquished her dower (Henrico 
1 CONT Deeds and Wills 1714-1718, page  233) 
1 CONT 7 May 1718, William  HARDING and Joseph PLEASANTS witnessed a deed of Henry 
1 CONT Hill, Henrico, saddler to  John Gibbs, planter, of same.  (Henrico Deeds and 
1 CONT Wills 1714-1718, pages  261) 
1 CONT 8 November 1726, Thomas  HARDING and William HARDING witnessed the deed of 
1 CONT Chas. Holms to John Pleasants,  Henrico County, North side of James River near 
1 CONT mouth of Four Mile  Creek. 
1 CONT 2 October 1734, William  HARDIN of Henrico County to Rich. Trueman, Jr. of 
1 CONT same for L20, land on N. side  White Oak Swamp and Bore(Boar) Swamp, being tract 
1 CONT granted to John Pleasants,  decd., 100 acres. Witnessed by Rich. Deane 
1 CONT (Henrico County Wills and Deeds  1725-1737, page 453).  This land is  located at the 
1 CONT present intersection of Route 60 and I-295 in eastern Henrico  County, 
1 CONT Virginia. 
1 CONT 9 October 1734, William  HARDIN and Arthur Moseley witnessed the deed of 
1 CONT William Williamson, Henrico, to  William Cheatham, same, 300 acres granted by 
1 CONT patent to said Williamson.  1 August 1734.  (Henrico Deeds and Wills 1725-1737, 
1 CONT page  453) 
1 CONT 23 April 1740, Frances  Wilkinson, widow of Henrico County to William HARDIN, 
1 CONT same, 130 acres on south  side of branch of Stratons Creek, next to Thomas 
1 CONT Cheatham, Arthur Moseley, John  Hamlin and said HARDEN.  Witnessed  by Thos. 
1 CONT Cheatham, Jno. Hamlin.  Recorded November 1740 (Misc. Court Records 1738-1746 
1 CONT Henrico  County) 
1 CONT October 1741, Thomas  HARDING, orphan of William HARDING. decd., chooses 
1 CONT William HARDING as his  guardian.  (Henrico County Orders  1737-1746, page 158) 
1 CONT September 1743, William  HARDING, guardian for Thomas HARDING, orphan, 
1 CONT presents account.  (Henrico Orders 1737-1746, page  231) 
1 CONT I am guessing that William  HARDING - the guardian of Thomas HARDING - was 
1 CONT probably his grandfather as this  William died in 1746 and Thomas father died 
1 CONT circa  1741. 
1 CONT >From Henrico County Deeds  and Wills 1744-1748, page 120: 
1 CONT Will of William HARDING,  written 12 December 1741: 
1 CONT To my son Thomas, the land  I live upon, likewise all land I hold and 2 
1 CONT Negroes, a Brass Kettle, 2 Iron  pots, a Skillet, 2 Basons, 2 Dishes, 2 Guns, a 
1 CONT large Chest, an Oval Tables, one  feather bed . . . To daughter Sarah, the bed I 
1 CONT now lie upon . . . To daughter  Martha, 1 Negro, 1 Feather bed, 2 Iron pots, 2 
1 CONT Dishes, 2 Plates, 1 Trunk, 1  Saddle, 1 Cow and calf. . . To son Thomas, the 
1 CONT remainder of my personal estate .  . . John Povall, executor. 
1 CONT W, the mark of Wm  HARDING 
1 CONT Witnessed by Peter  Varnier, Wm. Cheatham, Anne Cheatham 
1 CONT Proven April 1746   
1 CONT Last names of daughters  are not given. 
1 CONT Children of  WILLIAM HARDING  are: 
1 CONT i.   THOMAS5 HARDING. 
1 CONT ii.   SARAH HARDING. 
1 CONT iii.   MARTHA HARDING. 
1 CONT 6.  THOMAS4 HARDING  (THOMAS3, THOMAS2, GEORGE1) was born Abt. 1686 in 
1 CONT Henrico County,  Virginia, and died Abt. 1731 in Henrico County, Virginia.  He 
1 CONT married MARY GILES Abt. 1710 in Henrico  County, Virginia, daughter of WILLIAM 
1 CONT GILES and BETHENIAH KNOWLES.  She was born Abt. 1688, and died Aft.  1731. 
1 CONT Notes for  THOMAS HARDING: 
1 CONT Could be the son of  William HARDING, Immigrant, (Headright), Henrico Co., 
1 CONT granted land north side of  James River. 
1 CONT Another possibility is  Thomas HARDING, as stated in this genealogy report. 
1 CONT A patent was recorded for  Thomas HARDEN on 31 October 1716, 319 acr
1 CONT Henrico County, north side of  James River, on the east side of the main branch 
1 CONT of Tuckahoe Creek, beginning at  a Beaver Pond belonging to John Eless (ELLIS), 
1 CONT for 5 shillings and  transportation of six (6) persons.  (Virginia Land 
1 CONT Patents, Book 10, Page 298) 
1 CONT A survey of this property  was made on 6 February 1707 for Thomas HARDEN - 
1 CONT 319 acres in Henrico  county.  (Henrico Wills and Deeds  1706-1709, page 97) 
1 CONT On 6 May 1717, Benjamin  Woodson, Sr. of Henrico sold to Thomas HARDING of 
1 CONT Henrico for L10 currency, 150  acres in Henrico County on the south side of 
1 CONT Chickahominy Swamp (River), bindeth  on the northwest upon the line of Richard 
1 CONT Woodson, decd.  Sarah Woodson relinquishes  dower. 
1 CONT (Henrico Wills and Deeds  1714-1718, page 172) 
1 CONT This land was in the  general vicinity of his other land along Tuckahoe  
1 CONT Creek. 
1 CONT In April 1718, Thomas  HARDING and Nowel BURTON witnessed a deed of Thomas 
1 CONT Williamson of Varina Parish,  Henrico County, to Edmund Allen of James City 
1 CONT County.   
1 CONT (Henrico Wills and Deeds  1714-1718) 
1 CONT On 1 May 1726 Thomas  HARDING, Edmund Allen and James Howl witnessed the deed 
1 CONT of Robert Childers,  Henrico, to Charles Winfree, St. Peter's Parish, N
1 CONT Kent County, Virginia, 50  acres in Henrico. 
1 CONT (Henrico Wills and Deeds  1725-1737, page 24) 
1 CONT 17 May 1729, Thomas  HARDING of Verina Parish, Henrico, deeded to Edward 
1 CONT THOMAS (son-in-law) of St.  James parish, Goochland County, Virginia, 60 acres on 
1 CONT the east branch of  Tuckahoe Creek at Drinking Hole Branch (Goochland County 
1 CONT Deed Book 1, page  108) 
1 CONT This was probably a  wedding gift as the same land was given to his daughter, 
1 CONT Mary, in his will  written three months earlier. 
1 CONT The will of Thomas HARDING  of Henrico County is dated 1728/9 lists sons 
1 CONT William, Thomas, daughter Mary  Thomas and wife Mary.  This Thomas  also had a 
1 CONT daughter Susannah, who married Capt. Charles Ellis, born  1719. 
1 CONT Will was proved (recorded)  April 1731, Henrico County but was dated 10 March 
1 CONT 1728 or  1729. 
1 CONT Virginia Will Book  1725-1737, page 294 
1 CONT Henrico County  Miscellaneous Court Records, Vol. 3 1727-1737, page  34
1 CONT Henrico County, Virginia  Deed and Wills 1. part 2 -- 1725 - 1735, page 291-  
1 CONT 294: 
1 CONT Thomas HARDING of Henrico  County, deceased.  
1 CONT To my son, William  HARDING, all my land in Henrico County that lies below 
1 CONT the branch called  "Hardings Branch" by computation, 140 acres, and binding on 
1 CONT the little Tuckahoe  Creek. 
1 CONT To my son, Thomas, the  plantation whereon I now dwell and all  land between 
1 CONT Harding Branch and Drinking Hole Branch with all my land in  Goochland County 
1 CONT that lies between (Michael) Holland's Line and the Main  Road. 
1 CONT To my beloved daughter  Mary Thomas, all land that binds on Drinking Hole on 
1 CONT the upper side binding on  the Main Road on the upper side of the creek, 160 
1 CONT acres.  Also on heifer and one calf.   
1 CONT I do appoint and  constitute my wife, Mary, my whole and sole  executor. 
1 CONT Thomas Harding.   
1 CONT Witnessed by Nicholas COX  and John BOWIE 
1 CONT Inventory was made 16  April 1731 by Edward Curd, Luke Smith and Obediah 
1 CONT Smith and valued at L84.8.9,  presented by Mary HARDING (page 299) 
1 CONT By 1742 Mary Giles HARDING  had married Thomas HUGHES of Henrico Count
1 CONT Virginia. 
1 CONT Notes for  MARY GILES: 
1 CONT April 1742, William  HARDING versus Thomas HUGHES and Mary, his wife, 
1 CONT executors of John North, decd,  was continued (Henrico Orders 1737-1746, page 180).  
1 CONT This could have been either William  HARDING. 
1 CONT 8 October 1747, Thomas  HUGHES and Mary HUGHES, wife, of Henrico Parish, 
1 CONT Henrico County, Virignia,  "having a right of dower to and in one certain parcel . 
1 CONT . . which formerly  belonged to Thomas HARDING, decd" lying in Parish a
1 CONT County of Henrico on  Harding's branch, same tract which said Thomas HARDING gave 
1 CONT his two sons William  and Thomas . . . for consideration of L17.10 paid by 
1 CONT William HARDING, they  relinquish right of dower in land.   
1 CONT Witnessed by Wm. Street,  Thomas Finton, Charles Ellis and Thomas Elli
1 CONT Recorded January 1747/48.  (Henrico Wills and Deeds 1744-1748, page  335.) 
1 CONT Marriage Notes for  THOMAS HARDING and MARY GILES: 
1 CONT Brodie, John B., "Historic  Southern Families," Vol. 3, 1959, page 194 
1 CONT Wulfeck, Doroty Ford,  "HARDIN and HARDING of Virginia and Kentucky, a
1 CONT supplement. 
1 CONT More About  THOMAS HARDING and MARY GILES: 
1 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1710,  Henrico County, Virginia 
1 CONT Children of  THOMAS HARDING and MARY GILES  are: 
1 CONT 7.             i.   BETHENIA5 HARDING, b. Henrico County,  Virginia. 
1 CONT ii.   THOMAS HARDING. 
1 CONT Notes for  THOMAS HARDING: 
1 CONT Thomas HARDING was  given land where the home plantation was and all la
1 CONT between Harding Branch and  Drinking Hole Branch, plus all his father's land in 
1 CONT Goochland  County. 
1 CONT He sold the land  willed to him by his father to his brother William. 
1 CONT This might be the  Thomas HARDING who moved to Louisa County, Virginia and 
1 CONT bought land in 1753  (Louisa County Deed Book "A", page 503) 
1 CONT iii.   MARY HARDING, b. Bet. 1711 - 1715,  Virginia; m. EDWARD THOMAS, Abt.  
1 CONT 1728. 
1 CONT Notes for  MARY HARDING: 
1 CONT Mary Thomas inherited  160 acres on Drinking Hole Branch. 
1 CONT More About  EDWARD THOMAS and  MARY HARDING: 
1 CONT Marriage: Abt.  1728 
1 CONT 8.           iv.   SUSANNAH HARDING, b. 07 January  1718/19, Henrico County, 
1 CONT Virginia; d. Abt. 1817, Amherst County,  Virginia.9.         v.            
1 CONT WILLIAM  HARDING,  b. 23 February 1719/20, Henrico County, Virginia; d. Abt. 
1 CONT 1768, Goochland  County, Virginia.
