1 CONT WILL OF JAMES DANIEL SR. November 8, 1791.
1 CONT in the name of God, Amen, I James Daniel Sr, of Orange County being at present permitted to enjoy a sound state of mind and memory, Thanks be to God for it and calling to mind that it is appointed for all flesh to die, hereby revo
1 CONC king all other will or x'Llls, do constitute and appoint this my last will and testament.
1 CONT Viz: I Give my soul to God who gave it into existence In full comfi- that he will receive it into Glory and my body a Christian burial at the discretion of my executives hereafter appointed.
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my dear and well beloved children, Elizabeth Daniel Margaret Daniel, Frances Daniel, James Daniel, William Daniel Susanna Daniel and Mary Daniel the land where I now live, to them and their heirs for
1 CONC ever to remain a home for 'hen, undivided and unsold until consent of every one of the above named children shall be had, then to be equally divided among them item- will and desire is that, as my sons have received a feather bed 
1 CONC that my daughters shall each have a good one.
1 CONT Item: I give my riding horse to my daughter, Elizabeth Daniel.
1 CONT Item: I give all the residue of my estate after paying all my just debts to remain with my said children on same terms with my land.
1 CONT 1 do hereby constitute and appoint John Daniel, my executor of this my last will and testament in confirmation of I have here unto set my hand and seal this eighth day of November, one thousand seven hundred ninety one. (November 
1 CONC 8, 1791).
1 CONT James Daniel Sr.
1 CONT Will proved in Orange County, Virginia, 27 February 1792.
