1 CONT 4 MARY WARNER, fifth child of Augustine Warner II and his wife,Mildred Reade, married February 17, 1680, John Smith, of "Purton",Gloucester County, Va. She died November 13, 1700. Their childrenwere: i John Smith, married Anne Ale
1 CONC xander who afterwards married Col.Henry Willis. ii Elizabeth Smith, married first Henry Harrison andsecondly Col. Francis Willis. iii Augustine Smith (mentioned later asNo. 5). iv Sarah Smith, married John Taliaferro. Their daught
1 CONC er, aMary Taliaferro, married Col. Francis Thornton II, born in 1682, of"The Falls", Stafford County, Va. He was the son of Francis Thornton,born in 1651, who married Alice Savage, daughter of Capt. AnthonySavage, a justice of Glo
1 CONC ucester County, Va., in 1660. His grandfatherwas William Thornton, of "The Hills", Yorkshire, England, who came toVirginia about 1646 and settled in York County and afterwards moved toGloucester County and built a home about four 
1 CONC miles northwest ofGloucester Point which he named "The Hills". Late in life he moved toStafford County.
