0 @N6000000002303891135@ NOTE Author Name:janice mcalpine
1 CONT Author Email:mcalpage@cox.net
1 CONT Added:14 Oct 2007
1 CONT URL:
1 CONT Note:The Thomas Morrow who died 30 August 1830 in Casey Co., Kentucky, was not the Thomas Morrow who married Rebecca Small in Virginia. The Casey Co. Thomas Morrow was born in Pennsylvania and served 7 years -- from 1777 to 1785 -
1 CONC - in the Pennsylvania line during the Revolutionary War. I have a copy of his Revolutionary War pension file with his date of death written on the award certificate. He was an entirely different man.
1 CONT
1 CONT The correct Thomas Morrow was on Virginia records during the entire war and actually served in the Henry Co., Virginia, militia under his brother-in-law, Matthew Small. See, for example, Bk 3 page 36 Henry Co. VA Court Records 26 
1 CONC July 1782; LDS Film # 031979: "Matthew Small is appointed Captain of the Militia in the County [Henry] in the room of Thomas Henderson who hath removed out of the County. John Corn appointed Lieut. and Thomas Morrow, Ensign to the
1 CONC  said Small."
1 CONT
1 CONT I hope this is helpful.
1 CONT
1 CONT Janice
