1 CONT
1 CONT SOME RECORDS INDICATE DOB 1612. WESTERLY, R. I. (POP. 7300) IS A PLACE THAT ONE WOULD BE THRI LLED TO VISIT IF A DESCENDENT OF THE ABOVE ELDER JOHN CRANDALL.  MANY CHURCHES, UNUSAL LIBRAR Y THE OLD HOMESTEAD, BUILT IN 1665 (STILL 
1 CONC OWNED BY A MEMBER OF THE CRANDALL FAMILY) (DR. HARR Y FRANKLIN CRANDALL).  ONE SHOULD SEE THE ORIGINAL ORCHARD AND VISIT THE TWENTY-SEVEN PIONEE R GRAVES WITH THEIR PRIMITIVE STONE MARKERS.  WESTERLY WAS INCORPORATED IN 1669 AND T
1 CONC HERE WER E THIRTY FAMILIES SCATTERED ALL OVER THE 10 X 20 MILE TRACT. IT WAS A FRONTIER TOWN AND BOT H MASS. AND CONN. LAID CLAIM TO THE LAND AS THEIR OWN. THE BOUNDARY QUESTIONS WAS NOT SETTLE D UNTIL 1728 AND THE COLONY SAVED.
1 CONT   ELDER JOHN CRANDALL WAS BORN 1612 (ONE AUTHORITY SAYS 1609) IN MONMOUTHSHIRE, ENGLAND.  HI S FATHER WAS JOHN CRANDALL AND HIS MOTHER WAS ELIZABETH DRAKE A DESCENDENT OF THE PRINCESS EL IZABETH OF SCOTLAND, WHO IN TURN IS DESCEND
1 CONC ENT FROM MALCOLM II KING OF SCOTLAND.
1 CONT   JOHN CRANDALL CAME TO BOSTON ABOUT 1634 AND BY 1637 WAS LIVING IN PROVIDENCE.  HE WAS AN AC TIVE MEMBER OF THE BAPTIST CHURCH IN NEWPORT JULY 21, 1651.  LATER ON AT WESTERLY HE WAS TH E FIRST BAPTIST ELDER.  THE NAME OF HIS FIRS
1 CONC T WIFE IS UNKNOWN ALTHOUGH IT IS RECORDED THAT SH E DIED AUG. 1, 1670 AND WAS BURIED ON AUG. 2, 1670. (MILDRED SMALL OF ETNA, PA. STATES THAT S HE SUMS IN THE RECORDS AT WASH. D.C. THAT FIRST WIFE OF ELDER JOHN CRANDALL WAS MARY O
1 CONC PP, WH O DIED AUG. 20, 1969.)
1 CONT    JOHN CRANDALL WAS ONE OF THE ORIGINAL PURCHASERS FROM CHIEF SOSOA OF NARRAGANSETT OF THE M ISQUAMIOUTT TRIBE, OF THE LAND COMPROMISING. WESTERLY, R.I.  HIS HOUSE, NEAR BURDENS POND, ST ILL STANDS IN PART AND ACROSS FROM THE HOU
1 CONC SE IS THE OLD ORCHARD WITH THE CEMETARY IN IT AND T HE 27 GRAVES. HE DIED IN NEWPORT HAVING GONE THERE ON ACCOUNT OF THE INDIAN WAR.  DATE OF DEA TH 1676?  HE IS BURIED IN THE OLD CEMETARY AT WESTERLY.
1 CONT JOHN WAS THE FIRST BAPTIST ELDER, DEPUTY COMMISSIONER AND STATESMAN OF NEWPORT.
1 CONT HE ARRIVED IN BOSTON IN 1634.[test.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Ancestors of Index.FTW]
