0 @N6000000004548204046@ NOTE Eber Crandall, youngest son of John Crandal,l was born in 1676; died 1727 at Westport, Rhode Island. He was a ship builder. His first wife died leaving no children. His second wife was a daughter of George Lampere.
0 @N6000000004548288871@ NOTE Owned land in both Westerly and Kingston. In late 1678 hemarried Hannah (Gaylor d) Crandall, the widow of Elder JohnCramdall (see pp. 1-3 in "Elder John Cranda ll of R.I. and hisdescendants by John C. Crandall. 1949.  (Some lists 
1 CONC ie. Clyde Uries notes and Carl and Alson Cottrell's Geneological List showElizabeth (R in 14) as his wife) but the fact that Hannah wasthe wife of Elder John Crandall e xplains how he came to own theland in Kingston which had been
